eed for structured and inclusive environments to help autistic pupils overcome learning barriers.\u2022 Monitor practice and provide evidence of embedding good autism practice.\fSchools Standards Framework3 Why is it important to have specific standards for autistic pupils?\nAutistic pupils often face significant barriers to learning within the educational environment. These can be overcome by ensuring we create supportive teaching environments that are structured, consistent, and respectful of differences. The AET Schools Standards support school leaders to address the specific barriers to learning experienced by autistic pupils. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 2, "split_id": 2, "split_idx_start": 1213, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "106d9ac620f03ff76fe93577deb483b5eb0d7b6475bf4f09d820abb6bb8fe5d1", "range": [304, 379]}, {"doc_id": "8e49feb148a2e2a97b9653912cb5c2643b85d00a11539f6b908b34aa50339a3b", "range": [0, 126]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.027903439477086067, -0.08819510042667389, -0.02522677555680275, -0.004887815564870834, 0.029033998027443886, 0.006606665905565023, 0.023886464536190033, -0.0473237968981266, -0.04959440976381302, 0.0017373159062117338, 0.03020022064447403, -0.06672097742557526, 0.0006656128680333495, 0.018100803717970848, 0.005137742031365633, -0.05799458548426628, 0.02756979502737522, 0.02375297248363495, -0.03911493346095085, 0.027872838079929352, 0.02062922902405262, 0.01687312312424183, -0.008956128731369972, 0.02476322650909424, 0.024097256362438202, -0.012268425896763802, 0.015200409106910229, -0.004941846244037151, 0.03052905574440956, -0.057569243013858795, 0.030519122257828712, -0.0014346142997965217, 0.01280607096850872, 0.028613530099391937, 2.419334350634017e-06, 0.03772146627306938, 0.01822