ood autism practice, a practitioner guide and a suite of case studies.\f4 Schools Standards Framework\nThe Eight Principles of Good Autism Practice\nThis is how the Eight Principles of Good Autism Practice are embedded in the four themes. Principle One: Understanding the strengths, interests, and needs of each autistic pupil.\nPrinciple Two: Enabling the autistic pupil to contribute to and influence decisions.\nPrinciple Three: Collaboration with parents/carers and other professionals and services.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 3, "split_id": 8, "split_idx_start": 3955, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "4c6dbcadfa0e5a9fa006673f002e3cff795b08680031c6caf946c624cc120166", "range": [479, 584]}, {"doc_id": "121b52b22d1f081976d4ca491373dbcd0c12bfacfcd51b2005b9fa4efe965d91", "range": [0, 89]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.029930757358670235, -0.08028517663478851, -0.01906578429043293, 0.00276753306388855, 9.426848555449396e-05, 0.01461252011358738, -0.004988927394151688, -0.0538165383040905, -0.07129993289709091, 0.014712340198457241, 0.013250346295535564, -0.06469908356666565, 0.017951542511582375, -0.018947001546621323, -0.019973991438746452, -0.05401100590825081, 0.01373012363910675, 0.02431359887123108, -0.02956220880150795, 0.018279796466231346, 0.008625194430351257, 0.00784197449684143, -0.007963434793055058, 0.024201255291700363, 0.020106632262468338, -0.009640950709581375, -9.848198533290997e-05, 0.012150061316788197, 0.04246753081679344, -0.04777604714035988, 0.018231479451060295, -0.014379722997546196, 0.007416056003421545, 0.027988286688923836, 2.347167992411414e-06, 0.020589390769600868, 0.018876634538173676, -0.028248315677046776, 0.02931571565568447, -0.02271271124482155, -0.07100778818130493, 0.011318129487335682, 0.04879