13488993048668, -0.021082911640405655, 0.0009651492000557482, 0.0001920788927236572, -0.020827630534768105, -0.07621816545724869, -0.04204385727643967, 0.012501530349254608, 2.090563667938407e-34, -0.0077674491330981255, -0.0024221406783908606, 0.017295876517891884, -0.07163248211145401, 0.005232291761785746, -0.002384113147854805, -0.02172241359949112, 0.020803386345505714, -0.0011174798710271716, -0.024253934621810913, -0.02732953429222107], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "1eb6ede103efe81c775daae0c289e7f4cbf2089ee4aa91e650b012abe2669eee", "content": "This chunk details components of the AET Schools Professional Development Programme, which supports educators in enhancing their practices for autistic children. It specifically mentions the Schools Competency Framework and the Progression Framework, followed by a transition to a summary of the interconnections between the four themes, the Eight Principles of Good Autism Practice, and the AET Schools Standards and Competencies.In addition to the Standards the AET Schools Professional Development Programme consists of:\n\u2022 The Schools Competency Framework that enables practitioners to evaluate and reflect upon their own practice when working with autistic children.\n\u2022 A Progression Framework that is a comprehensive interactive assessment tool that supports practitioners to identify learning priorities, set key learning intentions, and track progress for autistic children and young people in both mainstream and specialist educational provisions.\nAET Schools Professional Development Programme.\fSchools Standards Framework7 At a Glance: The four themes, the Eight Principles of Good Autism Practice, the AET Schools Standards, and the AET Schools Competencies.\nThe following tables outline how the four themes, the Eight Principles of Good Autism Practice, the AET Schools Standards, and the AET Schools Competencies are interlinked.\f", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 6, "split_id": 15, "split_idx_start": 7668, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "df7499eda8043ef508b16e6904b8a64910101622ced3ee941dfc64e2f4cbb454", "range": [1008, 1248]}, {"doc_id": "e623083179e177ffb5ab977c32051a1392c7f5120c73dc0cd312d696a36f5a8b", "range": [0, 173]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.01545694749802351, -0.09099749475717545, -0.020463502034544945, -0.010741660371422768, 0.005681570619344711, 0.03412013128399849, 0.006027543917298317, -0.041180312633514404, -0.0808616355061531, 0.050892218947410583, 0.02814542129635811, -0.04111144319176674, 0.03177241235971451, 0.017762208357453346, -0.0006200126954354346, -0.07280459254980087, 0.014960026368498802, 0.030860699713230133, -0.04283474013209343, 0.033619098365306854, 0.026239939033985138, 0.00867235567420721, -0.03793497011065483, 0.04501751810312271, 0.037276580929756165, 0.005392199382185936, -0.000681039527989924, -0.0026198560371994972, 0.04203156381845474, -0.034060120582580566, 0.033012207597494125, 0.020855771377682686, 0.011066772043704987, -0.03152790293097496, 2.3154655082180398e-06, 0.025141390040516853, -0.0047060223296284676, -0.0197052750736475, 0.005735793150961399, -0.0016284449957311153, -0.056612465530633926, 0.02809339202940464, 0.044517386704683304, 0.05601836368441582, -0.02134901098906994, -0.060646407306194305, 0.010946126654744148, 0.049628548324108124, 0.04416276887059212, -0.01083841361105442, 0.002593100070953369, 0.016921520233154297, 0.033240318298339844, -0.03954583406448364, -0.08611258864402771, -0.04743035137653351, -0.003628538688644767, -0.058204155415296555, 0.054627787321805954, 0.055010050535202026, -0.023785188794136047, -0.006218848749995232, 0.018293442204594612, -0.024411041289567947, 0.050642769783735275, -0.014897157438099384, -0.016508929431438446, -0.0408899299800396, 0.032943