55, 0.015743885189294815, -0.008865517564117908, -0.014994830824434757, -0.013124067336320877], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "6da3c129636a7bd8890cd62fe080d6bf2a22e9bb5fe6086694425fbafbabba58", "content": "This chunk is part of the AET Schools Standards Framework, specifically under Principle One, which focuses on understanding the strengths, interests, and needs of each autistic pupil. It emphasizes the importance of recognizing co-occurring differences and the impact of anxiety and stress on behavior, as well as identifying key areas of difference in learning for autistic pupils.S2. We take into account how each pupil\u2019s co-occurring differences, including anxiety and stress, can affect behaviour and can cause barriers to learning. We are committed to understanding the causes and functions of behaviour.\nC1. I identify the key strengths and differences that autistic pupils face in the areas of social understanding and communication; flexibility, information processing and understanding, and sensory processing and integration.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 8, "split_id": 17, "split_idx_start": 8909, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "e623083179e177ffb5ab977c32051a1392c7f5120c73dc0cd312d696a36f5a8b", "range": [503, 507]}, {"doc_id": "dc5a5d6faeecdb0414ffb3e868ca3864b81fffd7840a170a3573935e0686ef11", "range": [0, 222]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.015138435177505016, -0.10559987276792526, -0.022454535588622093, 0.001192486030049622, 0.01902707666158676, 0.04385320842266083, 0.027962755411863327, -0.035967521369457245, -0.05381733924150467, 0.008137879893183708, -0.0158800408244133, -0.06753422319889069, -0.011940622702240944, -0.013132941909134388, -0.0016312302323058248, -0.04699420556426048, 0.026546591892838478, -0.0143