2181236743927], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "02b3af3eb9bb5f5b766880423218d0f5a37555683a90d6b3407f75dffe2022ac", "content": "This chunk is part of the AET Schools Standards Framework under the theme of \"Positive Relationships,\" specifically focusing on Principle Two: Enabling the autistic pupil to contribute to and influence decisions. It emphasizes the importance of involving pupils in their educational planning and decision-making processes to ensure their voices are heard and considered.I understand the importance of listening to the pupil and regularly consult and involve pupils in any decisions being made.\nC4. I see the pupil as a partner in their learning and actively involve autistic pupils as part of the \u2018Assess, Plan, Do, Review\u2019 cycle so that the pupil is at the centre of educational planning.\fSchools Standards Framework9 Positive Relationships\nPrinciple Three: Collaboration with parents/carers and other professionals and services.\nSTANDARDS COMPETENCIES\nS5. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 8, "split_id": 21, "split_idx_start": 10170, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "a0b56b8db68714f38adcc5de58564f6643244d4f9ca2d0f57b0a238a53ee2715", "range": [261, 385]}, {"doc_id": "430978c41c6a718626c895784502fb9731760f9ba05c5c9ea3ffff2d799c3d7d", "range": [0, 27]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.029308339580893517, -0.10789190977811813, -0.010519713163375854, 0.018667086958885193, 0.007977045141160488, 0.01783251389861107, 0.018223850056529045, -0.04985352233052254, -0.042846355587244034, 0.01149025373160839, 0.012963032349944115, -0.08481813222169876, 0.005670751444995403, -0.018298035487532616, -0.017772087827324867, -0.04966627061367035, 0.020051032304763794, 0.037184037268161774, -0.04194324091076851, 0.0255126543