he AET Schools Standards Framework, specifically under Principle Six, which focuses on creating an ethos and environment that fosters social inclusion for autistic pupils. It outlines standards related to providing supportive and predictable learning environments to enhance student wellbeing and learning participation.STANDARDS COMPETENCIES\nS11. Our enabling approaches foster a calm low-arousal learning environment and we promote a sense of wellbeing, security, and belonging for all our pupils.\nS12. Our learning environments are structured, understandable, and predictable. We adapt learning environments to enable pupils to participate fully in learning.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 10, "split_id": 30, "split_idx_start": 13161, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "1da6152bd9426eda7f4fb6eb056af0aaf60955600b605cc89c8db018e529427d", "range": [360, 388]}, {"doc_id": "f53d9541a701aa939993d84fed1a13187186a7652682cb080be7cbfb2ec401c1", "range": [0, 82]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.01548701710999012, -0.15130570530891418, -0.0160002950578928, 0.01648855395615101, 0.01073854137212038, 0.02603524923324585, 0.03548989072442055, -0.03444524109363556, -0.03553673252463341, 0.002659810706973076, 0.028663476929068565, -0.05049116164445877, 0.006615394726395607, 0.012319793924689293, 0.0061284760013222694, -0.053004488348960876, 0.04769481346011162, 0.03645859286189079, -0.054879024624824524, 0.02157333306968212, -0.023583365604281425, 0.01260167732834816, -0.032256726175546646, 0.031174588948488235, 0.03963388130068779, -0.013003571890294552, 0.03240136429667473, 0.0073775299824774265, 0.009740401059389114, -0.01813112571835518, 0.0516255721449852, 0.004212027415633202, 0.00835560355335474, -0.035918641835451126, 2.1402724996733014e-06, 0.0113