2586220800877, -0.019542977213859558, 0.0366266630589962, -0.032040081918239594, 0.008947845548391342, -0.028031185269355774, -0.005337628535926342, 0.0005138709675520658, -0.0025838071014732122, -0.014699232764542103, -0.025436952710151672], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "f53d9541a701aa939993d84fed1a13187186a7652682cb080be7cbfb2ec401c1", "content": "This chunk is part of Principle Six, focusing on creating enabling environments that foster social inclusion for autistic pupils. It outlines specific competencies related to adapting learning environments for better participation in learning, addressing barriers to learning, and ensuring classroom organization caters to the unique needs of autistic students.We adapt learning environments to enable pupils to participate fully in learning.\nC11. I understand the importance of focusing on identifying and addressing barriers to learning in the three areas of difference, namely social understanding and communication; flexibility, information processing, and understanding; and sensory processing and integration.\nC12. I provide a clearly organised classroom and an environment that takes into account the needs of autistic pupils.\f", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 10, "split_id": 31, "split_idx_start": 13421, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0a92a45b85e60215d71a1c2815daf75fdd3d95e93466dbcfdd9479e9b9f22a57", "range": [260, 342]}, {"doc_id": "bee799f38dd5f325509930b4a3a5f30c5ea1dff1af7bebaf7c1ce9c3fc5e53a8", "range": [0, 113]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.046576280146837234, -0.09270556271076202, -0.02835596725344658, 0.014253433793783188, 0.020590124651789665, 0.02795780450105667, 0.042242664843797684, -0.05549808591604233, -0.04286807030439377, 0.010774095542728901, -0.0049475631676614285