0028313067741692066, -0.0021075918339192867, 0.011884322389960289, -0.0827430710196495, -0.001957651926204562, -0.013633370399475098, -0.037108685821294785, 0.008805827237665653, 0.016803959384560585, -0.029915740713477135, -0.041097793728113174], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "21e37e705080f87e6ee3dcbb1c0162c7852379311872eb07492933b132c41786", "content": "This chunk outlines \"Principle Eight\" of the AET Schools Standards, which focuses on adapting the curriculum, teaching, and learning strategies to enhance the wellbeing and success of autistic pupils. It includes standards related to providing a balanced curriculum and promoting positive attitudes towards autism in educational settings.Principle Eight: Adapting the curriculum, teaching, and learning to promote wellbeing and success for autistic pupils.\nSTANDARDS COMPETENCIES\nS15. We provide a broad, flexible, and balanced curriculum that addresses the learning needs of autistic pupils and their social and emotional well-being, communication needs, and life skills.\nS16. We always promote positive attitudes towards autism and have high expectations for all of our pupils and staff.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 11, "split_id": 35, "split_idx_start": 14837, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0c46d97c5222df324a47f2050af5d727657da3442b4c0ea7c863fbd673750ce1", "range": [451, 570]}, {"doc_id": "e413c3702e269bd4a88b572f77818e5d060629e7db21d8733e4779c874faf261", "range": [0, 112]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.00036177068250253797, -0.0975877195596695, -0.016833392903208733, 0.02484963834285736, 0.02617039531469345, 0.01166673842817545, 0.004560532979667187, -0.06090739369392395, -0.051765479147434235, -0.008530550636351109, 0.0005166451446712017, -0.07195126265287399, 0.006005517