e guidance provided within the AET Schools Standards Framework on how to effectively assess and document progress in meeting the established standards for supporting autistic pupils. It emphasizes the importance of collecting various forms of evidence and utilizing a RAG (red, amber, green) rating system to evaluate areas for improvement.For each standard, you should aim to collect: \u2022 Documentary evidence (e.g. records of training events, assess, plan, do, review documentation, accounts from pupils, pupil\u2019s outcomes, observation schedules, and policy documents). \u2022 Photographs, or video clips of relevant practice.\n1. Give each standard, and each example under that\nstandard, a RAG (red, amber, green) rating: Room for improvement: Work needs to be done to develop practice in this area. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 12, "split_id": 38, "split_idx_start": 16095, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0c85e259d87f3fc0f67d88044ae9a1a2f7c2c83167709b8bc7f39adcc7f4dc9d", "range": [673, 748]}, {"doc_id": "929d9fbfa37645b47841552322384a02c1234055fc217a030d9a20d7379856db", "range": [0, 170]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0002322056534467265, -0.07839755713939667, 0.00620848685503006, -0.010151251219213009, -0.010435734875500202, 0.006106494925916195, -0.003369496902450919, -0.022488003596663475, -0.07423549145460129, -0.009888955391943455, 0.03969254344701767, -0.06290512531995773, 0.02601974457502365, 0.005131978075951338, -0.009064354002475739, -0.04985180124640465, 0.03372281417250633, 0.00814090296626091, -0.050999514758586884, 0.019698912277817726, 0.01568441465497017, 0.008608048781752586, -0.016282901167869568, 0.020273026078939438, -0.016851695254445076, 0.009700879454612732, 0.00499394116923213, 0.0082998713478446, 0.00909