1885103527456522, 0.04739471152424812, -0.012093535624444485, 0.06326442211866379, 0.034374915063381195, -0.028997166082262993, -0.0011720327893272042, 0.016415240243077278, -0.029430009424686432, 0.018243979662656784, -0.0017283996567130089, 0.007115555927157402, -0.004103054758161306, 0.019061345607042313, 0.011098090559244156, -0.006239274982362986, 0.007824916392564774, 0.020645538344979286, -0.025586608797311783, -0.041951246559619904, 0.05306451395153999, 0.0023358638864010572, 0.023087037727236748, 0.04278227314352989, -0.01729433797299862, 0.035352762788534164, -0.02586529590189457, -0.01929805800318718, 0.015597186051309109, -0.05810914188623428, 0.015919482335448265, -0.06074284017086029, 0.08220362663269043, -0.006347000133246183, 0.01500829216092825, -0.01069769635796547, -0.03532588854432106, 0.04270734637975693, 0.002668143482878804, 0.05006077140569687, 0.01790875568985939, -0.02320779114961624, 0.00862910132855177, 0.008424289524555206, 0.02041272073984146, 0.041975315660238266, -0.019788173958659172, -0.002516405889764428, -0.028780510649085045, 0.004422392696142197, -0.041474297642707825, 0.0875011533498764, -0.016395779326558113, -0.011755065992474556, -0.024559147655963898, 0.02465282939374447, -0.044106073677539825, -0.04692155867815018, -0.028483649715781212, 0.030305273830890656, 1.858083027769414e-34, 0.0002102715225191787, -0.0003661981609184295, 0.02157144993543625, -0.05587268993258476, 0.01310731377452612, -0.018467186018824577, -0.06612032651901245, -0.005729984492063522, 0.016788847744464874, -0.047264620661735535, -0.020252855494618416], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "f5fc6f56c914c6272645c65d644a3ac434c212df41c9d3e852623cacafcb4d04", "content": "This chunk is part of Principle One: Understanding the strengths, interests, and needs of each autistic pupil within the AET Schools Standards Framework. It outlines Standard One, focusing on the commitment to gathering comprehensive knowledge about autism and utilizing various sources to understand individual autistic pupils, emphasizing the need for pupil-centered approaches and detailed assessments.Standard One: We are committed to developing knowledge about autism, and we gather information from a range of sources to fully understand the individual autistic pupil.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWe collate information through observations and/or discussions with the autistic pupil, their parents/carers, other professionals who work with them, and from previous reports and assessments.\nExamples of how we can do this:\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWe use pupil-centred approaches to gather information on the strengths, and differences of each individual pupil in the areas of social understanding and communication; flexibility, information processing, and understanding; and sensory processing and integration.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWe understand the importance of taking time to build rapport and spend time finding out about the pupils interests.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nA detailed assessment of need should ensure that the full range of an individual\u2019s needs is identified, not simply the primary need. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 14, "split_id": 42, "split_idx_start": 17290, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "6c68775151f90914113c146e87dbce6eb46fa45d78e390c49ed1819b3bd3e8e9", "range": [397, 567]}, {"doc_id": "61950a56f847ffa3680b7d6e1cea789bace060401fd169ab3aa223f6bf99cc36", "range": [0, 188]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.036413319408893585, -0.10428197681903839, -0.01609968952834606, 0.01311870664358139, -0.013573728501796722, 0.022557159885764122, -0.010356317274272442, -0.0603569597005844