5562706, -0.06107845902442932, 0.038230061531066895, -0.008734595961868763, 0.0372634157538414, 0.011675422079861164, -0.01772870309650898, 0.018679669126868248, 0.009526938199996948, 0.019378891214728355, 0.029471365734934807, -0.02030077390372753, -0.005152672063559294, -0.03253239393234253, 0.012690388597548008, -0.06844528019428253, 0.07721562683582306, -0.024188349023461342, -0.019709868356585503, -0.020194312557578087, 0.01400323212146759, -0.03344760090112686, -0.041301876306533813, -0.032553333789110184, 0.009102359414100647, 1.980280486900939e-34, 0.006771621759980917, -0.006157991476356983, 0.014068766497075558, -0.07017189264297485, 0.013662572018802166, -0.01686905138194561, -0.04349309206008911, 0.006473760586231947, 4.927356349071488e-05, -0.04796822369098663, -0.022911446169018745], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "61950a56f847ffa3680b7d6e1cea789bace060401fd169ab3aa223f6bf99cc36", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Understanding the Individual\" section within the AET Schools Standards Framework. It emphasizes the importance of conducting comprehensive assessments to identify the full range of needs for autistic pupils, aligning with statutory frameworks and standards for headteachers regarding expectations for special educational needs and disabilities (SEND).ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nA detailed assessment of need should ensure that the full range of an individual\u2019s needs is identified, not simply the primary need. The support provided to an individual should always be based on a full understanding of their particular strengths and needs and seek to address them all (SEND Code of Practice, 2014:96).\nHead Teachers Standards (2020), Standard 5i: Headteachers ensure the school holds ambitious expectations for all pupils with additional and special educational needs and disabilities.\nLinks to statutory frameworks\fSchools Standards Framework15 Understanding the Individual\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? We document evidence of working on this standard through case studies, one page profiles, and the goals we co-produce with parents/carers and pupils (where possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 14, "split_id": 43, "split_idx_start": 18231, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f5fc6f56c914c6272645c65d644a3ac434c212df41c9d3e852623cacafcb4d04", "range": [941, 1129]}, {"doc_id": "04ef1b3e47c878411f5ee24453b2d6df440e5b5b1ef1ead9277ea68f4d3fd70a", "range": [0, 238]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.027144940569996834, -0.11319329589605331, -0.014574809931218624, 0.005489856004714966, -0.010509601794183254, 0.037389036267995834, -0.0005211468669585884, -0.043382640928030014, -0.022713884711265564, 0.017950469627976418, 0.04649467021226883, -0.08876294642686844, 0.030656302347779274, -0.01027874369174242, 0.002019063103944063, -0.07508616894483566, 0.022032972425222397, 0.038634080439805984, -0.043050367385149, 0.022755969315767288, -0.009326000697910786, 0.01618635281920433, -0.015938784927129745, 0.011287537403404713, 0.002360810060054064, -0.028071846812963486, 0.022495785728096962, 0.013482754118740559, 0.03244137018918991, -0.010880493558943272, 0.03628142178058624, 0.02268965356051922, 0.0035796542651951313, -0.03340698406100273, 2.158192046408658e-06, 0.020356088876724243, 0.015936296433210373, -0.026551654562354088, -0.02128930762410164, 0.005504246801137924, -0.09991088509559631, 0.006980235688388348, 0.03909130021929741, 0.05706004053354263, 0.001888694823719561, 0.02095789834856987, 0.009607684798538685, 0.008955168537795544, 0.01653711125254631, -0.020105406641960144, -0.008067730814218521, 0.02362019009888172, 0.004358063917607069, -0.043