338057518, -0.024049656465649605, 0.021289173513650894, -0.06097017601132393, 0.05949162691831589, 0.006434408947825432, -0.028815746307373047, 0.02553185075521469, 0.010232003405690193, 0.0031915975268930197, -0.04870666563510895, -0.06900330632925034, 0.004374736919999123, 2.1531164977914612e-34, -0.006157028488814831, 0.01258905977010727, 0.02137596532702446, -0.09443160891532898, 0.015402881428599358, -0.00021030337666161358, -0.0652410164475441, 0.010398144833743572, -0.023974133655428886, -0.03403223678469658, -0.025822266936302185], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "b1d8529706cb8a845c2f570b86095261999eb2562bd8e61f64c5f820b7fe3dd1", "content": "This chunk is part of the AET Schools Standards Framework, specifically located under \"Understanding the Individual,\" within Principle Two, Standard Three. It outlines how schools should document evidence of their practices in using pupil-centered approaches to support autistic pupils in expressing their hopes and aspirations, highlighting methods for evaluation and the impact on various stakeholders.We document evidence of working on this standard through case studies, one page profiles, and the goals we co-produce with parents/carers and pupils (where possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\nEvidence to show how we meet this standard:\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn staff:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn autistic pupils:\fSchools Standards Framework18 Understanding the Individual\nPrinciple Two: Enabling the autistic pupil to contribute to and influence decisions.\nStandard Three: We use pupil-centred approaches to support pupils to communicate their hopes, dreams, and aspirations.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we can do this:\nWe enable autistic pupils to identify and celebrate their strengths, hopes, dreams, and aspirations. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-fra