7, 0.059556737542152405, -0.02606017328798771, -0.029757684096693993, 0.004094198811799288, 0.00951682310551405, -0.01722262054681778, -0.05170297250151634, -0.05586374178528786, 0.018805356696248055, 1.651746920207269e-34, 0.007538053207099438, 0.03169994428753853, 0.008488337509334087, -0.0783262774348259, 0.015720747411251068, -0.0069020283408463, -0.005683782044798136, -0.0013952796580269933, 0.008479788899421692, -0.04752024635672569, -0.024287493899464607], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "1c5f53958f0ed0dbf31b0b64013c8e42ffab8c30573ca726c115cc06a452d7aa", "content": "This chunk is part of the AET Schools Standards Framework, specifically under Principle Two: Enabling the autistic pupil to contribute to and influence decisions. It outlines the standards related to actively involving autistic pupils in decision-making processes and ensuring their preferences are considered in educational planning and activities, emphasizing the importance of their perspectives and choices.ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we can do this:\nWe take on board the perspective of the autistic pupil across the range of activities in which they engage and we consider the preferences of pupils on how they can best be supported in their day-to-day activities and tasks, as well as their social preferences.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nPupils have regular opportunities to give feedback and participate in decision-making and we note the pupil\u2019s perspective in review meetings and transition planning.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWe engage pupils in making choices about curricular and extra-curricular activities. ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nGuidance\nSEN should arise from a four-part cycle, known as the graduated approach, through which earlier decisions are revisited, refined and revised, leading to a growing understanding of the pupil\u2019s needs and of what supports the pupil in making good progress and securing good outcomes\u2019. (NASEN: \u2018SEN support and the graduated approach\u2019, 2014:2).\nThe United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child established the right of all children to express their views and to have these views listened to and taken seriously when decisions are being made that affect them.\f", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 20, "split_id": 51, "split_idx_start": 23782, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "75a1cc2b1a1aeb198e01c7439ae961d9ceb37bdf8576a8563faab50828d6ffe8", "range": [692, 1041]}, {"doc_id": "6750d4f22b2fccdaa4efec6b6608f62d59bce9f57cb69c417f75db65813c617f", "range": [0, 222]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03144713491201401, -0.10053620487451553, -0.016918901354074478, 0.0008748520049266517, 0.00617367634549737, 0.037238482385873795, 0.04610821604728699, -0.05660811439156532, -0.024576546624302864, 0.005788098089396954, 0.02548304758965969, -0.06825646758079529, 0.010930603370070457, -0.011316136457026005, -0.008765759877860546, -0.04103497415781021, 0.028661610558629036, 0.012650697492063046, -0.0034070571418851614, 0.013328623957931995, -0.017119256779551506, -0.001132396748289466, -0.020541556179523468, 0.04935433715581894, 0.061404626816511154, -0.04099084436893463, 0.030391566455364227, 0.012091957964003086, 0.0338013656437397, -0.031146572902798653, 0.04161050170660019, 0.001976673025637865, -0.0016296700341627002, -0.009152517654001713, 2.1407033727882663e-06, 0.009519390761852264, 0.03149234876036644, -0.018896637484431267, 0.005631744395941496, -0.006300952285528183, -0.08844951540231705, 0.045204047113657, 0.02253001742064953, 0.05823179706931114, -0.02360699698328972, 0.02316937781870365, 0.0032980714458972216, -0.00813382025808096, 0.001