17f75db65813c617f", "content": "This chunk emphasizes the importance of children's rights as outlined by the United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child, particularly in relation to involving autistic pupils in decision-making processes. It appears in the context of documenting evidence and assessing the impact of practices that support the active participation of autistic pupils, under the principle of collaboration with parents/carers and professionals to enhance education.The United Nations Convention on the Rights of the Child established the right of all children to express their views and to have these views listened to and taken seriously when decisions are being made that affect them.\fSchools Standards Framework\n21 Understanding the Individual\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? We document evidence of working on this standard through case studies, one page profiles, and the goals we co-produce with parents/carers and children (where possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\nEvidence to show how we meet this standard:\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn staff:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn autistic pupils:\fSchools Standards Framework22 Theme two: Positive Relationships\f23 Schools Standards Framework\nPositive Relationships\nPrinciple Three: Collaboration with parents/carers and other professionals and services.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 20, "split_id": 52, "split_idx_start": 24897, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "1c5f53958f0ed0dbf31b0b64013c8e42ffab8c30573ca726c115cc06a452d7aa", "range": [1115, 1337]}, {"doc_id": "8d0b1ba05627dd11ead9273d87e63f935c006df6b3b6aa59dab5ca1c12dbb0b0", "range": [0, 256]}]}, "score": null, "embedding