32dd", "content": "This chunk is situated within the \"Positive Relationships\" section of the AET Schools Standards Framework, specifically under Principle Three, which emphasizes collaboration with parents and carers. It addresses the importance of engaging parents in their child's education and the recognition of their diverse backgrounds and needs, as well as statutory links to best practices in communication and involvement.ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWe proactively engage with parents and carers to establish and develop ways to communicate and share information, ideas, and progress.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWe understand the needs of parents who themselves may have diagnosed or undiagnosed autism as well as families from diverse cultural and religious backgrounds.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nLinks to statutory frameworks\nLocal authorities, Early Years providers and schools should enable parents to share their knowledge about the child and give them confidence that their views and contributions are valued and will be acted upon. At times, parents, teachers and others may have differing expectations of how a child\u2019s needs are best met. Sometimes these discussions can be challenging but it is in the child\u2019s best interests for a positive dialogue between parents, teachers and others to be maintained, to work through points of difference and establish what action is to be taken (SEND Code of Practice, 2014:21).\f", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 23, "split_id": 54, "split_idx_start": 26208, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "8d0b1ba05627dd11ead9273d87e63f935c006df6b3b6aa59dab5ca1c12dbb0b0", "range": [632, 822]}, {"doc_id": "788afadccbf61