ce of working on this standard through case studies, one page profiles, and the goals we co-produce with parents/carers and children (where possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\nEvidence to show how we meet this standard:\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn staff:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn autistic pupils:\fSchools Standards Framework25 Positive Relationships\nPrinciple Three: Collaboration with parents/carers and other professionals and services.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 23, "split_id": 55, "split_idx_start": 27017, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "6b1d58af0866b63ebe8cf3397c8a0da42ffb512ebebeb56675eef93f47da32dd", "range": [809, 1087]}, {"doc_id": "1109e279a565019618fdc0ceaee9a24400d776db9730b2f237d6821445e9cad8", "range": [0, 191]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04678301140666008, -0.07958122342824936, -0.005077604204416275, 0.015454227104783058, -0.02259082719683647, 0.03894538804888725, 0.022842468693852425, -0.03568117320537567, -0.08344726264476776, -0.00512005016207695, 0.052041515707969666, -0.08599472790956497, 0.0479087270796299, 0.015446236357092857, -0.0064242188818752766, -0.04402310773730278, 0.012798335403203964, 0.03687720373272896, -0.038997698575258255, 0.028298379853367805, 0.0008929065661504865, 0.016094958409667015, -0.015527527779340744, 0.02141382545232773, -0.01274111308157444, -0.015265416353940964, 0.006090444512665272, 0.03376834839582443, 0.009513705968856812, -0.03074454516172409, 0.029218418523669243, 0.0005281310877762735, -0.008917284198105335, -0.0235313568264246, 2.2117576463642763e-06, 0.029507357627153397, 0.014922335743904114, -0.014139441773295403, 0.005459118168801069, -0.006223994307219982, -0.06839831918478012, 0.0018