41, 0.013937139883637428, 0.007684893440455198, -0.021644968539476395, -0.02181931585073471, -0.009329833090305328], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "1109e279a565019618fdc0ceaee9a24400d776db9730b2f237d6821445e9cad8", "content": "This chunk is part of Principle Three of the AET Schools Standards Framework, which focuses on the importance of collaboration with parents, carers, and professionals in supporting autistic pupils. It outlines Standard Six, emphasizing the need for effective communication and partnership with various services to enhance educational outcomes for autistic learners.On staff:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn autistic pupils:\fSchools Standards Framework25 Positive Relationships\nPrinciple Three: Collaboration with parents/carers and other professionals and services.\nStandard Six: We work collaboratively with health, social care, and other professionals to improve educational experiences and outcomes for autistic pupils.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we can do this:\nWe develop links with professionals across services and contexts according to the needs of pupils. For example, this can include Educational Psychology, CAMHS, specialist autism teams, and the transition support service.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWe follow the graduated approach in the SEND Code of Practice and are confident in collecting assess, plan, do, review evidence for submitting to external professionals.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 24, "split_id": 56, "split_idx_start": 27746, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "788afadccbf61926d5c80e188fa6ca5a84f51dbfd7580cadb0fddf8c07a0016e", "range": [729, 920]}, {"doc_id": "f0143183a66d0bc9cfc42be19b26def3150fbb8b7a501edc5c95a69d97880b9