content": "This chunk is from the \"Positive Relationships\" theme of the AET Schools Standards Framework, specifically detailing how schools can document evidence of effective collaboration with parents and staff in supporting autistic pupils. It emphasizes the importance of co-producing goals and reasonable adjustments to track the impact of these practices on various stakeholders including staff, parents/carers, and autistic pupils, while transitioning into the \"Enabling Environments\" theme that follows.Schools Standards Framework30 Positive Relationships\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? We document evidence of working on this standard through case studies, one page profiles, and the goals we co-produce with parents/carers and children (where possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\nEvidence to show how we meet this standard:\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn staff:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn autistic pupils:\fSchools Standards Framework31 Theme three: Enabling Environments\fSchools Standards Framework32 Enabling Environments\nPrinciple Five: Leadership and management that promotes and embeds good autism practice.\nStandard Nine: We promote a supportive environment where leaders and managers are knowledgeable about autism and cascade information to their staff. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 30, "split_id": 64, "split_idx_start": 33484, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "397b1d14bfa13683a9f5c1f41bc1186dfc5c19084204836bc2753fd4e5ae469e", "range": [817, 927]}, {"doc_id": "feef289a08a45b945fdd8b994953029af7ef1c5bb9f1a4bcb4aa13683cb567b5", "range": [0, 149]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04279864951968193, -0.10903662443161011, -0.01089727133