cac", "content": "This chunk is situated within the \"Positive Relationships\" section, specifically under Principle Four: Workforce development related to good autism practice. It discusses the importance of accountability related to the exclusion of autistic pupils and links to statutory frameworks that emphasize the need for teachers to adapt their teaching to meet diverse needs, thus addressing the overall goal of enhancing inclusive practices in educational settings.ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nLinks to statutory frameworks\nThe All-Party Parliamentary Group on Autism (APPGA, 2017) report highlights that a lack of accountability is an important factor in the rise of school exclusions for autistic pupils.\nThe evidence suggests that children on the autism spectrum are regularly unlawfully excluded, with consequences for their academic progress, self-esteem and mental health. (APPGA: \u2018Autism and Education in England\u2019, 2017:13).\nTeacher Standards (2011), Standard 5: Teachers adapt teaching to respond to the strengths and needs of all pupils and have a secure understanding of how a range of factors can inhibit pupils\u2019 ability to learn, and how best to overcome these.\f35 Schools Standards Framework\nEnabling Environments\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? We document evidence of working on this standard through case studies, one page profiles, and the goals we co-produce with parents/carers and children (where possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 34, "split_id": 70, "split_idx_start": 37674, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "2ee6eabb25980a1ee42f56d9b0c51897cdf93f2b7306ff2057985d0351f55216", "range": [591, 859]}, {"doc_id": "50fd669d2669dc7776001d9078376019e5f93753d1e6ec55284961e46ced48ae", "range": [0, 240]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.041608817875385284, -0.08494006097316742, -0.013197295367717743, 0.006370363291352987, 0.008308365941047668, 0.03581133112311363, 0.014277406968176365, -0.06445030868053436, -0.04247204586863518, -0.010628840886056423, 0.040157005190849304, -0.048490505665540695, 0.03197626769542694, -0.018666453659534454, 0.03057621605694294, -0.06171270087361336, 0.014197232201695442, 0.05119462311267853, -0.059851422905921936, 0.018262848258018494, -0.009399179369211197, 0.02186146192252636, 0.00595677737146616, 0.0383613221347332, -0.011128634214401245, -0.0013129690196365118, 0.012206603772938251, 0.016039738431572914, 0.015599021688103676, -0.030645523220300674, 0.0363023616373539, -0.00878822710365057, -0.014076244086027145, -0.03800399601459503, 2.3432996840710985e-06, 0.012194608338177204, 0.013391323387622833, -0.010906162671744823, 0.019339581951498985, 0.013596342876553535, -0.10862626135349274, 0.0035203725565224886, -0.0006626491085626185, 0.06598532199859619, -0.0016687059542164207, -0.013844404369592667, 0.013287559151649475, -0.00818374752998352, 0.012314588762819767, -0.006881933659315109, -0.013522344641387463, 0.012638598680496216, 0.019740283489227295, -0.03500468656420708, 0.01994049735367298, -0.02434002235531807, 0.01367879007011652, -0.08625121414661407, 0.008030899800360203, 0.025137485936284065, -0.034299880266189575, 0.01518245693296194, 0.0160913597792387, -0.07087821513414383, 0.010225864127278328, -0.03328625485301018, 0.006417794153094292, -0.05854208022356033, 0.05321748927235603, -0.01105035375803709, 0.17967122793197632, 0.03231946378946304, 0.05054211989045143, 0.033559877425432205, 0.006059873849153519, 0.05176528915762901, -0.015685345977544785, 0.0060557774268090725, -0.06283129751682281, 0.030404092743992805, 0.011723947711288929, 0.009009254164993763, -0.03612854704260826, -0.00396832916885614