 in education, 2020:5).\f37 Schools Standards Framework\nEnabling Environments\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? We document evidence of working on this standard through case studies, one page profiles, and the goals we co-produce with parents/carers and children (where possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\nEvidence to show how we meet this standard:\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn staff:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn autistic pupils:\fSchools Standards Framework38 Enabling Environments\nPrinciple Six: An ethos and environment that fosters social inclusion for autistic pupils.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 36, "split_id": 73, "split_idx_start": 40026, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "195e92acd55df8fd75763eb75d27ce4305f96eeaefb1fa411796b6096ffa9aac", "range": [806, 1057]}, {"doc_id": "f4cad18a179e27b72f1db967aae537dd40c52ed32148b32730bcf8c7457829f4", "range": [0, 192]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03504396975040436, -0.1257355660200119, -0.006654772441834211, 0.0033455307129770517, -0.007403431925922632, 0.03265739977359772, 0.026082752272486687, -0.028651325032114983, -0.05264304578304291, -0.010804161429405212, 0.057976383715867996, -0.034607380628585815, 0.03541538491845131, 0.014817741699516773, 0.02616007626056671, -0.046174246817827225, 0.033106885850429535, 0.04670736938714981, -0.045774832367897034, 0.030176546424627304, -0.004299144260585308, 0.018202822655439377, -0.01812528632581234, 0.029600558802485466, 0.00816355086863041, -0.00743444636464119, 0.024941498413681984, 0.017740894109010696, -0.004721176810562611, -0.04147844761610031, 0.026955965906381607, -0.00672023044899106, -0.006361505016684532, -0.0581170916557312, 2.3292