1401064e-34, -0.0032330178655683994, -0.015423491597175598, 0.007942477241158485, -0.060801904648542404, 0.015583713538944721, -0.004483800381422043, -0.022330699488520622, 0.00253017689101398, -0.012541583739221096, -0.03954240679740906, -0.0055465237237513065], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "f4cad18a179e27b72f1db967aae537dd40c52ed32148b32730bcf8c7457829f4", "content": "This chunk is from the section discussing the sixth principle of the AET Schools Standards Framework, which emphasizes creating inclusive and supportive learning environments for autistic pupils. It outlines the importance of structured, understandable, and predictable settings that accommodate individual sensory and communication needs to enhance participation in learning.On staff:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn autistic pupils:\fSchools Standards Framework38 Enabling Environments\nPrinciple Six: An ethos and environment that fosters social inclusion for autistic pupils.\nStandard Twelve: Our learning environments are structured, understandable, and predictable. We adapt learning environments to enable pupils to participate fully in learning.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we can do this:\nStaff consider the accessibility of the learning environment for autistic pupils by taking account of potential physical barriers and processing difficulties, sensory needs, and social demands of working with or being with their peers.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWe support verbal and non-verbal communication through a range of approaches, including the organisation of the setting, visual aids, reducing and simplifying language, and providing sufficient time for processing and understanding of instruction.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 37, "split_id": 74, "split_idx_start": 40727, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "563cba68affad70d0f21cd3219fc4711e4c549e81ca8e787065d17f45f827d24", "range": [701, 893]}, {"doc_id": "f340f38209f5335097c9adbca62b23ce20f40eb132c0141cb2e1e7e6087ff9a4", "range": [0, 303]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03623278811573982, -0.12347497791051865, -0.031198089942336082, 0.024719035252928734, -0.007997230626642704, 0.032491233199834824, 0.048440102487802505, -0.022187255322933197, -0.04980550333857536, 0.004552850034087896, 0.01794135756790638, -0.04526754468679428, 0.05149523541331291, -0.021229488775134087, 0.014281404204666615, -0.059580642729997635, 0.03289758786559105, 0.04047411307692528, -0.0634969174861908, 0.019202785566449165, -0.03338070586323738, -0.005312409717589617, -0.03327469527721405, 0.00665437662974, 0.024969348683953285, -0.01351169217377901, 0.0059513188898563385, 0.0020105468574911356, -0.014378681778907776, -0.01519734039902687, 0.028309393674135208, 0.003366978606209159, 0.0008712952840141952, -0.05198897421360016, 2.0679067347373348e-06, 0.02053426019847393, 0.005269389133900404, -0.03043614886701107, 0.01610737293958664, 0.01928035356104374, -0.03228599950671196, 0.016896788030862808, 0.013880929909646511, 0.07562988996505737, -0.018760060891509056, -0.02364465408027172, 0.015792397782206535, 0.022258570417761803, 0.008897693827748299, -0.008592143654823303, -0.01401306502521038, 0.013343701139092445, -0.045348118990659714, -0.023990681394934654, -0.01606142148375511, -0.01429510023444891, 0.00990457646548748, -0.09062297642230988, 0.05576047673821449, 0.04438422992825508, -0.03539440780878067, 0.01829903945326805, 0.010384430177509785, -0.03959905356168747, 0.006047837436199188, -0.021005921065807343, -0.02186371572315693, -0.08668746054172516, 0.027950407937169075, 0.007061556447297335, 0.149037167429924, 0.034440379589796066, 0.004685200285166502, 0.040348686277866364, -0.01248925644904375, 0.036130134016275406, -0.03567