izes the importance of involving parents, pupils, and professionals in the assessment process, adapting assessment approaches for individual needs, and ensuring a comprehensive understanding of each pupil's strengths and challenges as outlined in the AET Schools Standards Framework.ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we can do this:\nParents, pupils, and external professionals (as appropriate), are actively involved in the identification of strengths and needs, in setting shared learning objectives, and in reviewing and assessing progress.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nThe assessment approaches we use are adapted in line with the needs of the pupil and include tools developed specifically for autistic pupils.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWe use a variety of assessment approaches to build a comprehensive profile of the pupil\u2019s performance of key skills across a range of environments.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nLinks to statutory frameworks\nA detailed assessment of need should ensure that the full range of an individual\u2019s needs is identified, not simply the primary need. The support provided to an individual should always be based on a full understanding of their particular strengths and needs and seek to address them all (SEND Code of Practice, 2014:96).\f", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 41, "split_id": 77, "split_idx_start": 43132, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b16c29939a2215dbd9b6044e3d26d9ec2cfacc19d0972c1caffb35bc71453e3f", "range": [775, 1072]}, {"doc_id": "b4f6a951e4c6a50a92d765710fa3969f33f6b4455f8ad82c94e57b7b33720ce9", "range": [0, 188]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.016054917126893997, -