898745741970ddc9e76b1", "content": "This chunk is part of the AET Schools Standards Framework, specifically under Principle Seven, which focuses on targeted support and measuring the progress of autistic pupils. It outlines Standard Fourteen related to developing and implementing personalized education plans in collaboration with pupils and parents, emphasizing the importance of regular reviews to ensure progress.On staff:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn autistic pupils:\fSchools Standards Framework43 Learning and Development\nPrinciple Seven: Targeted support and measuring the progress of autistic pupils.\nStandard Fourteen: We develop and implement targeted pupil-centred education plans in partnership with pupils and parents. These are regularly reviewed to monitor progress.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we can do this:\nAll autistic pupils have a pupil-centred education plan that is tailored to their strengths and needs, has clear learning targets and strategies, and monitors progress. The education support plan aims to improve the pupil\u2019s quality of life by reflecting their strengths, needs, skills, and experience. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 42, "split_id": 79, "split_idx_start": 44688, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b4f6a951e4c6a50a92d765710fa3969f33f6b4455f8ad82c94e57b7b33720ce9", "range": [640, 825]}, {"doc_id": "b6dc59f1650f9043dc7ff24ae3b9858c113c000f0e129e4182062e56dddaeeae", "range": [0, 133]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.037049803882837296, -0.1012115627527237, -0.01796208880841732, 0.0026184413582086563, 0.00023184010933618993, 0.01396156009286642, 0.016523096710443497, -0.046931192278862, -0.06747512519359589, 0.005636787042021751, 0.04332756623625755, -0.07462385296821