ers:\nOn autistic pupils:\fSchools Standards Framework45 Learning and Development\nPrinciple Eight: Adapting the curriculum, teaching, and learning to promote wellbeing and success for autistic pupils.\nStandard Fifteen: We provide a broad, flexible, and balanced curriculum that addresses the learning needs of autistic pupils and their social and emotional well-being, communication needs, and life skills.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we can do this:\nImproving social communication skills is often a priority for families. It is also the foundation for learning and a key predictor of positive long-term outcomes. It is a central element of our curriculum. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 44, "split_id": 82, "split_idx_start": 47208, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "2640865e59cb75420d24c238b03c6eb1f7e452e882972dd297d2a16d325799b3", "range": [988, 1211]}, {"doc_id": "19cf7f20e8ed3d2e80de8c063a5b61d4c8b03981e07e00b717502c63b8d2ec2f", "range": [0, 43]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.039713528007268906, -0.11687379330396652, -0.014644271694123745, 0.01898171380162239, 0.0265737846493721, 0.044361662119627, 0.045317962765693665, -0.0571853443980217, -0.04851679131388664, -0.014352011494338512, 0.014629003591835499, -0.07454685121774673, 0.021643389016389847, -0.01721116155385971, 0.008965736255049706, -0.062310293316841125, 0.04248102381825447, 0.046129655092954636, -0.01594279147684574, 0.011464187875390053, -0.013279937207698822, 0.02491196244955063, -0.03994952142238617, 0.024741876870393753, 0.042845480144023895, -0.01957463100552559, 0.03623366728425026, 0.013952991925179958, 0.014601456932723522, -0.024204833433032036, 0.04630320519208908, 0.004212309140712023, 0.009240579791367054, -0.028303