s and those of children and young people themselves; have high ambitions and set stretching targets for them; track their progress towards these goals; keep under review the additional or different provision that is made for them; promote positive outcomes in the wider areas of personal and social development, and ensure that the approaches used are based on the best possible evidence and are having the required impact on progress (SEND Code of Practice, 2014:25).\fSchools Standards Framework46 Learning and Development\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? We document evidence of working on this standard through case studies, one page profiles, and the goals we co-produce with parents/carers and children (where possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\nEvidence to show how we meet this standard:\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 45, "split_id": 84, "split_idx_start": 48438, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "19cf7f20e8ed3d2e80de8c063a5b61d4c8b03981e07e00b717502c63b8d2ec2f", "range": [551, 782]}, {"doc_id": "b145d1f080005ff81c6621bacd5dee759e82ecd81c7f1b6e740230710a4f5ad7", "range": [0, 100]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0019529747078195214, -0.10319456458091736, -0.011448943056166172, 0.004161942284554243, -0.006854682229459286, 0.030595306307077408, 0.027905264869332314, -0.04627992957830429, -0.03908286616206169, 0.006773020140826702, 0.05402980372309685, -0.05052390322089195, 0.042428307235240936, 0.004608219023793936, 0.0072618830017745495, -0.04171028733253479, 0.03503985330462456, 0.037693873047828674, -0.042196642607450485, 0.037379615008831024, -0.022557804360985756, 0.007943626493215561, -0.01661037653684616,