8184065669775009, -0.004693253431469202, -0.018289530649781227, 0.001943637733347714, 0.004010963253676891, -0.007764053996652365, -0.022506410256028175, -0.05529399588704109, 0.01790134236216545, 1.9339593514050694e-34, -0.002471288200467825, -0.013960467651486397, 0.022237418219447136, -0.08502133190631866, 0.005319065880030394, 0.0011178329586982727, -0.004388685803860426, -0.005463270004838705, -0.011212374083697796, -0.0389338955283165, -0.021793173626065254], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "b145d1f080005ff81c6621bacd5dee759e82ecd81c7f1b6e740230710a4f5ad7", "content": "This chunk pertains to the section on \"Principle Eight: Adapting the curriculum, teaching, and learning to promote wellbeing and success for autistic pupils,\" specifically focusing on Standard Sixteen. It emphasizes the importance of promoting positive attitudes toward autism among staff and students, and outlines methods to document the impact of implementing this standard on staff, parents/carers, and autistic pupils.Evidence to show how we meet this standard:\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn staff:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn autistic pupils:\fSchools Standards Framework47 Learning and Development\nPrinciple Eight: Adapting the curriculum, teaching, and learning to promote wellbeing and success for autistic pupils.\nStandard Sixteen: We always promote positive attitudes towards autism and have high expectations for all of our pupils and staff.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we can do this:\nNeurodiversity is embraced and viewed as a strength in our setting and we promote awareness and acceptance of autism. ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWe have a vision of including all pupils, and our positive approach to diversity and inclusion is proactively shared in our communications both internally and externally. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 46, "split_id": 85, "split_idx_start": 49557, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0f88e84295c2f351fcfc32b0b715b632f49469602cab2652d4a48dbf6c6892a7", "range": [1119, 1219]}, {"doc_id": "2098591c1cc65b7457134195f35d8b589036182898f1a125e5470bdf8ac7a216", "range": [0, 226]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.041150499135255814, -0.07521519064903259, -0.00893628504127264, 0.024207763373851776, 0.019120879471302032, 0.03808935731649399, 0.033526208251714706, -0.04530668631196022, -0.05816471949219704, -0.015826890245079994, 0.03709975257515907, -0.05718814209103584, 0.03117292746901512, -0.045818835496902466, 0.014500845223665237, -0.041392818093299866, 0.041879601776599884, 0.058758579194545746, -0.03292400762438774, 0.002283096546307206, 0.003879971569404006, 0.006940352730453014, -0.011285376735031605, 0.0059114606119692326, 0.009837079793214798, 0.001574042602442205, 0.028404779732227325, 0.017214661464095116, 0.019756944850087166, -0.03891914710402489, 0.030115267261862755, -0.012761673890054226, 0.023787355050444603, -0.02950448729097843, 2.138347099389648e-06, 0.0004315048281569034, -0.003282835241407156, -0.0023290691897273064, 0.02328070066869259, 0.016589652746915817, -0.06045542657375336, -0.014278086833655834, 0.005399294197559357, 0.07489407062530518, 0.006897559855133295, -0.013573488220572472, 0.01151430606842041, 0.04896675795316696, 0.014855852350592613, 0.024987202137708664, -0.019778825342655182, 0.007153577636927366, 0.009349256753921509, -0.025372689589858055, -0.0028640818782150745, -0.00807391107082367, 0.018366165459156036, -0.07775798439979553, -0.006037471815943718, 0.05764524266123772, -0.01392198447138071, 0.010101992636919022, -0.016008950769901276, -0.03865886852145195, -0.008338749408721924, -0.03888845071196556, -0.006087305955588818, -0.06094544380903244, 0.0545149706304073