622667611, 0.01595192588865757, -0.024052418768405914, 0.021467095240950584, -0.04833025485277176, -0.02349352464079857, 0.04298742488026619, -0.026833632960915565, 0.015730522572994232, -0.027378195896744728, 0.11817890405654907, 0.0022112238220870495, -0.006104941479861736, 0.01775127276778221, -0.051544249057769775, 0.04193396493792534, 0.012024076655507088, 0.057193126529455185, 0.004461335018277168, -0.05934865027666092, -0.003176653990522027, 0.013849986717104912, 0.03412090614438057, 0.030281636863946915, -0.023352282121777534, 0.005539223086088896, -0.0492967814207077, 0.03861917555332184, -0.05456265062093735, 0.07074610143899918, -0.019839180633425713, -0.02565774880349636, -0.004048438277095556, 0.000838342122733593, 0.003981592133641243, -0.018769284710288048, -0.0712236613035202, 0.005133528728038073, 2.257874625791324e-34, 0.0018774165073409677, -0.03168318048119545, 0.010672521777451038, -0.05080119147896767, 0.018994726240634918, -0.013790111057460308, -0.023969676345586777, -0.0007141006062738597, -0.004107743501663208, -0.032571300864219666, -0.014216632582247257], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "279f1b702e8b9d34b7bdb85bde112cdfb43ba4c8cf2eaf1e7cbf5f47c3f5c288", "content": "This chunk appears in the \"Author and Acknowledgements\" section of the AET Schools Standards Framework. It recognizes the contributions of key individuals, such as Natalie Reaney, Dr. Jamie Galpin, Alice Gair, and Pam Simpson, who played significant roles in developing training materials and strategies to support autistic pupils and promote inclusive education practices.Natalie Reaney, Specialist Advisory Teacher with the Special Educational Needs Inclusion Support Service (SENISS), Liverpool: providing advice and support for children with special educational needs, in order to promote their inclusion within mainstream and nursery settings, enabling them to achieve their full potential.\nFor the school-based materials, the training partner co-author was Dr Jamie Galpin, Developmental Psychologist, Lead AET Trainer and Researcher at The Bridge London Teaching School. A member of The Bridge London Trust, a unique Multi Academy Trust consisting of three special schools, one mainstream primary school, a teaching school and outreach service.\nWith thanks to:\nAlice Gair, Specialist Paediatric Occupational Therapist in The Sensational Thinking Project with Newcastle upon Tyne Hospitals NHS Foundation Trust: advocating for the needs of children and their families affected by sensory processing differences including raising awareness and education of the impact of sensory processing and integration on daily living in an effort to contribute to better wellbeing, health and education outcomes for children.\nPam Simpson, Autism advisor and previous AET hub lead for Birmingham Communication and Autism Team: providing a local authority approach to raising the capacity of schools to meet the needs of autistic pupils through the implementation of the AET standards and competency frameworks and the delivery of training. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "aet-schools-standards-framework.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/166LzAs4UUYY2nmfvEFE7NUcJyEIfBoc3", "source_id": "fd3b04f3804d8efbea64fc291fd78f2aefe37cddffb9972efcc9615a49cfdf8c", "page_number": 49, "split_id": 89, "split_idx_start": 52904, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b9e95c0ef06b3770f89d4ed473af5c28fd5f5a18eddb8cc01ecc0feb6d58fc9a", "range": [917, 1240]}, {"doc_id": "7b4ae892452d5c3d93512a5f5338e8336d23ba33fc1e53b810dc8a09c9965cd7", "range": [0, 313]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.019694004207849503, -0.09599751234054565, -0.032094020396471024, 0.012234626337885857, 0.022272678092122078, 0.024317780509591103, 0.04256972670555115, -0.04071669280529022, -0.024158913642168045, 0.007883666083216667, 0.03277403488755226, -0.03010202944278717, 0.012985248118638992, 0.014999769628047943, 0.0011720937909558415, -0.060059428215026855, 0.019451776519417763, 0.0457