980601311, -0.008061429485678673, 0.052575550973415375, 0.04087411239743233, -0.01177139300853014, -0.002615222241729498, -0.0710427314043045, -0.0010529141873121262, 0.02019505575299263, 0.004279039800167084, 0.025385381653904915, 0.04772781953215599, 0.009397942572832108, 0.004176405258476734, 0.06320560723543167, -0.06445024907588959, 0.024845385923981667, -0.008440779522061348, 0.005770934745669365, 0.032679200172424316, -0.01018914021551609, -0.02705521322786808, -0.030484754592180252, 0.02856379933655262, -0.021142004057765007, -0.06845971196889877, -0.034881591796875, 0.030409028753638268, 0.05228687450289726, -0.0062631526961922646, -0.02094339020550251, 0.015674754977226257, -0.013929026201367378, 0.02409719116985798, 0.05234815552830696, 0.04318145290017128, 0.07748834043741226, -0.016264788806438446, -0.024510983377695084, 0.02401999942958355, 0.022583091631531715, 2.4678143745404668e-05, -0.02958461456000805, 0.017916467040777206, -0.03562483191490173, 0.008149216882884502, 0.033833686262369156, 0.047618456184864044, -0.04541696980595589, -0.016321195289492607, 0.0007500019273720682, 0.03587237372994423, 0.007419180124998093, -0.07176391780376434, -0.01725771091878414, -0.007330330088734627, 1.6736574920581234e-34, 0.004741257056593895, -0.036283403635025024, 0.021520940586924553, -0.049076151102781296, -0.017058152705430984, 0.018028518185019493, 0.01953176036477089, 0.01061592809855938, 0.013857538811862469, 0.03937136009335518, -0.014532553032040596], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "ea72fea8d428ac1ad76298fec7da78c9ecce58ad1f9016690ec95186b956dbe0", "content": "This chunk is from the introduction of the EEF guidance report on improving behaviour in schools. It emphasizes the necessity for consistent behaviour policies and outlines the report's aim to assist school leaders in enhancing behaviour strategies, detailing proactive approaches and the significance of understanding individual pupil influences on behaviour.There\u2019s a clear need for school to have consistent and clear behaviour policies that promote positive behaviour in lessons. This EEF guidance report is designed to support senior leaders in primary and secondary schools to make better-informed decisions about their behaviour strategies. It includes a number of practical examples of programmes and approaches that should be helpful in schools and classrooms where behaviour is generally good as well as where there are problems. The recommendations in this report focus on three areas: The first details strategies to prevent misbehaviour happening. A key theme from these recommendations is the importance of knowing individual pupils well, so that schools and teachers know which factors might affect pupil behaviour and what the school can do to address these. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 4, "split_id": 1, "split_idx_start": 1742, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "3f571e831319d1c0a88046e824013dbe37b7fa715f78de89ec78f65649f53597", "range": [1742, 1866]}, {"doc_id": "0f8ef712f2f215f293cb576345ef7b3896a84319560f80eaaf27999acc20368f", "range": [0, 214]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.08484961092472076, -0.08388418704271317, 0.01144221518188715, -0.009234116412699223, -0.028772462159395218, 0.03730982542037964, 0.005816404242068529, 0.02683943510055542, -0.0010589741868898273, 0.020207397639751434, 0.048493947833776474, -0.005027992185205221, 0.010837001726031303, 0.003332095220685005, 0.03886750340461731, -0.07625561207532883, 0.03855536878108978, 0.00998778361827135, -0.04817193001508713, 0.011363225057721138, -0.008039250038564205, -0.01051991619169712, 0.0038252966478466988, -0.0035940816160291433, -0.021562695503234863, -0.024741176515817642, -0.014853539876639843, 0.008480936288833618, 0.010065835900604725