4044647, 0.0704842358827591, 0.017160577699542046, 0.002770571503788233, 0.04720147326588631, -0.06899736821651459, 0.005423557944595814, -0.01841030828654766, 0.02450002357363701, 0.03953016549348831, 0.004384960979223251, -0.014175722375512123, -0.020931968465447426, 0.014863971620798111, -0.016578439623117447, -0.058527760207653046, 0.007644451688975096, 0.018712949007749557, 0.07355555146932602, -0.005202432628720999, -0.008095607161521912, 0.010280760936439037, -0.02314617857336998, 0.034344855695962906, 0.0018641670467332006, 0.03969215601682663, 0.08456598222255707, 0.029916340485215187, 0.011995031498372555, 0.006350087001919746, 0.028238076716661453, -0.0035906333941966295, 0.0027887728065252304, 0.023332690820097923, -0.03565314784646034, 0.020824121311306953, -0.0048212348483502865, 0.04848936200141907, -0.04666665941476822, -0.01252266950905323, -0.024224987253546715, 0.021717814728617668, 0.03133092075586319, -0.03609836474061012, -0.020676741376519203, -0.02362234890460968, 1.6331790456221954e-34, -0.011964156292378902, -0.018763145431876183, -0.011653291992843151, -0.05610038712620735, 0.02078852616250515, 0.0010083692613989115, 0.014371741563081741, -0.004359116777777672, 0.04404963552951813, 0.032519616186618805, -0.035251129418611526], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "0f55ac83585650e0e54004a0bad2032ca3f5cb8edb6764532d1fcf6f8774e7e0", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing the importance of tailored behaviour management strategies in schools. It emphasizes the need for personalized approaches, such as daily report cards for students with high behaviour needs, and highlights the necessity for consistent implementation of behaviour policies across all levels of the school to improve overall pupil behaviour.A key message is that schools should use personalised approaches\u2014like daily report cards\u2014to address \u2018problem pupils\u2019, rather than universal systems. It recommends that teachers are trained in specific strategies if they\u2019re dealing with pupils with high behaviour needs. The third focuses on the importance of consistency and coherence when it comes to behaviour policies. This means that once senior leaders have considered the rationale for putting a new behaviour strategy or approach to work, they need to spend time and care embedding it across the entire school. To develop this report\u2019s six recommendations for improving behaviour we not only reviewed the best available international research, but also consulted with teachers and other experts. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 4, "split_id": 3, "split_idx_start": 2979, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0f8ef712f2f215f293cb576345ef7b3896a84319560f80eaaf27999acc20368f", "range": [636, 785]}, {"doc_id": "77fb8d6793bb4ad36889df419d80d675404bca61ed8e9a204e3a86d60b0e36d2", "range": [0, 185]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06841837614774704, -0.0490243174135685, 0.010840908624231815, -0.024267105385661125, -0.01677696593105793, 0.010826385580003262, 0.026575928553938866, 0.00199165940284729, -0.0007820394821465015, 0.026359068229794502, 0.05546955019235611, 0.01869083195924759, -0.03307381644845009, 0.03626835718750954, 0.02718443050980568, -0.07482871413230896, -0.002113746479153633, -0.033523350954055786, -0.05697539076209068, 0.028954939916729927, -0.00669359415769577, -0.0053603798151016235, 0.024800429120659828, -0.0002814779873006046, -0.013859341852366924, -0.011434896849095821, 0.021297166123986244, -0.01001715287566185, 0.0573381707072258, -0.031084317713975906, 0.09700677543878555, 0.02773670107126236, 0.00712240394204855, -0.01415428426116705, 2.2665296910417965e-06, 0.01639450155198574, 0.009783866815268993, -0.03037686087191105, 0.02338647097349167, 0.01960919052362