85701, 0.029584841802716255, 0.01735762134194374, 0.05576377734541893, -0.005083394702523947, -0.03292412683367729], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "77fb8d6793bb4ad36889df419d80d675404bca61ed8e9a204e3a86d60b0e36d2", "content": "This chunk is part of the introduction to the guidance report, emphasizing the development of six recommendations based on international research and consultations with educators. It highlights the ongoing commitment of the Education Endowment Foundation to support schools in implementing these strategies and the report's relevance in current educational discussions, particularly regarding behaviour management and exclusion policies.To develop this report\u2019s six recommendations for improving behaviour we not only reviewed the best available international research, but also consulted with teachers and other experts. As with all EEF guidance reports, its publication is just the start of how we aim to support schools in implementing these recommendations. We will now be working with the sector, including through our colleagues in the Research Schools Network, to build on them with further training, resources and tools. This report is well-timed for school leaders to consider alongside the recent Timpson report on exclusions, and to be part of professional conversations around behaviour that will be central to the Department for Education\u2019s Behaviour Support Networks.\nAnd, as ever, we will be looking to support and test the most promising programmes that put the lessons from the research into practice. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 4, "split_id": 4, "split_idx_start": 3547, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0f55ac83585650e0e54004a0bad2032ca3f5cb8edb6764532d1fcf6f8774e7e0", "range": [568, 753]