60091, 0.04921270161867142, -0.033136989921331406, -0.005969967693090439, -0.013976793736219406, 0.031306058168411255, 0.07518088817596436, 0.041848037391901016, 0.02581217885017395, 0.022429469972848892, 0.021595574915409088, -0.05698153376579285, 0.07558642327785492, 0.021796507760882378, 0.041939374059438705, -0.0016504096565768123, -0.015060832723975182, -0.043346378952264786, 0.006454842630773783, 0.0010392906842753291, 0.0329875610768795, -0.04000721499323845, 0.03550920635461807, 0.008303288370370865, 0.027261784300208092, -0.04618912935256958, 0.03991448134183884, -0.013564798049628735, 0.014784261584281921, 0.01206428837031126, -0.007250857539474964, 0.013534702360630035, 0.06710298359394073, 0.015810135751962662, -0.010762106627225876, -0.056968849152326584, 0.08259894698858261, 0.016153695061802864, -0.00708726467564702, 0.008845476433634758, -0.03002479299902916, 0.05305291712284088, -0.03882867842912674, 0.05109560489654541, -0.05595870316028595, -0.0024094353429973125, 0.00961095467209816, 0.026457201689481735, -0.0014014363987371325, -0.05191388726234436, -0.021217159926891327, -0.017225416377186775, 1.6791655555289393e-34, -0.013486196286976337, 0.027488145977258682, 0.0015602241037413478, -0.04812188819050789, 0.02163352631032467, -0.015007272362709045, -0.03013513796031475, -0.01843535341322422, 0.07967881113290787, 0.03396476432681084, -0.02088336832821369], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "ec66dc73dfef9d4eb709d4e185154cbf2087c235b5c799dbed4bc9ea2a8bbfa2", "content": "This chunk is found in the section titled \"Recommendation 1: Know and understand your pupils and their influences,\" which discusses the importance of building supportive relationships with students. It highlights how understanding individual pupil contexts can influence behavior management strategies, and it provides examples to illustrate these dynamics in the classroom.At the teacher level, regularly and intentionally focusing small amounts of time working on relationships with individual pupils can have a big impact. This could be as simple as asking about their weekend or how their football team is performing.\nKnow and understand your pupils and their influences\n\u2018A multitude of interrelated factors influence each child\u2019s developmental course and academic growth.\u2019 6 Chodkiewicz and Boyle (2017)\nTwo children are disruptive in a classroom this morning: Pupil 1 feels he is lacking attention from the teacher and wants this even if it is negative;\nPupil 2 wants to escape the classroom as she is bored, so acts up to get removed.\nIf the teacher\u2019s default is to send out the child, this would reinforce Pupil 2\u2019s unhelpful behaviour, whereas for Pupil 1, this strategy could dissuade the behaviour. Reprimanding the child in class could reorient Pupil 2 but would reinforce Pupil 1\u2019s misbehaviour. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 10, "split_id": 15, "split_idx_start": 14132, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "7a84da2502efdfc7ebf5deaf6f5a0594d1adebd1fd87546bb735ffe3860e93b5", "range": [450, 602]}, {"doc_id": "12f3f2d5f8e34d8568cb85bc5a0619ae9983e33747a307147b32c48eb9568326", "range": [0, 99]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.07429404556751251, -0.10991384834051132, -0.012865589931607246, 0.024837195873260498, -0.009802538901567459, 0.02903766743838787, 0.07303805649280548, -0.017624765634536743, -0.03891609609127045, 0.018315786495804787, 0.03433503210544586, -0.06951736658811569, 0.008608788251876831, -0.05727482959628105, 0.014357957988977432, -0.0852980837225914, 0.003105883253738284, 0.0018765132408589125, -0.05687187984585762, 0.028826318681240082, -0.009772200137376785, -0.015650378540158272, 0.008282012306153774, -0.009972670115530491, -0.01807572692632675, -0.04484782367