mstance, they could act to increase the number of positive influences or reduce the negative, perhaps through counselling. If behaviour deteriorates, they will be in a better position to counteract the negative influence with an appropriate positive intervention.\nConsider, for example, Pupil A in Year 8 who has experienced the death of a close relative. The pupil begins in Quadrant A (the optimal position). ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 11, "split_id": 17, "split_idx_start": 15567, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "12f3f2d5f8e34d8568cb85bc5a0619ae9983e33747a307147b32c48eb9568326", "range": [599, 840]}, {"doc_id": "7bb664735f00f77ba32330f38584e9b91670f665c9edb31070049bb2a054881b", "range": [0, 55]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.011143732815980911, -0.1083751991391182, -0.0015592830022796988, -0.013024700805544853, -0.02832266129553318, 0.05884706228971481, 0.011109180748462677, 0.00021292375458870083, -0.016701603308320045, -0.012511773966252804, 0.06195496767759323, -0.0354747474193573, 0.015659648925065994, -0.03268321603536606, -0.014235459268093109, -0.07697678357362747, -0.014514748007059097, 0.026906397193670273, -0.0584651380777359, 0.05407615751028061, -0.04784092679619789, 0.0002894654171541333, -0.0488809272646904, -0.012156947515904903, -0.0013148464495316148, -0.04820124804973602, 0.012987857684493065, 0.02750386856496334, 0.025241011753678322, -0.03287987411022186, 0.027528466656804085, -0.011501704342663288, 0.01001619454473257, -0.073878213763237, 2.1812634258822072e-06, 0.02171849086880684, -0.012412482872605324, -0.03691447898745537, 0.009922032244503498, -0.01172884926199913, -0.00710738729685545, -0.041756611317396164, 0.024244172498583794, 0.0014847740530967712, 0.005626403260976076, -0.01986014284193