12781, 0.016551116481423378, 0.017904067412018776, -0.025518937036395073, 0.024913525208830833, 0.0026129449252039194, -0.039576657116413116, 0.021868597716093063, -0.017354927957057953, 0.03736810386180878, -0.023512618616223335, 0.00305128819309175, -0.015577892772853374, 0.0030687893740832806, -0.02032623440027237, -0.012271411716938019, -0.018286369740962982, -0.026353538036346436, 1.9156001729850148e-34, 0.02066771872341633, -0.00701211579144001, 0.0030000691767781973, -0.0538921058177948, 0.005408019293099642, -0.03431115671992302, -0.018411433324217796, 0.02443232387304306, 0.02583589218556881, 0.02468281425535679, -0.03327411413192749], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "69d54ca9febe662fcb9fe2edc0490f10961c6fc0c93330f07633645d496c28a1", "content": "This chunk is part of the discussion in the document on understanding and addressing individual pupil behaviour. It illustrates a specific case of a student, referred to as Pupil B, whose social challenges and talents are identified by school staff. The focus is on tailoring interventions to improve her social influences and overall behaviour rather than solely applying disciplinary measures, highlighting the importance of supportive relationships in behaviour management strategies.Investigating this behaviour, the school staff team becomes aware that she has not made solid friendships so has low social confidence since moving to the school the previous term. Alongside implementing the sanctions in the school\u2019s behaviour policy, school staff focus on improving the influences on Pupil B\u2019s behaviour. An informal meeting with her form tutor reveals that she is a talented musician, so she is encouraged to join the school band where she makes more friends. She is also encouraged to have regular conversations with her in-school mentor. As her influences in school improve, Pupil B becomes more aware of her own behaviours as well as being positively influenced by the friends and mentor she has grown close to; she adjusts her behaviour positively without much disciplinary action being taken.9\nBeing in an informed position where staff can be aware of negative influences starting or continuing to affect a pupil\u2019s life is key to building understanding and to identifying the most effective behaviour management approach.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 11, "split_id": 19, "split_idx_start": 16695, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "7bb664735f00f77ba32330f38584e9b91670f665c9edb31070049bb2a054881b", "range": [472, 653]}, {"doc_id": "58100bc51949175f1b85d98a2a9bec1f202f5d55671360b4f4c49e148e033eac", "range": [0, 487]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.05350098758935928, -0.0686371698975563, 0.01532699167728424, 0.00030703595257364213, -0.008632687851786613, 0.0050660367123782635, 0.02188851684331894, -0.014806853607296944, 0.007408828940242529, 0.0576489083468914, 0.03626606613397598, -0.011954632587730885, -0.02140478417277336, -0.011849121190607548, 0.021636463701725006, -0.05757608637213707, -0.003278482938185334, -0.003500403370708227, -0.021107500419020653, 0.01896294765174389, 0.0008001064998097718, 0.013553272932767868, 0.023311331868171692, 0.0005025170394219458, -0.014111742377281189, -0.04054800420999527, 0.04063793271780014, -0.004507826641201973, 0.0557684488594532, -0.007272581569850445, 0.05542276054620743, 0.041922811418771744, 0.0023137193638831377, -0.008666842244565487, 2.227073764515808e-06, 0.032171573489904404, 0.011000503785908222, -0.040232524275779724, 0.029432641342282295, -0.02899976074695587, -0.03513999283313751, -0.022776376456022263, 0.030624421313405037, 0.046775441616773605, -0.032071564346551895, 0.014596235007047653, -0.030740128830075264, -0.014375722035765648, 0.0388258695602417, -0.040925282984972, -