, "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing the importance of understanding and addressing the various influences on pupil behavior in schools. It illustrates how positive peer relationships and mentorship can lead to improved self-awareness and behavioral adjustments in students, highlighting the need for staff to be aware of external influences on their students' lives.As her influences in school improve, Pupil B becomes more aware of her own behaviours as well as being positively influenced by the friends and mentor she has grown close to; she adjusts her behaviour positively without much disciplinary action being taken.9\nBeing in an informed position where staff can be aware of negative influences starting or continuing to affect a pupil\u2019s life is key to building understanding and to identifying the most effective behaviour management approach.\nQuadrant A: Optimal\nQuadrant B: Resilient\nQuadrant D: Investigate\nQuadrant C: Sub Optimal\nInfluences\nInfluences\nBehaviour Behaviour\n+\n-\n+-\nPupil B\nPupil A\nFigure 2: The link between positive and negative school behaviour\tand\tinfluences\f10\nEducation Endowment Foundation A good way to build positive relationships with pupils is the EMR method, which has promising results from a small study. Summarised below, it involves focusing intentionally on the pupils who it is most difficult to connect with, who may be most in need of a consistent, positive relationship. It is recommended that this technique should take no longer than 30 minutes per week and can be completed during periods the adult already spends with pupils, representing an efficient use of time. Establish Maintain Restore (R3)\nDefinition Intentional practices to cultivate a positive relationship with each student (i.e. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 11, "split_id": 20, "split_idx_start": 17254, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "69d54ca9febe662fcb9fe2edc0490f10961c6fc0c93330f07633645d496c28a1", "range": [559, 1046]}, {"doc_id": "1567e9ae4f8a96fa9382a5c5b892ad383f81762445eff315779a609b1ac13602", "range": [0, 126]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.05215208977460861, -0.06802640110254288, 0.0015738257206976414, -0.007462215144187212, -0.024097973480820656, 0.01404350996017456, -0.0016668447060510516, -0.028401754796504974, -0.017659343779087067, 0.028256969526410103, 0.027643268927931786, 0.004327739588916302, 0.010304751805961132, -0.020688356831669807, 0.010026076808571815, -0.0811796486377716, -0.01819990575313568, 0.019079413264989853, -0.050133589655160904, 0.03926559537649155, 0.002950970781967044, 0.0065024965442717075, 0.0038908901624381542, -0.03135419264435768, -0.03112996183335781, -0.006735581438988447, 0.003925960510969162, 0.03066774643957615, 0.06681356579065323, -0.009311197325587273, 0.058414656668901443, 0.03156745806336403, -0.003201868152245879, -0.032556790858507156, 2.312462584086461e-06, 0.012743351981043816, -0.05064765363931656, -0.03596898540854454, -0.006673743482679129, -0.005925259552896023, -0.009451615624129772, -0.0292675718665123, 0.046992894262075424, 0.0470380075275898, -0.00529259629547596, 0.02048797719180584, -0.020210374146699905, 0.015298631973564625, 0.06334458291530609, -0.03559356927871704, 0.012361930683255196, -0.04305491968989372, -0.046988241374492645, -0.021131526678800583, 0.03807282820343971, -0.019223686307668686, 0.013831117190420628, -0.01044648140668869, -0.04204423725605011, -0.027585064992308617, -0.014986452646553516, -0.031849898397922516, -0.036345768719911575, -0.06519614905118942, 0.07635854184627533, -0.04371003434062004, 0.041352178901433945, -0.042878612875938416, 0.019263198599219322, -0.013271717354655266, 0.06632449477910995, 0.04388665780425072, 0.05586899816989899, 0.015439575538039