025310754776, 0.019480466842651367, 0.04392297938466072, -0.01041780598461628, -0.012768138200044632, -0.002950891852378845, -0.05166087672114372, 0.04291726276278496, 0.02533329278230667, 0.02462673932313919, 0.09190203994512558, -0.011529587209224701, 0.015864001587033272, -0.00442872429266572, 0.023547811433672905, -0.008336595259606838, 0.0194248016923666, 0.02464132383465767, -0.06498496979475021, 0.035199567675590515, -0.003786425106227398, 0.02299429103732109, 0.0070562721230089664, 0.019863788038492203, 0.030257800593972206, 0.029067588970065117, -0.008549634367227554, -0.04192795231938362, -0.04705754294991493, 0.01111865695565939, 1.7463210656550618e-34, -0.022713245823979378, 0.010196956805884838, 0.006126868072897196, -0.0876794084906578, 0.007774880155920982, -0.0017093871720135212, -0.00742263812571764, 0.011122886091470718, 0.0005117660039104521, 0.032328613102436066, -0.02137841284275055], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "74c8197b6d32a3ff665a8ef1244c2f8f66152874f6ce60f455d79077fdcbf764", "content": "This chunk is situated within the section discussing strategies for addressing bullying in schools, highlighting effective interventions, policies, and training for staff and parents. It emphasizes the impact of bullying on student behavior and attainment and points to evidence from a systematic review on successful anti-bullying programs.14\nEducation Endowment Foundation \u2022 Whole-school anti-bullying policy\n\u2022 Classroom rules: often set collaboratively by the class\n\u2022 School conferences: assemblies to introduce the initiative and inform pupils about bullying\n\u2022 Cooperative group work: school staff cooperating to work with bullies and victims of bullying\n\u2022 Information for parents: this could include a manual to structure a teacher\u2019s conversation or a leaflet for parents to digest at home\n\u2022 Improved playground supervision\n\u2022 Classroom management: see recommendation 3\n\u2022 Disciplinary methods: punitive measures such as being sent to the headteacher or being deprived of privileges\n\u2022 Teacher training: training taking place over more than 4 days and lasting 10 hours or more was most effective\n\u2022 Parent training/meetings: educational events for parents relating specifically to bullying\nBullying\nA key influence on a child\u2019s behaviour in school is being the victim of bullying. As well as causing stress for the pupil, being bullied is linked to lower attainment outcomes. 14 School approaches to prevent and respond to bullying are likely to involve establishing and maintaining high quality behaviour management throughout the whole school with support from parents and other stakeholders. In a systematic review and meta-analysis of anti-\nbullying programmes produced by the Campbell Collaboration in 2009, the authors Ttofi and Farrington reviewed 53 school initiatives and pulled out effective programmes and programme features. 15 They found that anti-bullying programmes were often effective at reducing bullying, with an average reduction in bullying of 20-23% after implementing a programme. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 16, "split_id": 28, "split_idx_start": 25294, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "de434907dfd257d447c68b4d587c5c7871b2f90712d9f0617b20f63578083a16", "range": [818, 1759]}, {"doc_id": "378511b0e271b54c943821d13a9ce57c928681c3de56dc72e050e0fcd42d11b8", "range": [0, 167]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.10792146623134613, -0.07119462639093399, 0.011027412489056587, 0.021367570385336876, 0.0010322637390345335, 0.0246552973985672, 0.059539664536714554, -0.016505511477589607, -0.025793662294745445, -0.008145862258970737, 0.05679284781217575, -0.010183670558035374, 0.013879230245947838, -0.030105574056506157, 0.0