f625c5f6ede2ead", "content": "This chunk is located in the section discussing the importance of teaching and understanding pupil behavior, specifically highlighting the significance of strong teacher-pupil relationships in enhancing behavior, effort, and academic outcomes. It connects to broader recommendations on implementing effective behavior management strategies in schools, emphasizing relational dynamics.There is a strong evidence base that teacher-pupil relationships are key to good pupil behaviour and that these relationships can affect pupil effort and academic attainment.\nWhere\u2019s the evidence?\nFirst stop for further reading:\nSarah-Jayne Blakemore (2018) \u2018Inventing Ourselves: The Secret Life of the Teenage Brain\u2019 . Neuroscientist Professor Sarah-Jayne Blakemore explains the changes in the brain during adolescence and relates this to behaviour in children, teenagers, and young adults in an accessible and enlightening manner.\nChildren\u2019s Commissioner (2012) \u2018Practical Tips for Schools: outstanding safeguarding practice in primary schools\u2019. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 17, "split_id": 30, "split_idx_start": 27762, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "378511b0e271b54c943821d13a9ce57c928681c3de56dc72e050e0fcd42d11b8", "range": [971, 1146]}, {"doc_id": "6348da76f17a2229cb66113601730d611af3dd344037a97d68c14bfc0cb4654f", "range": [0, 115]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06314888596534729, -0.029322536662220955, 0.017895499244332314, 0.015701036900281906, 0.005889481399208307, 0.018256498500704765, 0.07172274589538574, -0.0005675256834365427, -0.038002170622348785, 0.02578202821314335, 0.013561554253101349, -0.03277101367712021, 0.01980680227279663, -0.04698997363448143, 0.028144434094429016