-0.009087860584259033, -0.024986306205391884, -0.0005192173412069678, 0.045603930950164795, 0.0669456347823143, -0.022711237892508507, -0.01213159505277872, -0.013739056885242462, -0.04011456295847893, 0.03663235902786255, 0.011263450607657433, 0.02994561567902565, 0.08060706406831741, -0.015464253723621368, 0.0009553017443977296, 0.01462397351861, 0.038828037679195404, 0.017162393778562546, 0.0010306626791134477, -0.0007613528869114816, -0.06085804104804993, 0.03963916376233101, 0.019630461931228638, 0.055912259966135025, -0.03643476590514183, -0.011377673596143723, 0.0076024276204407215, 0.014895185828208923, -0.008622917346656322, -0.03721027076244354, -0.007533106487244368, -0.04192762076854706, 1.8410702725174057e-34, -0.020249268040060997, -0.050013571977615356, 0.010224156081676483, -0.07999790459871292, 0.006266724783927202, -0.017783474177122116, 0.008982088416814804, 0.03393834829330444, -0.008034639991819859, -0.0004114119801670313, -0.025855591520667076], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "95d757291dc39e4a79bfdd12cc4480bca90992a5a363c760f3d2c81e0b185046", "content": "This chunk is located in the section discussing Recommendation 2 of the guidance report, which emphasizes the importance of teaching learning behaviours in conjunction with managing misbehaviour. It highlights how pupil behaviour is influenced by emotional, social, and cognitive factors, referencing Ellis and Tod's model to illustrate these relationships.In Recommendation 1 we explored the possible factors that influence pupil behaviour and the extent \u2018The successful management of behaviour relies on far more than a set of strategies to draw upon when pupils misbehave\u2019 16 Ellis and Tod (2018)\nEmotional\nSocial\nCognitive\f17Improving behaviour in schools\nto which schools can affect these. The framework suggests that learning behaviours fall within the realm of the school\u2019s\u2014and even the individual teacher\u2019s\u2014\ninfluence and thus warrant more attention from school practitioners. Ellis and Tod\u2019s model is adapted from a previous framework from Powell and Tod in 2004 22, shown in Figure 3. In this model, a single learning behaviour (from those detailed below) is placed at the centre of the model. The triangle surrounding this behaviour is the \u2018triangle of influence\u2019 representing the behaviour being influenced by emotional, social, and cognitive factors. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 18, "split_id": 35, "split_idx_start": 31562, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "589568db16178c9957cb0b2f86cf868f081f9e3724f2faafdd793284e44989c4", "range": [718, 1056]}, {"doc_id": "91f19d9cd62a65a6154cc2d0d703cd940586a8aa238ee3a247cc9fa9d805ffef", "range": [0, 160]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0567980632185936, -0.12425187975168228, -0.0019286725437268615, 0.003374326042830944, -0.026487313210964203, 0.06281588971614838, 0.03279354050755501, 0.015990909188985825, 0.014917193911969662, -0.008447020314633846, 0.033527638763189316, 0.00030921935103833675, 0.005504496395587921, -0.029412109404802322, 0.04585615545511246, -0.08930136263370514, 0.015522254630923271, -0.0032770477700978518, -0.03704755753278732, 0.029344484210014343, -0.006138973403722048, -0.01030018087476492, 0.014718362130224705, 0.006576002109795809, -0.016188543289899826, -0.021622201427817345, -0.011837027966976166, 0.004587519448250532, 0.004409411456435919, -0.028721749782562256, 0.06581605225801468, 0.04135555028915405, 0.0096896942704916, -0.04039028286933899, 2.2393160179490224e-06, 0.00024101280723698437, -0.019847923889756203, -0.013535510748624802, 0.03304901346564293, 0.014800576493144035, -0.013952620327472687, 0.04619574546813965, 0.03389780595898628, 0.019795982167124748, 0.0039985645562410355, 0.02956476248