388, 0.014697222970426083, 0.046601347625255585, -0.05088633671402931, -0.029199564829468727, 0.0014893047045916319, -0.027524109929800034, -0.013312110677361488, -0.08002156764268875, 0.0315522663295269, -0.014764336869120598, 1.7912210468478864e-34, 0.003017162438482046, -0.08584883064031601, 0.03646732494235039, -0.03917219862341881, -0.018442057073116302, 0.010686153545975685, 0.03342682123184204, 0.025495557114481926, 0.04352248087525368, 0.07146276533603668, -0.03702012822031975], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "3a96f29129490f21a55c79523ace320abb034d13ad791097c00de948e6905daf", "content": "This chunk is part of the recommendation section focusing on teaching learning behaviours as a strategy to improve classroom management and reduce disruptions. It emphasizes the importance of shifting from merely managing misbehaviour to fostering self-regulation and effective learning behaviours, aligning with findings from previous educational reports and EEF guidance.Several high-quality studies suggest that a shift of focus from managing a child\u2019s behaviour towards teaching a child learning behaviours may be beneficial. This research evidence fits with the message from the 2005 report from The Practitioners\u2019 Group on School Behaviour and Discipline led by Sir Alan Steer, \u201c\u2018Learning Behaviour\u2019\u201d. The body of evidence relating specifically to self-regulation is covered more thoroughly in the EEF\u2019s Guidance Report, \u2018Metacognition and self-regulated learning\u2019 .\f20\nEducation Endowment Foundation 3\n\u2018Pupils are potentially losing up to an hour of learning each day in English schools because of \u2026 disruption in classrooms. This is equivalent to 38 days of teaching lost per year.\u201925\nOfsted, 2014\nUse classroom management strategies to support good classroom behaviour\nTraining for classroom management\nEvidence suggests that effective training for building classroom management expertise involves teachers or school staff:\n\u2022 Reflecting on their own approach;\n\u2022 Trying a new approach; and\n\u2022 Reviewing progress over time. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 21, "split_id": 44, "split_idx_start": 38578, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "cd8d14d4bcecf6dcb52fedfeab6817cdea5a0c2478d2f3acae632f4f2068b86b", "range": [556, 713]}, {"doc_id": "70dd67321c464e22ad44fd0ba063d128d13fdf3fcd8a794db04d5727a3f301c4", "range": [0, 397]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.05804964900016785, -0.12268267571926117, -0.013716482557356358, -0.005843971390277147, 0.01286632101982832, 0.006923420820385218, 0.04475339129567146, -0.0268341563642025, -0.0016867915401235223, 0.009946828708052635, 0.01807539351284504, 0.036563992500305176, -0.03991563245654106, -0.037431295961141586, 0.04039639234542847, -0.06839257478713989, 0.009641204960644245, -0.021343089640140533, -0.04575485363602638, 0.035902343690395355, 0.0031815178226679564, -0.03621756657958031, -0.006099797785282135, -0.017381146550178528, -0.04845695570111275, -0.037747304886579514, 0.012922153808176517, 0.005436376202851534, 0.004297525156289339, -0.015863152220845222, 0.09531353414058685, 0.029789285734295845, 0.010684434324502945, -0.012982266023755074, 2.171375399484532e-06, 0.007876084186136723, -0.029467329382896423, -0.053709477186203, -0.0019276890670880675, 0.017832553014159203, -0.02438649907708168, 0.024576446041464806, 0.022441809996962547, 0.042557764798402786, -0.008390767499804497, 0.06443469226360321, -0.011524229310452938, 0.01532358955591917, 0.031329695135354996, -0.03510294482111931, 0.0117725795134902, 0.01679423823952675, -0.03631949424743652, -0.004572660196572542, 0.08258723467588425, -0.01834866777062416, 0.01010547298938036, 0.024996409192681313, -0.0018294889014214277, -