9997941256, -0.01807902753353119, -0.04732346907258034, 0.04850030317902565, 0.04096211865544319, 0.06353176385164261, -0.012206503190100193, -0.01829860545694828, -0.00676966505125165, -0.016672514379024506, 0.030452869832515717, -0.0072926366701722145, 0.03220902755856514, 0.04958219826221466, -0.06171029806137085, -0.003916393034160137, 0.0006614312878809869, 0.04452120140194893, 0.016887376084923744, -0.03562367334961891, -0.0006259105284698308, -0.042535848915576935, -0.023730237036943436, 0.013739417307078838, 0.061420515179634094, -0.02393863908946514, -0.033595647662878036, -0.006064045708626509, 0.013908729888498783, -0.014735264703631401, -0.07071872055530548, 0.008427522145211697, -0.04633593186736107, 1.5478467653302622e-34, 0.006875208579003811, -0.04517125338315964, 0.019490966573357582, -0.07097083330154419, 0.0021756854839622974, -0.010065706446766853, 0.01140879187732935, 0.010629415512084961, -0.002055294578894973, 0.023796524852514267, -0.0334264375269413], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "7b466a1e69e3fb70615c12ed898cf40b3d829a6e04e92098456265ea8ba7792a", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing classroom management strategies in the context of improving behavior in schools. It highlights the impact of effective classroom management on reducing challenging behavior, student disengagement, and bullying, while also addressing attendance issues and their correlation with lower attainment outcomes. The text provides advice specifically for early career teachers regarding behavior management challenges.27\nEffective classroom management can reduce challenging behaviour, pupil disengagement, bullying, and aggression, leading to improved classroom climate, attendance, and attainment. 28 While attendance at school and bullying are not wholly the preserve of schools,29 schools have a role to play. This is of particular concern as in 2019, \u2018\u2026 both authorised and unauthorised absence rates have increased since last year, the rate of the latter now being the highest since records began.\u201930 Increasing school absence or being bullied are linked to lower attainment outcomes. 31\f21Improving behaviour in schools\nEarly career teachers should understand that:\n\u2022 it is normal for them to have more issues with behaviour management in their classroom than more experienced colleagues; it is okay to ask for help;\n\u2022 even the most experienced teachers implementing universal classroom management strategies well will find they do not work for all pupils all the time; \u2022 some students will need a more tailored approach (see Recommendation 5) which may require reflection and adapting to the situation; and\n\u2022 what works for one teacher might not work for another with the same pupil: it may take a while to find the right strategy and it may help to ask a range of colleagues about their approaches. FemaleGender\nTeaching\nExperience\nHighest\nQualification\n1-5 years\n6-10 years\n11-15 years\n16+ years\nBachelor\u2019s degree\nMaster\u2019s degree\nMale\n-0.4 -0.2 0.0 +0.2 +0.4\nClassroom Climate Score\nSource: TALIS database. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 22, "split_id": 46, "split_idx_start": 40287, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "70dd67321c464e22ad44fd0ba063d128d13fdf3fcd8a794db04d5727a3f301c4", "range": [1049, 1231]}, {"doc_id": "5a6b751564cffc6d84552486a600dc895a266a44f00e8d80021a432899f5c6a4", "range": [0, 209]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.08400437235832214, -0.0876506119966507, -0.008886236697435379, 0.011297105811536312, -0.01090922299772501, 0.04052536189556122, 0.08557768911123276, -0.013632855378091335, -0.016517676413059235, 0.0317847914993763, 0.0495646670460701, -0.027091030031442642, -0.018010834231972694, -0.0350219532847