124427869915962, 0.024763520807027817, 0.05004430562257767, -0.07712879776954651, -0.02495155856013298, -0.08147084712982178, 0.0006753172492608428, 0.007277682423591614, 0.07285276800394058, 0.011904633603990078, 0.030251849442720413, 0.012156730517745018, -0.00048406163114123046, 0.009623469784855843, -0.02882545068860054, -0.04612564295530319, 0.021328750997781754, -0.0059100366197526455, 0.01265430636703968, -0.023346813395619392, 0.017780650407075882, 0.0117582306265831, -0.008884788490831852, -0.003927422687411308, -0.04296209290623665, 0.05465928092598915, 0.07385893911123276, 0.04198712110519409, 0.028340434655547142, 0.0008717639720998704, -0.026160920038819313, -0.05389655753970146, 0.021663257852196693, -0.02036234922707081, 0.02849423512816429, 0.06802497804164886, -0.08871317654848099, -0.0014177818084135652, -0.006105876062065363, 0.00837621372193098, -0.010555019602179527, -0.030648399144411087, 0.015911484137177467, -0.025157691910862923, -0.023161161690950394, 0.011012936010956764, 0.011412868276238441, -0.09190510213375092, -0.001277380739338696, -0.046604789793491364, -0.006105801556259394, 0.008466515690088272, -0.02457830309867859, 0.008809025399386883, -0.033795639872550964, 2.1820453678474496e-34, 0.03776839002966881, -0.03966325893998146, 0.009791407734155655, -0.10482346266508102, -0.003720040200278163, 0.01850619539618492, 0.03397030383348465, 0.02328755147755146, 0.034079767763614655, 0.07073687762022018, -0.01241131592541933], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "e818b83f75e3bbabc63aa9c181e6005d4d6c509cae18e8dbe1769da44bb426ad", "content": "This chunk is from the section discussing the challenges of classroom management for early-career teachers, referencing the OECD\u2019s TALIS survey. It highlights the correlation between years of experience and improved classroom climate, and introduces the Incredible Years\u00ae Teacher Classroom Management (TCM) program as an evidence-based solution to support effective classroom management.Classroom management tends to be more of a problem for teachers earlier in their careers than for those with more experience. The OECD\u2019s Teaching and Learning International Survey (TALIS) is a regular (5 yearly) survey of teachers and headteachers across over 40 countries which focuses on teaching practices and the working conditions of teachers and their headteachers. Figure 4 from the 2013 TALIS report in secondary schools demonstrates that while there is no statistically significant difference between male and female teachers or those with and without a Master\u2019s degree, there is a substantial improvement in classroom climate associated with being in the profession longer than five years.\f22\nEducation Endowment Foundation Several high-quality studies suggest that Incredible Years \u00ae Teacher Classroom Management (TCM) can have a positive effect on pupil behaviour. The TCM programme is part of a suite of programmes for children, parents, and teachers (www.incredibleyears.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 23, "split_id": 48, "split_idx_start": 42144, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "5a6b751564cffc6d84552486a600dc895a266a44f00e8d80021a432899f5c6a4", "range": [567, 693]}, {"doc_id": "c2058c08937c2b8104a6dd4b1253875cd31360275d7fc2091e1c3c9ae3befd4f", "range": [0, 109]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.045382507145404816, -0.05176599696278572, -0.00855114497244358, -0.00040853387326933444, 0.015306328423321247, 0.057190220803022385, 0.06768171489238739, -0.014071272686123848, -0.07096891105175018, 0.02394205890595913, 0.036710433661937714, 0.02166701853275299, 0.020161427557468414, -0.04560070484876633, 0.001065390883013606, -0.03430471196770668, 0.012307681143283844, 0.027489906176924706, -0.06453867256641388, 0.0594651922