0739746, 0.02241404727101326, 0.04183059558272362, 0.003918719477951527, -0.041537534445524216, -0.03609306365251541, -0.032447393983602524, 0.025118641555309296, -0.011004987172782421, -0.04272256791591644, -0.006159964483231306, -0.0129981879144907, -0.010982070118188858, 0.005365132819861174, -0.009902711026370525, -0.03921122848987579, 0.07413709163665771, 0.04602798819541931, 0.05890554189682007, -0.019057320430874825, -0.03544458746910095, -0.03274669498205185, -0.04627327248454094, 0.04367908835411072, -0.006349171511828899, 0.039487116038799286, 0.079694464802742, -0.03567684069275856, -0.0027196344453841448, -0.012504328042268753, 0.03672756627202034, 0.03491504490375519, -0.010201618075370789, 0.018714502453804016, -0.027726629748940468, -0.027235856279730797, 0.016724232584238052, 0.06667212396860123, -0.043200161308050156, -0.03822074458003044, -0.02659730240702629, 0.004901432897895575, 0.01405569352209568, -0.061042699962854385, 0.02466505952179432, -0.009711010381579399, 1.7558021622784128e-34, -0.004230127204209566, -0.0735342875123024, 0.037864960730075836, -0.11114106327295303, 0.012246615253388882, -0.002179438015446067, 0.02427082322537899, -0.023914959281682968, -0.014711779542267323, 0.016282416880130768, -0.03164688125252724], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "b04eb5f2aa89f5b6288a9d2046acdbde8437f576fbc7284f254f6d9933721448", "content": "This chunk is part of the guidance report focused on improving classroom management and student behaviour through the \"Incredible Years\" Teacher Training Program. It highlights the importance of teacher-parent collaboration and describes training methodologies aimed at enhancing teachers' skills in managing classroom behaviour effectively.The programme also helps teachers work with parents to support their school involvement and promote consistency between home and school. Teachers attend a full-day training session each month for six months using collaborative learning, discussions of staff\u2019s own experiences, and group work to find solutions to problems encountered in the classroom.\nBox 5: Incredible Years\u00ae Teacher Classroom Management\nUse selectively:\n\u2022 Loss of privileges\n\u2022 Timeout\n\u2022 Call parent\n\u2022 Work chore\nUse Liberally\nUse Liberally\nBenefits for child Teacher skills and strategies\nDisruptive behaviours\nNon-disruptive behaviours\nResponsibility\nPredictability\nObedience\nSocial skills\nAcademic skills\nMotivation\nProblem Solving\nCooperation\nSelf-esteem Empathy Attention and involvement\nPraise\nEncouragment\nClear limits\nClassroom structures\nNon verbal cues\nPositive verbal redirect\nConsequences\nReminder of expected behaviour\nWarning of consequences\nRe-engagment strategies\nDistractions\nIncentives\nCelebrations\nPlay Problem solving\nListening Talking\nFigure 5: The Incredible Years Teaching Pyramid \u00ae\nAdapted from Webster-Stratton, C. and Reid, M. J. (2001) Incredible Years Teacher Training Program: Content, Methods and Processes (Facilitator Manual), Seattle.\f23Improving behaviour in schools\nFirst stop for further reading\nOfsted (2014) \u2018Below the Radar - Low level disruption in the country\u2019s classrooms\u2019 https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/below-the-radar-low-level-disruption-in-the-countrys-classrooms This report provides an overview of the level of disruption occurring in classrooms in England. Carolyn Webster-Stratton (2012) \u2018Incredible Teachers: Nurturing Children\u2019s Social, Emotional, and Academic Competence\u2019, Seattle: Incredible Years Inc. Webster-Stratton pioneered the Incredible Years approach and in this book outlines strategies teachers can use to support 3-8 year-olds with their behaviour, including how to partner with parents.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4