69731891155, 0.03672133758664131, 0.04377413168549538, 0.04804573208093643, 0.05407937243580818, 0.035976607352495193, -0.005328682716935873, 0.007159550674259663, -0.07700181007385254, 0.010062074288725853, 0.02280549518764019, -0.02506641298532486, -0.04079072177410126, -0.020154708996415138, -0.012757704593241215, -0.02028413489460945, 0.010553041473031044, -0.008129388093948364, -0.048727210611104965, 0.053128745406866074, 0.015772854909300804, 0.048363231122493744, -0.007708718068897724, -0.026425983756780624, -0.011082939803600311, -0.041651468724012375, 0.042662229388952255, -0.008125467225909233, 0.021248076111078262, 0.08226390928030014, -0.03223445639014244, -0.03998590633273125, 0.009721442125737667, 0.053800299763679504, 0.013222779147326946, -0.003453341079875827, 0.02025998942553997, -0.012042759917676449, -0.001718296785838902, 0.04112008586525917, 0.04029281064867973, -0.03502245619893074, -0.036045707762241364, -0.015060481615364552, 0.020649081096053123, 0.03232923150062561, -0.06397104263305664, 0.005179164931178093, -0.0016605365090072155, 1.8279475540882797e-34, -0.020012658089399338, -0.03328118845820427, 0.014123493805527687, -0.0723651722073555, -0.005096542648971081, 0.013041667640209198, 0.006898076273500919, -0.01919618248939514, 0.04129752516746521, 0.04223855212330818, -0.029960675165057182], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "0ad6e1905cf2a75077723749283b85f583bac74065a213b2c5ba309f09c6d93c", "content": "This chunk appears in the section discussing effective classroom management strategies for improving pupil behaviour. It emphasizes the importance of implementing clear reward systems as part of a broader approach to behavior management, referencing Carolyn Webster-Stratton\u2019s work on the Incredible Years programme and its relevance for young children.Carolyn Webster-Stratton (2012) \u2018Incredible Teachers: Nurturing Children\u2019s Social, Emotional, and Academic Competence\u2019, Seattle: Incredible Years Inc. Webster-Stratton pioneered the Incredible Years approach and in this book outlines strategies teachers can use to support 3-8 year-olds with their behaviour, including how to partner with parents.\nReinforcing positive behaviours\nPutting in place clear reward systems can improve pupil behaviour in the classroom when used as part of a broader teacher classroom management strategy. Reward systems mainly involve the presentation of something such as a reward or praise to reinforce desirable behaviours, but can sometimes also involve removing something- such as a right to sit next to a friend or time to play - known as punishment. Following on from Recommendation 2, reward systems can be an effective way to improve pupils\u2019 learning behaviours. Reward systems are often included in whole-class and whole-school approaches to behaviour and could include star charts or house points systems.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 25, "split_id": 51, "split_idx_start": 45107, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b04eb5f2aa89f5b6288a9d2046acdbde8437f576fbc7284f254f6d9933721448", "range": [1586, 1934]}, {"doc_id": "a92fee52c1d68759f2a9d9be478d84b51c920666482df13bf41bfe7b1e81d1cd", "range": [0, 145]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06815416365861893, -0.08303675055503845, -0.0031759031116962433, 0.010180793702602386, -0.012991008348762989, 0.05573020130395889, 0.029972733929753304, -0.013411758467555046, -0.049523673951625824, 0.06278882920742035, 0.02049347385764122, 0.031391773372888565, 0.023134753108024597, -0.04687310382723808, 0.014783495105803013, -0.07734156399965286, 0.029988277703523636, 0.02100299298763275, 0.005181074142456055, 0.03072010912001133, -0.003992946818470955, -0.011612544767558575, -0.019428297877311707, 0.009328514337539673, -0.0415078