759738, 0.0041861506178975105, -0.05438511446118355, -0.006135293748229742, 0.013031057082116604, -0.002513066167011857, -0.03394755348563194, 0.029656939208507538, -0.02525036409497261, -0.0414099395275116, 0.015034332871437073, 0.0016676580999046564, -0.06544414162635803, 0.026729799807071686, 0.02935064397752285, 0.04800492152571678, -0.016484107822179794, -0.02714243158698082, -0.008366543799638748, -0.03144824877381325, 0.03383421525359154, -0.024270201101899147, 0.02233538217842579, 0.051796894520521164, -0.058605074882507324, -0.011478434316813946, 0.012503628619015217, 0.04546937346458435, 0.001712443889118731, -0.024635832756757736, 0.0068920389749109745, 0.0014046813594177365, -0.02493858151137829, 0.018557030707597733, 0.04245837405323982, -0.024422239512205124, -0.03819730505347252, -0.010461456142365932, -0.023611238226294518, 0.056190721690654755, -0.09523792564868927, -0.05947256460785866, -0.028145093470811844, 1.716707217592105e-34, 0.0022418489679694176, -0.047333359718322754, 0.012443799525499344, -0.09011752158403397, 0.0016176120843738317, 0.006678999401628971, 0.010962467640638351, -0.0070689087733626366, 0.04500340670347214, 0.042301781475543976, -0.04696381837129593], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "4531897848fb89b674695c66f3eb3a5b63c91b7aeff9081287d9f17acfbd0fdb", "content": "This chunk is part of the recommendations section in the EEF guidance report on improving behaviour in schools. It discusses the importance of combining teacher training with simple, effective reinforcement strategies to enhance student behaviour, highlighting low-cost approaches that can foster a positive learning environment and improve educational outcomes.This combination of training teachers alongside delivering a rewards-focused reinforcement programme holds most promise. Where\u2019s the evidence?\f24\nEducation Endowment Foundation 4\nUse simple approaches as part of your regular routine\nWhile perfecting your school\u2019s approach to behaviour is likely to require training, external expertise, and coordination across the school (see Recommendations 3, 5, and 6), some strategies that do not require complex pedagogical changes have been shown to be promising. The message here is not to overlook simple things done well, such as:\n\u2022 starting the day with a free breakfast club;\n\u2022 greeting each student positively at the door;\n\u2022 giving specific behaviour-related praise throughout the lesson;\n\u2022 using simple approaches to improve teacher\u2013\nstudent relationships (see Recommendation 2); and\n\u2022 using checklists to ensure behaviour policies and procedures are embedded with rigour.\nMost of these strategies have little or no cost, yet the research suggests that they could reduce challenging behaviour and lead to improved attainment, improved attendance, and a more purposeful learning climate.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 25, "split_id": 55, "split_idx_start": 48179, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0878b7d6cb55bf1989e7bf8696c63e53000e2f10fd351703abd4975a3da6c1d1", "range": [649, 770]}, {"doc_id": "b1e8ddc3cece7af59d177877a228e06485e56c7b33bb7042359ee156aba07999", "range": [0, 214]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0575537383556366, -0.050038959830999374, 0.01227863784879446, -0.0024086388293653727, -0.007280600257217884, 0.043029531836509705, 0.002558997366577387, -0.003753718687221408, -0.056152865290641785, 0.030377743765711784, 0.03374205157160759, 0.04361604154109955, -0.0012908832868561149, 0.014200790785253048, 0.03150442615151405, -0.08370372653007507, 0.030510276556015015, 0.012750990688800812, -0.03685785457491875, 0.02016778290271759, -0.005461522843688726, -0.03236900642514229, 0.0006959314923733473, -0.028172330930829048, -0.01439442019909620