 0.0429227240383625, -0.017580650746822357, -0.01817481964826584, -0.015322953462600708, -0.02399638667702675, 0.008781729266047478, -0.0808488056063652, -0.037293411791324615, -0.054093290120363235, 1.805358432715188e-34, 0.016442660242319107, -0.02557266689836979, 0.012642830610275269, -0.046063464134931564, -0.013283848762512207, -0.007653634529560804, 0.0256710946559906, -0.01483996119350195, -0.001982881687581539, -0.008167717605829239, -0.013976392336189747], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "5132c8324186ef2498fbd93ec08add56a76d7d091c9e4f6695eac908cff32a94", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing proactive strategies for improving pupil behaviour in schools. It emphasizes the importance of reinforcing positive behaviours through simple and effective methods, such as greeting students at the door, alongside more complex classroom management programmes that require extensive training.25Improving behaviour in schools\nSeveral \u2018pro-active\u2019 behaviour approaches aim to improve behaviour by reinforcing positive behaviours, prior to negative behaviours occurring. Some of these strategies are interwoven into classroom management programmes, which can be very effective but require substantial teacher training in order to ensure fidelity. Some pro-active approaches, however, are much simpler to implement. Below is a summary of two easily implemented \u2018behaviour kernel\u2019-\nbased approaches with very small-scale but promising results.\nRecent research conducted with 11-14 year-olds suggests that greeting students positively at the classroom door is not only very low cost but has a high yield in terms of improving pupil behaviour in the classroom.35 Misbehaviour often occurs in schools around the start and end of lessons and when moving around the school building. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 27, "split_id": 58, "split_idx_start": 50653, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "867f936417e36238bf009289afaab043ee3ea21cae063f0c190172601185e373", "range": [658, 834]}, {"doc_id": "4fefe404e0050f3b99456e990de520712ad730dcdbf455fb2deb212cacfdba0e", "range": [0, 334]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.060323651880025864, -0.059316813945770264, 0.0013227291638031602, 0.006966385990381241, 0.0013429878745228052, 0.005439446307718754, 0.016993220895528793, -0.007637518458068371, -0.013627775944769382, 0.014655554667115211, 0.05452316254377365, 0.009034009650349617, -0.05942296236753464, 0.012547961436212063, 0.05249689891934395, -0.08677810430526733, 0.020593004301190376, 0.0059032319113612175, -0.03576713800430298, 0.026010695844888687, 0.013733510859310627, -0.04678967967629433, -0.016375044360756874, 0.00022089225240051746, -0.04896191135048866, 0.007952551357448101, -0.024310491979122162, -0.0063553787767887115, 0.07839738577604294, -0.020406290888786316, 0.09596008062362671, 0.02303900755941868, 0.012434223666787148, 0.013554133474826813, 2.0614363620552467e-06, 0.0011059166863560677, 0.02310885861515999, -0.029687002301216125, 0.016320044174790382, -0.0016618084628134966, -0.02233150415122509, -0.02126307412981987, 0.010921009816229343, 0.005470362026244402, -0.02989261783659458, 0.027025233954191208, -0.0009371708729304373, 0.02652023546397686, 0.04968267306685448, -0.020371723920106888, 0.017764344811439514, -0.06531650573015213, -0.02974507585167885, 0.024962514638900757, 0.07382762432098389, 0.011175413616001606, 0.009570927359163761, 0.0008980553247965872, 0.0003880238509736955, -0.014210502617061138, -0.03521580621600151, -0.027221091091632843, -0.018855327740311623, -0.08075571805238724, 0.04280653968453407, -0.02111750841140747, -0.04823993518948555, -0.026973148807883263, -0.009523637592792511, 0.004463717807084322, 0.004277817439287901, 0.026965035125613213