ng behaviour in schools, aligning with the document's focus on effective behaviour management strategies.This paper describes 52 behaviour kernels with links to research surrounding them.\nInstitute for Fiscal Studies and National Children\u2019s Bureau (2016), \u2018Magic Breakfast: evaluation report and executive summary\u2019. https://educationendowmentfoundation.org.uk/projects-and-evaluation/projects/magic-breakfast/ The report from an evaluation funded by the EEF into the effect of universal, before-school breakfast clubs run by charity Magic Breakfast. You can also check if you are eligible for fundng by contacting Magic Breakfast at https://www.magicbreakfast.com/\nCharlie Taylor was a government expert adviser for behaviour and gathered the views of several headteachers of outstanding schools in deprived areas. He found that their approach to improving behaviour was similar: do the simple things well with consistency. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 29, "split_id": 65, "split_idx_start": 55875, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "43cdee9c1fab4479c9a7c728d4c0bac729ef0f64fd6971b8a4ba43871b622ce9", "range": [511, 594]}, {"doc_id": "66d0b138123c34d12a989a632b203a417958b1e415dfdea40c94ed29dfe87a54", "range": [0, 109]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.07168460637331009, -0.05976990610361099, 0.035629987716674805, 0.016106318682432175, -0.004483378026634455, 0.029283840209245682, -0.02707044407725334, -0.01737934909760952, -0.036874428391456604, 0.006853858940303326, 0.04422840476036072, 0.04620853066444397, -0.026267459616065025, 0.01910644769668579, 0.00821520946919918, -0.055035192519426346, 0.029777582734823227, 0.005627609323710203, -0.08923149853944778, 0.02972731553018093, -0.01424432173371315, -0.020574595779180527, 0