97, 0.013554261066019535, -0.015136918053030968, -0.0512915775179863, 0.003678056877106428, -0.0015808887546882033, -0.07769040018320084, 0.029925886541604996, 0.0022468846291303635, 0.05708850175142288, -0.04324139654636383, -0.005819160491228104, -0.008874645456671715, -0.01904941350221634, 0.040252719074487686, -0.01377253420650959, 0.01619289629161358, 0.06983450055122375, -0.020920071750879288, -0.044535234570503235, 0.015570019371807575, 0.019505713135004044, -0.00732871750369668, -0.005317130126059055, 0.03349054977297783, -0.03156775236129761, 0.007070911582559347, 0.016677644103765488, 0.027345282956957817, 0.007953142747282982, -0.02163511887192726, 0.021089425310492516, 0.009869416244328022, 0.04052610695362091, -0.05622263252735138, -0.06747785210609436, -0.006835584994405508, 1.5722642166374893e-34, -0.007948988117277622, -0.015717346221208572, 0.009803380817174911, -0.10472479462623596, -0.026205960661172867, 0.012597862631082535, -0.02855665050446987, 0.025175990536808968, 0.04731022194027901, 0.008525006473064423, -0.0325109101831913], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "07108ef3e53977f07cbf8a8671799cdb4de04fcf8bd611c01d56b567756517da", "content": "This chunk is located in the section discussing targeted approaches to meet the needs of individual students within the guidance report on improving behaviour in schools. It emphasizes the importance of tailoring behavioural support to complement existing school behaviour policies, highlighting effective programmes such as functional behavioural assessments and daily report cards.\u201cA tailored approach to support an individual\u2019s behaviour should complement the school\u2019s behaviour policy.\u201d\f29Improving behaviour in schools\nProgramme types with positive outcomes\nAdditional programmes may be put in place for pupils who are struggling with behaviour or in classes where behaviour is particularly poor. Large effects were seen for both:\n\u2022 functional behavioural assessment interventions, and\n\u2022 programmes using daily report cards.\nFunctional behavioural assessments involve shared training and collaborative decision-making between in-school staff and other key external bodies such as a social worker or speech therapist. Observation is used to learn about the reasons for a pupil\u2019s behaviour including any triggers for challenging behaviour. For example, an assessment by the teacher might conclude that a particularly disruptive child\u2019s behaviour is attention-seeking. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 30, "split_id": 70, "split_idx_start": 59475, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "c2b93d0f76fde8af5bd8227cad5b2e7ff2d2153c6d5d2869ba3ba0fd7a09d6ac", "range": [1192, 1511]}, {"doc_id": "9bbc69c6f5c4b6b234f70fb45768c7afccaa1e760f03bf4fbc559374a47bc772", "range": [0, 128]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.05643971264362335, -0.12916024029254913, -0.00810460839420557, -0.001433181343600154, -0.04568716138601303, 0.04559753090143204, 0.03857707604765892, 0.005466023460030556, -0.002459427108988166, 0.010917804203927517, 0.057054780423641205, -0.013829152099788189, 0.021477676928043365, 0.0005956441746093333, 0.03691025823354721, -0.09223899990320206, 0.027384663000702858, 0.009604205377399921, -0.060953158885240555, 0.029659904539585114, -0.001606999197974801, 0.0014712559059262276, -0.012266729958355427, 0.017238404601812363, -0.012625537812709808, -0.016074497252702713, 0.003933262545615435, -0.016261884942650795, 0.001829221728257835, -0.0420529730618, 0.073260098695755, 0.01853322796523571, -0.008321037515997887, -0.06623704731464386, 2.0356087588879745e-06, 0.03332669287919998, 0.0005019967793487012, 0.007414526771754026, 0.018894925713539124, 0.01682906597852707, -0.006507322657853365, -0.00575141189619898