 their effectiveness in addressing specific behavioural needs, particularly in primary school settings, while emphasizing the need for further research in secondary schools.Evidence for targeted interventions comes from 25 targeted studies, including 15 RCTs. Most of the research available is based in primary school settings: there is a need for more research on targeted interventions in secondary school settings. Targeted programmes tend to demonstrate a bigger effect on behaviour outcomes compared to whole-class or whole-school programmes\u2014this is to be expected as pupils are generally selected because they need specific support. However, targeted approaches have less consistent results than universal approaches, with studies varying from reporting no effect to very large effects.\nWhere\u2019s the evidence?\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 31, "split_id": 73, "split_idx_start": 61476, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "3251908af811b80f140b23542f62c4e6067f135a0392ef4d36de32c204359aae", "range": [581, 668]}, {"doc_id": "4988c3e29bd876040cde30411d6248a7c1cc65bed98dabefb47c07659b622475", "range": [0, 22]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.08161715418100357, -0.060889288783073425, 0.006303082220256329, -0.0167369581758976, -0.015035000629723072, -0.008081518113613129, 0.06083572655916214, -0.02929985523223877, -0.07304541766643524, 0.014642894268035889, 0.024026023223996162, 0.02480182982981205, -0.009316520765423775, -0.011571594513952732, 0.00495725404471159, -0.06010441109538078, 0.020628847181797028, 0.014211099594831467, -0.0457686223089695, 0.017233777791261673, -0.004989526234567165, 0.009032459929585457, -0.02389880083501339, 0.019080867990851402, 0.0012842713622376323, -0.0031701955012977123, 0.028740491718053818, 0.