2248, -0.005431900266557932, -0.06467466801404953, -0.042088087648153305, -0.005366606172174215, 1.8165189709745283e-34, 0.0024625384248793125, -0.00540916295722127, 0.008476090617477894, -0.13315320014953613, -0.0024287430569529533, -0.005622567608952522, 0.006054425612092018, 0.013107911683619022, 0.041439205408096313, -0.04956454038619995, -0.029757779091596603], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "4988c3e29bd876040cde30411d6248a7c1cc65bed98dabefb47c07659b622475", "content": "This chunk is located within the section discussing the effectiveness of targeted behavior interventions compared to broader approaches in schools. It emphasizes the importance of tailoring support for students with behavioral issues and the intersection with special educational needs, providing a practical example from St Mary\u2019s Catholic School.Where\u2019s the evidence?\n\u201cTargeted programmes tend to demonstrate a bigger effect on behaviour outcomes compared to whole-\nclass or whole-school programmes\u201d\nSEND and behaviour\nWhile pupils with behavioural issues might need a tailored approach, they do not necessarily have a special educational need. Similarly, children with special educational needs and disabilities will not necessarily need additional support with their behaviour. If you know that a pupil who has behavioural issues also has a special educational need, understanding best practice for supporting that particular need may help with their behaviour and thus could be a good starting point for their behaviour support.\f30\nEducation Endowment Foundation One school\u2019s approach: understanding pupils and tailoring support\nSt Mary\u2019s Catholic School in Blackpool utilises several recommendations from this report and several \u2018best bet\u2019 strategies as part of a tailored response to pupil behaviour. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 31, "split_id": 74, "split_idx_start": 62096, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "7aaf43939494456c0555daf93e52a0e0f0e14aae37fbf47b54b66499ae65c8b1", "range": [620, 642]}, {"doc_id": "822c76cdb175e66da23d2ba99ed86b616dd544ee1534e2bde4d8e637ca7f49e0", "range": [0, 274]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.057956013828516006, -0.07370328903198242, 0.006580862682312727, 0.01571730710566044, -0.018518000841140747, 0.03574173152446747, 0.042604073882102966, -0.032370880246162415, -0.06262138485908508, 0.013550903648138046, 0.05706615000963211, -0.008861030451953411, 0.010549168102443218, 0.005555564537644386, 0.03313440829515457, -0.06013590097427368, 0.01646120660007, 0.018423838540911674, -0.028515150770545006, 0.02456490881741047, 0.00266346987336874, -0.002485185395926237, -0.009192978031933308, -0.011252064257860184, 0.015152431093156338, -0.01809683069586754, 0.01589813269674778, 0.0206020325422287, 0.006689135450869799, -0.04161573573946953, 0.08113493770360947, 0.019675342366099358, -0.007573165465146303, -0.05012079328298569, 2.0028121525683673e-06, 0.05162161961197853, 0.005768768023699522, 0.002788401208817959, 0.026923825964331627, 0.002209228929132223, -0.06780735403299332, -0.010979597456753254, 0.030873380601406097, 0.062021251767873764, 0.007306897081434727, 0.06960234045982361, 0.013955841772258282, 0.042790431529283524, -0.012746354565024376, -0.019669316709041595, -0.0036971657536923885, 0.0006133521092124283, -0.026715658605098724, -0.029788333922624588, 0.08111811429262161, 0.010412310250103474, 0.00416230084374547, -0.05789943039417267, 0.02534840814769268, 0.021336998790502548, 0.011770381592214108, 0.03581446409225464, -0.046748414635658264, -0.024635162204504013, 0.010040582157671452, -0.017823483794927597, -0.040776900947093964, -0.07595982402563095, 0.017419593408703804, -0.021618278697133064, 0.07920639216899872, 0.07253894954919815, 0.