6463985424488783, 0.060605961829423904, -0.012016520835459232, -0.005777184851467609, -0.010931598022580147, -0.025863757357001305, 0.03461804986000061, -0.015108650550246239, 0.0485025979578495, 0.0760834738612175, -0.015874357894062996, -0.03682978078722954, -0.010233248583972454, 0.03512323647737503, -0.011532469652593136, 0.0025965357199311256, 0.047681212425231934, -0.030562838539481163, 0.01577075943350792, 0.011073886416852474, 0.05128820613026619, -0.022897033020853996, -0.00380116980522871, -0.003029176965355873, 0.015570327639579773, -0.023506958037614822, -0.05432877689599991, -0.030037634074687958, -0.02619345486164093, 1.968157053464382e-34, 0.005695578176528215, -0.030054623261094093, 0.0033966198097914457, -0.07833395898342133, 0.010414427146315575, -0.0005617481656372547, 0.020030606538057327, 0.011059688404202461, 0.03394129127264023, 0.007615311071276665, -0.017783837392926216], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "ac4a4f27b583de6a22a6de8205672467de106327530225821a6ef14cc5eea2ca", "content": "This chunk is situated within the document's section on \"targeted approaches to meet the needs of individuals in your school.\" It highlights the 2x10 model as a strategy for fostering positive relationships between teachers and students, emphasizing the importance of connecting with pupils on a personal level to address behavioural issues effectively.Based on similar principles to the EMR method outlined in Recommendation 1, the 2x10 model focuses on spending 2 minutes of non-\nschool-related conversation with target pupils for 10 days to try and form a relationship, establishing a human connection beyond the usual learning focus of the school. This interaction can support learning conversations further down the line and creates a supportive relationship that may help a pupil speak up about issues they have in and beyond school. Teachers are also encouraged to call home for as many pupils as possible, for positive reasons as well as when they have a concern, developing the relationship with the family around the pupil. The school\u2019s behaviour manager then looks at the \u2018need\u2019 from the information available and creates a \u2018roadmap\u2019 of intervention from the broad range available (see Table 2). This roadmap will look to strategically develop what intervention is required to target the main need. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 32, "split_id": 76, "split_idx_start": 63830, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "822c76cdb175e66da23d2ba99ed86b616dd544ee1534e2bde4d8e637ca7f49e0", "range": [1048, 1347]}, {"doc_id": "d4c7b1a73a5e53a7709233001552d0d4ee071478f437d31ddb465425ae78c638", "range": [0, 103]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04986908286809921, -0.07895133644342422, 0.009828602895140648, -0.003250467823818326, -0.012396418489515781, 0.040132343769073486, 0.03572295978665352, -0.036943744868040085, -0.02595861814916134, 0.006486142985522747, 0.044047918170690536, -0.02062750980257988, 0.008160356432199478, 0.007900330238044262, 0.02214980125427246, -0.08091982454061508, -0.01597616635262966, 0.03727967292070389, -0.04740167409181595, 0.03811531886458397, 0.0024890948552638292, 0.017211943864822388, -0.014280064031481743, 0.004016784019768238, -0.01854119263589382, -0.020851943641901016, -0.005873315967619419, 0.03205246105790138, 0.034955572336912155, -0.029435759410262108, 0.07588881254196167, 0.012488286010921001, 0.014849630184471607, -0.03737737610936165, 2.427538674965035e-06, 0.0036073937080800533, -0.02388363890349865, 0.007699212525039911, 0.01811653934419155, -0.008147369138896465, -0.01844850927591324, -0.06414545327425003, 0.052830811589956284, 0.043212853372097015, 0.005363420117646456, 0.03183971345424652, 0.006448099389672279, 0.04907407984137535, 0.03