0.03153127804398537, 0.033667877316474915, -0.010712887160480022, -0.0349346324801445, -0.08038333803415298, -0.042386338114738464, -0.004841006360948086, 1.7094275326060312e-34, -0.011870247311890125, -0.006272020284086466, 0.013119090348482132, -0.06905458867549896, -0.02555067464709282, -0.009640591219067574, 0.007039811462163925, 0.044853292405605316, 0.02943817526102066, -0.04880625382065773, -0.03884485736489296], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "9965e869b75871431a9ef78f94994bd261dbe9ddef0975adda382907f5b383ec", "content": "This chunk details the various targeted interventions implemented at St Mary\u2019s Catholic School to support students with behavioral issues. It emphasizes the importance of tailored support and outlines a range of services and programs designed to address individual needs, reinforcing the guidance on effective behavior management strategies.The intervention will typically run for 3-6 weeks depending on need.\f31Improving behaviour in schools\nInternal Learning Support Department\nLife Coach\nFamily liaison worker\nBehaviour Managment\nChaplaincy LAC co-ordinator\nExternal\nNurse\nPSP Lite\nPSP\nLink - internal\nManaged Move\nEducation welfare officer\nPart Time Timetable\nEarly Help Form L2\nLexonics\nAssessment (screening)\nTargeted Withdrawal Intervention\nEducational Psychology Involvement\nPerson-Centred Planning Approach\nKS4 Mentoring\nShared in-class support\nExam Access Arrangements\nLife Coach 1:1 Support\nAssessment of needs\nYouth mediation service (y11)\nFamily mediation - parent to child\nFamily liaison\nAttendance support\nReferral to external agency\n1:1 with pupil\nFinancial Assistance\nListening and communication\nBreaking Habits\nPositive Attitude\nManaging feelings & behaviour\nSelf Esteem\nSelf Awareness\nSocial Skills\nHandling Anger\nReintegration\nRetracking\nSkills for School\nPlanning for personal development\nResilience\nInterpersonal/ Self Management\nTeamwork\nParticipation & Exercise\nOne Page Profiles\n1 to 1\nRainbows/ Boys\u2019 group\nCouncelling\nPaid 1 to 1 Mentor\nHeadStart Referral\nFinancial Assistance\nAcademy Extra\nWomens Refuge\nYouth Therapy\nCAMHS\nFIN\nCIN\nCP\nWISH / AWAKEN\nResilience Coaches\nThe Link (Grange)\nCASHER\nAspired Futures\nYoung Carers\nNSPCC\nTable 2: Interventions at St Mary\u2019s Catholic School\nFirst stop for further reading\nhttps://educationendowmentfoundation.org.uk/tools/guidance-reports/ EEF guidance reports on: working with parents to support children\u2019s learning, teaching assistants, meta-cognition, and self-regulation.\nAngela Watson, \u2018The 2\u00d710 strategy: a miraculous solution for behavior issues?\u2019. https://thecornerstoneforteachers.com/the-2x10-strategy-a-miraculous-solution-for-behavior-issues/ In this blog, American teacher Angela Watson reflects on teachers\u2019 experiences of using the 2x10 strategy.\f32\nEducation Endowment Foundation 6\nConsistency is key\nWhile classroom-level strategies have a big impact on pupil behaviour, consistency and coherence are paramount at a whole-school level. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 32, "split_id": 78, "split_idx_start": 65081, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "d4c7b1a73a5e53a7709233001552d0d4ee071478f437d31ddb465425ae78c638", "range": [397, 466]}, {"doc_id": "98b02ac390e4c28b63f7dbeb3427dcb2ad0799155ca9a62015ce7159da6990ce", "range": [0, 191]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.032305758446455, -0.06331374496221542, 0.011965633369982243, -0.005173160694539547, -0.006768702995032072, 0.058857910335063934, 0.0178553257137537, -0.045153629034757614, -0.011477874591946602, 0.026978453621268272, 0.06731510162353516, -0.00999012216925621, -0.034962430596351624, 0.03232588246464729, -0.028545986860990524, -0.03447062894701958,