30048845801502466, -0.04674785956740379, -0.00024634547298774123, -0.014946474693715572, -0.07994673401117325, 0.04199410229921341, 0.038181327283382416, 0.022617055103182793, -0.019578732550144196, -0.03434676676988602, -0.014823666773736477, -0.029443003237247467, 0.08403120189905167, -0.034426234662532806, 0.02039184235036373, 0.04816998913884163, -0.05384053662419319, -0.022610999643802643, 0.02231689728796482, 0.032083142548799515, 0.020048584789037704, 0.01113914418965578, 0.004439323674887419, -0.04275379702448845, -0.01155797392129898, 0.005175393540412188, 0.021746231243014336, 0.019400794059038162, -0.05088502913713455, 0.015685193240642548, 0.023220036178827286, -0.015165884979069233, -0.0765383243560791, -0.02017758972942829, -0.028759917244315147, 2.372580604323761e-34, 0.00037016780697740614, -0.03626656532287598, -0.0031997046899050474, -0.09617931395769119, -0.018316686153411865, -0.0068175941705703735, -0.00583242904394865, 0.008591318503022194, 0.033357422798871994, -0.009693918749690056, -0.02097993530333042], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "0e3feb9619325267c2c45784363f63053e3e09bc932340666575ae8c40b1af93", "content": "This chunk is from the \"Consistency is key\" section of the guidance report, emphasizing the importance of evaluating and adapting behaviour policies based on the unique context of a school. It highlights that despite overall inadequate behaviour ratings, many classrooms may still have acceptable behaviour, suggesting the potential for positive practices among staff.Your school\u2019s context will affect your choices, and continuous assessment of how policies are working can ensure you deploy the most successful strategies.\nAs Figure 6 shows, even in schools where behaviour is judged by Ofsted to be inadequate overall, the behaviour in most classrooms is not inadequate. This should be treated as good news: even if behaviour is an urgent priority in your school, it is likely that on any given day, many lessons are not being disturbed by poor behaviour. It is likely you already have staff in your team who are behaviour experts and that they could share examples of what works for them with other staff.\nThe same report revealed that only a quarter of secondary and half of primary teachers agreed that the behaviour policy in their school was applied consistently by all staff. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 34, "split_id": 82, "split_idx_start": 68795, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "e79adacfe3e28c4cd1810f233d09849cfb544ee3ba158dd818c851c5e719cac9", "range": [842, 998]}, {"doc_id": "87b27a7ff740c562b9a626009775bf174a79437eb3ab93f571896acb0c474fd4", "range": [0, 175]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.057434145361185074, -0.03481419011950493, 0.007682898547500372, 0.0024947188794612885, -0.007423634175211191, 0.03424529731273651, -0.012990410439670086, 0.022569619119167328, -0.036911170929670334, 0.013900905847549438, 0.028349487110972404, -0.009189988486468792, 0.0014140722341835499, -0.002282054629176855, -0.003801218466833234, -0.04433013126254082, 0.013096359558403492, 0.018216680735349655, -0.0637243315577507, 0.020626509562134743, 0.006308810319751501, -0.010884452611207962, 0.02879605069756508, 0.010591628029942513, -0.0513869971036911, 0.004517838824540377, -0.003951282240450382, -0.03060607798397541, 0.020364273339509964, -0.020787693560123444, 0.07230480015277863, 0.0021247630938887596, 0.014109887182712555, -0.04841826111078262, 1.9986755432910286e-06, -0.006711097899824381, 0.009962019510567188, -0.008106838911771774, 0.05202467739582062, -0.015326960943639278, -0.045030221343040466, -0.042893704026937485, 0.01433117501437664, 0.03907950967550278, 0.010902853682637215, 0.06334364414215088, -0.00849729124456644, 0.021125389263033867, -0.0016