798681736, 0.03752792626619339, -0.022844277322292328, 0.016305934637784958, -0.04574831575155258, 0.027378691360354424, 0.007821595296263695, -0.057814132422208786, 0.04836558178067207, 0.016523998230695724, 0.0589282363653183, -0.017185019329190254, -0.08319873362779617, -0.004243228584527969, -0.035561297088861465, 0.06433837860822678, 0.024690885096788406, 0.023734688758850098, 0.058093756437301636, -0.012757444754242897, -0.04591449350118637, 0.03070901334285736, 0.025801358744502068, -0.01903400756418705, -0.024909822270274162, -0.006301273591816425, -0.038653939962387085, 0.014016709290444851, 0.04402029141783714, 0.05626733601093292, -0.03852539137005806, -0.009401543997228146, -0.0019051349954679608, 0.014683651737868786, 0.009992646984755993, -0.04735235869884491, 0.007833885960280895, -0.0070991176180541515, 1.9980456044552216e-34, -0.0010031865676864982, -0.056319113820791245, 0.020811812952160835, -0.09630610793828964, -0.00807213969528675, 0.015034020878374577, 0.03836949169635773, 0.007068421225994825, 0.017741680145263672, 0.013884305022656918, -0.027560438960790634], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "031531b4ee691cb9ad0ced833b6a9e062485f8cbf6e60b55e21e6125750e986d", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing the importance of consistency in behavior policies within schools, particularly addressing the implementation of zero tolerance behavior policies. It provides insights into the mixed views on these policies, highlighting both advocacy and criticism from educational leaders and policymakers regarding their impact on student outcomes and exclusions.This includes staff training, effective use of consequences, data monitoring, staff and student surveys and maintaining standards.\u201d Tom Bennett, 2017\n\u201cOnly a quarter of secondary and half of primary teachers agreed that the behaviour policy in their school was applied consistently.\u201d\f33Improving behaviour in schools\nZero tolerance behaviour policies, sometimes described as \u201cno excuses\u201d, aim to create a strict and clear whole-\nschool approach to discipline. Typically, under such policies, pupils will automatically receive detentions for a range of misbehaviours such as being late, forgetting homework or using rude language. Other more serious conduct, such as bringing a weapon to school, may result in exclusion \u2013 without exception.\nAdvocates of zero tolerance approaches include some successful leaders within the charter school movement in the United States, who regard zero tolerance approaches as key contributors to improving the outcomes of pupils in areas of high disadvantage. 41 On the other hand, some have criticised the use of zero tolerance, with MPs on the Education Select Committee in England expressing concern that such policies may be linked unnecessary exclusions. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 34, "split_id": 84, "split_idx_start": 70033, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "87b27a7ff740c562b9a626009775bf174a79437eb3ab93f571896acb0c474fd4", "range": [597, 1057]}, {"doc_id": "0da40085ea0cc402b335ce7e691175b8f0a249eb0de74a6e6d9aa99522fc2ac0", "range": [0, 200]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.037772390991449356, -0.04153944551944733, 0.015686441212892532, -0.01210070215165615, -0.014355223625898361, 0.0017623278545215726, 0.03800946846604347, -0.004136248491704464, 0.0008988495101220906, -0.007826450280845165, 0.07090003043413162, 0.0011948506580665708, -0.02366059646010399, -0.010355908423662186, 0.008298013359308243, -0.03299494460225105, -0.030010679736733437, 0.003166990587487817, -0.03680718317627907, 0.02068198285996914, 0.019448410719633102, -0.005729475524276495, -0.0016147354617714882, 0.030812302604317665, -0.05157146230340004, -0.024813324213027954, -0.0115