 0.04607056826353073, 0.01244262233376503, 0.027746865525841713, 0.024534685537219048, 0.03483511134982109, 0.01519434992223978, 0.017649540677666664, -0.07455912977457047, 0.001011934713460505, 0.00880764052271843, -0.017772171646356583, 0.03484879434108734, 0.0014563377480953932, 0.026908420026302338, -0.03131750971078873, 0.016029227524995804, 0.01069855410605669, -0.06906705349683762, 0.03931543976068497, 0.020621057599782944, 0.06435482949018478, -0.010882521979510784, -0.0667824074625969, 0.008067326620221138, -0.008300713263452053, 0.08103872835636139, 0.026336872950196266, 0.03239884600043297, 0.08408960700035095, -0.03469589725136757, -0.01785976253449917, 0.037127744406461716, 0.03792190924286842, -0.017660560086369514, -0.020953906700015068, 0.018147222697734833, -0.046689145267009735, 0.015737384557724, 0.04454359784722328, 0.03450274094939232, -0.04277058690786362, -0.027379289269447327, -0.007371921092271805, 0.025042301043868065, -0.007213774602860212, -0.06709535419940948, -0.03918297961354256, -0.01501060463488102, 1.938355746194893e-34, 0.01331611629575491, -0.05577507242560387, 0.008876041509211063, -0.09860144555568695, 0.0003072974504902959, 0.005048958584666252, 0.02691659890115261, 0.0037527536042034626, 0.024096103385090828, -0.0023614303208887577, -0.01289757527410984], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "cc8cfc989400d3587be4f2090a7eb13683625acd0c3df4ce6f636a1d1be09e5e", "content": "This chunk discusses the effectiveness of combining teacher training in classroom management with a consistent school-wide approach, particularly in the context of zero tolerance or alternative strategies for behavior management. It falls within the document's section that evaluates various behavior intervention approaches and the need for tailored methods to support individual pupil needs effectively.For example, providing training for teachers in classroom management and having a consistent approach across the school that can be adapted for some pupils with specific needs are likely to improve behaviour within zero tolerance or alternative approaches.\nBox 8: Zero tolerance / no excuses\nFigure 6: Number of behaviour judgements from lessons in two secondary and two primary school inspections in 2014 where \u2018behaviour and safety was judged to be inadequate overall. (From \u2018Below the Radar\u2019 )39\nGoodOutstanding\nNumber of lessons\nSecondary school\ncase study A (38)\nNumber of lessons observed in parentheses\nNo lessons were judged outstanding for behaviour in either of the primary school case studies\nNumber of behaviour judgements from lessons in two secondary and two primary schools inspections in 2014 where \u2018behaviour and saftey was judged to be inadequate overall.\nFrom \u2018Below the Radar\u2019\nSecondary school\ncase study B (26)\nPrimary school\ncase study A (11)\nSource: Ofsted Inspection\nPrimary school\ncase study B (18)\nRequires improvement Inadequate\f34\nEducation Endowment Foundation Consider combinations of strategies that are more powerful together\nWhen deciding which behaviour approaches to adopt as part of your school\u2019s behaviour strategy, it may be helpful to consider combining two intervention approaches which are supported by evidence: \u2022 tailor approaches to individual pupils, focus on improving relationships, and include intensive teacher training (over 20 hours); and\n\u2022 focus on academic issues, teaching coping and resilience skills (separate from any efforts to improve relationships).\nAs shown in Figure 7 , tailoring approaches to individuals and focusing on building relationships can be effective, but this needs to occur with an appropriate amount of teacher training. An alternative is to focus on academic issues and teaching learning behaviours (described in Recommendation 2), but not focus on relationships. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 35, "split_id": 86, "split_idx_start": 71609, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0da40085ea0cc402b335ce7e691175b8f0a249eb0de74a6e6d9aa99522fc2ac0", "range": [584, 841]}, {"doc_id": "3ba4b7bfc768de0f01e7a65d86e0babe6eee4e2c010a6403e48444317696632a", "range": [0, 144]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0565640926361084, -0.06347398459911346, 0.02207757532596588, 0.018206534907221794, -0.0008402012172155082, 0.023331619799137115, 0.051498863846063614, 0.014989507384598255, -0.054201893508434296, -0.0009684725082479417, 0.021472861990332603, -0.012568159028887749, -0.021603461354970932, 0.0014680607710033655, 0.03850166127085686, -0.0839971974492073, -0.02099735289812088, 0.014809499494731426, -0.087822325527668, 0.050784576684236526, 0.021608291193842888, -0.025406038388609886, -0.004410432185977697, -0.009934862144291401, -0.05853080749511719, -0.009294236078858376, -0.02091904915869236, 0.0010073648300021887, 0.02976241149008274, -0.042286764830350876, 0.07750677317380905, 0.022629782557487488, 0.018327996134757996, -0.01983547769486904, 2.1671023660019273e-06, 0.032640423625707626, -0.008758734911680222, -0.025339074432849884, 0.04141033813357353, -0.004705070983618498, -0.0467010997235775, -0.06086939200758934, 0.031140631064772606, 0.05697766691446304, 0.001801173435524106, 0.034023795276880264, -0.0025475621223449707, 0.04755750671029091, 0.01451911125332117, -0.034151166677474976, 0.005563426297158003, -0.0013113879831507802, -0.02349623292684555, -0.020627576857805252, 0.036584798246622086, -0.03569639474153519, 0.010159358382225037, -0.006881132256239653, 0.019692396745085716, -0.03504427522420883, -0.04020913317799568, -0.006862159818410873, -0.008573099039494991, -0.06649237871170044, 0.017874373123049736, -0.011336426250636578, -0.019257519394159317, -0.042661864310503006, 0.007603194564580917, -0.0019187575671821833, 0.056630801409482956,