31, -0.060289569199085236, -0.043350230902433395, -0.008521377108991146, 2.29530585567036e-34, 0.007477767765522003, -0.040474891662597656, -0.004899267572909594, -0.10558313131332397, -0.002326042391359806, 0.01019491720944643, 0.004535957705229521, 0.011707705445587635, -0.0052797324024140835, -0.022259509190917015, -0.02443276159465313], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "206f3e8115420aaee0a9f94460dc1b7bf7994ebb5e3af4d783603570ac105e57", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing the importance of careful implementation of behaviour policies within schools. It emphasizes the need for a comprehensive approach that includes consultation, feedback, and considerations of various elements that contribute to a positive school environment, as outlined in the whole-school approach for wellbeing interventions.\u201cEven relatively simple changes are likely to benefit from careful implementation, wide consultation and iterative feedback.\u201d\f36\nEducation Endowment Foundation An ethos and environment that promotes respect and values adversity\nCurriculum teaching and learning to promote resilience and support social and emotional learning\nLeadership and management\nthat supports and champions efforts to promote emotional health and wellbeing\nEnabling student voice to influence decisions\nStaff development to support their own wellbeing and that of students\nIdentifying need and monitoring impact of interventions\nWorking with parents/carers\nTargeted support\nand appropriate referral\nFigure 8: Elements of a whole-school approach for wellbeing interventions (PHE 2015) 44\nEnhance the effects of universal, whole-school approaches by considering how these interact with targeted approaches you employ.\nPublic Health England provides a model of elements of a whole-school approach for wellbeing interventions (Figure 8) which may be of relevance in considering whole-school approaches to behaviour. Each element needs considering by school leadership. It may be helpful to discuss as a leadership team: \u2022 Which elements is our school performing strongly in?\n\u2022 Which elements do we need to work on?\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 37, "split_id": 91, "split_idx_start": 76488, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "140bf63e07c64e0b08eed8f1d7232e612529b4601eabbab0ba731afc60dc6157", "range": [754, 1642]}, {"doc_id": "1c5a1599c6c776659922898856dc3fcd025e8ae592d11088f8ed5f78c76a5042", "range": [0, 40]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06784670054912567, -0.07236914336681366, 0.009893828071653843, -0.008079544641077518, -0.0013874610885977745, 0.034315075725317, 0.00022667022130917758, -0.0023909653536975384, 0.02459975704550743, 0.008415333926677704, 0.0615047849714756, 0.008694769814610481, -0.025140555575489998, 0.008510762825608253, 0.013809368014335632, -0.09069153666496277, -0.007667382713407278, 0.022821106016635895, -0.046595364809036255, 0.03219999372959137, 0.007540554273873568, -0.0077073099091649055, 0.01818852685391903, -0.02472977712750435, -0.006272729951888323, -0.011996590532362461, 0.007466774433851242, 0.0449165403842926, 0.03788147494196892, -0.02713606134057045, 0.0734141394495964, 0.017091017216444016, -0.03248368203639984, -0.0634077712893486, 2.213126208516769e-06, 0.040595892816782, 0.0019310468342155218, -0.00459167268127203, 0.03338686004281044, 0.0045525492168962955, 0.009550959803164005, -0.04243620112538338, 0.009558229707181454, 0.04939925670623779, 0.026128506287932396, 0.034869253635406494, 0.009984053671360016, 0.02397361770272255, 0.04430251196026802, -0.008876297622919083, -0.006164941005408764, -0.02219020016491413, -0.06011689081788063, -0.02770952880382538, 0.04251670092344284, 0.016737181693315506, 0.01395909022539854, -0.03390400484204292, 0.0245