areas for improvement. It highlights the practical application of positive reinforcement through the 'Headteacher Star' stickers initiative implemented by Headteacher Steve Wheeldon.\u2022 Which elements do we need to work on?\n\u2022 Are there any elements where we are unsure of our performance? What might we need to do to have enough information on how we are performing?\f37Improving behaviour in schools\nHeadteacher Steve Wheeldon gives out \u2018Headteacher Star\u2019 stickers every Friday. Steve visits all classrooms and asks each teacher and teaching assistant to publicly select a child for praise. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 38, "split_id": 92, "split_idx_start": 77731, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "206f3e8115420aaee0a9f94460dc1b7bf7994ebb5e3af4d783603570ac105e57", "range": [1243, 1283]}, {"doc_id": "4daeb9754c6e26f95e4c413cac2ce26e1188b9935a45a6a8f107c73d06944486", "range": [0, 112]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06605953723192215, -0.05325775593519211, 8.154094393830746e-05, 0.003808700479567051, 0.00941142626106739, 0.021829109638929367, -0.03476749733090401, 0.003560530487447977, -0.018677260726690292, 0.05074675381183624, 0.05746128410100937, 0.0259692445397377, -0.014057880267500877, 0.019259491935372353, 0.019229523837566376, -0.08996240049600601, -0.002229308243840933, -0.013425891287624836, -0.010796954855322838, 0.02587241679430008, 0.00803670659661293, -0.006508863065391779, -0.001466021523810923, -0.01130598597228527, -0.07637476921081543, -0.018405117094516754, 0.02963997982442379, -0.0029035857878625393, 0.06187088042497635, -0.0651121437549591, 0.037206728011369705, 0.026191024109721184, -0.015348583459854126, 0.019642213359475136, 2.1652474515576614e-06, 0.040674250572919846, 0.03003055043518