s research findings from the Centre for Economic Performance regarding the effects of mobile phone bans on pupils' exam performance, especially among those with lower attainment.Many schools are limiting mobile phone use to improve behaviour and refocus pupils on their learning \u2013 indeed, mobile phones will shortly be banned in all schools in France. But what does the evidence say? In 2015, the Centre for Economic Performance published a paper investigating the effects of mobile phone bans in schools. The research team surveyed schools in four cities in England on their mobile phone usage and compared this with their national test data. They found that pupils performed better in high-stakes exams following a mobile phone ban within a school, with improvements particularly seen from the lowest-attaining pupils, as long as pupils were compliant with the ban. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 40, "split_id": 94, "split_idx_start": 79209, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "4daeb9754c6e26f95e4c413cac2ce26e1188b9935a45a6a8f107c73d06944486", "range": [1183, 1357]}, {"doc_id": "af51fc67447b74ce2f0e1fe5a8602e55178db353c5f859f5612f2bfa946474a3", "range": [0, 224]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.014864559285342693, -0.038047417998313904, -0.036960188299417496, -0.055774152278900146, 0.021979164332151413, 0.026860689744353294, 0.10837379842996597, -0.031270984560251236, -0.019675839692354202, -0.042050186544656754, 0.04147862643003464, 0.013285750523209572, -0.008481480181217194, -0.07394648343324661, 0.023424798622727394, 0.009330863133072853, 0.018487457185983658, -0.001638917252421379, -0.04858686774969101, 0.03220142424106598, -0.010258902795612812, 0.009837090969085693, 0.03685324639081955, 0.03642531856894493, 0.0009590833797119