2022491069510579, -0.013885795138776302, -0.08831531554460526, -0.015709545463323593, 0.023321541026234627, 0.05157602205872536, 0.08321882039308548, -0.01464248076081276, -0.07370276749134064, -0.026645975187420845, 0.011537952348589897, 0.0970434620976448, 0.03706960752606392, 0.007458129897713661, 0.029824253171682358, -0.045700956135988235, 0.010016996413469315, -0.010183046571910381, 0.030359813943505287, -0.0328587107360363, -0.037806324660778046, 0.008690242655575275, -0.002657848410308361, 0.0117460573092103, 0.01575198955833912, 0.030794881284236908, 0.01482902280986309, 0.0231227558106184, -0.06387665122747421, 0.01465042494237423, 0.05606700852513313, -0.025955352932214737, 0.017868952825665474, 0.0011772760190069675, 1.4884701809062023e-34, -0.008401465602219105, 0.0036669252440333366, 0.031714629381895065, -0.06710561364889145, 0.005727499723434448, -0.016877656802535057, 0.030903726816177368, -0.0310501791536808, 0.049165792763233185, -0.0035546489525586367, -0.004036795347929001], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "4c8c0d254888f57e9830f77540b35f7b4b67ad00c52c17d047dc036234ac7df6", "content": "This chunk discusses the implications of implementing a mobile phone ban in schools as part of broader behavioral policies. It highlights that the success of such a ban depends on careful implementation and the overall context within which it is introduced, linking it to the document's focus on effective behavior management strategies in schools.Secondly, high compliance with a mobile phone ban implies a well-implemented policy. It may be the way the policy was implemented, or indeed other policies implemented at the same time, which caused the change, as a mobile phone ban is often part of wider changes. Ultimately, school leaders need to make decisions based on their context, but careful implementation of any change is likely to affect how it is received by pupils and thus how effective it is at changing behaviour and attainment outcomes.\nBox 8: Mobile phone usage\f39Improving behaviour in schools\nFirst stop for further reading\nPutting Evidence to Work - A School\u2019s Guide to Implementation https://eef.li/implementation/ The EEF guidance report on implementation is a key document for school leaders implementing any strategic change. Valdebenito, Eisner, Farrington, Ttofi, and Sutherland (2018), \u2018School-based interventions for reducing disciplinary school exclusion: a systematic review\u2019, Campbell Systematic Reviews https://campbellcollaboration.org/library/reducing-school-exclusion-school-based-interventions.html\nEdward Timpson (2019), \u2018Timpson review of school exclusion\u2019 , Department for Education https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/799979/Timpson_review_of_\nschool_exclusion.pdf This guidance report focuses on approaches to reduce behaviour incidents and support pupils to behave well. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 40, "split_id": 96, "split_idx_start": 80141, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "af51fc67447b74ce2f0e1fe5a8602e55178db353c5f859f5612f2bfa946474a3", "range": [466, 551]}, {"doc_id": "eb10a44af5895180850cd32344ee029f81e290561e83a821f098f902ea80879b", "range": [0, 623]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.05769465118646622, -0.044045187532901764, -0.002933541312813759, -0.08655201643705368, 0.03551047667860985, 0.012198730371892452, 0.054997146129608154, -0.014142432250082493, 0.0019277450628578663, -0.025015762075781822, 0.04067780822515488, 0.0013614182826131582, -0.029095062986016273, -0.013130896724760532, 0.0042198128066957, -0.02897578477859497, -0.032783351838588715, -0.0019033800344914198, -0.05236993357539177, 0.03246208280324936, 0.022405004128813744, 0.019238844513893127, 0.06937