6640525460243, 0.036952123045921326, -0.0035981282126158476, 0.004333256743848324, -0.038721513003110886, 0.0381208099424839, 0.017422828823328018, -0.06464654207229614, -0.001600813353434205, 0.01882876455783844, 1.5376276557009115e-34, 0.004260514862835407, -0.012146970257163048, 0.031255900859832764, -0.0742267519235611, -0.008534426800906658, -0.014356492087244987, 0.012995460070669651, -0.04299323260784149, 0.054292019456624985, -0.03757817670702934, 0.027040602639317513], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "eb10a44af5895180850cd32344ee029f81e290561e83a821f098f902ea80879b", "content": "This chunk is situated within the \"References\" section of the guidance report, highlighting systematic reviews and reports related to reducing school exclusions and managing behavior incidents. It emphasizes the need for school leaders to consider appropriate responses to serious misbehavior and references key studies that inform effective intervention strategies.Valdebenito, Eisner, Farrington, Ttofi, and Sutherland (2018), \u2018School-based interventions for reducing disciplinary school exclusion: a systematic review\u2019, Campbell Systematic Reviews https://campbellcollaboration.org/library/reducing-school-exclusion-school-based-interventions.html\nEdward Timpson (2019), \u2018Timpson review of school exclusion\u2019 , Department for Education https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/799979/Timpson_review_of_\nschool_exclusion.pdf This guidance report focuses on approaches to reduce behaviour incidents and support pupils to behave well. School leaders also need to make difficult decisions regarding consequences when serious misbehaviour occurs. The texts above provide support with considering an appropriate response. Most exclusions, whether fixed-term or permanent, are for behaviour-based reasons. The Campbell systematic review (2018) on exclusions exposes the differential rates at which children and young people aged 4-18 from different backgrounds are excluded from schools and reviews evidence for various interventions schools may use to reduce their exclusion rates. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 41, "split_id": 97, "split_idx_start": 80943, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "4c8c0d254888f57e9830f77540b35f7b4b67ad00c52c17d047dc036234ac7df6", "range": [802, 1425]}, {"doc_id": "b34af5e70b978372f22cbe4a8be762dfb8fc52b8292e4ede9ad288b3a7b58479", "range": [0, 277]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.07360439002513885, -0.08649276942014694, 0.008334232494235039, -0.01911451481282711, -0.0045052338391542435, 0.037377871572971344, 0.0639808252453804, -0.026535984128713608, 0.004587365314364433, -0.022146763280034065, 0.04548218846321106, -0.010105215013027191, 0.018499374389648438, -0.015787174925208092, 0.015228573232889175, -0.03329828754067421, 0.029752129688858986, 0.015316025353968143, -0.02865772321820259, 0.007921464741230011, -0.02552289143204689, 0.012754876166582108, -0.0017873769393190742, 0.03198612481355667, 0.011615864001214504, -0.0050916182808578014, 0.02596764639019966, 0.001678341068327427, 0.020662549883127213, -0.030052093788981438, 0.08116395771503448, 0.003869155654683709, -0.018666690215468407, -0.02735172025859356, 2.2121066649560817e-06, 0.00922608096152544, 0.01507752574980259, 0.017596742138266563, 0.03766155242919922, -0.01665387488901615, -0.053575173020362854, -0.0026549086906015873, 0.02045140229165554, 0.04683050885796547, 0.012139668688178062, 0.005187501665204763, 0.022611314430832863, 0.0096057103946805, 0.0016167189460247755, -0.03264549747109413, -0.0017173804808408022, -0.03399650380015373, -0.009854624047875404, -0.020528705790638924, 0.08407922834157944, 0.013420996256172657, 0.012736653909087181, -0.004085