004, -0.041072212159633636, 0.05465799570083618, -0.023318519815802574, 0.005573131609708071, -0.044718991965055466, -0.0006994158611632884, -0.007082716561853886, -0.01864960789680481, -0.02043755352497101, 0.01916148141026497, 0.06995541602373123, -0.03882456198334694, -0.03335701674222946, 0.012723845429718494, -0.012068657204508781, 0.07102089375257492, 0.016942864283919334, 0.030312448740005493, 0.053421031683683395, -0.04360847547650337, -0.026930877938866615, 0.007016435731202364, 0.0753972977399826, -0.012527448125183582, -0.03713579848408699, 0.031223108991980553, -0.04943401739001274, 0.03183606639504433, -0.014243179000914097, -0.00303747970610857, -0.018750252202153206, -0.010147912427783012, -0.014163658954203129, 0.01889139413833618, 0.028229089453816414, -0.04397951066493988, 0.0022269433829933405, 0.012767348438501358, 1.6396031681671873e-34, 0.022578313946723938, 0.004978986456990242, 0.0045573473908007145, -0.07191553711891174, 0.00716513441875577, -0.018060309812426567, 0.01330177579075098, -0.029371438547968864, 0.04151202365756035, -0.017377067357301712, 0.03324565663933754], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "09bd67ae5d0bb74499b0eb2322b4596af6d79242f21a046d8690a7f052204d38", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Implementation\" section of the guidance report, discussing the effectiveness of whole-school behaviour interventions compared to classroom-based approaches. It emphasizes how well-structured whole-school policies can enhance student outcomes over time, particularly when tailored to support individual students with consistent behaviour challenges.This may provide a useful springboard for discussion for school stakeholders contemplating a change in policy.\nAmong behaviour interventions, those at whole-school level more consistently improve attainment outcomes. The effects of whole-school approaches on behaviour and learning outcomes tend to be smaller and take longer to emerge than in classroom-based approaches.45 This is to be expected, particularly given the difference in the level of disruption between classrooms in most schools: improving behaviour across the school may not have much of an effect on the lessons where behaviour was already good, but that does not mean the policy is not working. The effect of a whole-school approach can be enhanced when deployed in combination with targeted additions and modifications for pupils who consistently struggle to meet the standard set by the approach.46\nWhere\u2019s the evidence?\f40\nEducation Endowment Foundation REFERENCES\n1. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 41, "split_id": 99, "split_idx_start": 83026, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b34af5e70b978372f22cbe4a8be762dfb8fc52b8292e4ede9ad288b3a7b58479", "range": [1193, 1304]}, {"doc_id": "36e2276c7f137754e1874a61de767d16960b9488011d360cedc21c9c80705dac", "range": [0, 48]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06144414469599724, -0.038663797080516815, 0.011553335003554821, -0.022996842861175537, -0.01700165495276451, 0.013901284895837307, 0.0441901758313179, 0.009013434872031212, -0.02159755304455757, 0.01151684857904911, 0.06580863147974014, 0.01457067858427763, -0.034003376960754395, 0.026664171367883682, 0.027737511321902275, -0.0644925981760025, 0.006586785428225994, 0.018242593854665756, -0.04838265851140022, 0.007859375327825546, -0.008190096355974674, -0.03416815027594566, -0.01995972730219364, 0.011076593771576881, -0.012477686628699303, -0.015011844225227833, 0.0025348723866045475, 0.02159104496240616, -0.0035108376760035753, -0.032380685210227966, 0.09806279838085175, 0.03961674124002457, 0.0015323713887482882, -0.0301273912191391, 2.3270267774933018e-06, 0.027862606570124626, -0.009511983953416348, -0.002187195932492614, 0.045500729233026505, 0.029674