894103020429611, -0.010930703952908516, 0.006751640699803829, 0.02838139794766903, 0.011925792321562767, 0.011518402025103569, 0.011471649631857872, -0.038491882383823395], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "568ee2fbe74be6df79a713a6147fb6213ae7713b9615177bf6a5a43b5942af62", "content": "This chunk is part of the guidance on improving behaviour in schools, specifically focusing on the implementation of a behaviour policy. It emphasizes the importance of collaborative expectation setting between staff and pupils, regular communication of behaviour standards, and leadership training to reinforce effective school culture.Collaborative expectation setting\n\u2022 Refresh behaviour policy in collaboration with pupils and staff. Launch \u2018Expectations\u2019 and provide clarity to all pupils about the standards expected. \u2022 Half termly assemblies promoting ethos and behaviour expectations.\n\u2022 Staff briefing to have daily reminders about expectations (over-communicate).\nTraining\nLeadership:\n\u2022 Use the \u2018Creating a Culture\u2019 paper from Tom Bennett to re-establish the basics for how a leader should operate.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 49, "split_id": 149, "split_idx_start": 104369, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "711d0d9b30a51dbcb7d53d81a8120a2009f8dcab1c2837c62598292f72471aa7", "range": [261, 362]}, {"doc_id": "1f7d3326c4b557d0e3f4d963460022e5e9d7c885a3e3bb15c8af1fb28e8e7eb8", "range": [0, 135]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0687117651104927, -0.04436678811907768, 0.0079488605260849, 0.009981479495763779, 0.01135640125721693, 0.015064531937241554, -0.038528021425008774, -0.018230296671390533, -0.0036221116315573454, 0.03896814212203026, 0.059280816465616226, -0.009385133162140846, -0.0299157835543155