d on improving behavior in schools. It outlines the expectations for new staff training and the impact of staff feedback on school leadership, as well as the short-term goal of ensuring pupils understand the school's behavior rules.\u2022 All new staff complete induction programme. Any new staff to post holder positions also attend additional coaching/training. \u2022 Staff opinion on SLT (via staff voice) starts to make significant improvement.\nImplementation Outcomes (How Well?)\nShort term (3 months):\n\u2022 Pupils understand the school rules and the behaviour expected of them.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 49, "split_id": 159, "split_idx_start": 108128, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "2d66390a9e1374d50b2c00b1cb0ae85649f1ed8c6cfdb4e7631b319d5b1cf088", "range": [358, 404]}, {"doc_id": "bf707b0c157ed88f7cc86b7318fe381e7ba9bb2df4cacc1c2ed039b52c0f8fcd", "range": [0, 96]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.057731423527002335, -0.08806520700454712, 0.019709616899490356, -0.008974792435765266, -0.00473643047735095, 0.00634720828384161, -0.0289244893938303, 0.016536224633455276, -0.01757238432765007, -0.01874624937772751, 0.04764978587627411, 0.013864765875041485, -0.014362314715981483, 0.0028505504596978426, 0.018415411934256554, -0.07269008457660675, 0.030318422242999077, 0.026546159759163857, -0.09879246354103088, -0.0014222998870536685, -0.001171229057945311, -0.007014364469796419, 0.00023577392857987434, 0.0005820929072797298, -0.0469767190515995, -0.011425061151385307, -0.03450772538781166, 0.0345551073551178, -0.0074911536648869514, -0.03719143196940422, 0.07742726802825928, 0.02972210757434368, 0.019791962578892708, -0.04142541065812111, 1.917258032335667e-06, 0.006758307572454214, 0.0030343516264110804, -0.015594681