0.05339653789997101, 0.021949373185634613, -0.014625915326178074, 0.020753463730216026, -0.025004440918564796, 0.038537006825208664, 0.014316349290311337, -0.04893156513571739], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "bf707b0c157ed88f7cc86b7318fe381e7ba9bb2df4cacc1c2ed039b52c0f8fcd", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Implementation Activities\" section in the guidance report on improving behavior in schools. It outlines short-term and medium-term goals for behavior management, emphasizing the understanding of rules, support for high-needs pupils, and the resolution of behavioral incidents within departments to foster a positive school environment.Short term (3 months):\n\u2022 Pupils understand the school rules and the behaviour expected of them.\n\u2022 There are fewer incidents of pupils challenging a staff member on their response to a behaviour incident.\nMedium term (6 months):\n\u2022 Pupils who are classed as \u2018high needs\u2019 report that they feel supported when asked by behaviour leader or pastoral lead.\n\u2022 More behaviour incidents are resolved within departments, without pupils being sent to SLT.\n\u2022 Fewer students involved in serious behavioural incidents. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Improving_behaviour_in_schools_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/18VgDE6jXP5eN_4w_IPbsUVu8tW-V4ep2", "source_id": "7a1d3f44ce494b71f1d9e0fe5b7517c578d4c867369077d76a9ccd359cf1603d", "page_number": 49, "split_id": 160, "split_idx_start": 108372, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "cbe7bf537f7dfa9e0fc32198a20f8a9c0a72e4eaf29f4abb9c5868c1cddf3460", "range": [244, 340]}, {"doc_id": "49aaaf2d9ac709023cd79cc7331b50b0ef0e7dda66fd22d1e1af18d2c970f292", "range": [0, 60]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0694066509604454, -0.11026281863451004, 0.015291016548871994, 0.008390418253839016, -0.005353508051484823, 0.04436396807432175, 0.007493746001273394, -0.005097059532999992, -0.04236359894275665, 0.013638769276440144, 0.08