84046078, -0.008628211915493011, -4.444571095518768e-05, 0.009745090268552303, -0.05873933434486389, -0.028478479012846947, -0.001457952312193811, 1.8924571687757202e-34, 0.014459441415965557, -0.03161613270640373, -0.014086872339248657, -0.07184014469385147, 0.018466763198375702, -0.01741597428917885, -0.05041912943124771, 0.02676180750131607, 0.03302270546555519, 0.024987630546092987, 0.009349692612886429], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "47b6f137b8fed9db72fe0c71469f274fb9c4e3da824e469e6526c161b4eabc97", "content": "This chunk is situated in the \"Introduction\" section of the guidance report, where it outlines the efforts made by the Education Endowment Foundation (EEF) and Early Intervention Foundation (EIF) to gather evidence regarding current practices in primary schools related to social and emotional learning (SEL) through a survey.In addition to the evidence review, the EEF and EIF commissioned a survey of what primary schools in England are currently doing to support children\u2019s social and emotional development. This information is used to provide context for the recommendations, and to identify where there are gaps between current practice and the evidence. More information about the report and how it was produced is provided at the end of this guidance report. Some key references are included for those wishing to explore the subject in more depth. The full evidence review and survey will be published separately, and will contain more comprehensive methods and reference sections.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 5, "split_id": 8, "split_idx_start": 6656, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "aa8503f26edbcdd4c83a31ac76da58b14fc483f8d0b98c439fda07b833e7faf5", "range": [761, 946]}, {"doc_id": "a261fb5b69351155b2fdc392e58b06