-0.014845222234725952, 0.028016788884997368, -0.009996187873184681, -0.01462202612310648, -0.005700614303350449, -0.018762467429041862, 0.07685454189777374, 0.01847061514854431, 0.0869605541229248, -0.019775476306676865, -0.021373864263296127, -0.03967789560556412, -0.03206817805767059, 0.020556829869747162, -0.029885131865739822, 0.03282620385289192, 0.048367198556661606, -0.04233606904745102, -0.0011737281456589699, -0.026614269241690636, 0.042484916746616364, 0.005203563719987869, 0.011269869282841682, 0.00848629791289568, -0.09566324949264526, 0.02649766579270363, 0.018712548539042473, 0.0609036348760128, -0.024522142484784126, 0.046162329614162445, -0.008093695156276226, 0.008033262565732002, 0.015081778168678284, -0.04018315300345421, -0.039785195142030716, 0.003768613561987877, 1.95462968488031e-34, 0.001986216753721237, -0.03440400958061218, -0.00825035572052002, -0.09811913967132568, -0.01582525297999382, -0.011242374777793884, -0.006270261947065592, 0.025552434846758842, 0.011583494953811169, 0.003298720344901085, -0.011587521992623806], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "647a4c3d47417f441119b9400020833b586745729a25fd3d74f337eab441c31e", "content": "This chunk defines Social and Emotional Learning (SEL) and outlines its significance in primary education, emphasizing the skills involved such as self-awareness, self-management, social awareness, relationship skills, and responsible decision-making. It situates SEL within a broader context of related concepts and introduces the core competencies that are essential for children's emotional and social development, as discussed in the guidance report.Social and Emotional Learning refers to the process through which children learn to understand and manage emotions, set and achieve positive goals, feel and show empathy for others, establish and maintain positive relationships, and make responsible decisions.1 There are a range of other terms that schools use that overlap with SEL (though have different emphases), including: supporting children\u2019s mental health and wellbeing; character education; development of children\u2019s resilience; bullying prevention; life skills; behaviour management; personal development; and Spiritual, Moral, Social and Cultural Development.\nThroughout this report we refer to \u2018SEL \u2019, as defined by the Collaborative for Academic, Social, and Emotional Learning (CASEL), because this definition is widely used internationally. It consists of five core competencies (see Table 1).2 These are skills that have been linked to a range of positive outcomes, 3 as explained in more detail in the section below.\nTable 1: Core Skills at the heart of SEL\nSchool climate, Policies and Practices\nFamily and Community Partnerships\nClassroom Curriculum and Instruction\nSocial, Emotional and Academic Learning\nSelf-\nAwareness\nSelf-Awareness\nSelf-\nManagement\nRelationship Skills\nResponsible Decision Making\nSocial Awareness\nThe ability to accurately recognise one\u2019s own emotions, thoughts and values and how they influence behaviour. The ability to accurately assess one\u2019s strengths and limitations with a well-grounded sense of confidence and optimism.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 6, "split_id": 13, "split_idx_start": 9685, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "e8394b0da5eb83234ae677a76c6b10eeeb4854708276f05a6cd6fdc3ca7b3b34", "range": [583, 1205]}, {"doc_id": "54dee5d513303364c422545a7eb3ab30dc7706ca26c956baac82ba9d66cf973c", "range": [0, 120]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03646666929125786, -0.08099545538425446, 0.011219413951039314, 0.002916693687438965, 0.017126519232988358, 0.07054994255304337, 0.01691253110766411, -0.07263616472482681, 0.044288571923971176, 0.016180075705051422, -0.00719925342127680