00 studies show that on average SEL has a positive impact on academic attainment, equivalent to 4 additional months\u2019 progress.\nSocial and emotional learning\nModerate impact for moderate cost, based on extensive evidence +4\f6\nEducation Endowment Foundation INTRODUCTION\nHow does SEL relate to mental health?\nSocial and emotional skills are protective factors for mental health. They equip children with the tools and resources to address mental health challenges that interfere with life, learning and well-\nbeing (for example, difficulty regulating emotions, concentrating, and interacting with peers). 13 Indeed, recent research has shown that SEL skills at age nine predicted Key Stage 2 test scores at age 11 (controlling for prior attainment), via their influence on mental health difficulties in the interim. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 7, "split_id": 20, "split_idx_start": 16984, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "2b471aae9f754986ac899922b6a9c7e0d35d2bec37844a96292f84fc9801f87c", "range": [2258, 2428]}, {"doc_id": "c4440b887f62ed74924adf977654b952116318f5263fba50ea53fbd4e1aca114", "range": [0, 211]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.015927249565720558, -0.055576350539922714, -0.005453519988805056, -0.005339386407285929, -0.0025258513633161783, 0.06777720898389816, 0.051732975989580154, -0.022138889878988266, 0.05447220802307129, -0.011630594730377197, 0.008486620150506496, 0.03717626631259918, 0.006122616585344076, -0.017109215259552002, 0.02593211457133293, -0.038589123636484146, -0.007050770800560713, 0.023899078369140625, 0.028843360021710396, 0.011222866363823414, -0.020322732627391815, 0.0022078966721892357, -0.0073730917647480965, -0.025048598647117615, 0.011129225604236126, -0.0032923046965152025, 0.004104082938283682,