es quality over quantity in teaching practices.Start early and think long term.\n\u2022 Balance teacher-led activities with active forms of learning, such as: role-play, discussion and small group work, to practise skills.\n\u2022 Focus your time: quality matters more than quantity. Brief regular instruction appears more effective than infrequent long sessions.\n\u2022 Be explicit: clearly identify the skills that are being taught and why they are important. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 11, "split_id": 32, "split_idx_start": 24509, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b5aa475bfe07f1891119e6e3d9656808dbf3074343187e19f5fe806c8f8e1b35", "range": [564, 597]}, {"doc_id": "079ad55efdb193e2b5a5521976794fdbe4306ae6f292592d9f5d9d6dea8ceeb3", "range": [0, 93]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03659685701131821, -0.09041937440633774, -0.002551063196733594, -0.012879976071417332, 0.0069730086252093315, 0.0481860414147377, 0.011891106143593788, -0.061609867960214615, 0.012471252121031284, 0.003383270464837551, -0.0038296065758913755, -0.019994346424937248, -0.0025192026514559984, 0.01562413014471531, 0.010858087800443172, -0.09550689905881882, 0.007715614512562752, 0.03520890325307846, -0.007725843694061041, 0.013313058763742447, 0.00841320026665926, 0.016933806240558624, -0.02014230750501156, -0.018651055172085762, -0.004871635232120752, -0.01807454787194729, -0.0008506430312991142, 0.023471374064683914, 0.013816059567034245, -0.06072341278195381, 0.07520431280136108, 0.009100387804210186, 0.004192657768726349, -0.07352844625711441, 2.5359413484693505e-06, -0.022499579936265945, -0.008357360027730465, -0.020592566579580307, 0.04490458220243454, -0.01759576052427292, 0.02708967961370945, -0.03798408433794975, 0.052308060228824615, 0.0451326966285