288570046, 0.02092099003493786, -0.011282051913440228, 0.0007421242189593613, 0.02584075927734375, -0.055756326764822006, 0.0012868823250755668, 0.02312861569225788, 0.06893803924322128, -0.02581842802464962, 0.019942643120884895, -0.042809948325157166, 0.036899808794260025, 0.015074619092047215, -0.026800962164998055, -0.013741519302129745, 0.02324790135025978, 2.3969870353714493e-34, 0.0033429148606956005, -0.04112280160188675, 0.010313478298485279, -0.13023042678833008, 0.01757325790822506, -0.01133448351174593, -0.00953286699950695, 0.021152539178729057, 0.014151754789054394, 0.0024703212548047304, -0.03437216207385063], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "54c1a8c6c0ce0ff6363e7e6502591b3f68ba09835f0f0d84a6399c7ef326a949", "content": "This chunk is part of Recommendation 5, which focuses on reinforcing social and emotional learning (SEL) skills through a whole-school ethos and activities. It emphasizes the importance of engaging parents in skill reinforcement at home, establishing a shared vision for SEL, involving teachers in planning, providing necessary training, and prioritizing the quality of SEL implementation for improved outcomes.\u2022 Actively engage with parents to reinforce skills in the home environment. Page 30\nReinforce SEL skills through whole-school ethos and activities\n5\n\u2022 Establish a shared vision for SEL: ensure it is connected to rather than competing with other school priorities.\n\u2022 Involve teachers and school staff in planning for SEL.\n\u2022 Provide training and support to all school staff, covering: readiness for change; development of skills and knowledge; and support for embedding change.\n\u2022 Prioritise implementation quality: teacher preparedness and enthusiasm for SEL are associated with better outcomes.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26