hunk is part of Recommendation 1 in the guidance report, which focuses on teaching social and emotional learning (SEL) skills explicitly. It specifically addresses the concept of self-awareness, explaining its significance in recognizing emotions and thoughts, and how educators can support children in developing this essential skill.Strategies to enhance children\u2019s self-awareness\nWhat do we mean by self-awareness?\nSelf-awareness is concerned with the ability to recognise our emotions and thoughts, and to understand how they influence our behaviour. It also means being aware of our strengths and having a belief in oneself (\u2018self efficacy\u2019). Good self-awareness is associated with reduced difficulties in social functioning and fewer externalising problems, in particular aggression. 20 Two areas that teachers can support are children\u2019s knowledge of emotions, and ability to express emotions.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 12, "split_id": 38, "split_idx_start": 27595, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "599c6561c113eff72d0613eb18882a77874406529034ffc8fd7469f2b70bf9aa", "range": [557, 640]}, {"doc_id": "7a3e4ab6904c4f0855f54940e94bba14798f01023e3978ebe49865ba505f922d", "range": [0, 110]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.027386847883462906, -0.09108160436153412, 0.0018719150684773922, 0.022846288979053497, 0.03299781680107117, 0.029145756736397743, 0.021939773112535477, -0.056373871862888336, 0.07998141646385193, -0.018611907958984375, -0.02143695577979088, 0.030669063329696655, -0.043311916291713715, -0.008239511400461197, 0.03320310637354851, -0.06458801031112671, 0.021560577675700188, 0.004830620251595974, 0.007301439065486193, 0.020385198295116425, 0.005802323576062918, -0.007898013107478619, -0.010660635307431221, 