ways by, for example, giving them the ability to take turns, share, and express emotions (such as anger or frustration) in appropriate ways. 22 Self regulation of emotions complements self-regulated learning, which is discussed in EEF guidance reports on Metacognition and Preparing for Literacy .\nThe \u2018Turtle Technique\u2019 is a strategy that is taught formally in evidence-based prevention programs such as the Incredible Years and PATHS (Promoting Alternative Thinking Strategies). The aim is to help children calm themselves when they feel angry. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 14, "split_id": 43, "split_idx_start": 31531, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "4d214bd0695cdf2bee2e44467682ef4937eaaa0e40e88d52835f49847075521e", "range": [1201, 1407]}, {"doc_id": "7bcb54726987022874e16c5085bb0444f3b30393a1b14520902630494e921a78", "range": [0, 66]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.053494010120630264, -0.06376159936189651, -0.009843442589044571, -0.013878830708563328, 0.005352354608476162, 0.06357007473707199, 0.05191754922270775, -0.008535251952707767, -0.016182707622647285, -0.010948914103209972, -0.026389434933662415, 0.05302371829748154, -0.010310688056051731, -0.03528883680701256, 0.016420794650912285, -0.07427693158388138, 0.0016833603149279952, 0.05286937206983566, 0.02477724850177765, -0.007103944197297096, 0.01198013685643673, -0.015895171090960503, -0.03037223219871521, 0.021006425842642784, -0.04282565414905548, -0.0574193112552166, 0.019512243568897247, 0.04092581197619438, -0.007566347718238831, -0.06441888958215714, 0.06745164841413498, 0.008154656738042831, 0.011686318553984165, -0.04990118369460106, 2.1639680198859423e-06, -0.0003212347801309079, -0.005194762721657753, -0.04150579124689102, 0.027343565598130226, 0.0071753