hildren experience a strong emotion such as anger, often there is an underlying thought (self-talk) accompanying this emotion which intensifies how they are feeling (\u201cI\u2019ve been left out\u2026no one likes me\u201d). When self-\ntalk is negative, children can get angry, frustrated, or anxious more easily. Teach children to use positive-\nself talk (helpful thoughts) to calm their emotions.\n\u2022 Recognise body cues. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 14, "split_id": 46, "split_idx_start": 33436, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f26f4e922ab65062475ca06d251477ef2953843f8d4da15b14454dd049c4bc31", "range": [534, 571]}, {"doc_id": "e12ace194b3a0fe35c78e2ad8100c076ed91d54397ef7f7cbcda92b8b8b39180", "range": [0, 23]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.056411031633615494, -0.02932877466082573, -0.022127093747258186, 0.015046428889036179, 0.03895511105656624, 0.037881411612033844, 0.04136690869927406, -0.037084534764289856, 0.05972074717283249, -0.026095950976014137, -0.027314262464642525, 0.031878940761089325, 0.004351647570729256, -0.031270794570446014, -0.003099587047472596, -0.08854227513074875, -0.026903899386525154, 0.02838704362511635, 0.05634687468409538, 0.008586570620536804, 0.023408763110637665, -0.023215413093566895, -0.01979219727218151, -0.005650486331433058, -0.059059638530015945, -0.03589131310582161, 0.04660504311323166, 0.028483664616942406, 0.0033213060814887285, -0.09267570078372955, 0.0401570089161396, 0.009649449028074741, 0.014323721639811993, -0.03622298687696457, 2.2198414626473095e-06, 0.004815621301531792, -0.009354421868920326, -0.039465539157390594, -0.004934175405651331, 0.022020990028977394, 0.07853934913873672, -0.09416800737380981, 0.018421219661831856, 0.016540739685297012, 0.024091340601444244, -0.0172