76702881, 0.09421048313379288, 0.04997595399618149, -0.014096902683377266, 0.011059658601880074, 0.004217199515551329, 0.008969161659479141, -0.014422374777495861, -0.0078858258202672, -0.011709658429026604, 0.015474563464522362, -0.027291012927889824, 0.021974990144371986, 0.02316400781273842, -0.0021937380079180002, -0.006190261337906122, 0.03427577391266823, 0.01375253964215517, 0.0007890450651757419, 0.03130415454506874, -0.0338643342256546, -0.03098965436220169, 0.010344499722123146, -0.01078928355127573, 0.007505163550376892, -0.015003259293735027, 0.01792706362903118, 0.0038884603418409824, -0.0053418222814798355, -0.007664279546588659, -0.023553403094410896, 0.010771078057587147, 0.027779819443821907, 0.06378056108951569, -0.0027739405632019043, 0.062475644052028656, -0.040312353521585464, -0.0414360836148262, 0.005275338888168335, -0.06953761726617813, 0.0194382406771183, 0.0860266238451004, 0.008505293168127537, 0.013998709619045258, -0.028841456398367882, 0.04802596569061279, -0.05076053738594055, 0.008299377746880054, 0.0017784754745662212, -0.08578494191169739, 0.014802289195358753, 0.014030421152710915, 0.0455620251595974, -0.07278221845626831, 0.018800262361764908, -0.017666276544332504, 0.012491113506257534, -0.00690408144146204, -0.04149559140205383, 0.009819082915782928, -0.005975592415779829, 1.8871745614479722e-34, 0.00439614849165082, -0.022891132161021233, -0.02358308620750904, -0.09208739548921585, 0.021764319390058517, -0.016622409224510193, -0.06380122154951096, 0.000303200475173071, 0.0368611104786396, -0.0012877254048362374, 0.020390478894114494], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "be66728b1408331cd1dc1538c71ed25bdd819136bee47cea56d5887189bc3ea9", "content": "This chunk is situated in the section discussing social awareness as part of social and emotional learning (SEL). It highlights the importance of empathy and perspective-taking in children's development and provides a specific classroom activity that encourages children to articulate emotions and consider supportive behaviors, reinforcing key SEL skills.Understanding the perspectives of others and developing a sense of empathy are considered fundamental building blocks for the positive development and mental health of children. 24 Longitudinal research has shown that good social skills\u2014including high levels of empathy\u2014developed by the age of ten, are predictors of a range of adult outcomes (age 42), such as life satisfaction and wellbeing, labour market success, and good overall health.25\nAsk children to each write about a situation where they have experienced a strong emotion. After doing this, ask children to swap accounts and write a brief summary of what emotion the other child was feeling. Working together, they then record three things an ally could do to help someone in that situation. To draw connections with other subjects, in a follow-up history lesson, they could consider what it means to be an ally to another nation, and how this is different or similar to being an ally to someone in school. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 15, "split_id": 49, "split_idx_start": 34895, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "7cc5e37d9da7933092eebd31722cc1c16dba8935fe1cf56010c7b06810d52f61", "range": [641, 819]}, {"doc_id": "bf19f1e1fbd8606d9d8a67e1fc3edfbb6006c4f830748c6a681e07423463677a", "range": [0, 215]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.030672339722514153, -0.04000428691506386, 0.004357925150543451, 0.005065198987722397, -0.003561324207112193, 0.058534473180770874, 0.033560480922460556, -0.044044915586709976, 0.038340140134096146, -0.0006287497817538679, 0.03440113738179207, -0.025807153433561325, 0.011206185445189476, -0.06185119226574898, 0.0007578344666399062, -0.09637761861085892, 0.025908956304192543, 0.0