0.007818920537829399, 0.01354261301457882, -0.028970660641789436, 0.045465804636478424, -0.02522164396941662, -0.025289999321103096, 0.03867168352007866, 0.03659173846244812, 0.046185147017240524, -0.015088032931089401, -0.02257062867283821, -0.028200432658195496, 0.0372898243367672, 0.0011057115625590086, -0.03939851000905037, 0.0317622534930706, 0.012208613567054272, 1.4989378203470306e-34, -0.0074158948846161366, -0.0309168491512537, 0.018836427479982376, -0.027167610824108124, 0.045893725007772446, -0.02476898580789566, 0.005585142411291599, 0.036593783646821976, 0.03871238976716995, 0.048019129782915115, -0.01299974787980318], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "e8e076ba007b74e24578b277309f164dd00e3dabc0756f486479f9f05f73746e", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing strategies for enhancing children's relationship skills within the guidance report on improving social and emotional learning (SEL) in primary schools. It highlights practical scenarios and role-play activities that facilitate teamwork, effective communication, and conflict resolution among peers, emphasizing the importance of collaborative skills in social interactions.Sample scenarios include trying to join in a game out in the playground, trying to get the teacher\u2019s attention in class, or talking to a parent whilst playing on a phone.\n\u2022 Children can identify and practise the skills needed for working in groups and teams\u2014such as building on one another\u2019s contributions, making sure everyone can contribute, probing to check understanding, and trying to reach a shared agreement. They can use sentence stems \u2014such as \u2018I agree because...\u2019, \u2018I disagree because\u2026\u2019\u2014to support their discussions.\f15Improving social and emotional learning in primary schools\nRelationship building \u2022 Role play can be used to demonstrate ways to interact with friends in different circumstances\u2014for example, introducing yourself, taking turns, asking to share, or dealing with conflict. Scenarios involving joining a new class, or club, and welcoming newcomers to such a group, can also be explored.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 16, "split_id": 54, "split_idx_start": 38641, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "027e091f6dc8ecdd5475c7b712e4396cedf6269ecc88e8b9a6b926fb8535901d", "range": [1159, 1330]}, {"doc_id": "e09f92706d3bdf2dc206c867a5d89ee874a11e86b1a730737d1d58e890d44808", "range": [0, 113]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.07067568600177765, -0.046560563147068024, -0.01511880662292242, 0.040559589862823486, -0.019175449386239052, 0.014276009052991867, 0.029238281771540642, -0.04872041568160057, -0.014727002941071987, 0.007900510914623737, 0.00010862819181056693, -0.06120096519589424, 0.04280534014105797, -0.011371240951120853, -0.012239456176757812, -0.11220786720514297, 0.014119663275778294, 0.029695020988583565, 0.0505511499941349, 0.0068942345678806305, 0.012934919446706772, 0.005217899568378925, 0.0011227033101022243, 0.009654730558395386, -0.06395924091339111, -0.009008694440126419, -0.002544074086472392, 0.005088938865810633, 0.04380878061056137, -0.001042995136231184, 0.07161340862512589, 0.010770997032523155, -0.016045093536376953, -0.0300904531031847, 2.4859159566403832e-06, 0.002039074432104826, 0.007037706673145294, -0.026094678789377213, 0.01706109382212162, -0.026529468595981598, 0.015216460451483727, 0.0006674109026789665, 0.025965888053178787, 0.02485714666545391, -0.046338632702827454, 0.014695393852889538, 0.04612603411078453, 0.021542197093367577, 0.03751957416534424, -0.011270624585449696, 0.00936530064791441, -0.009030938148498535, -0.05460299178957939, -0.05174015834927559, 0.058063045144081116, -0.014643143862485886, -0.007073539774864912, 0.037713959813