is best to begin problem solving when children are calm and relaxed. If a child is very anxious or angry, help them to calm down first (quiet time, taking deep breaths) or leave problem-solving for another day when you know the child is ready to participate. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 18, "split_id": 64, "split_idx_start": 43475, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "95ba49b35a792ed1b8a3e1634e771e9943a8e59da33e35d610b1b54f3d1da213", "range": [287, 354]}, {"doc_id": "14ffc10356b76dcd8f54f116535cc0d0e067d63ade9b7bdd5ef4ca28c88ada12", "range": [0, 190]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03644275665283203, -0.07410065829753876, -0.017214424908161163, -0.014993280172348022, -0.020910006016492844, 0.019626827910542488, 0.009663429111242294, -0.01928321085870266, 0.00030405589495785534, 0.03217880055308342, 0.042728424072265625, 0.010942134074866772, -0.009906384162604809, -0.010525253601372242, -0.04303915426135063, -0.07295975834131241, -0.01815660111606121, 0.022609572857618332, 0.06631239503622055, 0.013574988581240177, -0.007453901693224907, -0.02473706565797329, -0.01721573807299137, -0.006381018552929163, -0.06538073718547821, -0.04084663465619087, 0.011223480105400085, 0.016748731955885887, 0.024854568764567375, -0.06814496219158173, 0.07445446401834488, 0.007387859746813774, -0.006625213660299778, -0.0467095784842968, 2.400736320851138e-06, -0.011219751089811325, -0.03395414724946022, -0.04169122874736786, -0.00033740137587301433, -0.010415613651275635, -0.009073754772543907, -0.028593165799975395, 0.0066277277655899525, 0.03971109539270401, -0.01115868054330349, 0.024478672072291374, 0.029627295210957527, 0.09857989102602005, 0.03679071366786957, -0.0026899410877376795, 0.0009038746356964111, 0.027773912996053696, -0.0207780543714