nce children's responsible decision-making under Recommendation 1 of the guidance report. It emphasizes the importance of helping children calm down before engaging in problem-solving to address behavioral issues and includes a practical example related to goal setting and problem resolution techniques.If a child is very anxious or angry, help them to calm down first (quiet time, taking deep breaths) or leave problem-solving for another day when you know the child is ready to participate. When you encounter behavioural issues in your classroom, try to resolve them together using a problem-solving approach. Where a child has behaved inappropriately, re-run the scenario with them later to help them identify alternative courses of action. Box 5 provides an example related to problem solving and goal setting.\f17Improving social and emotional learning in primary schools This activity starts with the teacher providing a written vignette detailing a goal and a problem preventing the goal from being reached. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 18, "split_id": 65, "split_idx_start": 43754, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "bfb151aa16397a22e9aef5e0406b527637a2ca6a86f53b4c8a9b2b96e34e6c07", "range": [279, 469]}, {"doc_id": "d2ccb0a26a5ca536ea9fcb7a9399ce7c17a75e5d187ceafcd77c7cbaac649447", "range": [0, 199]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04973859712481499, -0.09451480209827423, -0.006814745720475912, -0.023982882499694824, -0.02302667498588562, 0.017030663788318634, 0.029110845178365707, -0.017876164987683296, -0.04492878541350365, 0.019457679241895676, 0.0811145231127739, -0.009145328775048256, 0.0251986775547266, -0.02404002845287323, -0.012117930687963963, -0.09348296374082565, -0.0004398979071993381, 0.02942616492509842, 0.01778700761497020