121320724, -0.04917415976524353, -0.016172310337424278, -0.01744227111339569, 0.037250906229019165, 0.013374196365475655, 0.052119508385658264, -0.01644033193588257, 0.014203746803104877, 0.027842504903674126, 0.0434885211288929, 0.03613936901092529, 0.0550406277179718, 0.011480867862701416, -0.0044716051779687405, 0.08520298451185226, -0.014937112107872963, -0.06467323005199432, 0.030177168548107147, -0.030063992366194725, -0.03766882047057152, -0.07054436206817627, 0.039442360401153564, 0.033219628036022186, 0.014328607358038425, -0.03310022130608559, -0.03147893026471138, 0.0589354932308197, 0.032125357538461685, 0.02697659470140934, -0.026379508897662163, 0.019232075661420822, -0.03598880395293236, -0.06550709158182144, 0.00853156577795744, 0.00801874790340662, 0.0010263292351737618, 0.05859120935201645, -0.007725845091044903, 0.013222724199295044, 0.024508411064743996, 0.03897273540496826, 0.008170881308615208, 0.006721431389451027, 0.0036775912158191204, -0.005425548180937767, 0.0033950135111808777, 0.007090134546160698, 0.030161751434206963, -0.03405141830444336, -0.02212570048868656, 0.011475634761154652, -0.0013426946243271232, 0.017737407237291336, -0.047278959304094315, -0.06301259994506836, -0.04038948938250542, 2.713737074758717e-34, -0.017453404143452644, 0.01689966954290867, -0.013859359547495842, -0.08414626121520996, 2.0753624994540587e-05, -0.013440643437206745, 0.043182678520679474, 0.03024224564433098, 0.01713530346751213, 0.06578777730464935, -0.04973987117409706], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "87cbb75db71a1ee43cabe80f8bc5996bdf867ffd42f792bc2b8d2512f93f96bf", "content": "This chunk is located within the section discussing strategies to integrate and model social and emotional learning (SEL) skills in everyday teaching. It specifically focuses on the WOOP framework, which aids children in goal-setting and problem-solving by identifying obstacles and planning solutions, enhancing their SEL skills through practical application.This framework has been described as \u2018Wish, Outcome, Obstacle, Plan\u2019 (\u2018WOOP\u2019). There is evidence from small trials that helping children to set goals, identify potential barriers, and anticipate \u2018if\u2026then\u2026\u2019 solutions in this way can lead to better outcomes than a comparison group who are encouraged simply to think positively about achieving goals. 35\nBox 5: Identifying barriers to goals, and how to overcome them\f18\nEducation Endowment Foundation 2\nIntegrate and model SEL skills through everyday teaching\nModel the behaviours you want children to adopt\nIn addition to explicit teaching, children learn by observing other people, getting ideas about how new behaviours are formed, and using the ideas to guide their actions. 37 Teachers navigate stressful situations nearly every day, and children are watching, and learning from the way teachers manage frustration, maintain control of themselves and the classroom, and stay focused in the face of distractions. 38 Modelling\u2014or demonstrating appropriate behaviours\u2014teaches and enhances children\u2019s social and emotional skills. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 19, "split_id": 67, "split_idx_start": 45032, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "d2ccb0a26a5ca536ea9fcb7a9399ce7c17a75e5d187ceafcd77c7cbaac649447", "range": [765, 844]}, {"doc_id": "9c0082d16c09449e20ad092e77eb00d4e637a50c98fc8e52828803bc50d21ba8", "range": [0, 114]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.08596541732549667, -0.08212507516145706, -0.0014042311813682318, -0.01233483012765646, -0.02880372665822506, 0.040195513516664505, 0.015209377743303776, -0.03904226794838905, -0.012476619333028793, 0.023374412208795547, 0.04193495959043503, 0.011962084099650383, 0.030225388705730438, 0.016943469643592834,