2673, -0.02447100169956684, 0.006020952016115189, 0.029326656833291054, 0.010458201169967651, -0.0027284242678433657, -0.04053359851241112, 0.05839192494750023, 0.014395100995898247, 0.07197391986846924, -0.010020704939961433, -0.0031192132737487555, -0.0411963053047657, -0.03351876139640808, 0.01021041814237833, -0.06823862344026566, 0.005318855866789818, 0.07330644130706787, -0.011193502694368362, 0.018426978960633278, -0.005718740168958902, 0.05815491825342178, 0.008161804638803005, 0.010960137471556664, 0.007895371876657009, -0.07906726002693176, 0.024963537231087685, 0.01835532858967781, 0.0396365188062191, -0.03703146427869797, -0.008092056959867477, -0.019902093335986137, 0.020716818049550056, -0.004765029530972242, -0.043649591505527496, 0.008433682844042778, -0.024255020543932915, 1.9373510658669244e-34, -0.008289413526654243, -0.005707030184566975, 0.011300822719931602, -0.06541156023740768, 0.02487005479633808, -0.010374633595347404, -0.026464320719242096, 0.02177109383046627, 0.018105177208781242, 0.06374900788068771, -0.02646035887300968], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "273e32c3b6b1fa4f6c5824299bd819ea05a774d9a085aaaab2f09aaa0d5eaa60", "content": "This chunk is found in the section discussing the integration of Social and Emotional Learning (SEL) into classroom practices. It highlights the importance of collaborative learning and structured discussions for enhancing students' social and emotional skills, emphasizing the need for effective communication and interaction among peers to support SEL development across various subjects.20\nEducation Endowment Foundation Provide support for effective group work and classroom talk\nThe effects of SEL work can be amplified through classrooms that help children to practise their skills in their everyday interactions.44 For example, collaborative (or cooperative) learning approaches may be particularly beneficial for supporting pupils\u2019 peer interactions.45 Such approaches typically involve pupils working together on activities or learning tasks in groups small enough for everyone to participate on a collective task that has been clearly assigned. The impact of collaborative approaches on learning is consistently positive, with approaches promoting talk and interaction between learners linked to greater gains.46\nStructured whole-class discussion also provides opportunities for students to practise social and emotional skills, including grappling with multiple perspectives, communicating effectively, and disagreeing respectfully. Teachers can support this by establishing ground rules for talk, as well as acting as guide and facilitator by using well-designed questions to draw out students\u2019 thinking, modelling effective communication, and supporting children to build on one another\u2019s contributions. For example, a ground-rule during a discussion could be: \u2018you need to reference a class-mate\u2019s name and contribution in your response\u2026\u2019 to encourage active listening and a cumulative dialogue. There is evidence that such approaches to improving the quality of classroom talk can improve academic and non-academic outcomes (see Box 7 for an example).47\nEmbed SEL teaching across subject areas\nTeaching SEL skills in the context of the wider curriculum is engaging and helps children to apply what they have learnt. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 22, "split_id": 73, "split_idx_start": 50044, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "bbeea279a51efaeab433f020cd7536f5401f0c8d7cb60196069bb0117bbc898f", "range": [816, 1381]}, {"doc_id": "2c0ad90e6d4483de50f2abe3cd438c4f776b0bc041855d7afe4cdcf096eea1c2", "range": [0, 321]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.07846994698047638, -0.07724806666374207, 0.002806187141686678, 0.02288185246