44240427017, 0.02047794684767723, 0.06305532157421112, -0.024426599964499474, -0.014047057367861271, -0.024776317179203033, -0.03353225812315941, 0.007316479925066233, -0.032468218356370926, 0.005124551709741354, 0.06447587162256241, 0.0068576885387301445, 0.0006702474202029407, 0.017310258001089096, 0.04769819229841232, 0.005727415904402733, -0.01901705376803875, -0.006840718910098076, -0.07696067541837692, 0.036930181086063385, 0.021253887563943863, 0.04473403841257095, -0.04816450551152229, -0.008583751507103443, -0.028304073959589005, 0.018489297479391098, -0.030058639124035835, -0.03293560445308685, 0.03966231271624565, -0.04883825406432152, 2.0992818411774256e-34, -0.0004761825839523226, -0.029114119708538055, 0.012390048243105412, -0.03132251277565956, 0.006764410063624382, -0.014784598723053932, -0.010165408253669739, 0.01567440666258335, 0.020295344293117523, 0.05010403320193291, -0.02443629316985607], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "2c0ad90e6d4483de50f2abe3cd438c4f776b0bc041855d7afe4cdcf096eea1c2", "content": "This chunk is situated within the section discussing the integration of Social and Emotional Learning (SEL) into everyday classroom practices, specifically highlighting the importance of embedding SEL teaching across various subjects. It emphasizes how linking SEL with core curriculum areas, such as English and History, can enhance both academic and non-academic outcomes for students.There is evidence that such approaches to improving the quality of classroom talk can improve academic and non-academic outcomes (see Box 7 for an example).47\nEmbed SEL teaching across subject areas\nTeaching SEL skills in the context of the wider curriculum is engaging and helps children to apply what they have learnt. The suggestion here is not to replace core curriculum teaching on knowledge and skills, but to identify opportunities for linking and embedding SEL skills in ways that complement everyday teaching. Many areas of the curriculum offer opportunities for SEL. For example:\n\u2022 In English lessons, children can use stories as the basis for discussing characters\u2019 feelings and motivations, extending a normal inference activity (see Box 6).\n\u2022 In history lessons children can develop an understanding of others\u2019 perspectives and feelings based on real events. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 22, "split_id": 74, "split_idx_start": 51464, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "273e32c3b6b1fa4f6c5824299bd819ea05a774d9a085aaaab2f09aaa0d5eaa60", "range": [1420, 1741]}, {"doc_id": "45b9eb41853aacc1ea3015d13b1ae796dd125f120c7677868cfec286bd443cbf", "range": [0, 118]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03391145169734955, -0.0350978784263134, -0.007579920347779989, 0.014480882324278355, -0.0065843393094837666, 0.07275174558162689, 0.019698049873113632, -0.07068369537591934, 0.03415530174970627, -0.0037895396817475557, 0.007697136141359806, 0.017299635335803032, 0.02825743891298771, -0.01129135861992836, 0.021969305351376534, -0.10204453021287918, -0.005574342794716358, 0.057211317121982574, 0.012301696464419365, 0.027138667181134224, -0.012301318347454071, 0.009232565760612488, 0.004972186405211687, -0.027109110727906227, -0.014648699201643467, -0.011702878400683403, -0.024067724123597145, 0.003501842264086008, 0.03703729063272476, -0.011143567971885204, 0.0445074662566185, 0.010840501636266708, 0.03149394318461418, -0.044948674738407135, 2.5122185434156563e-06, -0.015174046158790588, -0.02062358520925045, -0.046083830296993256, -0.001234677154570818, -0.007492986507713795, 0.044488511979579926, 0.04918595775961876, 0.030532242730259895, -0.016050197184085846, -0.0130336107686162, 0.027632372453808784, 0.02182075008749962, 0.0483010970056057, 0.030938534066081047, 0.0107944430783391, 0.011