754616498947, -0.03011457435786724, 0.017535347491502762, 0.020937491208314896, -0.11092019081115723, 0.06262656301259995, 0.022817429155111313, 0.04287509620189667, -0.07618153095245361, 0.008502529002726078, -0.001020147348754108, 0.005297008436173201, 0.018593059852719307, -0.04387256130576134, 4.4502066884888336e-05, -0.00917808897793293, 1.6622755154586722e-34, -0.008708025328814983, -0.039038822054862976, -0.016757626086473465, -0.09548094868659973, 0.013575481250882149, -0.0070517840795218945, 0.004717632662504911, 0.02410138212144375, 0.023264462128281593, 0.04128389060497284, 0.0010410541435703635], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "a3081924ef1bef1833df1d2f88cb44cef739adc10719c3c655ec599035979666", "content": "This chunk is situated in the section discussing structured SEL (Social and Emotional Learning) programmes, highlighting their characteristics, such as explicit curricula and lesson structures. It emphasizes the importance of these programmes in teaching SEL skills effectively, connecting to previous recommendations about teaching strategies and outcomes for children in primary schools.They are often introduced in the context of specific topics, such as: bullying, friendship, health education, and staying safe (see Box 8 for an example). 50\nCommon characteristics of SEL programmes include:\n\u2022 an explicit curriculum of scheduled lessons;\n\u2022 a teacher\u2019s handbook or manual (ranging from broad principles to heavily scripted);\n\u2022 resources (such as worksheets) for use with a whole class; and\n\u2022 a lesson structure (indicating a sequenced and regular progression).\nRecommendations 1 and 2 focused on flexible teaching strategies that can be adapted to schools\u2019 needs. This recommendation focuses on structured programmes as a way of delivering a SEL curriculum\u2014as such they can be a \u2018vehicle\u2019 for introducing a wide range of practices and strategies, such as those mentioned in Recommendations 1 and 2, in a planned and prescribed way.\nThere is extensive international evidence that teaching SEL through planned programmes can have a positive impact on children\u2019s attitudes to learning, relationships in school, academic attainment, and a range of other outcomes. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 24, "split_id": 79, "split_idx_start": 55856, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f984adb55a766d1d0297d5049c4a9267a606a434c930e135e2bd69c799f97cbc", "range": [1112, 1267]}, {"doc_id": "ce369e77be893fbdd188d02a1ddb791e94938ab8f50c9ccb31339a350f5f19a4", "range": [0, 228]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.047493815422058105, -0.10870030522346497, 0.00617847079411149, -0.0024874689988791943, -0.029675455763936043, 0.06811680644750595, 0.07309151440858841, -0.032634176313877106, -0.010293853469192982, 0.00928904302418232, 0.026470141485333443, 0.002793273888528347, 0.027320360764861107, -0.0025650402531027794, 0.021492095664143562, -0.10851625353097916, 0.0022716140374541283, 0.020052440464496613, -0.031443990767002106, 0.021961312741041183, -0.002684436971321702, 2.0028270228067413e-05, 0.0032118940725922585, -0.020827535539865494, 0.012198423035442829, -0.023525472730398178, -0.05020883306860924, 0.03366582840681076, -0.01199882198125124, -0.04765773564577103, 0.05137435719370842, 0.03755144402384758, -0.0020405154209583998, -0.0750955268740654, 2.2631818410445703e-06, -0.01730838045477867, -0.03505134582519531, -0.02978825382888317, 0.002948841778561473, 0.04160512983798981, -0.012351366691291332, -0.021439751610159874, 0.028491606935858727, -0.0016688236501067877, 0.012174924835562706, 0.02917550504207611, 0.03118925541639328, 0.02019195444881916, 0.028426729142665863, -0.009076589718461037, 0.014462840743362904, -0.028560161590576172, -0.04247518256306648, 