7919708192348, 0.05280609056353569, 0.04050801694393158, 0.019102713093161583, -0.003420576686039567, 0.0373288057744503, -0.036264535039663315, -0.030903583392500877, 0.001171401352621615, -0.003816523589193821, 0.0028662928380072117, 0.013100795447826385, 0.01422359049320221, -0.009145082905888557, -0.016022542491555214, -0.01987672783434391, -0.024358801543712616, 0.06090454384684563, 0.028732677921652794, 0.08649050444364548, -0.015458137728273869, -0.0030281872022897005, -0.043521106243133545, -0.025249939411878586, 0.03306993842124939, -0.028662990778684616, 0.0018616142915561795, 0.06466905772686005, -0.04851232469081879, 0.017166700214147568, 0.009112627245485783, 0.051576241850852966, 0.001577504794113338, 0.025966478511691093, 0.008955556899309158, -0.1000729575753212, 0.015697583556175232, 0.00936100073158741, 0.061200570315122604, -0.010665827430784702, 0.007553722243756056, 0.000549105170648545, -0.007685116957873106, 0.040622249245643616, -0.038300078362226486, -0.03317903354763985, -0.026079785078763962, 2.3193203787381937e-34, 0.012723575346171856, -0.03111858479678631, -0.013499058783054352, -0.09206593036651611, 0.004510838072746992, -0.020052412524819374, -0.013331038877367973, 0.02572566457092762, 0.015048780478537083, 0.023022117093205452, -0.022419534623622894], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "3d638d96aa2e0b6adacb3155f0c6088b41295f78f54c7842a8112ca50558b807", "content": "This chunk is located in the section that discusses the effectiveness of structured Social and Emotional Learning (SEL) programmes in primary schools. It emphasizes their positive impact on various outcomes and highlights the importance of evidence-based practices while allowing for schools to develop tailored curricula that incorporate core SEL skills.Overall, there is good evidence that structured SEL programmes have a positive impact on children\u2019s outcomes.52 Seven large evidence reviews suggest that, on average, these programmes have positive impacts on outcomes including social and emotional skills, attitudes, behaviour, emotional distress, and academic achievement. As such, SEL programmes represent an evidence-based approach that schools should consider carefully\u2014they are likely to be a better bet than adopting a programme without evidence, creating a new approach for your school from scratch, or doing nothing. For an overview of evidence-based programmes, schools can use the Early Intervention Foundation Guidebook .\nSome schools, however, will want to construct their own curriculum, building on their existing effective practice and tailored to their particular context. In this case it will be important to ensure coverage of the core skills at the heart of SEL (self-awareness, self-\nmanagement, social awareness, relationship skills, responsible decision making) in a carefully sequenced progression that follows the SAFE principles described in Recommendation 4. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 25, "split_id": 81, "split_idx_start": 57805, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "ce369e77be893fbdd188d02a1ddb791e94938ab8f50c9ccb31339a350f5f19a4", "range": [1101, 1426]}, {"doc_id": "a71d91d6a8b77d5d1f519e50d6b9e75ec3da31eafa8f8fa1c01b6401d2805b33", "range": [0, 296]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03865516558289528, -0.0894450694322586, 0.003432173514738679, -0.004422346130013466, -0.012734356336295605, 0.07525715231895447, 0.059245456010103226, -0.054211560636758804, 0.006511785555630922, 0.012635985389351845, 0.024974185973405838, 0.01819075457751751, 0.028070775792002678, 0.02744256518781185, 0.017962511628866196, -0.07179705053567886, 0.01744008995592594, 0.026244819164276123, 0.023630063980817795, 0.02040221355855465, -0.013155671767890453, -0.005428554955869913, -0.013518642634153366, -0.0