.06769383698701859, 0.009567310102283955, 0.018399018794298172, -0.017577076330780983, 0.003494730917736888, 0.01455848291516304, -0.05003182962536812, -0.039922576397657394, -0.020225219428539276, 2.1998901526946493e-34, -0.004687769804149866, -0.030181871727108955, -0.014070517383515835, -0.11222489923238754, 0.010156325064599514, -0.02593296580016613, -0.011461053043603897, 0.02858891710639, -0.0021343473345041275, 0.022202908992767334, -0.0281269159168005], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "a71d91d6a8b77d5d1f519e50d6b9e75ec3da31eafa8f8fa1c01b6401d2805b33", "content": "This chunk is located in the section discussing the careful planning required when adopting social and emotional learning (SEL) programmes in schools. It emphasizes the importance of covering essential SEL skills in a structured manner while weighing the potential challenges against the advantages of a tailored approach, in line with the SAFE principles.In this case it will be important to ensure coverage of the core skills at the heart of SEL (self-awareness, self-\nmanagement, social awareness, relationship skills, responsible decision making) in a carefully sequenced progression that follows the SAFE principles described in Recommendation 4. Schools should also balance the potential limitations\u2014the time taken to create a programme, and limited evidence\u2014against the benefits of increased tailoring and flexibility.\f24\nEducation Endowment Foundation Plan carefully before adopting a programme\nDespite the good evidence of promise for SEL programmes overall, the impact of individual programmes varies substantially: simply adopting a SEL programme\u2014even one with a strong track record\u2014is not a guarantee of success. Some recent evaluations of SEL programmes in England, such as PATHS and FRIENDS for Life, have not reproduced the positive impacts that have been reported previously (see Box 8 for an example). 53 It is therefore especially important to identify an approach that fits your needs and context, consider whether and how your school can implement it, and to plan carefully to deliver it with quality.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 25, "split_id": 82, "split_idx_start": 58645, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "3d638d96aa2e0b6adacb3155f0c6088b41295f78f54c7842a8112ca50558b807", "range": [840, 1136]}, {"doc_id": "dedf695e4a0728df18388f85edf2fbf798fe26a7891a0c9f563ca93ba8c88c14", "range": [0, 203]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.050204772502183914, -0.08493015915155411, 0.007400126196444035, 0.003664765041321516, -0.015858931466937065, 0.09004838764667511, 0.029011309146881104, -0.06790748238563538, 0.011540641076862812, 0.02088843658566475, 0.036292269825935364, 0.029255591332912445, 0.0010191757464781404, 0.02057412639260292, 0.007768017239868641, -0.062101516872644424, 0.018826236948370934, 0.02372555620968342, -0.027053961530327797, 0.016986500471830368, -0.013846607878804207, 0.007007824257016182, -0.00954425148665905, -0.028125494718551636, -0.00018242817895952612, -0.012664898298680782, -0.022210387513041496, 0.028119301423430443, 0.015717830508947372, -0.051757775247097015, 0.022527486085891724, 0.010919084772467613, -0.00044896872714161873, -0.07514848560094833, 2.2993344828137197e-06, -0.03299029543995857, -0.032795604318380356, -0.03201866149902344, 0.02519070915877819, -0.011699949391186237, 0.00101769610773772, 0.015523315407335758, 0.034627385437488556, 0.029307590797543526, 0.005501724313944578, 0.028320206329226494, 0.025143910199403763, 0.020791329443454742, 0.021021900698542595, 0.0028860182501375675, 0.011094904504716396, -0.011438664048910141, -0.04975259304046631, -0.04110293090343475, 0.027307134121656418, -0.010786009952425957, 0.011495936661958694, -0.04180200770497322, -0.0008117423