, 0.012617358937859535, 0.0063043320551514626, -0.01734653301537037, -0.036672789603471756, -0.03336099535226822, 0.021236514672636986, 0.015145139768719673, 0.05283268541097641, 0.012490072287619114, 0.018554674461483955, -0.03433437645435333, -0.041871000081300735, 0.016110025346279144, -0.05567063391208649, 0.028766294941306114, 0.07747135311365128, -0.06021493300795555, 0.0416601300239563, 0.013551970943808556, 0.04765194654464722, -0.01790017820894718, 0.017726512625813484, 0.004460594151169062, -0.07097429782152176, 0.029380224645137787, 0.029545575380325317, 0.046978555619716644, -0.008387560956180096, 0.0344061404466629, -0.04540073499083519, 0.024832647293806076, 0.007082797586917877, -0.044114887714385986, -0.009794874116778374, -0.008613699115812778, 2.2464144742257684e-34, -0.006219410337507725, -0.05304626375436783, -0.01152834203094244, -0.09339028596878052, -0.001541230478323996, -0.04013289138674736, -0.008185764774680138, 0.04679432511329651, 0.020802512764930725, 0.05663004890084267, -0.03578103333711624], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "06db156950a7feae651cccaebf45dee10c0d48b121bed0b1e05eeddb0d529aa9", "content": "This chunk is located in Recommendation 4, which discusses the importance of using a SAFE curriculum (Sequential, Active, Focused, and Explicit) for teaching social and emotional learning (SEL). It specifically addresses the need for sequenced instruction in SEL, highlighting the spiral curriculum approach to reinforce and develop skills across different age groups in primary education.\u2018Sequencing\u2019 refers both to the development of content within each year, and across year groups. A \u2018spiral curriculum\u2019 is a common feature of evidence-based SEL programmes. It involves revisiting key concepts progressively in age-appropriate contexts as children get older, so that they are recalled and embedded.\nTable 3 shows how a particular area of social and emotional learning (the ability to recognise and understand feelings) might evolve and become increasingly sophisticated across age groups. The strategies used to teach and practise the skills would also vary by age.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 29, "split_id": 100, "split_idx_start": 66406, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "33bc685924ebad6983072fd35304bd88732e5b127d854ef1c047246e27a8cd99", "range": [672, 769]}, {"doc_id": "93c8448e6353f852e1ba21085ca9a076b266324960d1fe51b6cfe099f3372b67", "range": [0, 77]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03732209652662277, -0.09077393263578415, 0.0048582833260297775, -0.003043112577870488, -0.011367580853402615, 0.08004499226808548, 0.027155110612511635, -0.05777144059538841, 0.0256358552724123, 0.03845299407839775, 0.0044433013536036015, 7.067406113492325e-05, 0.03507375344634056, -0.00524410093203187, -0.0032229903154075146, -0.10319673269987106, 0.024871505796909332, 0.009289724752306938, 0.02603713609278202, 0.010428906418383121, -0.035612739622592926, 2.611206582514569e-05, -0.02416561357676983, -0.008075032383203506, 0.0019051667768508196, -0.027496960014104843, -0.017931297421455383, 0.01631982997059822, 0.014956566505134106, -0.06492762267589569, 0.056715164333581924, 0.020489852875471115, 0.02314039133489132, -0.045124609023332596, 2.380073738095234e-06, -0.029570387676358223, -0.01268936600536108, -0.020448483526706696, 0.015517817810177803, 0.003182432847097516, 0.03983159363269806, -0.0015858816914260387, 0.044752154499292374, 0.008511441759765148, 8.688430534675717e-05, -0.006126696243882179, 0.02479090727865696, 0.02771013416349888, 0.02001427300274372, -0.03205966576933861, 0.007143304217606783, -0.013032370246946812, -0.04038751870393753, -0.04761049151420593, 0.07597573846578598, -0.007250642869621515, -0.006929263938218355, 0.0133002158254385, 0.0