n identifying and expressing emotions from Nursery/Reception through to Years 5 and 6, highlighting the increasing complexity of feelings understood by children.The strategies used to teach and practise the skills would also vary by age.\nNursery/Reception\nCan identify and express basic emotions - happy sad, angry, worried or scared\nCan identify, express and predict an increasingly complex range of feelings (for example frustrated, hopeful, hopeless, disappointed, guilty.) Can identify, express and predict a broad range of feelings (such as ashamed, embarrassed, ecstatic, agitated, despairing, defensive, nervous). Can understand and express mixed feelings.\nY1 and Y2\nY3 and Y4\nY5 and Y6\nCan identify and express a wider range of feelings (such as, anxious, proud or jealous). ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 29, "split_id": 101, "split_idx_start": 66910, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "06db156950a7feae651cccaebf45dee10c0d48b121bed0b1e05eeddb0d529aa9", "range": [504, 581]}, {"doc_id": "a20ec7c09b633b43ae8275ac1adba593ab7a2771c812370d0d0655961ae74ebe", "range": [0, 119]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.02335025928914547, -0.01930665224790573, -0.01151348277926445, 0.017083922401070595, 0.01771092601120472, 0.03686051070690155, 0.020594028756022453, -0.04201263189315796, 0.052763085812330246, 0.005294712260365486, -0.005669748410582542, -0.011593217961490154, 0.008838696405291557, -0.025667771697044373, -0.020975537598133087, -0.09654471278190613, 0.01348030660301447, 0.03972836211323738, 0.038553353399038315, 0.015095856040716171, -0.016729062423110008, 0.008952716365456581, -0.006635625381022692, -0.01547315064817667, -0.04779990017414093, -0.018771260976791382, -0.026659520342946053, -0.013968375511467457, 0.007930221036076546, 