7, 0.042723286896944046, -0.0121302530169487, 0.0031569511629641056, 0.022285552695393562, 2.4320475319171664e-34, -0.020316418260335922, -0.03786611184477806, -0.008539007976651192, -0.030552122741937637, 0.04232415556907654, -0.014416316524147987, -0.03673934191465378, 0.0469324104487896, 0.070127472281456, 0.03885185718536377, 0.012589531019330025], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "a20ec7c09b633b43ae8275ac1adba593ab7a2771c812370d0d0655961ae74ebe", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing the developmental progression of social and emotional learning (SEL) competencies across different year groups in primary education. It highlights how students in Year 1 and 2, Year 3 and 4, and Year 5 and 6 can identify and express a wider range of emotions, emphasizing instructional strategies that enhance their emotional vocabulary and understanding.Y1 and Y2\nY3 and Y4\nY5 and Y6\nCan identify and express a wider range of feelings (such as, anxious, proud or jealous). Can understand and use words representing different intensities of emotions (for example, from irritated to furious).\nTable 3: SEL key strategy\u2014Recognising, labelling and understanding feelings\f28\nEducation Endowment Foundation Use active forms of learning\nA series of SEL lessons might include a range of pedagogical strategies such as teacher-led instruction, written worksheets and discussion of a stimulus (eg, a story or video). Evidence on SEL suggests that in combination with these approaches, it is particularly active forms of learning that have been associated with greater impacts, including interactive methods such as games, simulations, and small group work, which help children to practise using skills in real contexts. 58\nFocus your time\nCurrently, less than a third of primary school teachers say that they have time dedicated to teaching SEL.59 Increasing this time is likely to be beneficial, though there are a number of considerations to balance what is effective and what is practically feasible:\n\u2022 Frequency and lesson length: aim for 30\u201360 minutes per week. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 29, "split_id": 102, "split_idx_start": 67413, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "93c8448e6353f852e1ba21085ca9a076b266324960d1fe51b6cfe099f3372b67", "range": [503, 622]}, {"doc_id": "f53cba923384624c3652187d58131d1c2d39f0782c8bbcb407e50fe9fbc4d580", "range": [0, 347]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.029379939660429955, -0.039331596344709396, -0.015016802586615086, 0.009402678348124027, 0.016486749053001404, 0.04513972997665405, 0.022990772500634193, -0.06692501902580261, 0.01533485483378172, 0.014926265925168991, -0.011160357855260372, -0.014701698906719685, 0.0032574571669101715, -0.006636675912886858, -0.0035357766319066286, -0.11565342545509338, -0.007552673574537039, 0.04379383474588394, 0.03723696246743202, 0.025012418627738953, -0.004825390409678221, 0.0050971326418221, -0.0023734623100608587, -0.012500787153840065, -0.04383695870637894, -0.010843425989151001, -0.030866499990224838, -0.006991328205913305, 0.03222018480300903, -0.0489831268787384, 0.04600261151790619, 0.04558425769209862, 0.028179733082652092, -0.038403090089559555, 2.615245193737792e-06, -0.026216212660074234, -0.013448779471218586, -0.05636022239923477, 0.017974572256207466, 0.03268798440694809, 0.0669492781162262, -0.022630171850323677, 0.0328775979578495, -0.005871644709259272, -0.017261173576116562, -0.012935645878314972, 0.05172295495867729, 0.007116671185940504, 0.05423823371529579, -0.02054797112941742, 0.006632481701672077, 0.008281121961772442, -0.05513335019350052, -0.025590363889932632, 0.06690584868192673, 0.005840045865625143, -0.0026949532330036163, -0.0005007082363590598, 0.0703597217798233, -0.04820392280817032, -0.067