5, 0.00940637942403555, -0.04256349056959152, 0.038611456751823425, 0.016991471871733665, 0.04221249744296074, -0.04491181671619415, 0.018512411043047905, -0.03433322533965111, 0.02277221716940403, 0.022413045167922974, -0.03339497372508049, 0.03896882385015488, -0.027600007131695747, 1.9961434617410492e-34, 0.011142355389893055, -0.05822189152240753, 0.014371388591825962, -0.060746025294065475, -0.01699223928153515, -0.014290363527834415, -0.002739861374720931, -0.0074278684332966805, 0.003226952627301216, 0.03069632314145565, -0.011997172608971596], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "6ccb1e9b66560550558a1140dd27561eef371e9ee56a8e117d7799de44b2edbe", "content": "This chunk is located in the section discussing Recommendation 5, which focuses on reinforcing social and emotional learning (SEL) skills through a whole-school ethos and activities. It emphasizes the importance of framing schoolwide norms positively, aligning routines, and integrating SEL into school systems to enhance student learning and well-being.Look to frame schoolwide norms in a positive manner rather than focusing on what not to do. When you have agreed your school\u2019s norms, they can be embedded into school-wide systems for recognition and reward. 71\nWhen messages, routines and strategies are aligned across the classroom and whole-school setting, students learn and apply social and emotional skills more rapidly and more effectively. 66 A large review of evidence related to SEL concludes that going beyond the curriculum to consider the whole school (for example, changes to school ethos, professional development, liaison with parents, community involvement, and coordinated work with outside agencies) is needed for maximising positive impacts. 67 However, the evidence underpinning the effectiveness of whole school approaches to SEL is less strong than the adoption of classroom-based SEL interventions; 68 they are also more challenging to implement due to the number and complexity of school systems that need to be addressed. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 32, "split_id": 108, "split_idx_start": 72073, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "098bc8e15ca93d54e9c77e6feac15de1a44c3db2b7cbdd9b2f2f9ac2e68fcded", "range": [677, 769]}, {"doc_id": "4f6147d2be7593bf085e35e09d31ec2d07130d147eea5b17318b0e7fb046f101", "range": [0, 286]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.079667828977108, -0.08372006565332413, 0.02002716436982155, 0.0011528527829796076, 0.0074547999538481236, 0.04794969782233238, 0.045243751257658005, -0.045445963740348816, 0.026178278028964996, -0.0007359563023783267, -0.0029541447293013334, 0.0063180215656757355, 0.015215858817100525, 0.021343637257814407, 0.023914366960525513, -0.050756487995386124, 0.0055440873838961124, 0.047773316502571106, 0.004755363799631596, -0.009493269957602024, -0.003405436873435974, 0.002883192151784897, 0.019535422325134277, -0.029651068150997162, 0.020002538338303566, -0.007190705742686987, 0.020849140360951424, 0.03691756725311279, -0.01743764989078045, -0.0509212389588356, 0.07313460111618042, 0.02132628671824932, -0.015924574807286263, -0.08004980534315109, 2.3839572804718046e-06, -0.03509476035833359, -0.025438744574785233, -0.029399804770946503, 0.046960778534412384, 0.012821606360375881, 0.040876202285289764, -0.011236605234444141, 0.021145274862647057, 0.02423703484237194, 0.005480340216308832, 0.012319757603108883, 0.020767252892255783, 0.06786488741636276, 0.0024657747708261013, 0.004135196562856436, 0.0033617080189287663, -0.008117800578474998, -0.039350464940071106, -0.0274405088275671, 0.037773847579956055, 0.031242793425917625, 0.016930243000388145, -0.013039426878094673, 0.02144918218255043, 0.006328450050204992, 0.005884039681404829, 0.011322690173983574, -0.01840486377477646, -0.04