2439128160477, -0.006433920934796333, -0.004297357983887196, 0.058699652552604675, 0.0037970240227878094, 0.007557286415249109, 0.005832601338624954, -0.07754041254520416, 0.03164450079202652, 0.002829173346981406, 0.04936669021844864, -0.044982727617025375, 0.0027988720685243607, -0.004810929298400879, 0.010968484915792942, 0.015545600093901157, -0.04481898620724678, -0.008398951962590218, -0.043833233416080475, 2.227370088210005e-34, 0.01440528966486454, -0.040121711790561676, -0.01695508509874344, -0.09723285585641861, 0.007082921918481588, -0.020189762115478516, -0.002651345683261752, 0.003158557927235961, 0.01974646747112274, 0.02712792530655861, -0.012957444414496422], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "57d35251ff3353d412a95be7c23c95099daf68844eb52b6f535d2d2e6fc12b36", "content": "This chunk is situated within the section discussing the importance of whole-school approaches to social and emotional learning (SEL) in primary schools. It highlights the limited evaluation of school councils and the effectiveness of a school action group from a recent trial, emphasizing how structured support and training can enhance school environments, reduce bullying, and improve student well-being.There has been little evaluation of school councils in primary schools to date. However, in a recent randomised trial of one SEL programme in 40 English secondary schools, a school \u2018action group\u2019 (comprising at least 6 pupils and 6 staff, meeting twice per term) was used to review and revise school-wide policies that could improve the school environment. Together with staff training in restorative practices and a SEL curriculum, this programme of support was found to lead to reductions in bullying, and increases in pupil well-being.70\nBox 10: School councils\f31Improving social and emotional learning in primary schools\nSEL routines\nSchool routines are important opportunities to introduce and reinforce SEL skills taught in the classroom. Here are examples of whole-school routines commonly used across evidence-based SEL programmes: \u2022 Regular school assemblies are devoted to children\u2019s social and emotional development, encouraging the use of particular skills or strategies for the week ahead. There might, for example, be a focus on helping others or respecting differences. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 32, "split_id": 110, "split_idx_start": 73695, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "4f6147d2be7593bf085e35e09d31ec2d07130d147eea5b17318b0e7fb046f101", "range": [911, 991]}, {"doc_id": "e43c0cca0c07e4cc8af602f95caccc11cc86d37d4e4650a83ebc7a9dec596849", "range": [0, 82]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06652338057756424, -0.06623928993940353, 0.005582458805292845, 0.0347754992544651, -0.015295787714421749, 0.05809452757239342, 0.05284842476248741, -0.03985990956425667, -0.0038105202838778496, -0.004466746933758259, 0.0461028590798378, -0.010610949248075485, 0.012325870804488659, -0.02368997037410736, 0.02628764696419239, -0.08931324630975723, 0.0038775557186454535, 0.05013356730341911, -0.017553383484482765, 0.01392342522740364, -0.003871918423101306, -0.011140218935906887, -0.002461508847773075, -0.003638940630480647, -0.010227948427200317, -0.02301902510225773, -0.012526380829513073, 0.029724635183811188, 0.021088428795337677, -0.013828597962856293, 0.0698583647608757, 0.014201327227056026, -0.032725848257541656, -0.04411013424396515, 2.22807261707203e-06, 0.015564698725938797, -0.009295430034399033, -0.01515313982963562, 0.03563404828310013, 0.031211214140057564, 0.020005779340863228, -0.021297171711921692, -0.00048246452934108675, 0.018274957314133644, 0.017678681761026382, 0.011253711767494678, 0.025706468150019646, 0.003528754925355315, 0.034187570214271545, -0.0015824424335733056, 0.0068731