the \ufb01t and feasibility with the school context\nPrepare practically e.g.\ntrain staff, develop\ninfrastructure\nSupport staff and solve problems using a \ufb02exible leadership approach\nReinforce initial training\nwith follow-on support\nwithin the school\nUse implementation data\nto drive faithful adoption\nand intelligent adaption\nPlan for sustaining and\nscaling the intervention\nfrom the outset\nContinuously acknowledge support and reward good implementation practices\nTreat scale-up as a new\nimplementation process\nSystematically explore programmes or practices to implement\nADOPTION DECISION\nSTABLE USE OF APPROACH\nDELIVERY BEGINS\nNOT READY\n- ADAPT PLAN\nREADY\nAssess the readiness of\nthe school to deliver the implementation plan\nDevelop a clear, logical and well speci\ufb01ed plan\nFigure 3: cycle of implementing changeTreat implementation as a process, not an event The EEF\u2019s guidance report, Putting Evidence to Work\u2014A School\u2019s Guide to Implementation, can support schools to think through the process of managing change around SEL. Figure 3 sets out the steps for successful implementation.\f36\nEducation Endowment Foundation Focus on implementation quality\nHow SEL approaches are implemented really matters. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 37, "split_id": 120, "split_idx_start": 84279, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f0ee75c1a4e56c28a307131479d6cbcf65a98de547d85c2ad107f05d0853db62", "range": [1066, 1287]}, {"doc_id": "1971ad3d45c22ff67b691b905a102f067c304b887f18337ad2dd4bba45ba2655", "range": [0, 117]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.048047225922346115, -0.06109211966395378, 0.004954892210662365, 0.005055885761976242, 0.0017426529666408896, 0.03823006525635719, -0.006118725519627333, -0.06530258059