745071, 0.07095187157392502, 0.03711143508553505, 0.08451820909976959, -0.011269562877714634, -0.018952714279294014, -0.03135938197374344, -0.02903212048113346, 0.03209702670574188, -0.03362385556101799, 0.0105994688346982, 0.08134529739618301, -0.06450249254703522, 0.0053644017316401005, 0.00544913113117218, 0.056522123515605927, 0.012854041531682014, 0.03275032341480255, 0.0013058183249086142, -0.09132397919893265, 0.014599844813346863, 0.002202450530603528, 0.035979803651571274, -0.010095259174704552, 0.021691160276532173, -0.012361966073513031, 0.002364157000556588, 0.018938884139060974, -0.03328099101781845, -0.0411541722714901, -0.05278726667165756, 2.1689528403376856e-34, 0.025895992293953896, -0.024875279515981674, 0.004734974354505539, -0.0650017112493515, 0.023766309022903442, -0.017889581620693207, -0.000673556060064584, 0.02551201358437538, 0.017573263496160507, 0.052871860563755035, -0.0186634361743927], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "e2b455cd95690b0e994592c4be473d353813aa63e93ff68ee489c283b2d6225a", "content": "This chunk is located in the section discussing the importance of providing training and support to school staff for effective implementation of Social and Emotional Learning (SEL) programs. It emphasizes that well-trained teachers can better embed SEL practices in their teaching, ultimately benefiting students\u2019 social and emotional development.88 This may be because there is more opportunity for practice to become embedded over time. A partial exception to this may be more targeted forms of support, where specialist input is likely to be more beneficial. 89\f37Improving social and emotional learning in primary schools\nProvide training and support to school staff\nChildren are more likely to benefit from SEL when staff receive training and the programme or practice is implemented well and embedded into everyday teaching and learning. 90 Teachers, however, often receive little or no training in how to promote these skills and report limited confidence in their ability to respond to students\u2019 emotional, social and behavioural needs. 91 Teachers who have received training related to SEL are more likely to agree that SEL has improved their relationship with their children, more likely to agree that emotion is fundamental to learning, and more likely to agree that their children had consistent behavioural goals between school and home. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 38, "split_id": 123, "split_idx_start": 87274, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "580cbd16b29d8fa90c0d75e5a9bf6d66bebb47d2d922523d3fc524b298fc71d0", "range": [751, 843]}, {"doc_id": "969d5edab8db29abf173c5f480cad7a6e70ed8bce509d9876d707bdc00101b39", "range": [0, 306]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.05769508332014084, -0.10344714671373367, -0.0021052975207567215, 0.02269953489303589, -0.007689045742154121, 0.07183084636926651, 0.051974888890981674, -0.054005708545446396, -0.01058947667479515, -0.0011480217799544334, 0.03613587096333504, 0.017736559733748436, 0.03465937077999115, -0.028429517522454262, 0.02812855876982212, -0.1136842891573906, -0.003840505378320813, 0.06573531776666641, -0.006837244611233473, 0.031249195337295532, 0.015084700658917427, 0.015961699187755585, 0.005421060603111982, -0.016976207494735718, -0.013638145290315151, 0.008614019490778446, -0.024612147361040115, 0.01944134198129177, -0.00012036746920784935, -0.03641420975327492, 0.04453826695680618, -0.0036460564006119967, 0.01300372276455164, -0.08957087248563766, 2.2014316982676974e-06, 0.00019790540682151914, -0.026946375146508217, -0.019372494891285896, 0.01662059873342514, 0.00022239284589886665, 0.01321418397128582, -0.027819344773888588, 0.02310546115040779, 0.02410302124917507, 0.015333982184529305, 0.02305293083190918, 0