embedding": null}, {"id": "969d5edab8db29abf173c5f480cad7a6e70ed8bce509d9876d707bdc00101b39", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing the importance of training and professional development for teachers in implementing Social and Emotional Learning (SEL) effectively in schools. It highlights the positive impact of such training on teacher-student relationships, emotional understanding, and behavioral consistency, and outlines key goals for professional development related to SEL.91 Teachers who have received training related to SEL are more likely to agree that SEL has improved their relationship with their children, more likely to agree that emotion is fundamental to learning, and more likely to agree that their children had consistent behavioural goals between school and home. 92\nProfessional development on SEL should broadly focus on meeting three key goals:\n1. Readiness for change. This involves ensuring that school staff recognise and agree with the perceived needs for the approach, and understanding the procedures and process for achieving the goal. 93\n2. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 39, "split_id": 124, "split_idx_start": 87972, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "e2b455cd95690b0e994592c4be473d353813aa63e93ff68ee489c283b2d6225a", "range": [698, 1004]}, {"doc_id": "1eaf5d32e89e1b904224b829b3756434e3391bdd74aaa969a33fea7a6deb7fc6", "range": [0, 6]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0544360876083374, -0.04959839954972267, -9.249972208635882e-05, 0.0008890895987860858, 0.0014049130259081721, 0.03719469904899597, 0.003696439554914832, -0.0709831565618515, -0.035999130457639694, 0.020255813375115395, 0.011722303926944733, 0.025785621255636215, 0.015603503212332726, 0.012732217088341713, 0.013383469544351101, -0.1