g": null}, {"id": "ea86bd5f460abc18d3f13b099c274a6d3518c337f4237e4ec200fec6b4b512eb", "content": "This chunk is part of Recommendation 6, which emphasizes the importance of planning, supporting, and monitoring the implementation of social and emotional learning (SEL) in schools. It discusses how schools can effectively evaluate their SEL strategies through regular monitoring, feedback collection, and the use of measurement tools to enhance their approaches and outcomes.Schools should ensure that their monitoring and evaluation is proportionate to the scale of their needs and efforts (and doesn\u2019t become a further barrier). As a starting point, regular, low-intensity and efficient auditing is likely to be helpful\u2014focused on indicators that are proxies for SEL development, such as pupil behaviour or well-being, or teacher perceptions. Collecting regular feedback by surveys from children and staff on issues like class or school climate is relatively straight-forward, could help to identify ongoing issues, and should also promote a positive culture in which the school listens to and responds to needs. This is likely to provide valuable information for:\n\u2022 identifying needs;\n\u2022 focusing efforts; and\n\u2022 checking whether approaches are having an impact.\nTo extend these efforts schools should also consider assessing children\u2019s SEL development using validated measurement tools. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Social_and_Emotional_Learning.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1ux2ZVY-H62jpu0xzPvuWIaW6mMGtPxRN", "source_id": "e8d637c88ad0e99d399f844be26e40bf15211fc84f01bf87ff947205064caf09", "page_number": 40, "split_id": 129, "split_idx_start": 90949, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "c02c37cfbb1a17715092d72f1e2765c25b9f3117ae16657097a0f5ad49c7e302", "range": [714, 870]}, {"doc_id": "19b1e5ddbc570f147db7fe428d11c6f616f2e711673d668b11394c69a314b173", "range": [0, 125]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04105059