0.012055263854563236, 0.03610559552907944, 0.01502075046300888, -0.013392423279583454, 0.001584499143064022, -0.05608436465263367, 0.00632782606408, -0.03685012087225914, 0.04470992833375931, -0.07177946716547012, -0.035758595913648605, 0.028689255937933922, -0.02036455273628235, 0.026035016402602196, -0.01167514268308878, -0.041641414165496826, -0.03198042884469032, 2.5035146037935363e-34, 0.007563169579952955, 0.006141208577901125, 0.004637689795345068, -0.07808341830968857, -0.014786832965910435, -0.04161059111356735, 0.06389199942350388, 0.015747927129268646, 0.02376210317015648, 0.013856588862836361, -0.04934733361005783], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "5016ffe253c0dfc058b857209c21e8fe451dd05d8761f6f9e2bc44a63c310a44", "content": "The chunk is located in the Foreword of the guidance report on Special Educational Needs in Mainstream Schools. In this section, Professor Becky Francis emphasizes the importance of collaboration with education professionals to enhance support for vulnerable pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND) and highlights the goal of closing the disadvantage gap.By engaging with professionals to deliver a research-led approach we can realise our mutual aim to support the attainment and life-chances of some of our most vulnerable pupils. Professor Becky Francis\nChief Executive\nEducation Endowment Foundation\n\u201cClosing the disadvantage gap means finding better ways to support pupils with SEND.\u201d\nFOREWORD\n50 40\n30\n20\n10 0\nAverage Attainment 8 score per pupil\nPupils with SEN\nPupils eligible for FSM\nOther Pupils\f3Special Educational Needs in Mainstream Schools 3\nINTRODUCTION\nWhat does this guidance cover? This report presents five recommendations for mainstream primary and secondary schools seeking to improve their provision for pupils with SEND. Some of the recommendations included here will also be helpful for pupils in special schools, although we recognise that the approaches might need to be adapted and supplemented with specialist support for pupils with profound learning needs. The EEF is currently considering how it can support special schools in the future with tailored guidance and resources.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 4, "split_id": 7, "split_idx_start": 4382, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "01573e5cada17a9894236b46aa1788af18580233ef9219f5ac6a4d96d059c3de", "range": [590, 768]}, {"doc_id": "e1b74a520d7a3c5c1dcb5d8c68e85f6d1b986c8db34a4bab415f07fed11b7f87", "range": [0, 120]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.02749319188296795, -0.10827095061540604, -0.008911876939237118, 0.004785539116710424, 0.0035871933214366436, 0.03309423103928566, 0.04736411198973656, -0.038017917424440384, 0.001352196792140603, -0.003386472584679723, 0.061736784875392914, -0.02455640770494938, 0.05731881782412529, 0.004695541225373745, 0.01612972840666771, -0.06699250638484955, 0.03148587420582771, 0.04327782988548279, -0.06178867816925049, 0.02383686602115631, -0.03343655914068222, 0.00631733937188983, -0.012907344847917557, 0.01401323638856411, -0.0011901158140972257, -0.020650213584303856, 0.0169881209731102, 0.02529650181531906, 0.0008818126516416669, -0.013238122686743736, 0.06099405139684677, 0.026545198634266853, -0.020186156034469604, -0.06167298182845116, 2.276173745485721e-06, 0.010681895539164543, 0.022339850664138794, -0.005319508723914623, -0.005819116253405809, -0.0018125377828255296, -0.09489689022302628, 0.009643721394240856, 0.003269003238528967, 0.051267072558403015, -0.00025921131600625813, 0.03532793000340462, 0.01164811197668314, -0.034347351640462875, -0.014477875083684921, -0.014836866408586502, 0.009110750630497932, -0.026687435805797577, 0.01039128564298153, -0.042615387588739395, 0