ents, teaching assistants, educational researchers, and programme developers, can utilize the guidance to enhance support for pupils with SEND in mainstream schools.\u2022 School governors can use the guidance to support and challenge their school leadership on SEND. \u2022 Parents, carers, and families may find the guidance useful to inform their interactions with schools. \u2022 The strategies recommended in this guidance are highly relevant to the work of teaching assistants. Schools can find additional resources on the EEF site.\n\u2022 Educational researchers can work to fill in the gaps in the evidence base identified in this report and the associated evidence review.1 \u2022 Programme developers can use the evidence in this guidance to develop more effective programmes.\f", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 5, "split_id": 13, "split_idx_start": 8016, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "10b14adab5ad0ac834eb5a27e1b5571d9afc9839354531314a5856837656f5d2", "range": [593, 691]}, {"doc_id": "83785fe85eb80f0c5383c676a1228dcbcb4216305fbd4c7ca58bea61de57a095", "range": [0, 238]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.05537133291363716, -0.09630504250526428, -0.013730259612202644, 0.007516199257224798, 0.005657278001308441, 0.04777512326836586, 0.03403685986995697, -0.026682086288928986, -0.010317651554942131, -0.0059372177347540855, 0.06265130639076233, -0.02371908538043499, 0.046789344400167465, 0.014594636857509613, 0.03178122639656067, -0.08518563956022263, 0.03540225327014923, 0.030315952375531197, -0.051618896424770355, 0.02547159045934677, -0.011567234992980957, 0.019493939355015755, -0.025296414270997047, 0.018048172816634178, 0.008037716150283813, -0.03919428586959839, 0.01398005336523056, 0.0261709187179803