 0.025460880249738693, -0.02152818813920021, 0.015528042800724506, -0.015376175753772259, -0.05875080078840256, -0.022969212383031845, 2.6208417969750627e-34, -0.006237296853214502, 0.0018959346925839782, -0.00908966176211834, -0.08881466835737228, -0.004410420544445515, -0.02458282560110092, 0.0413019023835659, -0.00939368735998869, -0.016170639544725418, 0.006845691706985235, -0.04720805585384369], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "83785fe85eb80f0c5383c676a1228dcbcb4216305fbd4c7ca58bea61de57a095", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Introduction\" section, where the document outlines how various stakeholders, including educational researchers and programme developers, can utilize the guidance provided about Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND) to enhance educational practices and fill gaps in the existing evidence base.\u2022 Educational researchers can work to fill in the gaps in the evidence base identified in this report and the associated evidence review.1 \u2022 Programme developers can use the evidence in this guidance to develop more effective programmes.\f4\nEducation Endowment Foundation INTRODUCTION\nActing on this guidance\nMajor decisions about your school\u2019s approach to Special Educational Needs are likely to be most effective if made in conjunction with a range of stakeholders including parents, carers and families, teaching and non-teaching staff, pupils, and specialist outside agencies. To maximise its impact, this report should be read in conjunction with other EEF guidance, including Putting Evidence to Work: A School\u2019s Guide to Implementation. This report is designed to complement the statutory guidance on SEND as set out in Special Educational Needs and Disability Code of Practice: 0\u201325 years . Schools may also want to seek support from our Research Schools at r esearchschool.org.uk a national network of schools funded by the EEF and the Institute for Effective Education to support teachers to implement the evidence-based recommendations contained in our guidance reports and keep them in touch with the latest research. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 5, "split_id": 14, "split_idx_start": 8375, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "ac74a939422b735a7ac09eb7226b580248a2dc3163d6e3e127879c5637b867ae", "range": [359, 597]}, {"doc_id": "b4382458f894ea2e6ccc63546b166bb40304a706afb906a5bf439712bdf7837b", "range": [0, 331]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.01703217253088951, -0.09759487956762314, -0.0027267856057733297, -0.006837868597358465, 0.0029133977368474007, 0.031094178557395935, 0.03271489590406418, -0.043376315385103226, -0.002926679328083992, -0.021700818091630936, 0.059664536267519, -0.02530968002974987, 0.05057048797607422, 0.029011256992816925, 0.0318317748606205, -0.08479838073253632, 0.020770631730556488, 0.025680677965283394, -0.052954137325286865, 0.017875397577881813, -0.004100285470485687, 0.004032440483570099, -0.029223313555121422, 0.001001277007162571, 0.010576908476650715, -0.026586415246129036, -0.0029571987688541412, 0.042158905416727066, -0.0001567784493090585, -0.04098395258188248, 0.04225170612335205, 0.06545019149780273, 0.016362648457288742, -0.049184076488018036, 2.3996890377020463e-06, 0.028820432722568512, 0.03497512638568878, -0.01073396485298872, 0.0006196207250468433, -0.029026437550783157, -0.08614508807659149, -0.029430069029331207, 0.036014676094055176, 0.042311377823352814, 0.029552452266216278, 0.020990611985325813, 0.046360570937395096, -0.014143399894237518, 0.012103371322154999, -0.03228530287742615, -0.0011268764501437545, 0.0022178234066814184, 0.0013470810372382402, -0.02034468948841095, 0.07304703444242477, 0.018846791237592697, 0.009878304786980152, -0.0659690722823143, 0.0