9, 0.022603632882237434, -0.02973807416856289, 0.037332288920879364, 0.00010902178473770618, 0.0334819033741951, -0.025679849088191986, 0.07896807789802551, -0.038188379257917404, 0.004015016369521618, -0.026788903400301933, -0.02920244261622429, 0.03779549151659012, 0.03231867030262947, 0.0340755470097065, 0.053545281291007996, -0.0058285994455218315, -0.0011610889341682196, -0.003874710528180003, 0.039492327719926834, 0.012711001560091972, -0.0040183300152421, 0.005022053606808186, -0.06777144223451614, 0.03541466221213341, -0.030263274908065796, 0.07988034933805466, -0.042521968483924866, -0.03440828248858452, -0.021927017718553543, -0.0019225017167627811, 0.033503852784633636, -0.02846253663301468, -0.03570926934480667, -0.018211504444479942, 2.0502354873330676e-34, 0.019969230517745018, 0.004573097452521324, 0.007877876982092857, -0.07974527776241302, 0.008018353953957558, -0.02743326500058174, 0.04398409277200699, 0.007226768881082535, 0.007796246092766523, -0.06308859586715698, -0.04996633902192116], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "1f3c02afd83173e77b7e81c6dfd4d2637249346191e650d3330cc7b6cd9aebe3", "content": "This chunk is found in the \"Introduction\" section of the guidance report, specifically under a discussion about the importance of inclusive language when referring to students with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It highlights a teacher's perspective on accommodating diverse learning needs and the role of parental involvement in supporting children with SEND at home.Parents are involved in regular reading and talk activities at home. The other two SEND Support pupils have provision made for a moderate learning difficulty and the other for their social, emotional, and mental health needs.\u2019\nBox 1: A teachers\u2019 view of needs in their classroom \u201c \u201c\nLanguage matters\u2014talking about SEND\n\u2018Pupils are SEND\u2019\nIt is not helpful to say that a pupil \u2018is SEND\u2019 or \u2018there are SEND pupils in our class\u2019, and this language may undermine efforts to establish and maintain high expectations for the learning of all pupils. It is more helpful to say pupils \u2018have SEND\u2019 or \u2018there are pupils with SEND\u2019 within a class. SEND is not a fixed or permanent characteristic; it is a recognition that at a specific time a child has additional learning needs. At times, many pupils will require tailored or additional support to fully participate in everything the school has to offer.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 7, "split_id": 19, "split_idx_start": 12948, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "83405c53b97306516900cf22d1cd2cd03f5cf2dcf0dfc65f7a01b4d964e181b8", "range": [642, 711]}, {"doc_id": "9f31cdf38a6c3da451e9a35d4d973da0db938fb6af577122ef117a66428aafdf", "range": [0, 126]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.02744195982813835, -0.09766868501901627, -0.004910803399980068, 0.02506246790289879, 0.010496829636394978, 0.02918490394949913, 0.04102917015552521, -0.01962977834045887, -0.007516517303884029, -0.043947212398052216, 0.03797706961631775, -0.06930921971797943, 0.025159887969493866, -0.01448321808129549, -0.0031628285069018602, -0.0485202856361866, 0.030149409547448158, 0.05925857275724411, -0.06076614186167717, 0.018261676654219627, -0.013025932013988495, 0.03386380895972252, -0.009605268016457558, 0.026814652606844902, 0.007629557978361845, -0.04093364626169205, 0.013015457428991795, 0.006831868086010218, 0.0023380049970000982, 0.030914951115846634, 0.08307250589132309, 0.01906179077923298, -0.0031600710935890675, -0.030388804152607918, 2.3063093976816162e-06, 0.03494122624397278, 0.018688982352614403, -0.014081723988056183, -0.026114247739315033, -0.026915917173027992, -0.055688980966