9344559, -0.011216199025511742, 0.00662981579080224, -0.012926185503602028], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "9f31cdf38a6c3da451e9a35d4d973da0db938fb6af577122ef117a66428aafdf", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Introduction\" section of the guidance report, which discusses the variability in pupils' special educational needs and disabilities (SEND). It emphasizes the need for tailored support and challenges the misconception that SEND is a fixed condition, highlighting how pupils\u2019 needs may evolve over time.At times, many pupils will require tailored or additional support to fully participate in everything the school has to offer.\nChallenging the view that \u2018a pupil with SEND will always have SEND\u2019\nPupils\u2019 development is not linear. As pupils age, the complexity of their needs will change. Some pupils might not have SEND to begin with but will develop SEND as they mature. Others who are considered to have SEND at the beginning of their lives may no longer have these needs later in life. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 7, "split_id": 20, "split_idx_start": 13715, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "1f3c02afd83173e77b7e81c6dfd4d2637249346191e650d3330cc7b6cd9aebe3", "range": [767, 893]}, {"doc_id": "7cdfb7b423cabf09699057fd7bd83d179f8a038e816ca907c26ee367f78a0790", "range": [0, 117]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.02411356382071972, -0.06251242011785507, -0.013366342522203922, -0.016025690361857414, 0.008091644383966923, 0.013775801286101341, -0.0035682397428900003, -0.03739824891090393, 0.017132066190242767, -0.0013111220905557275, 0.06890233606100082, -0.050140876322984695, 0.025276295840740204, 0.00026863053790293634, -0.013819212093949318, -0.10687252879142761, 0.0133219