87470cd57c6b1d66f4986fa02d6d377d93fe0", "content": "This chunk is situated within the \"Introduction\" section of the guidance report, which discusses the variability of special educational needs categorized under the SEND Code of Practice. It emphasizes that individual needs can differ significantly even within the same category, illustrating the complexity of understanding and addressing these needs in educational settings.There is variation within each of the four categories in the Code of Practice. For example, two pupils who both have needs related to communication and interaction could have quite different individual needs; one might have difficulty producing or understanding the sounds of spoken language while the other might struggle to understand conventions of social interaction, such as turn-taking in conversations. In some cases, difficulties in one area will lead to difficulties in another. For example, a child with Speech, Language, and Communications Needs (SLCN) may also present with literacy learning difficulties as a result of the SLCN. In other cases, it may be that needs co-occur. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 9, "split_id": 27, "split_idx_start": 18036, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "9203db6c5ef51fd41767f4ce1e86717a112affe80cbcfa748a601e767014d473", "range": [782, 861]}, {"doc_id": "6280c189f34a08435b2647a25a9c1062c9a1ee2505535fdbfd7272c99a601a45", "range": [0, 47]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04141171649098396, -0.10687699913978577, -0.024260174483060837, 0.028235014528036118, -0.01917991228401661, 0.058145951479673386, 0.03737754002213478, -0.0141621557995677, -0.02678275667130947, -0.003793182084336877, 0.04506899416446686, -0.07588104158639908, 0.07520632445812225, 