363285, -0.009698837995529175, -0.05550341308116913], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "7ce7b02f52135d5e3a24f5ccf0223b59cba5e0110ae75f4004eb528543e184c0", "content": "This chunk is part of Recommendation 5, which discusses the effective use of teaching assistants (TAs) in supporting pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It emphasizes the importance of TAs complementing classroom teaching and highlights the need for careful implementation of interventions to ensure they benefit pupils with SEND.School leaders should pay careful attention to the roles of TAs and ensure they have a positive impact on pupils with SEND.\n\u2022 TAs should supplement, not replace, teaching from the classroom teacher. \u2022 The EEF\u2019s guidance report Making Best Use of Teaching Assistants provides detailed recommendations. Page 36\nWork effectively with teaching assistants\n5\n\u2022 Small-group and one-to-one interventions can be a powerful tool but must be used carefully. Ineffective use of interventions can create a barrier to the inclusion of pupils with SEND. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 11, "split_id": 31, "split_idx_start": 21036, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "97bf4db6bc3578d94c5229db6a786246274a1fdf8d63997477748d2a5cc4f304", "range": [803, 927]}, {"doc_id": "8f89249447f175d4a553f194ec4cd48403fc3d671f02a666ad412c18e20f7307", "range": [0, 92]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.030108189210295677, -0.10384583473205566, -0.021851522848010063, 0.006451316177845001, 0.027595825493335724, 0.004053478129208088, 0.05797922983765602, -0.06933456659317017, -0.0032633966766297817, -0.00604971032589674, 0.04152625799179077, -0.02837217226624489, 0.019926883280277252, -0.01912376657128334, 0.0