2271408215165, 0.04743576422333717, -0.025217656046152115, -0.03752116858959198, -0.05812355875968933, 2.271695867963102e-34, -0.014501901343464851, -0.013133453205227852, 0.021746790036559105, -0.08018659800291061, -0.011804305948317051, -0.03706812486052513, 0.057475801557302475, -0.001396720064803958, 0.01395359542220831, 0.016694430261850357, -0.05313478037714958], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "d948d9205a8838464ecbb505fc79d0bfb463cecd3998291d3b0dc76016c47829", "content": "This chunk is part of the recommendation that emphasizes the importance of high-quality teaching for all pupils, particularly those with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It suggests specific strategies teachers should develop, including flexible grouping and scaffolding, to ensure inclusive and effective teaching practices in mainstream schools.Teachers should develop a repertoire of these strategies they can use flexibly in response to the needs of all pupils. \u2014 flexible grouping; \u2014 cognitive and metacognitive strategies; \u2014 explicit instruction; \u2014 using technology to support pupils with SEND; and \u2014 scaffolding. Page 22\nEnsure all pupils have access to high quality teaching\n3\f10\nEducation Endowment Foundation 1\nCreate a positive and supportive environment for all pupils without exception\nCreating a positive and supportive environment for all pupils means placing support for pupils with SEND at the heart of school priorities\u2014being inclusive by design. This approach to pupils with SEND should be reinforced in the language, activities, routines, and strategies across the classroom as well as whole-\nschool settings. This chapter explores how to create a positive and supportive environment for all pupils with SEND by promoting positive relationships and active engagement for all pupils\u2014by including all pupils in the best teaching you can offer and adopting a positive and proactive approach to behaviour for learning.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 11, "split_id": 34, "split_idx_start": 22554, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "a1772c31f099d98269f1f129111f38e43ef4cb8a631c7fabe1bd85822b013b45", "range": [605, 724]}, {"doc_id": "38d867aec36198d2bbf866ac1e485126500159c08554010cc407fc77109e62fc", "range": [0, 305]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03237432613968849, -0.1099032312631607, -0.028535597026348114, 0.007802555803209543, 0.02964947558939457, 0.004743628669530153, 0.009203416295349598, -0.06017352640628815, -0.01527456846088171, 0.00762229273095727, 0.01544650737196207, -0.027569644153118134, 0.02805139310657978, -0.008397414349019527, 0.026480209082365036, -0.1409524530172348, 0.0319189615547657, 0.031696368008852005, -0.06791801005601883, 0.028485357761383057, -0.029908789321780205, 0.012184531427919865, -0.009112090803682804, -0.025076868012547493, -0.015351979061961174, -0.022312471643090248, 0.01074349507689476, 0.029342766851186752, 0.03953414782881737, 0.005418180953711271, 0.0493086613714695, 0.033902835100889206, -0.0006451495573855937, -0.03607665374875069, 2.238771003248985e-06, 0.04040995240211487, -0.005715991370379925, -0.035016659647226334, -0.008993840776383877, -0.04315745085477829, -0.063682422041893, -0.023255640640854836, 0.012423336505889893, 0.051735468208789825, -0.0013402201002463698, 0.06626679003238678, -0.010489712469279766, -0.02924630232155323, 0.06351099908351898, -0.03740125149488449, 0.005624813959002495, 0.000852719706017524, -0.026278754696249962, -0.001305146492086351, 0.05378086492419243, -0.00268450821749866, -0.017459934577345848, -0.05205122008919716, 0.04146616905927658, -0.00658305361866951, -0.021090740337967873, 0.024089809507131577, 0.006034763064235449, -0.061941973865032196, 0.0309