lusive practices within schools, illustrated through the example of Maria, a headteacher addressing her new role.This chapter explores how to create a positive and supportive environment for all pupils with SEND by promoting positive relationships and active engagement for all pupils\u2014by including all pupils in the best teaching you can offer and adopting a positive and proactive approach to behaviour for learning.\nMaria is a headteacher in a new role in September. Her new school has a much higher number of students with special educational needs than her previous school and she knows that supporting these children is a priority.\nHer first instinct is to speak to the SENCo and understand the interventions and additional support in place for pupils with SEND; however, she doesn\u2019t want to limit her attention to interventions and extras. How can she ensure inclusivity runs through every part of the school? ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 12, "split_id": 35, "split_idx_start": 23337, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "d948d9205a8838464ecbb505fc79d0bfb463cecd3998291d3b0dc76016c47829", "range": [783, 1088]}, {"doc_id": "c625c7f2fcf561f85b4d865bf913e6d60c19458e399ba104def1117ad0f5df4e", "range": [0, 70]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.033578213304281235, -0.09298744797706604, -0.016481826081871986, 0.02230847254395485, 0.020134560763835907, 0.012571417726576328, -0.007446934003382921, -0.039664462208747864, -0.005351410247385502, 0.018042465671896935, 0.03796667233109474, -0.03502554073929787, 0.031408000737428665, 0.0069929757155478, 5.972452345304191e-05, -0.09621162712574005, 0.02462540753185749, 0.03815878555178642, -0.08200317621231079, 0.008904598653316498, -0.01077441405504942, 0.00913615