319397, -0.03253481164574623, 0.028564969077706337, -0.0317918062210083, 0.008973582647740841, -0.03718331456184387, 0.02819252759218216, 0.03273169696331024, -0.015627391636371613, -0.007217879872769117, 0.015862803906202316, 0.03051726706326008, 0.008131247013807297, 0.027423180639743805, -0.019139502197504044, -0.011512485332787037, -0.014207719825208187, -0.026016613468527794, 0.03869987279176712, 0.006009313277900219, 0.02748526819050312, 0.038780685514211655, -0.015321571379899979, -0.0053068529814481735, 0.04936594516038895, 0.039823804050683975, 0.007445766590535641, -0.03550521656870842, 0.008516896516084671, -0.060128942131996155, 0.013481964357197285, -0.006982653867453337, 0.03495214134454727, -0.03572476655244827, -0.027503427118062973, 0.012761373072862625, -0.018613385036587715, 0.018182937055826187, -0.0257708802819252, -0.02761835791170597, -0.06034981459379196, 1.8489729465505412e-34, -0.025575971230864525, 0.003250101814046502, 0.014123568311333656, -0.07695948332548141, -0.019841574132442474, -0.0358240082859993, 0.10097775608301163, -0.0058637335896492004, 0.050434909760951996, 0.0072642359882593155, -0.05501159653067589], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "7d38a59947f82ab7f91262cbc1edec4c518a5d3c783d3669ab42459801b57e09", "content": "This chunk is from the section discussing the findings of a significant research project on U.K. pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It highlights the detrimental effects of separating pupils with Education, Health and Care (EHC) plans from mainstream classrooms, and the implications of streaming on their educational experience and quality of teaching received.The largest observational research project conducted on U.K. pupils with SEND found that, in primary schools, pupils with EHC plans experienced a high degree of separation from the classroom, teacher, and peers.13 (It should be noted that the majority of the pupils in the study outlined here had a primary need related to cognition and learning, and the results, therefore, do not claim to be representative of other types of SEND.)\nThe research project found that, in Year 5, these pupils spent over a quarter of their time away from the mainstream class, most often with other pupils identified as \u2018low-attaining\u2019 or as having SEND. In secondary settings, pupils with SEND experienced a form of \u2018streaming\u2019 where lower-attaining pupils and those with SEND were taught alongside each other away from their average- and higher-attaining peers. 12 This situation could lead to pupils with SEND experiencing a lower quality of teaching, especially if provided by a less-\nexperienced or less-qualified member of staff (see Recommendation 5). Wider evidence from the EEF Teaching and Learning Toolkit also shows that, on average, streaming (or setting) has a negative impact for low-attaining pupils. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 14, "split_id": 45, "split_idx_start": 30961, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "de2d4f61d31f6a1f97306a518ce7fd3ad93beccb9d1b5e348d6427ac24e001b0", "range": [882, 1316]}, {"doc_id": "df163658c8e1126a469c276c7937b4b3a5167363d5bcc3a547fbc2a5ed386581", "range": [0, 158]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [-0.007431767415255308, -0.09030336141586304, -0.016679709777235985, -0.00932028703391552, -0.012399707920849323, 0.04777330905199051, 0.043668363243341446, -0.03836999833583832, -0.0026894251350313425, -0.028314869850873947, 0.04264773428440094, -0.053281206637620926, 0.03102087415754795, 0.02539723925292492, 0.01537305023521185, -0.08881372213363647, 0.011578875593841076, 0.027417218312621117, -0.07517119497060776, 0.025504104793071747, -0.012341652996838093, -0.008866268210113049, -0.016060784459114075, 0