92139816284, 0.022752536460757256, 0.015976503491401672, 0.010031834244728088, 0.005210695322602987, -0.06406469643115997], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "ab642ea658a93de0a1e1f8c8ee523c92f304d3833c0b5d3306493d029dd32fb7", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing the importance of understanding individual learning needs of pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It highlights a specific scenario involving a teacher, Mark, who faces challenges in adapting his teaching strategies effectively for a diverse class with various needs, reflecting the guidance's emphasis on tailored support and informed practice.Mark is preparing to welcome his class for the year. It is a class with diverse needs: some of the pupils have an autism diagnosis, others have a speech and language difficulty, and there is one pupil with moderate learning difficulties. Mark knows that some of his pupils will need additional support but is unsure how to interpret the general information he has in order to meet their individual needs effectively. He has looked at the guidance provided centrally by the school SENCo but is struggling to convert this knowledge into practical steps.\nDiscussion questions:\nHow might the diagnostic labels of some pupils alter approaches to teaching?\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 16, "split_id": 51, "split_idx_start": 35898, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "e048c4cf8836f786655b130bb79802f8063d9b1291e6d439ee115170ecd68357", "range": [1170, 1223]}, {"doc_id": "771a233e34964e8b25c0ffba1d8e339001282af53f5c59d797042d74066ede2f", "range": [0, 99]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0484691746532917, -0.09094876796007156, -0.03079533763229847, 0.034295372664928436, -0.0