0b3e22771836959d523559134", "content": "This chunk is part of the recommendation focused on building a holistic understanding of pupils' learning needs, emphasizing the importance of gathering information from various stakeholders, including teachers, parents, and external professionals. It illustrates the practical application of this approach through the example of a student named Sam transitioning from primary to secondary education.What are their strengths, interests, and aspirations?\nWhat support do they need to access the curriculum?\nHow can the school\u2019s provision be improved to support this pupil to learn?\f16\nEducation Endowment Foundation Assess\u2014build a holistic picture of the pupil\u2019s learning needs by gathering information from several sources, such as the pupil, parents and carers, colleagues, and external professionals. Sam\u2019s primary and secondary SENCos and Year 6 teacher met to share information at transition from Year 6 to Year 7. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 17, "split_id": 56, "split_idx_start": 40004, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "7063d9387879b2395075dc388dce23ab1df27a23cb5a9c7c9656faa9596e0d14", "range": [610, 664]}, {"doc_id": "caae48d5d33f9b1f8a7f3ed13161032ff3f2bb20214d6223be1394537b9929c3", "range": [0, 116]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.031833093613386154, -0.0783408135175705, -0.013052280060946941, -0.004164983052760363, -0.0031020566821098328, 0.008249292150139809, -0.009275966323912144, -0.05666274577379227, -0.003584119724109769, 0.011621978133916855, 0.016587795689702034, -8.751658606342971e-05, 0.03798210620880127, -0.03371758386492729, -0.04072614759206772, -0.11378657817840576, 0.011821159161627293, 0.009975751861929893, -0.05611166357