141185760498, -0.04887090250849724, 0.012414412572979927, -0.00775872590020299, 0.06763151288032532, 0.0042336019687354565, -0.03972062095999718, -0.03255145996809006, 0.0032063915859907866, -0.020289765670895576, -0.012122581712901592, -0.02856207825243473, -0.03732270002365112, 2.148227864742231e-34, 0.009774502366781235, 0.0014286373043432832, 0.04542133957147598, -0.08150777965784073, -0.013850163668394089, -0.030945762991905212, 0.0547519326210022, 0.006552889943122864, 0.02395615726709366, -0.03636910766363144, -0.04219452291727066], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "b70f28cd0df4ce424fdf44a9413be4d18675079d5e97cb0179494e832a55f4b7", "content": "This chunk is part of a dialogue during a parents' evening, discussing a pupil's speech and language difficulties and the potential intervention from a Speech and Language Therapist. It exemplifies the collaborative approach between teachers and parents in addressing the educational needs of a child with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND), reflecting the holistic understanding recommended in the guidance report.Have you noticed anything? Children can be very different at school\u2014 we\u2019ve noticed she isn\u2019t very clear when she speaks with us. Would it be okay if we asked the Speech and Language Therapist to work with her?\nShe is really making progress. Although she didn\u2019t pass the Phonics Screening Check, I\u2019m confident the extra support will help her to pass in Year 2.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 19, "split_id": 63, "split_idx_start": 43510, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "666394dd92d3407b3acd8de25b2a7e68c2a06bafa51b89ed741580e9e4b9ee47", "range": [417, 444]}, {"doc_id": "9981f1b8c09f42395a48d28aa2b200e286ac8142