089242219924927, -0.015054874122142792, 0.007631961721926928, 0.011333754286170006, -0.05455728992819786, 0.027532070875167847, -0.042581308633089066, 0.06052122265100479, -0.025114931166172028, -0.05201767757534981, 0.01890883594751358, -0.0321333110332489, -0.04527631774544716, -0.036160506308078766, -0.05644867941737175, 0.019893724471330643, 2.116832293259439e-34, 0.01157747209072113, -0.0005848111468367279, 0.021661629900336266, -0.0280025415122509, -0.00237030116841197, -0.035457171499729156, 0.01794528402388096, 0.02186562493443489, 0.010163255035877228, -0.020828140899538994, -0.0411033034324646], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "64dbe598f87f80bf0a49d19a6993aa5aa25454be7fd495c8b2f6e26a08afdd13", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing the importance of involving parents and carers in the assessment and decision-making processes for pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It emphasizes the collaborative approach required to build a holistic understanding of each child's needs during transitions between year groups and various school stages.How can we help you thrive?\nSecondary SENCo\nPrimary SENCo\n:)\nIn the playground, first week at school...\nYear 1 to Year 2 transition\nYear 5\nParents\u2019 Evening, six weeks later...\nIn the classroom, a week later...\nTransition meeting\n1\n3\n5\n7\n2\n4\n6\n8\nYear 4 parents\u2019 evening\nBuilding a holistic picture of the child\u2026\nFigure 3: Comic strip\u2014an holistic approach to \u2018assess, plan, do, review\u2019\f18\nEducation Endowment Foundation Including parents and carers\nThe SEND Code of Practice makes it clear that pupils, parents, and carers must be actively involved in the assessment and decision-making process for pupils with SEND at all stages. In particular, schools must make sure that:\n\u2022 \u2018Information gathering should include an early discussion with the pupil and their parents. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_S