tions or strategies to use will be informed by discussions with the SENCo, parents and carers, and\u2014especially if the pupil has an EHC plan\u2014relevant external professionals. More guidance on specialist intervention is provided in Recommendation 4. A newly qualified teacher, Binda, only received limited information about supporting pupils with SEND in her initial teacher training. She is conscious that she needs to learn more but a lot of the information on offer is contradictory. Binda starts exploring particular interventions and strategies commonly associated with different diagnostic labels but it is difficult to work out what is likely to be effective. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 22, "split_id": 75, "split_idx_start": 51225, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f8f38728f539d314b4d83ce88debae0536803c323d24d900e57c829990568d79", "range": [1623, 1836]}, {"doc_id": "43a2e99b0f990b227e20e407db5d43f08c51e694a669bedf033a3d6c67b91aa3", "range": [0, 180]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04120572283864021, -0.09686683863401413, 0.00416978495195508, -0.003520364174619317, 0.014141560532152653, 0.013606308028101921, 0.010554857552051544, -0.010215256363153458, 0.0037981432396918535, -0.012799861840903759, 0.05436340346932411, -0.03775426372885704, 0.010395212098956108, 0.0014839207287877798, -0.017285745590925217, -0.10594317317008972, -0.015247859060764313, 0.01359914243221283, -0.01750844344496727, 0.022684255614876747, 0.003916780464351177, 0.031148657202720642, -0.027725763618946075, 0.004827529191970825, 0.010304923169314861, -0.049147311598062515, 0.039815232157707214, 0.018447887152433395, 0.05063355341553688, -0.025020714849233627, 0.054900962859392166, 0.029917476698756218, -0.022415310144