red visual aids like Venn diagrams and mind maps in enhancing understanding and organization of knowledge for these pupils.Planets are large natural objects that travel (or orbit) around stars. From the Greek \u2018plan\u0113tes\u2019, meaning \u2018wanderers\u2019.\nAn example: graphic organisers\nGraphic organisers represent a cognitive strategy that has been extensively researched with pupils with SEND.30 Graphic organisers are used to organise knowledge, concepts, and ideas. Examples include Venn diagrams\u2014for example, the Venn diagram illustrating the overlap between the two concepts \u2018SEN\u2019 and \u2018disability\u2019 in English law\u2014T-charts of pros and cons, mind-maps, cognitive maps, semantic maps, and chronologies or event chains. They can be effective tools for supporting learning. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 25, "split_id": 90, "split_idx_start": 58379, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "c089ad6c5f4c4b91ad8c71b44eae1863bcdee928f887a52b0c8910a4b939eeaa", "range": [268, 339]}, {"doc_id": "69f156fa8207b156862629395468090afb3053879982bddad7041b35e63ba95a", "range": [0, 53]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.02415652945637703, -0.08806014806032181, -0.038495734333992004, 0.017812909558415413, -0.015521361492574215, 0.014028710313141346, 0.06676173955202103, -0.02381618693470955, 0.0403558649122715, 0.011243315413594246, 0.03623898699879646, -0.03210996836423874, -0.011008689180016518, 0.009835046716034412, -0.003932623658329248, -0.15658074617385864, -0.006912408862262964, 0.00038482825038954616, -0.00710291787981987, 0.016936779022216797, -0.04665889963507652, -0.003899725154042244, -0.03364091366529465, 0.03013511933386326, -0.023130882531404495, -0.06238485500216484, -0.025