107206345, 0.025480842217803, 0.03628791496157646, 0.06353964656591415, 0.03148274123668671, -0.06141678988933563, 0.019956428557634354, -0.05740252882242203, 0.009692673571407795, -0.022137928754091263, 0.03448162227869034, 0.03974781930446625, -0.051181819289922714, 0.010918655432760715, -0.032294511795043945, 0.029348483309149742, 0.015903104096651077, -0.0020229073707014322, -0.054068103432655334, 2.5631883908420374e-34, -0.0346362441778183, -0.007739666849374771, 0.0055489568039774895, -0.055079136043787, -0.028064636513590813, -0.024066302925348282, 0.06795557588338852, -0.022512244060635567, 0.018748430535197258, 0.054308321326971054, -0.022457849234342575], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "85ad4b20ee073bd14d5f40d30c25c6ed02bf77b2723c5300a8fb768af376eae9", "content": "This chunk appears in the document during the discussion on effective teaching strategies for pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It highlights the role of technology in supporting teaching, specifically through the use of instructional and non-instructional apps, as well as speech-generating tools, emphasizing their potential benefits within educational settings.Box 9: Misconceptions in maths\nUsing technology to support pupils with SEND\nThe evidence review for this guidance report found evidence that, for pupils with SEND, technology can be a useful tool for supporting teaching. 1 Successful approaches could include using: 34\n\u2022 instructional apps\u2014apps that provide instruction, modelling, or practice opportunities for a wide range of skills;\n\u2022 non-instructional apps\u2014apps that provide tools to aid learning, such as note-taking apps; and\n\u2022 speech-generating apps to augment the communication skills of pupils with communication difficulties.\nMore guidance on the successful use of technology can be found in the EEF guidance report, Using Digital Technology to Improve Learning.\f26\nEducation Endowment Foundation Scaffolding\n\u2018Scaffolding\u2019 is a metaphor for temporary support that is removed when it is no longer required. Initially, a teacher would provide enough support so that pupils can successfully complete tasks that they could not do independently.35 This requires effective assessment to gain a precise understanding of the pupil\u2019s current capabilities. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 27, "split_id": 97, "split_idx_start": 63103, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "77f07996162aaeaf2d85ec40b44b95d539c9e28a11ab97404f05d8568ae6316b", "range": [494, 715]}, {"doc_id": "25f4d3d0c70b37b42d003d5ea638e5ee07daf53637ffddb1ac7b740db8bb8f8b", "range": [0, 241]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.01756812259554863, -0.12690715491771698, -0.024390598759055138, -0.030049173161387444, -0.021882472559809685, 0.04187147691845894, 0.09556084126234055, -0.0246301107108593, -0.05320979282259941, -0.020825961604714394, 0.03795082867145538, -0.020030628889799118, 0.08658525347709656, -0.007595872040838003, 0.03142691031098366, -0.10051925480365753, 0.013678197748959064, 0.006254916079342365, -0.04217953234910965, 0.04461715370416641, -0.015141027048230171, 0.010819917544722557, -0.05219203233718872, 0.030689580366015434, -0.025310905650258064, -0.08085458725690842, 0.0015722835669294, 0.001977464882656932, -0.04336217790842056, -0.021934181451797485, 0.052119381725788116, 0.03681926429271698, -0.03880414366722107, -0.04071572795510292, 2.2071274088375503e-06, 0.024398073554039, 0.01442017499357462, 0.002956574782729149, -0.06738515943288803, 0.02168957330286503, 0.006711636669933796, 0.03241022676229477, 0.004073524381965399, 0.048520561307668686, -0.045784689486026764, 0.03982967138290405, 0.023082101717591286, -0.02832028642296791, -0.033703044