436862327158451, -0.05104459822177887, 0.047756846994161606, 0.10100437700748444, -0.028480637818574905, 0.0029741916805505753, 0.034271497279405594, 0.05380602180957794, 0.014798402786254883, -0.0014530839398503304, 0.004589251708239317, -0.04709579423069954, 0.008466852828860283, -0.018812617287039757, 0.02913028933107853, 0.038207441568374634, -0.05455508828163147, 0.05447167903184891, -0.006570607423782349, 0.005732996854931116, -0.026427747681736946, -0.04402030259370804, -0.04472378268837929, 2.3706975174750415e-34, 0.0006423855666071177, 0.00769320223480463, 0.02294021099805832, -0.05606577545404434, -0.030912239104509354, -0.05921825021505356, 0.026412557810544968, 0.009228251874446869, 0.02391711249947548, 0.04533369094133377, -0.036461398005485535], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "2b57d82e8a0c0188b4203abc9418dc81ee9493cc486c9a782fc5b88a8abce65e", "content": "This chunk is located in the section discussing effective teaching strategies for supporting pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It specifically addresses the use of scaffolding as a pedagogical approach to help all pupils, particularly those with SEND, by providing structured support and visual aids to enhance their learning and independence.Example: using scaffolding\nA teacher might initially scaffold for a whole class by providing a writing frame for all pupils to work from. Over time, writing frame headings are written on the board for pupils to use as a scaffold if they choose to with an expectation that they are also considering their own structure. Eventually, a teacher would use their questioning to ensure that pupils with SEND are structuring their work appropriately, perhaps formulating a structure together based on the pupil\u2019s spoken ideas. At St Mary\u2019s Church of England Primary School in Barnet, teachers have used task checklists as a visual scaffold to support pupils to independently complete a task (see Figure 5). Teachers have created task checklists for tasks like entering the classroom at the beginning of the day and settling down to independent reading. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 28, "split_id": 99, "split_idx_start": 64556, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "25f4d3d0c70b37b42d003d5ea638e5ee07daf53637ffddb1ac7b740db8bb8f8b", "range": [587, 725]}, {"doc_id": "511fa21381b6024417ce88fafb57aeff6685e3285309e80e9259b3bb22a344a9", "range": [0, 146]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.007554459851235151, -0.14054641127586365, -0.013037511147558689, -0.010389513336122036, -0.03197590261697769, 0.018983010202646255, 0.08870916068553925, -0.03599539026618004, -0.024776741862297058, 0.0013509267009794712, 0.06412388384342194, -0.02397657185792923, 0.05367973819375038, 0.012479664757847786, 0.021554769948124886, -0.1355830729007721, 0.006813819985836744, 0.0037636219058185816, -0.045891497284173965, 0.015856679528951645, -0.03170042484998703, -0.02394331805408001, -0.04418305680155754, 0.013411326333880424, 0.003917050082236528, -0.06704463064670563, -0.026730231940746307, 0.020268017426133156, -0.014661770313978195, -0.009098654612898827, 0.05715963616967201, 0.059879232197999954, -0.004865172319114208, -0.047303374856710434, 2.0831660094700055e-06, 0.03940938785672188, 0.007773141842335463, -0.020726855844259262, -0.04667646810412407, 0.012930047698318958, -0.053381532430648804, 0.00860913097858429, -0.0075127603486180305, 0.0366341695189476, -0.01170351728796959, 0.004183528479188681, 0.02833707258105278, 0.05288461968302727, -0.0060083335265517235, -0.04046112671494484, 0.000769021746236831, -0.0017282002372667193, 0.0038178383838385344, -0.021792195737361908, 0.030218152329325676, -0.020323200151324272, -0.036163244396448135, 0.00074258411768823