9888, 0.027411090210080147, -0.04978319630026817, -0.03254039213061333, -0.02480413392186165, 0.033401913940906525, 0.03174712136387825, 0.02604779228568077, 0.028556695207953453, -0.03719966113567352], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "ce2f87ce8c54463be2d865c00ad07bec8cbcafed3cd3d98764ef560959bb6a95", "content": "This chunk is part of the section titled \"Applying these strategies\" in the guidance report. It emphasizes the importance of flexibility and responsiveness in teaching strategies for pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It encourages teachers to adjust their approaches based on students' ongoing needs and highlights the necessity of targeting specific skills over time for effective support.How will you adjust the strategy as you develop this fuller understanding? See Recommendation 2 for more guidance on understanding pupils\u2019 needs. \u2022 Intensity and time: Pupils might require the application of strategies over a longer period of time or a more intense focus on a small number of important, clearly-defined skills or concepts. \u2022 Flexibility: These strategies are good starting points but there is no guarantee that they will work well for all pupils all the time. If an approach does not appear to be working for a pupil, teachers need to consider what is not working and how it could be changed.\f", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 29, "split_id": 103, "split_idx_start": 66694, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "5599162dba582240d7049759c5baadb9b812a655cb8dc01b1f2ad8e6f6e4a26f", "range": [756, 831]}, {"doc_id": "3a0e9fa621a41718a15c383ab71021da3695bf83591c57e3d90b0ad7262a1ff9", "range": [0, 133]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.048723358660936356, -0.144944906