ding": null}, {"id": "51ac52954e40072a71f1f1c6124e535b32345d0f9ce370e7306ada717fdb0313", "content": "This chunk is from the section discussing the importance of adopting targeted interventions for pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It emphasizes the necessity for teachers to evaluate whether they have maximized access to quality teaching before implementing specific interventions, highlighting the importance of context in intervention effectiveness.Have you maximised their opportunity to access the best possible teaching you can offer?\f30\nEducation Endowment Foundation Targeted interventions\nA large amount of research has examined the use of interventions to support pupils with SEND. The evidence review for this guidance report focused on the factors that make interventions more, or less, effective. The key finding was that teachers can increase the chances of the intervention working well by checking that it is a good fit for their context.1 Questions to ask before adopting an intervention include: Is this the right intervention for the pupil? \u2022 Does the pupil really need this intervention? ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 31, "split_id": 113, "split_idx_start": 71972, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "00d801f774bdacbbe34460bf1be05028acd5ffb0a38fb267912a15dcb7e5e0d2", "range": [464, 553]}, {"doc_id": "48b0a9b2af0dd67d6bfd24bd9c31d894f580585a10bfbb1eec44a0bbc9945b6c", "range": [0, 48]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04621307551860809, -0.12556466460227966, -0.0048892502672970295, -0.009970705956220627, -0.031246960163116455, 0.029003800824284554, 0.04384009540081024, -0.033099692314863205, -0.04942271113395691, -0.004619911313056946, 0.031769588589668274, -0.03112