wing that a pupil\u2019s primary need is a specific learning difficulty in literacy is unlikely to be enough to shape an effective intervention. It is far more useful to understand the specific nature of the pupil\u2019s difficulty. Do they, for example, appear to struggle with reading and pronouncing individual words or with understanding the meaning of text? If they appear to be struggling to pronounce words, are there particular letters and sounds that are causing difficulty?\nCan we provide the support required for our staff to deliver the intervention well? ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 32, "split_id": 115, "split_idx_start": 73045, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "48b0a9b2af0dd67d6bfd24bd9c31d894f580585a10bfbb1eec44a0bbc9945b6c", "range": [465, 621]}, {"doc_id": "1562f1b1f1af3d71ca326cdc78ee73d6a1e43f7b4a4be9f1f27253ecb06c012f", "range": [0, 84]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.011267497204244137, -0.11060048639774323, -0.014551111496984959, 0.00019103493832517415, -0.032195571810007095, 0.035811521112918854, 0.03146762773394585, -0.0048067751340568066, 0.00471141142770648, 0.002960717771202326, 0.04768115654587746, -0.02481021359562874, 0.05944312736392021, -0.019127434119582176, -0.005538840312510729, -0.09086977690458298, 0.009849675931036472, 0.0022797181736677885, -0.01143175270408392, -0.0018295175395905972, 0.017855534330010414, 0.032700564712285995, -0.04586918652057648, -0.00991737935692072, 0.012949975207448006, -0.07893624901771545, 0.010573921725153923, 0.017336903139948845, 0.028354685753583908, 0.0006009513163007796, 0.03517955169081688, 0.05625763162970543, -0.02751793898642063, -0.03950406238436699, 2.2087376692070393e-06, 0.033488985151052475, 0.021180296316742897, -0.04666