39087, -0.03182535991072655, -0.03513624146580696, 0.032615259289741516, 0.029653556644916534, 0.032176729291677475, -0.016591966152191162, -0.04124382510781288], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "1562f1b1f1af3d71ca326cdc78ee73d6a1e43f7b4a4be9f1f27253ecb06c012f", "content": "This chunk is part of the discussion on effectively deploying teaching assistants (TAs) within the context of supporting pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disability (SEND). It emphasizes the necessity of equipping staff with appropriate training and ensuring that the most experienced teachers engage with pupils who have the greatest needs to enhance educational outcomes.Can we provide the support required for our staff to deliver the intervention well? \u2022 Do the staff have a good understanding of the teaching strategies required in the intervention? Would additional training be useful?\n\u2022 Are we ensuring that pupils with the greatest needs have access to teaching from our most experienced staff? \u2022 Schools\u2019 deployment of trained teaching assistants is a critical issue in providing effective education of pupils with SEND. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 32, "split_id": 116, "split_idx_start": 73535, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "9f4e478f61e52212cf722bfe64ca062bb124168addd818c49d5acf159aed306f", "range": [490, 574]}, {"doc_id": "dcf883d6a2d87a54aa8c3d2b1ea09012dd6ddf7c33586e7ae98e3e668a42ab9b", "range": [0, 127]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03302460163831711, -0.10402926802635193, -0.01962454803287983, 0.008776423521339893, 0.032532453536987305, 0.005906399805098772, 0.02672935463488102, -0.07601979374885559, -0.01742466539144516, -0.009362595155835152, 0.05671066418290138, -0.013003358617424965