eds and Disabilities (SEND). It highlights the collaboration between a school and a speech and language therapy service to enhance staff understanding and provide targeted interventions for students with speech, language, and communication needs (SLCN).The school works with Alma to access specialist intervention and to support staff to develop their understanding of speech, language, and communication needs (SLCN). \u2018There are many advantages to cross-sector collaborations to support children with SEND. It\u2019s a win-win scenario. The school has developed a partnership with the commissioned speech, language, and therapy service from the local health care trust. The partnership provides a lead speech and language therapist (SALT) working for one day a week, followed by three days of support by a speech and language therapy assistant. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 35, "split_id": 121, "split_idx_start": 77438, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "95dd0dab1b3708a81fb355930a375e175b89ddd12b635beafe7aa8928926f5c2", "range": [1516, 1682]}, {"doc_id": "154391741615aa63eb7ad145fdb364cafdfa6372b2caaa40602e9eabe7b3ccbd", "range": [0, 175]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04149523004889488, -0.10271477699279785, -0.009823229163885117, 0.021553022786974907, -0.031130200251936913, 0.038969479501247406, 0.07364557683467865, -0.02996583841741085, -0.023670058697462082, -0.006514755077660084, 0.036225058138370514, -0.03256819024682045, 0.06201053038239479, -0.003940459340810776, -0.011746518313884735, -0.08743540942668915, 0.004805436823517084, 0.017387209460139275, -0.02250800095498562, 0.0015945624327287078, -0.0006165583617985249, 0.0441412478685379, -0.05320398882031441, 0.024685634300112724, 0.02464189194