57040024, 0.0424249991774559, 0.022776655852794647, 0.08076216280460358, -0.019589869305491447, -0.029234688729047775, 0.02370976097881794, 0.018964966759085655, 0.03309999778866768, -0.012715593911707401, -0.04709050431847572, 0.02075081877410412, 0.01101245079189539, -0.0013898377073928714, -0.010089129209518433, 0.04411924630403519, -0.01864010840654373, -0.036959949880838394, -0.025765160098671913, 0.0109102763235569, -0.05051377788186073, -0.003497745143249631, 0.03560751676559448, 0.02955036237835884, 0.03915497660636902, -4.1849196463772387e-07, 0.04407316446304321, 0.007029455155134201, -0.04843834042549133, 0.05132493004202843, -0.03177081421017647, 0.019181450828909874, -0.05603242665529251, 0.02946394681930542, 0.016042031347751617, 0.04172133654356003, -0.03897133097052574, -0.008196982555091381, -0.021898342296481133, -0.021198740229010582, 0.02808462828397751, 0.07129886746406555, 0.011134402826428413, -0.03864648565649986, 0.030029622837901115, 0.024524858221411705, 0.023147664964199066, 0.040527649223804474, -0.022372940555214882, -0.04814242199063301, 0.0029239377472549677, 0.0066052572801709175, 0.054700009524822235, -0.03677802160382271, -0.03365363925695419, 0.013448105193674564, -0.0025349047500640154, -0.029799936339259148, -0.04809648171067238, -0.05138566717505455, 0.010040046647191048, 1.8296017409628255e-34, 0.0012684554094448686, -0.004830888006836176, 0.050502050668001175, -0.024845657870173454, 0.016005385667085648, -0.005511485505849123, -0.01733247935771942, 0.03931540995836258, 0.026976240798830986, -0.011678042821586132, -0.050336919724941254], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "0326edc5379b1b7eb3d7549183f85b51d991e19cbe7ce50f9dfcde6ce3fafb96", "content": "This chunk is located in Section 4 of the guidance report, which discusses the importance of targeted interventions for pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It specifically highlights the role of Speech and Language Therapy (SALT) in providing effective support through flexible, integrated approaches involving parents and the community to enhance children's progress and outcomes.Interventions can be delivered flexibly, responding to needs of each child, resulting in accelerated progress. There has been an increase in early and appropriate referrals to a SALT resulting in effective, timely intervention for children who are likely to have difficulties and closer, supportive dialogue with parents and carers.\nThe links with the local community, including parents and carers, have been of great benefit. The school hosts drop-in sessions, joint SALT sessions, and other support such as SEND breakfast meetings. This integrated approach directly impacts on outcomes, not only for the child but the entire Ash Grove School and the community it serves.\u2019\nBox 12: A view from a speech and language therapist \u201c \u201c\f34\nEducation Endowment Foundation 5\nBetween 2003 and 2008, the Deployment and Impact of Support Staff (DISS) project surveyed nearly 18,000 school leaders, support staff, and teachers to obtain reliable data on the deployment and characteristics of support staff and their impact on pupil outcomes and teacher workloads. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 35, "split_id": 123, "split_idx_start": 78682, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "154391741615aa63eb7ad145fdb364cafdfa6372b2caaa40602e9eabe7b3ccbd", "range": [831, 942]}, {"doc_id": "3fd151a7f88c5a6446662aaed8e502e2747d202ca99cdc30f36826156aaa9a87", "range": [0, 517]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.02411116659641266, -0.10663113743066788, -0.01714860461652279, 0.0009387634927406907, -0.0205344520509243, 0.025910090655088425, 0.052483391016721725, -0.030564816668629646, -0.030360057950019836, -0