756398678, 1.8120344141083932e-34, -0.005279110744595528, -0.018003365024924278, 0.011247921735048294, -0.04385140538215637, 0.002620119834318757, -0.029367296025156975, 0.019703544676303864, 0.0017680026357993484, 0.053951095789670944, 0.03258297219872475, -0.049046989530324936], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "1cfe234818ce2497a65149ba5911f5ef781a7e9e6b1cb9049784347fa5867f35", "content": "This chunk is situated in the section discussing the effective deployment of teaching assistants (TAs) in supporting pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND). It highlights the challenges and consequences of TAs primarily working with these pupils away from whole-class instruction, leading to isolation and reduced peer interactions.TAs were principally working with pupils with SEND or pupils not making expected levels of progress. As a result of high levels of TA support, pupils with the most complex needs spent less time in whole-class teaching, less time with the teacher, and had fewer opportunities for peer interaction compared with their classmates. The net result of this approach results in TAs in mainstream schools regularly adopting the status of \u2018primary educator\u2019 for pupils in most need. Although this arrangement is often seen as beneficial for the pupils and the teacher\u2014because the pupils in need receive more attention while the teacher can concentrate on the rest of the class\u2014it causes a \u2018separation\u2019 effect. Box 14 presents a case study describing an alternative approach.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 37, "split_id": 131, "split_idx_start": 82962, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "43ffbb59bd111c29bf130f00557c48a144d76187634c9a1dd59a9db6b4fdad33", "range": [627, 728]}, {"doc_id": "54c24f9f782ce22d9dd3bf2bc7b3d2ac1070ea3f6b85cf9c367a934d0a487d58", "range": [0, 65]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.052998729050159454, -0.10466664284467697, -0.01984231173992157, 0.036765970289707184, 0.0006862341542728245, 0.033606406301259995, 0.057700444012880325, -0.06807119399309158, -0.036893330514431, -0.004881615750491619, 0.05220817029476166, -0.027534332126379013, 0.03409886360168457, -0.03330617398023605, 0.010589884594082832, -0.12825711071491241, 0.006689212750643492, 0.0287362989038229, -0.03626716136932373, 0.02158369868993759, -0.009292670525610447, 0.008505419827997684, -0.021336426958441734, 0.023528987541794777, 0.019629769027233124, -0.045818645507097244, 0.011724354699254036, 0.004892343655228615, 0.03753296658396721, 0.05165422707796097, 0.04974982514977455, 0.010686646215617657, -0.002374448347836733, -0.030169343575835228, 2.238854676761548e-06, 0.06801639497280121, 0.007978147827088833, -0.02640553005039692, -0.024958185851573944, 0.003311038250103593, -0.109518863260746, 0.0351119264960289, 0.02529800496995449, 0.039619844406843185, -0.02024267055094242, 0.0259481780230999, -0.013865097425878048, -0.048410188406705856, 0.020639454945921898, -0.03851328417658806, 0.00919466931372881, 0.0075386445969343185, -0.04308924451470375, -0.0358155220746994, 0.05367949977517128, -0.05606641620397568, -0.008854465559124947, -0.10106927156448364, 0.019225696101784706, -0.0008880891255103052, -0.016553495079278946, 0.01110257487744093, 0.002879910636693239, -0.06994767487049103, 0.016373304650187492, 0.011834760196506977, -0.0011826741974800825, -0.0669366642832756, 0.035969480872154236, -0.017640000209212303, 0.10010518878698349, 0.06525939702987671, 0.012072032317519188, 0.061550240963697433, 0.000826635689008981, 0.0390968881547451, -0.008011138997972012, -0.020322615280747414, -0.04520184174180031, -0.009757004678249359, 0.005569204222410917, 0.07143837958574295, -0.06849731504917145, 0.01794855296611786, -0.033224