83327484, 0.00819043442606926, -0.0359642431139946, -0.0076109194196760654, -0.026378141716122627, 0.03883761167526245, 0.006349741946905851, 0.045709382742643356, 0.04369516298174858, -0.031765054911375046], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "36b3dd17e59b8eabf3d3971f031fd6a0606b70a149e499df298dd3151ee7df5d", "content": "This chunk is located in the section discussing effective deployment and support of teaching assistants (TAs). It emphasizes the importance of training TAs to use a specific framework that helps them provide appropriate support, enhancing student independence while maintaining structured interactions between TAs and pupils.We made the framework a key feature of our approach to deploying and supporting TAs. By training TAs to consider and use the framework, we enabled them to provide the right level of support at the right time.\u2019 The framework is shown below. The initial expectation is that pupils work independently while the TA observes their performance. TAs should then only intervene appropriately when pupils demonstrate they are unable to proceed. The aim is to provide opportunities for pupils to experience and develop independence while giving structure and consistency to TAs\u2019 talk.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 39, "split_id": 141, "split_idx_start": 88437, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "577c07718ea8bf851f64eaf5782ffba692aa11b75eabb7ee199a992dc6ae0e61", "range": [804, 889]}, {"doc_id": "25ece78ee7ceb9b2ba6c102866851e3df8c8e605b4fe9c8c2de803d22d3d54a0", "range": [0, 139]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0687813013792038, -0.14373725652694702, -0.01843475177884102, -0.002580528613179922, -0.025396812707185745, 0.040955714881420135, 0.040188323706388474, -0.0427634