lines various strategies, such as modelling and prompting, to foster greater pupil independence.Several clues may be needed. Modelling: TA demonstrates the next step the child needs to complete and then asks the child to take this step. \u2018I am using the word-bank to find a word to help me describe my character \u2026\u2019\nCorrecting: The TA provides answers and requires no independent thinking. Occasionally it is appropriate to do this, however, TAs should always aim instead to model and encourage pupils to apply new skills or knowledge first.\nBox 15: A view from an assistant headteacher\u2013Supporting effective TA-pupil interaction\nMore help from TA\nGreater pupil independence\nSelf-scaffolding\nPrompting\nClueing\nModelling\nCorrecting\n\u201c \u201c\f38\nEducation Endowment Foundation REFERENCES\n1. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 39, "split_id": 143, "split_idx_start": 89553, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "25ece78ee7ceb9b2ba6c102866851e3df8c8e605b4fe9c8c2de803d22d3d54a0", "range": [680, 709]}, {"doc_id": "c6b79b40ec54bc9d01d641077bff4f1cccedb1ec049a44945c7122655cf2ccd8", "range": [0, 240]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03337910398840904, -0.10450346022844315, -0.017085613682866096, 0.0010788693325594068, -0.02259678579866886, 0.02160636894404888, 0.02725115232169628, -0.07805591076612473, -0.008111951872706413, 0.006653963588178158, 0.04000721871852875, -0.02918473817408085, 0.03362391144037247, -0.010225160047411919, -0.0064864992164075375, -0.12508940696716309, 0.021027300506830215, -0.02694064751267433, -0.03443678095936775, 0.003668546210974455, -0.013666100800037384, -0.007978672161698341, -0.035629771649837494, 0.025832535699009895, -0.021827224642038345, -0.05903513729572296