nt": "This chunk is part of the \"References\" section in the guidance report on supporting pupils with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND) in mainstream schools. It cites a specific study published in the British Educational Research Journal that examines the educational experiences of pupils with SEND in mainstream primary settings, contributing to the evidence base for the report's recommendations.The Nature and Quality of the Educational Experiences of Pupils with a Statement for Special Educational Needs in Mainstream Primary Schools\u2019, British Educational Research Journal, 41 (2) DOI: 10.1002/\nberj.3144\fSpecial Educational Needs in Mainstream Schools 41\nThis guidance report draws on the best available evidence regarding supporting pupils with SEND in mainstream schools. It is based on a review conducted by a team from CEDAR at the University of Warwick led by Mairi Ann Cullen, Geoff Lindsay, Richard Hastings, and Louise Denne.1 The guidance report was created over several stages:\n\u2022 Scoping. The EEF consulted with teachers, academics, parents and carers, and other stakeholders about the scope of the report. We then appointed an advisory panel and the review team and agreed research questions for the review. \u2022 Evidence review. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "EEF_Special_Educational_Needs_in_Mainstream_Schools_Guidance_Report.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1JdqrM1riD57oBlBO2rxsYWM-BECtkBOI", "source_id": "74ab0c4b037724e2e6a15bac6c92262e5c8cee040eab7233c78628898f0a7eb6", "page_number": 42, "split_id": 167, "split_idx_start": 100830, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "07081fee42bb3ca0609989d69589237f830a21ac8be431bdc6bf2e78d67ba124", "range": [312, 694]}, {"doc_id": "506150048485ae2819a9161d45157cedbaf5c0493c5bbae55c6d67a2034f5a2d", "range": [0, 19]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.05079067498445511, -0.11603622883558273, 0.0034670396707952023, 0.007617936469614506, 0.007657004985958338, 0.055