3560444712638855, 1.4373404240371301e-34, 0.005628142040222883, 0.019221406430006027, 0.015531087294220924, -0.07206898927688599, 0.055468544363975525, -0.00968249887228012, -0.004295357037335634, -0.009012538939714432, 0.020944800227880478, -0.023642314597964287, -0.008061054162681103], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "54c32de5a21f974a1109df166b0e6a2d9b66ccd0f62a17f6f3fc71af8b7c7291", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study A, which focuses on the experiences of an 8-year-old autistic pupil named Tom at Watermore Primary School. It describes his challenges with anxiety, behavior, and self-esteem, highlighting the staff's efforts to understand and reduce his anxiety through collaboration with a local authority autism advisor.He ran away from staff frequently when he was not able to cope with the situation. Tom was also very sensitive to noise and movement. He was very self-critical and often blamed himself when things went wrong. He was not sleeping well and sleep deprivation made him less able to cope at school.\nActions taken and impact\nWith support from the local authority autism adviser, staff explored the likely causes of Tom\u2019s anxiety and how this might be reduced. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 2, "split_id": 3, "split_idx_start": 1535, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "43b399890abaf150b3b2e0b53760971c5aa895d8c29b0fdd3a4f4e165d4d5a6b", "range": [331, 414]}, {"doc_id": "295b79bf0315813038c7621fa4a783ea0b1e07f8c4835a065cd9d833b7b27e38", "range": [0, 160]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0512155182659626, -0.040295589715242386, 0.0008335252059623599, 0.010172856040298939, 0.0009667114354670048, 0.04116690903902054, 0.03188853710889816, -0.06386767327785492, -0.03827660158276558, -0.008749186992645264, 0.02123136445879936