egular breaks. He has breaks away from the classroom eight times a day including break and lunch times. At these times, he may go on a listening walk outside, play football in the hall, draw, or bake.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n4 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nTom was very good at using the iPad and this was sometimes used as an incentive. The whole class use iPads for Maths Rockstars Times Tables https://ttrockstars.com and he enjoys this. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 3, "split_id": 9, "split_idx_start": 4010, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "20ab0e0d71bebe45d0be72e2f5a155b708f618919f56496e9e678e2734798a59", "range": [353, 431]}, {"doc_id": "95ab5b3d01a18909cf23341a2985aa09090ffbdd1b9dc5f80c9d88b9225c1c20", "range": [0, 103]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04061746597290039, -0.07014290988445282, -0.03694473206996918, -0.01476498693227768, -0.028336578980088234, 0.027200987562537193, 0.08533332496881485, -0.03858715295791626, -0.05800106003880501, -0.018073737621307373, 0.06565035134553909, -0.05071405693888664, 0.03676310181617737, -0.006381159648299217, -0.03339515998959541, -0.06330093741416931, 0.009810337796807289, 0.012075938284397125, -0.046064991503953934, 0.045614227652549744, -0.0061899167485535145, 0.016218461096286774, -0.022055471315979958, 0.04015038534998894, 0.02951103262603283, -0.05884399265050888, 0.020283399149775505, -0.002435951493680477, 0.029888683930039406, -0.05806228891015053, 0.056000396609306335, 0.015037359669804573, -0.017464255914092064, -0.0015525500057265162, 2.215076619904721e-06, 0.02781277522444725, 0.02283499203622341, -0.013628742657601833, -0.009852240793406963, 0.004726585932075977, -0.024491164833307266, -0.0035586480516940355, 0.020270485430955887, 0.055322982