54, -0.036738086491823196], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "95ab5b3d01a18909cf23341a2985aa09090ffbdd1b9dc5f80c9d88b9225c1c20", "content": "This chunk is from Case Study A: Watermore Primary School, focusing on strategies implemented to support Tom, an 8-year-old autistic pupil with significant anxiety. It highlights the use of iPads to facilitate learning in Mathematics and English, as well as to reduce anxiety associated with writing tasks.The whole class use iPads for Maths Rockstars Times Tables https://ttrockstars.com and he enjoys this. Using the iPad also reduces anxiety for Tom ( e.g. he enjoys playing games and these can be used as a \u2018bridge\u2019 to the next activity).\nThe computer is used in English and for written project work as Tom gets anxious about handwriting. Any writing activity is chunked with breaks and although he gets distracted, he can engage with the work well.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 4, "split_id": 10, "split_idx_start": 4438, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "79621bf49ee6eb5912c26e523d0f0f3a1e62280df3144d5aeb340e819292c421", "range": [428, 531]}, {"doc_id": "6a35e46849ca2d13e3c3e809fd7e4fe568fe59afe2ea630daa7dab8b8354420b", "range": [0, 111]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.004903579596430063, -0.03688594326376915, -0.04166682809591293, -0.010471591725945473, -0.02215711772441864, 0.03715872764587402, 0.09756747633218765, -0.013497198931872845, -0.05210920423269272, -0.019241763278841972, 0.0399782769382, -0.06617806106805801, 0.03529832512140274, -0.018550198525190353, -0.03855166211724281, -0.03103664331138134, 0.011516626924276352, 0.0304262675344944, -0.012804756872355938, 0.035421114414930344, 0.008213899098336697, 0.0015845611924305558, -0.04291556030511856, 0.03051591105759144, 0.01789642