3, -0.0001314533583354205, -0.021942783147096634, -0.013338347896933556], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "f8338cf649ef4d5b078289a16a18ddbfab50b9f809cb78b1c69a78fedc88f058", "content": "This chunk is from Case Study A, focusing on Tom, an 8-year-old autistic pupil at Watermore Primary School. It discusses the strategies employed to support his transitions within the school environment, including the use of pre-teaching, social stories, and personalized approaches to help him manage changes effectively.Good Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n6 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nTom needed extra support for transitions. The TA would drip feed information to Tom about changes ahead. She used pre-\nteaching and encouraged Tom to look at the timetable every day. If appropriate, Social Stories are used (Gray, 2015). Tom relates well to Social Stories and will write his own which do not follow Carol Gray\u2019s suggested formula but work for him. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 6, "split_id": 22, "split_idx_start": 9122, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f81b1d5e1863b9eedffee36b7869ae0691fbde57e7a3a119ab488361228541b7", "range": [266, 391]}, {"doc_id": "14dbad9d417dd18f9d481fb3cd4c3c9608cbaa9c8bda49624cbc13efb13000a2", "range": [0, 127]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0511067770421505, -0.05170845612883568, -0.01298295333981514, -0.006186192389577627, -0.03130624443292618, 0.006179299671202898, 0.037261269986629486, -0.05979827046394348, -0.06459330767393112, -0.019348178058862686, 0.06999234855175018, -0.055988654494285583, 0.03701038658618927, 0.06152968108654022, -0.01579289697110653, -0.08327974379062653, 0.023298712447285652, 0.033677153289318085, -0.027890847995877266, 0.017543073743581772, -0.025100959464907646, 0.02191971