 B: Oasis Academy Connaught, which focuses on strategies to support the inclusion of autistic children. The text highlights the importance of providing feedback to staff on their interactions with pupils to ensure consistency in language development, along with environmental reminders to reinforce these practices. It falls under the section on leadership and management that promotes effective autism practices.They provide very specific feedback on their interaction with the children with the aim of developing consistency.\nThere are reminders displayed throughout the whole environment to support staff working with the children. This includes a consistent approach to the development of language through the use of \u2018A Helping Hand to Develop Language\u2019.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n12 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nEnabling environments\nP5 \u2013 Leadership and management that promotes and embeds good autism practice\nLeaders take every opportunity to extend provision into outdoor learning and create safe spaces using creative approaches. For example, a small cycle shed was purchased to use as an outdoor quiet reading area as this was much cheaper than purchasing bespoke equipment (see photo).\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 11, "split_id": 44, "split_idx_start": 20214, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b4970d4fadfa9d62aebf663e547ffe9689a31c17bf49bebce02c16168bd9c5b1", "range": [573, 688]}, {"doc_id": "defc59042d6d8f02cc459dcdb2956c61cc47dbc1456a06c06dd906b8f3159235", "range": [0, 158]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.038765452802181244, -0.08483938872814178, -0.02150520123541355, 0.03986894711852074, 0.0007516109617426991, 0.015834854915738106, 0.02442372776567936, -0.04388752207159996, -0.05260222405