3247, -0.027820121496915817, -0.047102607786655426, 0.028977559879422188, 0.006623140536248684, 0.06700313091278076, 0.013906850479543209, 0.012760426849126816, -0.01255777757614851, 0.023090464994311333, 0.005321086384356022, 0.034622546285390854, -0.007929437793791294, -0.0031543467193841934, -0.05206013843417168, 0.008981321938335896, -0.03322092443704605, 0.04884855076670647, -0.045148685574531555, -0.03948374465107918, 0.006122026592493057, 0.0038009255658835173, -0.012682405300438404, -0.07311620563268661, -0.032623011618852615, -0.002332555130124092, 1.8948445472927174e-34, 0.012844342738389969, -0.015902340412139893, 0.035195235162973404, -0.04510069265961647, 0.021724563091993332, -2.2227464796742424e-05, 0.011164795607328415, -0.00747286481782794, 0.012299755588173866, -0.022157609462738037, -0.03491302579641342], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "defc59042d6d8f02cc459dcdb2956c61cc47dbc1456a06c06dd906b8f3159235", "content": "This chunk is located in Case Study B: Oasis Academy Connaught, which discusses the strategies and principles implemented to support the inclusion of autistic students. It highlights the school\u2019s commitment to creating a supportive and flexible learning environment, emphasizing the importance of adapting provisions to meet every child's individual needs for successful engagement and progress.For example, a small cycle shed was purchased to use as an outdoor quiet reading area as this was much cheaper than purchasing bespoke equipment (see photo).\nThe academy has an organisation-wide approach to inclusion with the view that their provision is planned to include everyone. The senior leadership view is to \u2018 allow them to be who they are\u2019 and \u2018 the child is always at the centre\u2019.\nSenior leaders feel that, \u2018 We\u2019re the people who have to change, not the child with autism\u2019 and the focus is on key aspects linked to learning and well-being as a result. This is illustrated by their view that it doesn\u2019t matter whether the child is sitting on the carpet or not \u2013 the important thing is that they are accessing the learning and making progress. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 12, "split_id": 45, "split_idx_start": 20866, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0433e603c87f3c6620592ad675754cc4b1abed3504f0bb86a35955c4b17e5f6b", "range": [652, 810]}, {"doc_id": "d7b862093178beb2b832331cadf413462ed1a1e98c3b381f7e907066364b656a", "range": [0, 190]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.031468331813812256, -0.08612992614507675, -0.025393739342689514, 0.04552673548460007, -0.004530813079327345, 0.027752229943871498, 0.02840133011341095, -0.05281209573149681, -0.03271394595503807, -0.0022994880564510822, 0.04071690887212753, -0.024920374155044556, 0.027453651651740074, -0.022401120513677597, -0.003982231020927429, -0.04393815994262695, 0.04814205318689346, 0.02116202935576439, -0.09043338894844055, 0.012621701695024967, -0.02885000966489315, 0.01996948942542076, -0.007219234481453896, 0.018013939261436462, 0.02252052165567875, -0.008832750841975212, 0.0020026476122438908, 0.017075762152671814, 0.02594667486846447, -0.005554242059588432, 0.031378258019685745, -0.009614556096494198, 0.0006544147036038339, -0.01549450121819973, 2.2768024336983217e-06, 0.025916418060660362, 0.009655877016484737, -0.02792474813759327, -0.0016228981548920274, -0.0419205017387867, -0.0823068842291832, 0.04421082139015198, 0.014622308313846588, 0.039223093539476395, 0.011411338113248348, 0.0017409283900633454, 0.00019223296840209514, 0.032188981771469116, -0.020098354667425156, -0.02347118780016899, 0.0037709984462708235, 0.008801685646176338, -0.016568511724472046, -0.0062332465313375, 0.045237947255373, -0.020311782136559486, 0.018754666671156883, -0.06894778460264206, 0.04