 creating a learning environment where children can access education in a way that suits their needs, showcasing a philosophy that values understanding behavior and promoting de-escalation strategies.This is illustrated by their view that it doesn\u2019t matter whether the child is sitting on the carpet or not \u2013 the important thing is that they are accessing the learning and making progress. Children are very accepting of others as a consequence of this view.\nSenior leaders say, \u2018We understand all behaviour has meaning\u2019 and they look to identify the meaning in the behaviour. Staff do not confront behaviour immediately as sometimes there needs to be the opportunity to de-escalate before a conversation can be had with a child so staff might direct an escalated child to an activity before discussing an issue. This approach is embedded throughout the organisation.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 12, "split_id": 46, "split_idx_start": 21429, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "defc59042d6d8f02cc459dcdb2956c61cc47dbc1456a06c06dd906b8f3159235", "range": [563, 753]}, {"doc_id": "2386b94e57459a03d1b36d1b6400319455e102200d97e9c2c734655575c205e3", "range": [0, 55]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04725833609700203, -0.06974103301763535, -0.01858041249215603, 0.036516524851322174, -0.0003014098620042205, 0.046010375022888184, 0.02131868153810501, -0.021952984854578972, -0.017487334087491035, 0.004222531337291002, 0.03786437585949898, 0.005096199456602335, -0.005213103257119656, 0.007097948342561722, -0.0068326713517308235, -0.02299470081925392, 0.0262496005743742, 0.04996287077665329, -0.03728853538632393, 0.013626888394355774, -0.02990221604704857, -4.5594715629704297e-05, -0.0014241761527955532, 0.013043132610619068, 0.00596095621585