27545, -0.00393658597022295, -0.02518138289451599], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "0a6be240d7f1f807e9da7335cfeb6ab408517e75d5e9e07afa5a17374004e6b6", "content": "This chunk is located in Case Study C: Hinderton Special School. It describes the creation of a sensory-friendly space within a classroom, referred to as a Gruffalo cave, where children with autism can self-regulate and find calmness using visual cues that guide them in managing their emotions.The room is set up to reduce sensory stimulation with a low-lit area. There is a section in the classroom which has been enclosed and covered to create a Gruffalo cave. This provides a dark haven for children to go to when needed.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n13 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nChildren are taught how to self-regulate in this space. Visuals are displayed to encourage self-regulation by giving the children a sequence of actions to do when they are angry.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 12, "split_id": 50, "split_idx_start": 23286, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "737a8e642647d7fbc774ab13e54ef068bac1207e8366ff054757a7461e79542f", "range": [461, 531]}, {"doc_id": "f1d519655401efa33f6c0e7477d3588340c5a3f93201c2736b90fcb703a2623c", "range": [0, 123]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.05428982898592949, -0.08165623992681503, -0.020231042057275772, 0.012919615022838116, -0.04120851680636406, 0.027316071093082428, 0.08516784012317657, -0.01959616132080555, 0.012657811865210533, -0.006831449922174215, 0.007725568488240242, -0.008798627182841301, -0.005602354183793068, -0.00376704684458673, 0.028445003554224968, -0.11121419817209244, 0.0008690948598086834, 0.05308139696717262, -0.030593305826187134, 0.018789848312735558, -0.031335435807704926, 0.0080316