{"id": "fd84f58547360e73f0fc58fa95ccec0d99d6e4588850a844cac0d28fceb9786f", "content": "This chunk is situated within Case Study B: Oasis Academy Connaught, highlighting specific strategies employed to enhance communication and storytelling among autistic children. It discusses the use of the 'Tales Toolkit,' which helps students articulate their narratives through structured symbols, fostering engagement and expression in both small group and whole-class contexts.Staff use the \u2018Tales Toolkit\u2019 ( https://talestoolkit.com ) and have found this effective in encouraging children to communicate and to tell their stories. They have also had safeguarding disclosures as a result. The Toolkit uses four clear symbols (character, setting, problem and solution). These are used during small group sessions or as a whole class. The children can then use these symbols in their own stories.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 14, "split_id": 56, "split_idx_start": 26093, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "8e2c517e8eaa7f545c13ee2f13a97ee4f9da25b6a814e9a6587e2faa22d094a4", "range": [285, 440]}, {"doc_id": "f7b3a9342542ab2d10ceaea89170f619d3c24ad5792f9dd3b011c9ee944dfe54", "range": [0, 62]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0046175019815564156, -0.07221787422895432, -0.033985480666160583, 0.016325244680047035, -0.04263639077544212, 0.019301848486065865, 0.04978335648775101, -0.03414662927389145, -0.053422920405864716, -0.005213460884988308, 0.061765678226947784, -0.04253874719142914, 0.0523940771818161, 0.08377807587385178, -0.0014723459025844932, -0.050563350319862366, 0.022921966388821602, 0.0029941853135824203, -0.0009664521785452962, 0.02393205836415291, -0.005929843056946993, 0.05687161535024643, -0.05283606797456741, 0.06336376070976257, -0.01936015