464651108, 0.0018519751029089093, -0.024833688512444496, 0.017031561583280563, 0.005376536399126053, -0.04965675249695778, -0.07897759228944778, -0.057096123695373535, 0.015446936711668968, 2.382299325293421e-34, -0.005526560824364424, -0.020971907302737236, 0.011550727300345898, 0.029694870114326477, 0.048634011298418045, 0.005105109419673681, 0.02859572134912014, -0.011097341775894165, 0.029572954401373863, -0.0004927597474306822, -0.03801723197102547], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "f7b3a9342542ab2d10ceaea89170f619d3c24ad5792f9dd3b011c9ee944dfe54", "content": "This chunk appears in Case Study B of the \"Good Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies,\" focusing on the use of the Tales Toolkit to enhance children's storytelling abilities in a nursery setting. It discusses how children can incorporate symbols into their narratives, supporting their understanding of characters, settings, problems, and solutions. The document emphasizes inclusive strategies and resources for fostering communication and creativity in autistic children.The children can then use these symbols in their own stories.\nNursery Examples\nIn this example, the children are able to talk about characters, settings, problems and solutions. Tales Toolkit is an online resource and more information can be found at https://talestoolkit.com .\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n15 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nTransferable practice \u2013 actions you could try in your setting\n\u2022 Consider creating outdoor safe spaces by repurposing storage equipment\n\u2022 Create a den inside the classroom to provide a safe space with reduced sensory stimuli\n\u2022 Create individual pupil cards listing pupils\u2019 interests and targets for all staff\n\u2022 Create visuals to provide learning prompts for staff in the environment\n\u2022 Use visuals in which the children model use of equipment and reinforce these with the use of symbols\n\u2022 Use zones of regulation resources linked to characters in films such as Inside Out\n\u2022 Include activities which directly link to individual children\u2019s interests\n\u2022 Create a staffed nurture space where children can go at lunch or break time.\nReferences\nBuron, KD and Curtis, M (2012) The Incredible 5-Point Scale (2nd. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 14, "split_id": 57, "split_idx_start": 26449, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "fd84f58547360e73f0fc58fa95ccec0d99d6e4588850a844cac0d28fceb9786f", "range": [356, 418]}, {"doc_id": "ad3e3e0055f38efa69f6e53c54b79b5712aa34a9cbb52e1dc71ff076fe5b10ba", "range": [0, 77]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03648969903588295, -0.0937492698431015, -0.034837882965803146, 0.025002870708703995, -0.029770469292998314, 0.04690218344330788, 0.046574916690588, -0.025656281039118767, -0.06151320040225983, -0.005937278736382723, 0.04801825061440468, -0.022715482860803604, 0.0692349523305893, 0.05340409278869629, 0.0037801044527441263, -0.07430847734212875, 0.014923270791769028, 0.024789897724986076, -0.027343178167939186, 0.020430605858564377, -0.021562060341238976, 0.05005089193582535, -0.04174857214093208, 0.06689579784870148, -0.01809052936732769, -0.06961550563573837, 0.015445171855390072, 0.015710381790995598, 0.006874307058751583, -0.062163881957530975, -2.248149576189462e-05, -0.03451116755604744, 0.021141299977898598, -0.009347530081868172, 2.109313982145977e-06, -0.01965896226465702, 0.02156144380569458, -0.014231862500309944, -0.001674377708695829, -0.04491202160716057, -0.03247229754924774, 0.023036887869238853, 0.025572972372174263, 0.04064835235476494, 0.012641005218029022, -0.004515891894698143, 0.05124024674296379, 0.0863255187869072, -0.03006734699010849, -0.013114121742546558, -0.0008283961797133088, 0.020383425056934357, 0.