04553feac344a95dd113257941d9c4", "content": "This chunk is part of the Autism Education Trust (AET) resources, which include training hubs designed to support educators in their work with autistic children and young people aged across different stages, from Early Years to young adulthood. The document contains various case studies showcasing best practices and interventions in schools, including Hinderton Special School.Early Years, 5 to 16 and 16 to 25 years) \u2013 see the AET website ( http://www.autismeducationtrust.org.uk /) for details of the training hub closest to you\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n17 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nCase Study C: Hinderton Special School\nType of school Community special school for autistic students at all levels of ability in the North West of England\nSchool website hinderton.cheshire.sch.uk\nNumber on roll 44\nAge range 3 to 11 years\nFocus of the case study\nYoga, Forest schools and Outdoor Learning, Colourful Semantics\nPrinciples illustrated\n1. Understanding the strengths, interests and challenges of the autistic child and young person\n4. Workforce development to support autistic children and young people\n6. An ethos and environment that fosters social inclusion for children and young people on the autism spectrum\n7. Targeted support and measuring progress of children and young people on the autism spectrum\n8. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 16, "split_id": 59, "split_idx_start": 28934, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "ad3e3e0055f38efa69f6e53c54b79b5712aa34a9cbb52e1dc71ff076fe5b10ba", "range": [1398, 1987]}, {"doc_id": "47888e3222f37f49a20128fb1bca799dca51defecb0e276509a9d5fa9aec1f13", "range": [0, 95]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04123667627573013, -0.080