s chunk is part of Case Study C from Hinderton Special School, which outlines the school's approach to individualized support for autistic students. It specifically describes the implementation of a yoga program tailored to each child's needs, emphasizing the importance of flexibility in teaching methods to enhance emotional regulation and engagement in learning.She collects the child from their classroom and begins to assess their needs that day through how they walk to the session and interact with her.\nA yoga programme is specifically designed for each child. For example, she does balance postures with one child to work on proprioception as she found this helps to calm the pupil. No picture visuals are used as she physically models the positions and movements. She felt a visual timetable might be a barrier to activities and she needs to use a flexible structure that is not too prescriptive so that she can be responsive to the children\u2019s needs on that day. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 18, "split_id": 66, "split_idx_start": 32106, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "8bbb062a9fc82944c9c8254910e333d604b66a98ee6835091ec755b606f12806", "range": [374, 520]}, {"doc_id": "fc7aaa65a1f2002634812605d100d70004ff2a6aff563a0f4ec867859db0d95d", "range": [0, 199]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0325903445482254, -0.10050035268068314, -0.044805023819208145, 0.01915956474840641, -0.0027720152866095304, 0.013055010698735714, 0.03628797084093094, -0.026900412514805794, -0.032280083745718, 0.02137158438563347, 0.03795229271054268, -0.04690546169877052, 0.02654772438108921, -0.025126855820417404, -0.030522627755999565, -0.12142934650182724, 0.007898618467152119, 0.013773717917501926, -0.03639796003699303, 0.03284827247262001, -0.0046487832441926, 0.0