oga as a therapeutic intervention for autistic students to promote emotional regulation and physical well-being, highlighting specific adaptations made for individual needs and the collaborative efforts between the yoga teacher, staff, and parents.For example, one child always sat in the W position and he can now sit cross-legged which puts less strain on his hips. The yoga teacher also uses gestures. For example, a tap on the knee reminds the child to move from the W pose to crossed legs. These gestures are passed on to the staff and to the parents at home so they can be used as a reminder.\nThis close involvement between the yoga teacher and the child has provided insights that staff would never have had into the child\u2019s needs ( e.g. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 18, "split_id": 69, "split_idx_start": 33436, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "aca0ec0455ae102c0fdaa160735949d47471b50b25d947d551e196348e5aa0c9", "range": [348, 468]}, {"doc_id": "75ea8787e42b8dbceea330b2ff33985fe5dae9482c19b4a6d0f9bae61965be6d", "range": [0, 146]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.02661394700407982, -0.06737722456455231, -0.03838367015123367, 0.016515759751200676, 0.022500911727547646, 0.025874337181448936, 0.030482502654194832, -0.012724390253424644, 0.008132281713187695, 0.0061714062467217445, 0.02130173146724701, -0.03834696486592293, 0.031365446746349335, -0.03378940373659134, -0.01856616884469986, -0.057048749178647995, -0.0007143520633690059, 0.01301959715783596, -0.02539236843585968, 0.03482821211218834, 0.005087243393063545, 0.02750886231660843, -0.008436694741249084, 0.03318554162979126, -0.007956581190228462, -0.03938482329249382, 0.017447223886847496, 0.011081904172897339, 0.036449383944272995, -0.061214663088321686, -0.01881672441959381, -0.0