school staff say and then changing their practice to accommodate the needs of the children. Over time, they have developed their knowledge of what works but are also reliant on the staff to continue to guide them.\nStaff had an initial two-hour meeting with the providers to talk through case studies of the children\u2019s needs and to discuss requirements in detail. The team proved to be very flexible and open to adapting their way of working with a special school. The providers are responsive to issues arising with the children in their planning. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 19, "split_id": 75, "split_idx_start": 35935, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "455ba04a478574a4721221c7060595d0d68f88f0b5c58987852b92689e49447d", "range": [371, 536]}, {"doc_id": "1e141b341a07def87590fb1746290aa41609b2d209af453508709c43eff1b27f", "range": [0, 84]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0475425198674202, -0.05145574361085892, -0.04646195098757744, 0.0041342382319271564, 0.009129631333053112, 0.0037380296271294355, 0.008901878260076046, -0.08766347914934158, -0.06422284990549088, 0.013841874897480011, -0.001970606856048107, 0.04938216507434845, 0.036382365971803665, 0.03830093890428543, -0.03760732337832451, -0.08343061804771423, -0.002044256078079343, -0.012585210613906384, -0.0626482367515564, 0.036967791616916656, -0.005114693194627762, 0.015161010436713696, -0.01148449257016182, 0.03838958591222763, 0.01734074205160141, -0.038306936621665955, -0.02102305367588997, 0.028048334643244743, 0.06378791481256485, -0.039182864129543304, 0.039212893694639206, -0.01340924296528101, 0.013369061052799225, -0.015954557806253433, 2.5745978291524807e-06, 0.010759091936051846, 0.000646244443487376, -0.02786129154264927, -0.002437085146084428, -0.025136539712548256, -