act of outdoor learning initiatives, including the use of yoga and forest schools, on the engagement and social skills of autistic students. It emphasizes the importance of creating a supportive environment that fosters independence and collaboration among students.Impact\nThe lead teacher for this said, \u201c engagement is the most important pre-requisite for learning\u201d and, in terms of engagement, this initiative has had a real impact. It has also raised expectations for the staff team about what the children are capable of. It has demonstrated that the children can do the activities and barriers to their participation have been removed through the providers \u201c encouraging independence in an outdoor safe environment\u201d. The impact has also been apparent through improvements in shared learning and the children\u2019s ability to work in larger groups. The school has seen huge positives in the development of social skills and interaction. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 20, "split_id": 81, "split_idx_start": 39271, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "89d1ff26d4b9d28611b49deb1c160e35e61abf8750a5b924f7776a27ee01c7e8", "range": [302, 472]}, {"doc_id": "0fc904465f0cdcf2326c66725349544b823d2347e55ba62df38ceb781e9520c7", "range": [0, 88]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.007643468212336302, -0.0666130855679512, -0.01587638258934021, -0.0002449478197377175, 0.023698102682828903, 0.009759464301168919, 0.030414795503020287, -0.056782688945531845, -0.020642101764678955, -0.0038781780749559402, -0.00213214592076838, 0.0035183674190193415, 0.002946598455309868, -0.009412226267158985, -0.03819975629448891, -0.07732415199279785, 0.01657756231725216, -0.030213424935936928, -0.04018254578113556, 0.009378636255860329, -0.019347036257386208, -0.002