ool. It is thought to have great benefits for children, with the exciting activities, familiarity and visual supports helping pupils to develop their attention, communication and interaction skills.\nThere is strong use of visuals throughout the school which are the same size and colour. Photos on the classroom and office doors show who is in and out.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n23 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nEach class has an iPad and photos are taken of people and activities that are happening at the school. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 22, "split_id": 92, "split_idx_start": 44864, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "d4b6e37ac0ca80dd732da0345e01cb5095737b5a997f168a86339e0434ee3b3a", "range": [694, 831]}, {"doc_id": "19c3ff4a39be0387d324370dadd18ba172db366fa5cbc7cf79575b71918c0ca6", "range": [0, 187]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.026225730776786804, -0.0554971881210804, -0.03981197997927666, 0.0025311659555882215, -0.003924089018255472, 0.021279780194163322, 0.0339958518743515, -0.03609307482838631, -0.035093776881694794, -0.01380440779030323, 0.012234832160174847, -0.0580386221408844, 0.01903742179274559, 0.01623615063726902, 0.006962713785469532, -0.1022423729300499, 0.005075122229754925, -0.0029243282042443752, -0.052196960896253586, 0.03520887717604637, 0.0004269333148840815, 0.011527284979820251, 0.010234391316771507, 0.027415290474891663, -0.015737639740109444, -0.04694989323616028, -0.003183905966579914, 0.016095532104372978, 0.04965927451848984, -0.03800363466143608, 0.019048327580094337, 0.02506956458091736, -0.02040138840675354, 0.0060284812934696674, 2.3178574792837026e-06, 0.022303182631731033, 0.059447985142469406, -0.05012190341949463, -0.003486974397674203, 0.003212228650227189, -0.0323