 the use of structured visual aids to support autistic students in learning environments. It emphasizes the importance of clear communication and routines to facilitate transitions between activities, helping maintain students' attention and engagement.\u2022 Visual plans are shown on a mini whiteboard showing the sequence of activities.\n\u2022 Items are crossed off the visual plan as they are completed.\n\u2022 The adult clearly indicates the transition between activities ( e.g. \u201c flour shake has finished\u201d).\n\u2022 Using repetition of a routine and anticipation of their turn helps to maintain the pupils\u2019 attention.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 23, "split_id": 95, "split_idx_start": 46753, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "54251627ea7d6fe5f009a0e4755d87256a1082d3020ada835007b1460ebc823b", "range": [792, 874]}, {"doc_id": "2eb94ee58d283f8753fc62610ed88a6cf99cd95d9e7a07104abcae4572fa30b1", "range": [0, 104]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.008072962984442711, -0.08859559148550034, -0.033396780490875244, 0.012003148905932903, -0.019914131611585617, -0.005998291540890932, 0.03943892568349838, -0.03504209592938423, -0.02961524948477745, -0.0009688547579571605, 0.02412145771086216, -0.06191851571202278, 0.0015743691474199295, 0.04241572692990303, -0.022297900170087814, -0.09777528792619705, 0.014887713827192783, -0.005710652098059654, -0.036182451993227005, 0.028810102492570877, -0.015347594395279884, -0.00574555154889822, -0.033973973244428635, 0.03723563998937607, 0.01598544977605343, -0.0481388159096241, -0.006550542078912258, 0.005978098139166832, 0.021115915849804878, -0.0963708907365799, 0.013412196189165115, 0.02978629805147648, -0.002751437947154045, -0.013979408890008926, 2.4334731278941035e-06, 0.01407157443463802