 Laurent, A and Rydell, P (2006) The SCERTS model: a comprehensive educational approach for children with autism spectrum disorders Baltimore: Brookes.\nWatson, J. Davies, G. and Winterton, A (2017) An evaluation of the Attention Autism approach with young children with autism, Good Autism Practice Journal, 18, 2, 79\u201393\nFurther resources\nAutism Education Trust ( http://www.autismeducationtrust.org.uk/)\nNational Standards for Schools 5-16 which sets out key elements of good autism practice in settings for autistic children and young people aged 5 to 16 years\nCompetency Framework for Staff 5-16 which sets out knowledge and skills required for teaching staff working with autistic children and young people aged 5 to 16 years\nAET Parent/Carers Guide: What to look for in your child\u2019s school: a document for parents/\ncarers to complete identifying what they deem to be important for their autistic son or daughter \u2013 free to download from the AET website.\nAET Tools for Teachers\nAET Progression Framework \u2013 a means of recording progress specifically for autistic children and young people and for setting learning intentions.\nThe AET also has a number of autism training hubs in different parts of England which offer training on autism at different levels and for the different age phases ( i.e. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 26, "split_id": 106, "split_idx_start": 52461, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "e02b93cd6742fc187826cb5cee22e18cdd61059283c7b5c36ed0b591101fad70", "range": [933, 1119]}, {"doc_id": "292aa50b0826724d7b3cc6524854c5b9389906dd937fd7b49a14bd5dd649bf9f", "range": [0, 171]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.07001372426748276, -0.12936362624168396, -0.025300029665231705, 0.001978709828108549, 0.000225182244321331