14220844954252243, 0.021916989237070084, 0.02603420987725258, -0.055808283388614655, 0.009011817164719105, -0.052414651960134506, -0.028486452996730804, 0.01780959777534008, -0.05954264849424362, -0.02880984917283058, -0.06673381477594376, 0.08619221299886703, 0.012779776006937027, 0.027369020506739616, -0.0042510926723480225, -0.028924569487571716, 0.036782752722501755, 0.014150834642350674, 0.061671704053878784, 0.04051161929965019, -0.02004898339509964, -0.011039186269044876, 0.014328084886074066, 0.01708311028778553, 0.04824143275618553, -0.00929868221282959, -0.006980474106967449, -0.02840183675289154, 0.006579904351383448, -0.010226632468402386, 0.059825509786605835, -0.03452426940202713, -0.03415437415242195, 0.010994627140462399, -0.00881524570286274, -0.0010100651998072863, -0.03372149541974068, -0.017017371952533722, -0.015270262956619263, 1.9737576411975773e-34, 0.02706080675125122, -0.01527688093483448, 0.028010837733745575, -0.09606900066137314, 0.004715456161648035, 0.001247590989805758, -0.0522896908223629, -0.005053296685218811, 0.005711158271878958, -0.01745481975376606, -0.03424949571490288], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "b6bbb21c27454a873dcf4a5f992735e7f3b9119d692ea3fab1502a62294ac6b7", "content": "This chunk is from Case Study D in the Good Autism Practice Guide, which focuses on Hinderton Special School. It discusses the actions taken to create a supportive learning environment for autistic students by designing a low arousal setting. The training of staff in the SCERTS framework is also highlighted as a critical component in understanding and addressing the needs of autistic children.Good Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n28 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nActions taken and impact\nThe school moved to its own newly designed site and the staff had a great deal of input into the design to make it a low arousal setting. As a result, the environment is calm throughout and there are many spaces available that are secure and allow break out space for students. The site is a state-of-the-art learning space and was awarded the 2014 RIBA architectural prize for the Best Educational and Community Building in London.\nUnderstanding the individual with autism\nP1 \u2013 Understanding the strengths, interests and challenges of the autistic child and young person\nStaff have been trained in SCERTS by Emily Rubin who developed the programme with colleagues in America (Prizant et al ., 2006). ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 28, "split_id": 110, "split_idx_start": 55878, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "806ed6098ea50a09f2a6d41f98e60733f0202b2625730c45f345a5dd8b020fe9", "range": [583, 830]}, {"doc_id": "95c337e2f5ed4eaf5a5001ec4ed6666d7fdc7544b9c1758c16a5dff0de25086e", "range": [0, 9]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.01690567098557949, -0.12710890173912048, -0.03460901603102684, -0.0015037597622722387, -0.022201912477612495, 0.03023521788418293, 0.06515728682279587, -0.04913369566202164, -0.060688335448503494, 0.022827178239822388, 0.011364935897290707, -0.03594524785876274, 0.014422301203012466, 0.00891873612999916, -0.004682896193116903, -0.041123390197753906, 0.03730718418955803, 0.02991016022861004, -0.06483948975801468, 0.008718258701264858, -0.024838216602802277, 0.009568051435053349, -0.0348450168967247, 0.015600143931806087, 0.029325224459171295, -0.0734609067440033, -0.005321737844496965, 0.020410316064953804, 0.013425818644464016, -0.034679193049669266, 0.053207818418741226, 0.020477738231420517, 0.01429239846765995, -0.02648865059018135, 2.3028612758935196e-06, 0.028080465272068977, 0.019283011555671692, -0.028858529403805733, 0.006764137651771307, -0.004488957114517689, -0.048413991928100586, 0.03613210469484329, 0.011144980788230896, 0.046628888696432114, -0.0