915922, 0.015965376049280167, 0.03418222814798355, 0.028013037517666817, -0.0003940673777833581, -0.029954876750707626], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "54fef421288f4327786453700e4a7334fca256b5d19d29fb88840cc1a522d38e", "content": "This chunk is found in Case Study E: Priestnall Secondary School, focusing on collaboration among staff, including speech and language therapists. It illustrates the supportive strategies used to aid students resistant to change and the resources available, such as on-site therapy offices and NHS support, enhancing the school's inclusive practices for autistic students.In another example, with a student who was very resistant to change, the team agreed to use the same language and the same pausing. This close collaboration provides benefits for all staff with different levels of expertise as the more experienced staff model to less experienced staff and share strategies in the discussion and planning.\nThe speech and language therapists have an office on site. This has a room next door with a one-way window so that therapists can observe the students. The school uses NHS speech and language provision and boosts this with additional time they purchase. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 30, "split_id": 125, "split_idx_start": 62754, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "95c1fd4d66b09521e12428576f6acfaaadc734c075cf51c6f06347ae6c0ea009", "range": [368, 500]}, {"doc_id": "cc0fb6a096eac8bea1ea85d5324b2961cceda5a73bc87a421aeb876919561ba8", "range": [0, 102]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04045293852686882, -0.06049002334475517, -0.019669614732265472, 0.027004411444067955, -0.03232065588235855, 0.023973507806658745, 0.05013159662485123, -0.03695924952626228, -0.03160717710852623, 0.0014017445500940084, 0.024745106697082