{"id": "c699cb9b9ee279781064fddd136d78db08f32f42a137ab5a304b44a2d5476a04", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Enabling environments\" section within various case studies highlighting effective practices in schools for autistic children. It focuses on the leadership and management strategies that support the induction and training of staff, ensuring an inclusive environment tailored to the needs of autistic students.Enabling environments\nP5 \u2013 Leadership and management that promotes and embeds good autism practice\nThere is an intensive induction programme in place to bring new staff up to speed with the school\u2019s ways of working. Different people input to the content of this that has evolved over time. All staff including TAs, office staff and the Business Manager attend the induction programme as all have contact with students. Information about the extensive range of professional development on offer is detailed under collaboration and workforce development.\nP6 \u2013 An ethos and environment that fosters social inclusion for children and young people on the autism spectrum\nThe whole environment had been designed with the needs of autistic young people in mind and with input from staff.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 31, "split_id": 128, "split_idx_start": 64052, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "293c89069d960cf25f8977db5bdd93461d6e727b213127705ec71d3c653a955f", "range": [398, 614]}, {"doc_id": "ea474032d0d16f0b38141616c41f18ef79fa5a5a5f4d93bba05b07ef85e9784d", "range": [0, 228]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.049240730702877045, -0.08873937278985977, -0.018966345116496086, 0.011697718873620033, 0.03159851208329201, 0.023508869111537933, 0.016565343365073204, -0.046654798090457916, -0.046514738351106644, 0.01987479999