nix School, which focuses on the implementation of vocational pathways for students with autism and other special needs. It details how students engage in horticulture by growing herbs and lavender, contributing to the school caf\u00e9, which enhances their communication and practical skills while providing work-related experience.herbs are grown and used to make soup to sell in the school caf\u00e9 and lavender is used to make lavender bags). Students work in the garden doing work-related activities, which go towards their ASDAN (qualification to help young people develop knowledge and skills for learning, work and life htt ps://www.asdan.org.uk/about) in horticulture.\nThere is a school caf\u00e9 and this is staffed by students and sells drinks and snacks to staff and visitors. The emphasis is on communication as well as developing other skills. Visuals are very evident in the cafe.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 34, "split_id": 145, "split_idx_start": 71563, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "4ef6a98e6d7fa4b4f64c1b34d8030803f5b9bf03a713b2ff89cfbab8c78d609a", "range": [337, 447]}, {"doc_id": "62ce0bee53b87624b329a436d215b04b7f2f6c6346d63598477f85f99b350adb", "range": [0, 38]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0011737573659047484, -0.021411234512925148, -0.0250077061355114, 0.03648530691862106, 0.0009588172542862594, -0.005738256964832544, 0.035044047981500626, -0.018239261582493782, 0.006337616126984358, -0.0023911106400191784, 0.05334799736738205, 0.04195462912321091, 0.007229503709822893, 0.01845635659992695, -0.03615301474928856, -0.036426298320293427, 0.013037582859396935, 0.018684694543480873, -0.10918646305799484, 0.00012785392755176872, -0.0017613322706893086, 0.027402127161622047, 0.017412280663847923, 0.03709438443183899, -0.042