ning resources provided by the Autism Education Trust (AET). It emphasizes the availability of specialized autism training hubs across England, catering to different age groups and educational phases, contributing to the overall theme of improving practices for autistic children in schools.The AET also has a number of autism training hubs in different parts of England which offer training on autism at different levels and for the different age phases ( i.e. Early Years, 5 to 16 and 16 to 25 years) \u2013 see the AET website ( http://www.autismeducationtrust.org.uk ) for details of the training hub closest to you\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n37 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nCase Study E: Priestnall Secondary School\nType of school Mainstream secondary school in the North West of England.\nSchool website www.priestnall.stockport.sch.uk\nNumber on roll 1276\nAge group 11 to 16 years\nFocus of the case study\nDeveloping a whole school ethos on inclusion for all students and multi-disciplinary working\nPrinciples illustrated 1. Understanding the strengths, interests and challenges of the autistic child and young person\n2. Enabling the voice of the autistic child and young person to contribute to and influence decisions\n3. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 36, "split_id": 150, "split_idx_start": 76368, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "e4f816ae5db9e1d0eee465f8f50c93237dcc0966cde23a3839683f5ebcc32341", "range": [2191, 2362]}, {"doc_id": "0536c97ff0eafe3f72cfe0cfcaf84cf6bcb184b727f2eeca133077aaf2c392fd", "range": [0, 102]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.04457683116197586, -0.10542068630456924, -0.01633850671350956, 0.03273257985711098, 0.005954553838819265, 0.03925640881061554, 0.029685014858841896, -0.0527181290090