g the effective employment of staff including teaching assistants and therapists, as well as key details about student engagement and success, specifically referencing the case of a student named Max.The NEET (Not in Education, Employment or Training) figure is zero.\nThe school employs 14 TAs, two Speech and Language Therapists (1.4 FTE), a part-time Educational Psychologist (EP) and a full-time psychotherapist. There are excellent links with Inscape House School (an independent school run by the Together Trust). Priestnall school has four autistic students on dual roll at Inscape House school.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n38 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nUnderstanding the individual with autism\nP1 \u2013 Understanding the strengths, interests and challenges of the autistic child and young person\nCase study of Max (fictitious name) Year 10 (aged 15) (information taken from a discussion with Max and his form teacher)\nIn Year 7, Max said there were lots of changes to adjust to, the two main ones being new pupils and the new environment. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 37, "split_id": 153, "split_idx_start": 78021, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "529f0aa4dfe59e976d0b1ac26d38c73f1dd8c3ae4dc2fd16fafa323742da1e39", "range": [432, 500]}, {"doc_id": "93b9effb0d686723308ed7370c653717792c08f290a4e37ca4b69d9273129297", "range": [0, 466]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.038267139345407486, -0.08844882994890213, -0.005298770032823086, 0.019932424649596214, 0.01379241794347763, 0.013239285908639431, 0.04717617854475975, -0.06173185259103775, -0.055034562945365906, -0.005440243054181337, 0.032552413642406464, -0.047503452748060226, 0.0018840237753465772, -0.01292519923299551, 0.011487843468785286, -0.01914421841502189