269219756, 0.0028992369771003723, 0.04680914804339409, 0.053466375917196274, -0.008558396250009537, 0.011742232367396355, -0.04249601438641548, 0.008314787410199642, -0.022666215896606445, 0.06901796907186508, -0.03803003951907158, -0.028158757835626602, -0.013887202367186546, 0.023189198225736618, -0.024512214586138725, -0.03217633441090584, -0.010693330317735672, 0.02296033874154091, 2.088197296791156e-34, 0.02559775300323963, 0.03445020690560341, 0.025471998378634453, -0.047365669161081314, 0.006982327904552221, 0.012449854984879494, -0.019705474376678467, -0.010560853406786919, -0.023642636835575104, -0.0031335894018411636, -0.021625040099024773], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "93b9effb0d686723308ed7370c653717792c08f290a4e37ca4b69d9273129297", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study E from the \"Good Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies,\" which describes the experiences of Max, a Year 10 student with autism at Priestnall Secondary School. It highlights his challenges and adaptations during his transition from primary to secondary education, emphasizing supportive staff practices and peer relationships.Good Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n38 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nUnderstanding the individual with autism\nP1 \u2013 Understanding the strengths, interests and challenges of the autistic child and young person\nCase study of Max (fictitious name) Year 10 (aged 15) (information taken from a discussion with Max and his form teacher)\nIn Year 7, Max said there were lots of changes to adjust to, the two main ones being new pupils and the new environment. It said it was hard for him to adapt to the new classrooms and to the teachers. He felt that variety was a good thing and that he now had a lot more friends than he had at primary school. He described Priestnall as a very friendly place and said that staff gave advice on how to calm down, rather than criticising you when you had a meltdown. He said, \u201c If staff see I am upset, they will ask me what\u2019s wrong and what\u2019s making you feel depressed \u2013 or say, Can I do anything to help you?\u201d\nMax\u2019s form tutor is very proactive and inclusive and visited him at primary school before he started at Priestnall. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 38, "split_id": 154, "split_idx_start": 78423, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "36b45c1769967429407117de5b2be5ee13a2c272f607f454a1d22cfeda6284c5", "range": [402, 868]}, {"doc_id": "2100a04ae13eb428317f62f841ea41f7bfb4c6bf639f78c040c3a531fe59f24e", "range": [0, 261]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.05863003432750702, -0.10111456364393234, 0.0015898223500698805, 0.025476062670350075, 0.020594289526343346, 0.022338777780532837, 0.013273023068904877, -0.05664413049817085, -0.04293972626328468, 0.003800611710175872, 0.03480525314807892, -0.07325218617916107, 0.0018779145320877433, -0.025822943076491356, -0.009301308542490005, -0.0739738866686821, 0.010421977378427982, 0.02974501997232437, -0.05527166277170181, -0.0017378986813127995, 0.003019861411303282, 0.0014134369557723403, -0.004653956741094589, 0.03125190734863281, 0.020145755261182785, -0.03763534501194954, 0.01186300814151764, 0.03778452426195145, 0.041033461689949036, -0.008107651025056839, 0.0280928872525692, -0.004526112228631973, -0.013833657838404179, 0.004918460734188557, 2.456779611748061e-06, 0.037504635751247406, 0.016981227323412895, -0.037301983684301376, -0.003272325498983264, 0.01384637039154768, -0.07452195882797241, 0.007516201585531235, 0.005190878175199032, 0.05122214928269386, -0.006876371335238218, -0.028624413534998894, 0.013373780064284801, -0.006896711885929108, 0.04623008519411087, -0.014908905141055584, -0.015868986025452614, 0.017510762438178062, -0.020690884441137314, -0.0348721