developing an inclusive environment for autistic students. It highlights the support provided for autistic girls, including tailored social skills groups, the use of technology for homework assistance, and fostering a school culture that encourages students to disclose their diagnoses and engage with their peers.Four of the girls felt it was easier to do homework at school as there were fewer distractions. Some staff use the App My Homework which they found helpful.\nThe SALT and TAs run groups for the girls on social understanding and to practise the skills required. Some girls do not want to share their diagnosis but the school ethos helps some to disclose their autism. Priestnall convenes several social groups for children and uses the Talkabout (Kelly) approach to develop conversation skills.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 39, "split_id": 161, "split_idx_start": 82074, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "5e6553c9f3fca57763bef3f8a95eea9d86a7201db80e8c7f9ae6dcb1ac91b48c", "range": [782, 878]}, {"doc_id": "b22ec9a68d529738b21e4a84d05c2ee3c008cd4bbd0b09c4e15a9db26717735a", "range": [0, 127]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0353090763092041, -0.06821694225072861, -0.033013444393873215, -0.013195717707276344, 0.025022048503160477, 0.018493961542844772, 0.05738624930381775, -0.04844506457448006, -0.03516770154237747, 0.006435210816562176, 0.030627114698290825, -0.015531708486378193, 0.008402662351727486, 0.039221424609422684, 0.0022875331342220306, -0.015818258747458458, 0.009004447609186172, 0.01195555180311203, -0.015877163037657738, 0.017431091517210007, 0.0011216859566047788, 0.041309621185064316, -0.015278380364179611, 0.020627623423933983, 0.04326488450169563, -0.04622206091880798, 0.03142794594168663, -0.0090892119333148, 0.0230392385