9807831645012, -0.05073000118136406, 0.013069985434412956, -0.04284501448273659, 0.015496219508349895, 0.03156578168272972, -0.046693071722984314, 0.038373950868844986, -0.029828691855072975, 0.0773979052901268, -0.026518097147345543, -0.03863679990172386, -0.012722407467663288, -0.08415288478136063, 0.05151650309562683, 0.04145537316799164, 0.04116629436612129, -0.008224699646234512, -0.034897081553936005, -0.005815798416733742, 0.02534785121679306, 0.05154730752110481, 0.017736176028847694, -0.002055839169770479, 0.004745997954159975, -0.06763680279254913, 0.012973984703421593, -0.05312779173254967, 0.0413978137075901, -0.03170435503125191, -0.024099988862872124, 0.019318703562021255, 0.013281469233334064, 0.007970979437232018, -0.01993807964026928, -0.049663037061691284, -0.01752469316124916, 1.817993504659715e-34, 0.03916707634925842, -0.0006770297768525779, 0.025958852842450142, -0.04803572967648506, 0.020254524424672127, 0.002469473984092474, 0.021737955510616302, -0.022808752954006195, -0.0028448959346860647, 0.024267541244626045, -0.005012763664126396], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "48f4484b6446e379f60a4609069eb8a3d67dffdfa540a5a0791bd0e24c0644ca", "content": "This chunk is from Case Study E, which focuses on Priestnall Secondary School's inclusive practices for autistic students. It highlights a parent's, Debby's, positive experience with the school's approach, emphasizing effective communication regarding her son Max's progress and the individualized support provided by teachers, showcasing the school's commitment to fostering an inclusive environment.Her experience has proved that the whole school has developed an ethos of including students with very diverse physical, developmental and emotional needs, including autism.\nDebby explained that, \u201c At parents evening \u2013 whereas I used to have to explain possible interventions in the past, and the staff always asked why he would not join in or sit in the circle and I had to tell them. At Priestnall school, we do not talk about strategies, we just talk about Max and his progress.\u201d\nDebby also explained how one of the subject teachers interviewed Max instead of asking him to do a piece of writing and marked him on the interview.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n40 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\n\u201c There are some teachers at Priestnall school who don\u2019t get it as well as others \u2013 as there are in every school \u2013 but I feel his subject teachers have been chosen just for him and his form teacher is amazing and is so straight with me. The school is not defensive and is very open to collaboration. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 39, "split_id": 165, "split_idx_start": 84367, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "9364d1cc37823902e545bcb446a4bd496ed92a0dd3f5e63b63f90fe5e9d1bd02", "range": [783, 957]}, {"doc_id": "187b42fea5817fd5428e731f76f689d59e7ac0be9605d379e7762e07581bbb1b", "range": [0, 63]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.040825922042131424, -0.07211833447217941, -0.03189289569854736, 0.04349236190319061, -0.03063897415995598, 0.036566056311130524, 0.03286108374595642, -0.038153670728206635, -0.07570508867502213, -0.0066185807809233665, 0.050725530833005905, -0.06400808691978455, 0.04057401418685913, -0.005925625562667847, -0.03053884208202362, -0.011786543764173985, 0.0066508278250694275, 0.05297177657485008, -0.05325163155794144, 0.011367359198629856, -0.0076508899219334126, 0.02697751112282276, -0.007471762597560883, 0.03686243295669556, 0.020472610369324684, -0.027891242876648903, -0.015397310256958008, 0.030745867639780045, 0.006285212468355894, -0.019613562151789665, 0.03169441223144531, -0.006607802119106054, -0.02469027042388916, -0.017617931589484215, 2.1078715235489653e-06, 0.0378