010125710628926754, 0.02630896307528019, -0.06894408911466599, 0.020672684535384178, -0.019968602806329727, 0.02656017430126667, -0.019196955487132072, -0.0028220312669873238, 0.021630926057696342, -0.023389926180243492], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "187b42fea5817fd5428e731f76f689d59e7ac0be9605d379e7762e07581bbb1b", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study E: Priestnall Secondary School, which highlights the inclusive practices and supportive environment for autistic students. It specifically describes the positive experiences of Max, a student with autism, and his mother's trust in the school's approach to collaboration and understanding of autism-related challenges.The school is not defensive and is very open to collaboration. I thought I might have to come in a lot, but I don\u2019t as I trust them such a lot. Other parents seem similarly happy.\n\u201c Max did not talk until he was four and his self-regulation was very poor. He has had meltdowns at Priestnall but even a teacher who does not know autism well will come into the corridor and ask Max if he is OK rather than telling him off. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 40, "split_id": 166, "split_idx_start": 85320, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "48f4484b6446e379f60a4609069eb8a3d67dffdfa540a5a0791bd0e24c0644ca", "range": [953, 1016]}, {"doc_id": "af8b850cfc37b303b0251c9528b43cc54516237607195b97dba85945eb1df4c3", "range": [0, 165]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03372664749622345, -0.025456668809056282, -0.024791380390524864, 0.02354685589671135, 0.014708636328577995, 0.012407136149704456, 0.021749790757894516, -0.07194556295871735, -0.05704515427350998, 0.011381208896636963, 0.028444992378354073, -0.051361083984375, 0.015983622521162033, -0.0033672056160867214, -0.02904743