15825, -0.021588562056422234, 0.034502334892749786, 0.042801424860954285, 0.03583848848938942, 0.03243923559784889, -0.003947085700929165, -0.04433716461062431, 0.02100677788257599, -0.03444427624344826, 0.05023915320634842, -0.06264679878950119, -0.04423091933131218, 0.008861481212079525, 0.01915862411260605, 0.03458506241440773, -0.038135282695293427, -0.02765427716076374, 0.006510206498205662, 1.9373958356713015e-34, 0.013424216769635677, 0.008282436057925224, 0.02342858538031578, -0.07005343586206436, 0.04353618249297142, -0.013404184952378273, -0.03934089466929436, -0.006990769878029823, 0.008969008922576904, 0.023952946066856384, -0.03501592203974724], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "af8b850cfc37b303b0251c9528b43cc54516237607195b97dba85945eb1df4c3", "content": "This chunk is from Case Study E: Priestnall Secondary School, which focuses on developing an inclusive ethos for autistic students and the leadership that supports effective practices in special educational needs (SEND). It highlights how staff interact with students like Max during moments of distress, emphasizing understanding and support rather than confrontation, reflecting the school's commitment to autism inclusivity.He has had meltdowns at Priestnall but even a teacher who does not know autism well will come into the corridor and ask Max if he is OK rather than telling him off. He tries to comfort him. Staff don\u2019t confront him \u2013 they try to understand him.\u201d\nP5 \u2013 Leadership and management that promotes and embeds good autism practice\nGareth Morewood, the school\u2019s Director of Curriculum Support, has been a huge influence on the development of the school\u2019s SEND policy and practice and has developed a website which contains many of the resources developed. He has written about the need for the whole setting to be saturated in an inclusive ethos (Morewood et al ., 2011) and has developed the school\u2019s workforce and expertise to address the needs of students with autism and with SEND.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 40, "split_id": 167, "split_idx_start": 85576, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "187b42fea5817fd5428e731f76f689d59e7ac0be9605d379e7762e07581bbb1b", "range": [256, 421]}, {"doc_id": "1c9cb630defae4d76b47747b42c23a4a2c3834db0eb8a622bad5d76d0b3115a8", "range": [0, 123]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06711611896753311, -0.09677258878946304, -0.025829104706645012, 0.05073897913098335, 0.017805639654397964, 0.039315398782491684, 0.016410792246460915, -0.03177664056420326, -0.04323955997824669, -0.0074956463649868965, 0.038874611258506775, -0.030316254124045372, 0.012593889608979225, 0.004426497966051102, 0.009526029229164124, -0.03810622915625572, 0.004719986114650965, 0.06200210005044937, -0.011722797527909279, 0.027664875611662865, 0.009499896317720413, 0.022278351709246635, -0.0033350144512951374, 0.024666961282491684, 0.036424942314624786, -0.002936007222160697, -0.010020805522799492, 0.04619688168168068, 0.015810390934348106, -0.023371096700429916, 0.02218129299581051, -0.03327489644289017, -0.023716280236840248, -0.03209952265024185, 2.14605825021863e-06, 0.04371827468276024, -0.003978850319981575, -0.019913027063012123, 0.03052731417119503, -0.027392495423555374, -0.05716043710708618, 0.0025462054181843996, -0.020394260063767433, 0.04928501695394516, 0.006293751765042543, 0.0210895799100399, 0.009780323132872581, 0.06504152715206146, 0.015557583421468735, 0.004091883543878794, -0.0034052652772516012, 0.01959262043237686, -0.023881061002612114, -0.014511793851852417, 0.007796964142471552, -0.02331024967133999, 0.032381173223257065, -0.09555190056562424, 0.01799011044204235, 0.031246529892086983, -0.01623641699552536, 0.03059798665344715, -0.024854198098182678, -0.04799541085958481, 