tion skills and promote social interactions, emphasizing the importance of voluntary participation in these activities.Lego groups have also been set up. Ellen has trained up three TAs in interventions and they now run these groups on their own.\nThrough discussion, Ellen helps to raise students\u2019 awareness about their conversation skills and how this is the basis of forming friendships. Attendance at the groups is always a choice. Ellen explains the group to a student and then suggests they give it a go. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 40, "split_id": 171, "split_idx_start": 87632, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "6279d703eae89c5b8d80e2c75206967e30395d44eb7c4f618f3d9e591f738b89", "range": [364, 399]}, {"doc_id": "defc92f4512ec2ca474773341180aeecc4205eec63aea449593f60943c3946f9", "range": [0, 75]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03817690536379814, -0.042980652302503586, -0.03746534883975983, 0.03493700176477432, 0.023224910721182823, 0.026677731424570084, 0.04352741315960884, -0.0599110946059227, -0.06520367413759232, 0.018930159509181976, -0.00036184731288813055, -0.0640028789639473, 0.03050728142261505, -0.010012838989496231, 0.010135621763765812, -0.05249356850981712, 0.015926964581012726, 0.010065530426800251, 0.004212955944240093, -0.0026569399051368237, 0.009351172484457493, 0.026876842603087425, -0.028944306075572968, 0.0344780758023262, 0.026875203475356102, -0.011337489821016788, 0.030438197776675224, -0.03107241354882717, 0.027760948985815048, -0.007669424172490835, 0.050399571657180786, 0.013519350439310074, -0.010899427346885204, 0.003917003516107798, 2.239329660369549e-06, 0.055252183228731155, 0.043302278965711594, -0.04234936088323593, -0.02848108485341072, -0.013957275077700615, -0.06289549171924591, 0.024159677326679