77314233779907, 0.01763729192316532, 2.8939448384335265e-05, -0.015807919204235077, -0.008904964663088322, 0.04989856481552124, -0.008170600049197674, -0.018176354467868805, -0.009147522039711475, -0.020482972264289856, 0.004826158285140991, -0.02137775532901287, 0.03271515667438507, 0.00660339230671525, 0.01809060014784336, 0.008142123930156231, -0.0027169224340468645, -0.06783711910247803, 0.04021899774670601, 0.036035556346178055, 0.035445742309093475, 3.7316203815862536e-05, -0.014212253503501415, 0.008978365920484066, -0.03244507685303688, -0.0016540109645575285, 0.027888376265764236, -0.04301956295967102, -0.005018218886107206, -0.07284092903137207, 0.09354148060083389, -0.002889244584366679, 0.033456314355134964, -0.001806954969651997, -0.03876147046685219, 0.01944558694958687, 0.0028556406032294035, 0.056117311120033264, 0.020329615101218224, -0.022830039262771606, -0.023487159982323647, 0.029108040034770966, 0.034320175647735596, 0.03684293478727341, 0.02773101069033146, 0.01739457994699478, -0.04307929426431656, 0.027650916948914528, -0.05581563711166382, 0.05290752649307251, -0.03126029297709465, -0.03465213626623154, 0.03997045010328293, 0.010886702686548233, 0.0036054227966815233, -0.046052806079387665, -0.05727988854050636, 0.016950199380517006, 1.7844341740930705e-34, 0.00714716175571084, 0.022461216896772385, 0.016348889097571373, -0.0618622824549675, 0.033644311130046844, 0.007353449240326881, -0.0010727184126153588, 0.010569782927632332, 0.029177213087677956, -0.02025407738983631, -0.03476540371775627], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "39511293e36440f5c2b60723f965aec61c15aa500c8795a24374ce301c832694", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study E, focusing on Priestnall Secondary School, which highlights the support structures for autistic students. It discusses the role of Ellen, the school's Speech and Language Therapist, in attending post-diagnostic meetings to develop action plans for autistic students, alongside the training and roles of Teaching Assistants at the school.Ellen also attends ADAPT meetings \u2013 the post diagnostic meetings commissioned and funded by the CCG (Clinical Commissioning Group) and part of the Local Authority Autism Pathway. These are held at the school and result in an action plan for the autistic students.\nDiscussion with Julie: the manager for the Teaching Assistants\nThe 14 TAs at the school are solely employed for students with SEND. There are 3 TAs for the students on dual roll with Inscape House special school (employed by Inscape House school), 2 TAs for Looked After Children and 9 other TAs. All the TAs receive a lot of training in their paid time and their career development is encouraged. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 41, "split_id": 175, "split_idx_start": 88946, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0a87ae662f0703c120ea9af01cfc45bec81700dd70e956c937e42ed33eb47c9b", "range": [350, 529]}, {"doc_id": "b8e5bec0810fdefdad6064a2deb0facf8158eb72889ba46266c86d3431f8ff53", "range": [0, 101]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.014398046769201756, -0.0788484439253807, -0.012149949558079243, 0.025981556624174118, 0.012145144864916801, 0.03043844737112522, 0.015508024953305721, -0.045470479875802994, -0.04657277092337608, 0.005697664339095354, 0.04341655969619751, -0.04243315011262894, 0.005263196304440498, -0.002565281465649605, -0.005693957209587097, -0.06386129558086395, 0.00038457009941339493, 0.006495221517980099, -0.058492545038461685, -0.007841595448553562, 0.018441680818796158, 0.04719049856066704, -0.012316429987549782, 0.041726019233465195, 0.023448064923286438, -0.01976937986910343, 0.015341011807322502, 0.011316074058413506, 0.05110599473118782, 0.007596313487738371, 0.02556237392127514, -0.0035666648764163256, -0.023116523399949074, 0.004