.019564589485526085, 0.0038027416449040174, 0.010857938788831234, 0.037557609379291534, 0.010333424434065819, -0.029800094664096832], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "8a441884d14a05b086e270611a1d9d99c2829a9ab86961d0b343a5c4d1234c9c", "content": "This chunk is from Case Study E about Priestnall Secondary School, which highlights the challenges faced by an autistic student, particularly regarding transitions from primary to secondary school. It discusses the implementation of a flexi-schooling package for the student and the efforts by TAs, Tanisha and Sheridan, to enhance reading skills and understanding of autism-related behaviors among staff.He has found transition from the primary school hard and the student currently leaves school after Period 3 as a short-term measure as part of an agreed flexi-schooling package. Sheridan did a Boost Your Reading course last term and wants to roll this out to other students. She tried this successfully with a Year 9 student with a low reading age.\nBoth Tanisha and Sheridan thought that most staff used the student passports very well. They said that some staff struggle to know which behaviours arise from their autism and which are a choice. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 41, "split_id": 180, "split_idx_start": 91050, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b8fa233cab8402acabd6b0938ea4ba524c375522853e1a15badd386d2eeef6cc", "range": [399, 577]}, {"doc_id": "64accac5b49ef166a1b19ed389e07cb73a7689eea99caf5be080bc682c37bf88", "range": [0, 108]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.01804657094180584, -0.08121468871831894, -0.03469977527856827, 0.00370555161498487, -0.0194717887789011, 0.05051529407501221, 0.0638727992773056, -0.017456091940402985, -0.038798537105321884, -0.011164703406393528, 0.07396062463521957, -