732214078307152, -0.01258984487503767, 0.058370884507894516, -0.006244480609893799, 0.042181599885225296, 0.023109812289476395, -0.05797557160258293, -0.01779990643262863, 0.04865730553865433, 0.06676174700260162, 0.01767764985561371, 0.02552078478038311, 0.004501025192439556, -0.05716300383210182, 0.00133652170188725, -0.02558879181742668, 0.06967008858919144, 0.014493489637970924, -0.02710823342204094, 0.009763621725142002, 0.008908961899578571, 0.0037097339518368244, 0.007034321781247854, -0.08992824703454971, -0.005645745899528265, 2.105480048401869e-34, 0.009249018505215645, 0.02687130495905876, 0.027174435555934906, -0.07942826300859451, -0.0153744425624609, -0.0108032850548625, -0.033694375306367874, 0.009174736216664314, -0.007601393852382898, -0.007920365780591965, -0.044696927070617676], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "1b072affdc817f82cfe18bfa34381628356b4a6c8a6b0a12af47bff9aef7f306", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study E: Priestnall Secondary School, which focuses on developing an inclusive ethos for students, particularly those with autism. It discusses the positive perspective of Rachael, the school's Educational Psychologist, regarding the support provided by staff and the implementation of flexi-schooling to accommodate the needs of autistic students. Additionally, it highlights the collaboration with Dr. Caroline Bond from the University of Manchester for research purposes related to educational psychology.Rachael\u2019s view of the school is that Priestnall staff are very supportive and creative. Flexi-\nschooling is often not well regarded by other schools but Priestnall school has found that some autistic students find full-time attendance overwhelming and do not have the emotional capacity for this. Attending part-time and studying fewer subjects can work very well and serve to keep students in education. This is an example of flexi-schooling and is used as part of a planned, short-term measure designed to enhance engagement.\nDiscussion with Dr. Caroline Bond from the University of Manchester on their research links with Priestnall school\nCaroline\u2019s main role is to provide a link to the Trainee Educational Psychology course run by Manchester University. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 42, "split_id": 187, "split_idx_start": 94510, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "62848dd2d88e46f3ae572a00a70739ee77a1864414fe87fd214c9a594ef13b98", "range": [566, 654]}, {"doc_id": "5eab44edfa459a88c9d539854a03ae7288a3f16b2ed65aeb18461d694233544f", "range": [0, 232]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.012736871838569641, -0.06208113208413124, -0.03178887441754341, 0.010122339241206646, -0.008867457509040833, 0.05370418727397919, 0.032015856355428696, -0.06298741698265076, -0.019597666338086128, 0.02362806163728237, 0.04270503669977188, -0.020821984857320786, -0.020036524161696434, 0.017919665202498436, 0.0026232621166855097, -0.046575386077165604, -0.005382510367780924, 0.026375355198979378, -0.04053902253508568, 0.014418807812035084, -0.006134328432381153, 0.018159786239266396, -0.012623228132724762, 0.011458939872682095, 0.024276992306113243, -0.026553256437182426, 0.012901204638183117, 0.007579993922263384, 0.06412529945373535, 0.0021660192869603634, 0.03966669365763664, 0.015381595119833946, -0.023889437317848206, 0.013933422975242138, 2.5022820864251116e-06, 0.049390558153390884, 0.018193840980529785, -0.026796478778123856, -0.007791657466441393, -0.016717582941055298, -0.11045821011066437, 0.030029797926545143, 0.025033295154571533, 0.05419064685702324, -0.0007644017459824681, 0.0031537143513560295, 0.0005054674111306667, -0.005244053900241852, 0.02974819950759411, -0.05559656396508217, -0.005178044084459543, 0.008511669933795929, 0.01657133176922798, -0.010254759341478348, 0.0