ng and exams for students who struggle with traditional writing methods.It is designed for use in exams, but is not so good for Maths symbols. Some readers have individual dictionaries and it is possible to change the speed, volume, and handedness. Students also use Read, Write, Gold where what is typed is read back.\nDragon Dictate with predictive text is used for the majority of GCSE exams at Priestnall for one student. He started using it at the beginning of Year 11 and then the school applied for access arrangements to ensure he could use the software for his exams.\f", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 43, "split_id": 190, "split_idx_start": 96327, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "8821100ed2a11f2b5177cc7696dac25871d4744b43d92c8f03c5e6ef2380ce94", "range": [616, 687]}, {"doc_id": "420732137872669c836303c0a2cb88dd4aa332494c1d7470e3aec54ddd998dc8", "range": [0, 151]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [-0.007351167034357786, -0.04461217671632767, -0.038145456463098526, 0.0009817482205107808, -0.03164926543831825, 0.00389019213616848, 0.06967184692621231, -0.002359897829592228, -0.009992690756917, -0.014110643416643143, 0.024121439084410667, -0.04660049080848694, 0.044032108038663864, 0.009268022142350674, -0.009750875644385815, -0.059549685567617416, 0.0009858510456979275, -0.015131528489291668, -0.044845834374427795, 0.00939424429088831, 0.002331296680495143, 0.011283120140433311, -0.06480888277292252, 0.055956121534109116, -0.0002802833041641861, -0.05293041095137596, -0.007977285422384739, -0.00941024161875248, 0.00747205875813961, -0.03682679310441017, 0.01613287441432476, 0.0583820715546608, -0.02462249994277954, 0.05860273167490959, 2.1091786948090885e-06, 0.005333131179213524, 0.03034784644842148, -0.02493247389793396, -0.02606556750833988