-0.03253902122378349, 0.0017257648287340999, 0.02083701081573963, -0.06835708022117615, -0.0024848429020494223, -0.07285827398300171, 0.05842597410082817, -0.0013268039328977466, -0.03906572610139847, -0.017582964152097702, -0.024144383147358894, 0.07349954545497894, 0.007084072567522526, 0.06818117946386337, 0.02969159185886383, 0.011313906870782375, -0.027819685637950897, 0.019076410681009293, 0.0351702943444252, 0.030514968559145927, -0.004212574101984501, -0.0006830699276179075, -0.03984830155968666, -0.007337288931012154, -0.014846669510006905, 0.014627127908170223, -0.0015876601682975888, 0.01220923662185669, -0.01235383190214634, 0.0003154281002935022, -0.009362980723381042, -0.07165774703025818, -0.012452052906155586, 0.0018657564651221037, 1.6910887875838717e-34, -0.036539457738399506, 0.010071221739053726, 0.027305977419018745, -0.0047360984608531, 0.0024648536927998066, 0.006640505511313677, 0.030297743156552315, 0.0012416699901223183, 0.040286675095558167, -0.03116978146135807, -0.03292421996593475], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "47cd3569e8cdeaa217d8d7647682d98d5e3f948cb56229c75a7aea11bec03b75", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Transferable Practice\" section in the Good Autism Practice Guide, providing actionable recommendations for educators and staff. It suggests strategies for enhancing inclusive practices, collaborating with professionals, fostering community support, and utilizing technology to support autistic students' learning and development in various educational settings.Transferable practice \u2013 actions you could try in your setting\n\u2022 Consider how a whole school or setting approach to good inclusive practice can be developed or enhanced\n\u2022 Consider the employment of different professionals to support the work with autistic students ( e.g. SALT, EOP, OT, psychotherapist)\n\u2022 Consider making links with local Universities to develop research ideas and evaluate practice\n\u2022 Transition \u2013 make resources with photos of key staff and places for students who would benefit and use Social Stories to support their understanding\n\u2022 Run peer awareness sessions for different year groups to inform them about hidden disabilities including autism\n\u2022 Organize an event for parents and carers to provide information, education, support and to foster community and belonging\n\u2022 Consider how TAs and subject staff are kept up to date with key information on autism and individual students\n\u2022 Consider alternative ways to record for those students who find handwriting difficult ( e.g. Dragon Dictate, voice activated software)\n\u2022 Support students with reading by using a Reader pen.\nReferences\nMorewood, GD., Humphrey, N and Symes, W (2011) Mainstreaming autism: making it work, Good Autism Practice Journal, 12, 2, 62\u201368\nParsons, S. and Kovshoff H. (2019) Building the evidence-base through school-research partnerships in autism education: The Autism Community Research Network @ Southampton [ACoRNS]], Good Autism Practice Journal, 20, 1, 5\u201312\nHebron, J. and Bond, C. (eds) (2019) Education and Girls on the Autism Spectrum, Developing an Integrated Approach. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 44, "split_id": 192, "split_idx_start": 97220, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "420732137872669c836303c0a2cb88dd4aa332494c1d7470e3aec54ddd998dc8", "range": [540, 811]}, {"doc_id": "2368be8f5b6712a362e675f66be4ed68e9c44b2b6e8ce2b242d6cccbc366937b", "range": [0, 456]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06471080332994461, -0.10882643610239029, -0.02554251439869404, 0.010037336498498917, 0.0002711524721235037, 0.030280867591500282, 0.0627177506685257, -0.034233760088682175, -0.04432696849107742, -0.023175407201051712, 0.02715877629816532, -0.040409669280