autism and PDA: a personal perspective from a 14-\nyear old student, Good Autism Practice Journal, 20, 1, 27\u201328\nhttp://www.gdmorewood.com \u2013 a website which contains many resources developed at the school.\nAutism Education Trust ( http://www.autismeducationtrust.org.uk/)\nNational Standards for Schools 5-16 which sets out key elements of good autism practice in settings for autistic children and young people aged 5 to 16 years\nCompetency Framework for Staff 5-16 which sets out knowledge and skills required for teaching staff working with autistic children and young people aged 5 to 16 years\nAET Parent/Carers Guide: What to look for in your child\u2019s school: a document for parents/\ncarers to complete identifying what they deem to be important for their autistic son or daughter \u2013 free to download from the AET website.\nAET Tools for Teachers\nAET Progression Framework \u2013 a means of recording progress specifically for autistic children and young people and for setting learning intentions.\nThe AET also has a number of autism training hubs in different parts of England which offer training on autism at different levels and for the different age phases ( i.e. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 44, "split_id": 193, "split_idx_start": 98336, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "47cd3569e8cdeaa217d8d7647682d98d5e3f948cb56229c75a7aea11bec03b75", "range": [1116, 1572]}, {"doc_id": "7e775ad195b9be33bc75c1c3cd37380a53a0c18b9b86d2beef387afc72438711", "range": [0, 171]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06972895562648773, -0.10962595790624619, -0.0127364881336689, 0.013307832181453705, 0.009882636368274689, 0.038374174386262894, 0.06555989384651184, -0.04969834163784981, -0.05276937782764435, -0.0279112309217453, 0.03084835410118103, 