l}, {"id": "17cc65a74a8c9b5244f8d3334fcdf109cc146c89fbba0b347baad4b99e7a65a6", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study F: Phoenix School, which details the school's outreach efforts and partnerships with local institutions to support autistic students within mainstream education. It highlights the collaboration with the Phoenix Outreach Service and its role in aiding students' transition and educational success in the Tower Hamlets area.The two schools are close and accessible. There are strong links to a Post-19 college within Tower Hamlets and the school is looking to start their own Post-\n16 College later this year.\nOutreach work\nThe Phoenix Outreach Service (POS) consists of six specialist advisory teachers with experience and expertise in supporting pupils with a diagnosis of autism. The team supports 600 pupils in mainstream education and this is majority funded by the Local Authority.\nThe service provides very effective support for pupils across the borough of Tower Hamlets and shares the strategies developed and used at Phoenix school. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 47, "split_id": 199, "split_idx_start": 102843, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "5be416db37f8e6070f9e187f23cfb761a6bc74f4f4887c3dbb8201479e02da9f", "range": [459, 501]}, {"doc_id": "18fe5886de3bdfc8e195f77fafbf8c812d1257457257139b7aa174ac1362f80a", "range": [0, 155]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0006929165683686733, -0.08852576464414597, -0.013506042771041393, 0.004470622166991234, 0.011151470243930817, 0.047320932149887085, -0.02384134568274021, -0.0560331866145134, -0.02351875603199005, 0.010838665999472141, 0.032802682369947433, -0.010386377573013306, 0.01167632918804884, 0.02031225711107254, -0.016642523929476738, -0.062254663556814194, -0.00312258629