d30d36aacee5053ee7f0f9151b80be0c37b1202283c7de64ca25f", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study F: Phoenix School, which focuses on autism-specific strategies within the school's framework. It discusses the implementation of the Zones of Regulation approach and communication systems like PECS as part of efforts to support students with autism in understanding their emotions and enhancing communication skills.The school uses the Zones of Regulation approach developed by Leah Kuypers (2011). Staff have the coloured zones on their lanyards. Pupils will come and ask questions in class and staff will help the children identify which zone they are in.\nCommunication systems are visible around the school ( e.g. the use of the Picture Exchange Communication system (PECS) (Bondy and Frost, 2002)). ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 48, "split_id": 204, "split_idx_start": 105879, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "74410f067b0891281afd81247268782ab270f2f1cfe3ef4b9cd132ca8868e80f", "range": [785, 868]}, {"doc_id": "a1c40fb17b5c7e99004e9d20a93f93e1896d8db27036379608c765a1df4d54f8", "range": [0, 86]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0665806382894516, -0.08036615699529648, -0.0385558195412159, 0.010127472691237926, -0.0071044075302779675, 0.004406696185469627, 0.026664547622203827, -0.03974524885416031, -0.02603219635784626, -0.013071446679532528, 0.029657946899533272, -0.017756083980202675, 0.029148606583476067, 0.025730058550834656, -0.02053108997642994, -0.08243798464536667, -0.02197348326444626, 0.022717120125889778, -0.009030555374920368, 0.04695690795779228, 0.03533036261796951, 0.0533994697034359, -0.0027088134083896875, 0.03677170351147652, -0.015296992845833302, -0.019873561337590218, 0.0024352113250643015, 0.02335241436958313, 0.02724589779973