5, -0.035395193845033646, 0.039442285895347595, 0.044581592082977295, 0.020132608711719513, 0.03558037802577019, -0.003441982204094529, -0.008479198440909386, 0.002879879903048277, -0.0354357473552227, -0.0022593033500015736, 0.049975570291280746, -0.044086866080760956, -0.02288379706442356, -0.034388378262519836, 0.009837321937084198, -0.0328327901661396, -0.007657242938876152, -0.018244197592139244, -0.04562658071517944, -0.014427976682782173, -0.0006115059368312359, 0.05154168978333473, -0.02207060158252716, 0.014856520108878613, -0.01246646884828806, -0.012087403796613216, 0.02497100457549095, -0.014234938658773899, 0.040145616978406906, 0.007756000384688377, 0.021625066176056862, 0.010532698594033718, 0.05331328138709068, 0.03907828405499458, 0.01477761659771204, -0.03414355218410492, 0.018253091722726822, -0.03817392513155937, 0.04919785261154175, -0.053855761885643005, 0.025772228837013245, -0.06278195977210999, -0.02133079618215561, 0.026501765474677086, -0.027258047834038734, -0.02657002955675125, -0.07666041702032089, -0.017050383612513542, -0.03431030362844467, 1.8906358412981669e-34, -0.01450301893055439, 0.004502485040575266, -0.006980757229030132, -0.05471530556678772, 0.02169531211256981, 0.0011301959166303277, 0.10240384936332703, -0.027017252519726753, 0.014090154320001602, -0.016399016603827477, -0.01608300767838955], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "0514eb0f7e58c3637ca3abcde3b768c9848b015e3a89947e615de2fb302d6672", "content": "This chunk is situated within the case study of Phoenix School, focusing on the use of various interventions to support autistic students. It specifically highlights the MAPS (Making Action Plans) approach and the use of Talking Mats to empower students in voicing their preferences and aspirations. The inclusion of 'The Ideal Self' intervention further illustrates the school's commitment to developing self-awareness among pupils.The image shows an anonymised MAP. An example of a Talking Mat work is shown in the photo.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n49 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nAn intervention called \u2018The Ideal Self\u2019 (which is based on the philosophy and theory of Personal Construct Psychology 1955, http://drawingtheidealself.co.uk) is also used with pupils where they begin by talking about what they would not want to be and then talk about their ideal self. This is not autism-specific but works very well with helping pupils to understand themselves and their aspirations. Heather Moran, a psychologist, has used this approach effectively with autistic students (Moran, 2006). ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 48, "split_id": 207, "split_idx_start": 106945, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "fc5cd2a55355c083b31af1ffb2e635ef000156c1640bc3217ccc62aef6046849", "range": [469, 504]}, {"doc_id": "f45bd75dab6e48703c1d87490e542f709fe17eadac86dac89be199e75907000d", "range": [0, 104]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.064345583319664, -0.07924402505159378, -0.019361793994903564, 0.00960839819163084, -0.015441459603607655, -0.015823137015104294, 0.02534230425953865, -0.08329355716705322, -0.017285650596022606, 0.011381312273442745, 0.0576106496155262, -0.013777846470475197, -0.018829667940735817, 0.01914489082992077, 0.0009567571105435491, -0.08048591762781143, 0.011554264463484287, 0.006795801687985659, -0.050179313868284225, 0.004507371224462986, -0.0199714545160532, 0.015758201479911804, -0.037800539284944534, 0.05976064130663872, -0.019883207976818085, -0.046668242663145065, 0.009293639101088047, 0.005020666401833296, 0.0261150561273098, -0.060160569846630096, 0.012437193654477596, 0.022600945085287094, 0.0028070297557860613, -0.008939232677221298, 2.4075814053503564e-06, 0.03664054721593857, 0.021895766258239746, -0.0417980514466