9ce5caab4a7d849fc", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study F: Phoenix School, which focuses on the school's outreach work and collaboration with parents. It highlights the school's commitment to providing workshops and resources for parents to better understand autism and to support their children, ensuring effective communication and involvement in the educational process.Most of these workshops take place during the day but once a term an evening session is provided for parents who work. Every parent that is referred has an information sheet provided to explain what is available to attend. The young people also have an information sheet that is shared with them. The school runs a parents\u2019 conference and a parents\u2019 forum and aims to provide a one-stop shop for parents.\nThe staff work hard to support students to understand their diagnosis where that approach is agreed with parents. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 50, "split_id": 215, "split_idx_start": 110441, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "bd54556e63a3cad6cb3b58ec53539145d8c1012361d7d8c25b88c6e7e24fa58c", "range": [404, 523]}, {"doc_id": "239be6c25d307aa9c2061d06350886873ce771dfe87660f385e296f0d65d6d17", "range": [0, 114]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [-0.003398603294044733, -0.09028133749961853, -0.03238246217370033, 0.03136533498764038, -0.003308496903628111, 0.04676491394639015, -0.01923871785402298, -0.0358608178794384, -0.045503199100494385, -0.003270055167376995, -0.007536951452493668, -0.03126385062932968, 0.03766248747706413, -0.016434479504823685, -0.0430474579334259, -0.04351602494716644, -0.020500440150499344, 0.014914583414793015, -0.06153898313641548, 0.030025003477931023, 0.009606406092643738, 0.048392485827207565, -0.013972759246826172, 0.01323886774480