 on enhancing assessment practices through technology and collaboration with parents and external services, such as CAMHS and the National Autistic Society, to improve support for autistic children.The school is involved in an Earwig pilot ( http://earwigacademic.com/) with Early Years. This is a Cloud-based assessment system which has not yet been shared with parents. The idea will be to upload and share photos and videos of the children in school and use these for assessment and reporting. Staff are currently working towards training TAs to add comments using an iPad.\nThe Outreach service is part of a Parent working party made up of representatives from CAMHS, Social Care, the National Autistic Society (NAS) and the Parent Advice Centre. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 50, "split_id": 218, "split_idx_start": 111782, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "c6c8ad737b891a9044da6f19e684aeddcfded2500aa784c4e2bea4953e413fe4", "range": [505, 595]}, {"doc_id": "97156b40ab68470719bcc0bad0973175961d793e4672e1b930f841423b7aab48", "range": [0, 173]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03941125422716141, -0.07836779206991196, -0.035608064383268356, -0.02311105467379093, -0.0314190648496151, 0.029767272993922234, 0.0643567442893982, -0.031073279678821564, -0.04829396679997444, -0.03697457164525986, 0.019474051892757416, -0.061512794345617294, 0.049514368176460266, 0.02136579342186451, -0.014007034711539745, -0.050469908863306046, -0.0208039078861475, 0.005066656041890383, -0.0747244656085968, 0.04671717435121536, 0.020722253248095512, 0.044006820768117905, -0.03958544507622719, 0.024727851152420044, -0.009785219095647335, -0.022944599390029907, -0.02023443765938282, 0.0052248453721404076, 0.017673995345830917, -0.049090806394815445, 0.011366487480700016, 0.0