's commitment to embedding the SCERTS framework, involving various stakeholders in a collaborative effort to enhance educational practices and support within a network of autism-focused schools.There is a SCERTS working group consisting of the Deputy Head, the SALT, an Outreach Team member, a number of teachers and three parents. The group focuses on how best to embed SCERTS. The school is part of a group called PLASN (Pan-London Autism Schools Network), a group of 20 schools where staff meet termly to support each other. Many types of provision are included and PLASN-R is an offshoot which focuses on doing research. Thirty people from a range of universities are involved so practice and research combine to inform each other.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 51, "split_id": 221, "split_idx_start": 113224, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "89cad023ceef2d4561fa37981bccec4d513dbad903384b63d8a50a79ac886a77", "range": [460, 598]}, {"doc_id": "e0239d417ffdc1c6bc0e26e6e62bcdb2188d26c0dee7fd98272ab25f36660bdc", "range": [0, 111]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.020607374608516693, -0.13581407070159912, -0.033255189657211304, -0.0004706015170086175, -0.006115980911999941, 0.014770540408790112, 0.017413577064871788, -0.06563244760036469, -0.05069303140044212, 0.012097050435841084, 0.03919035941362381, 0.0210969690233469, 0.025835631415247917, 0.056084223091602325, 0.009441078640520573, -0.06624679267406464, 0.009921271353960037, 0.036441292613744736, -0.06505649536848068, 0.012649692595005035, 0.027663614600896835, 0.025773674249649048, -0.005592182744294405, 0.020948901772499084, 0.023869970813393593, -0.029636884108185768, 0.004863237030804157, 0.02065187320113182, 0.04997479170560837, -0.013554049655795097, 0.04517744481563568, 0.012181250378489