sm.The potential of a sensory circuit was recognised by the staff when they saw it introduced by an OT into a Key Stage 3 class where there were problems at the start of the day.\nSpecialist staff use a coaching approach in the classroom to support staff. An Occupational Therapist provides support in the class to build capacity and to work with the staff on the sensory circuit. They provide training throughout the school and the whole school workforce will have had training on the sensory circuit by the end of 2019.\nEach class also has sensory boxes which contain equipment to support pupils with sensory regulation issues and the children can ask for these at any time. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 51, "split_id": 224, "split_idx_start": 114575, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "c5bea68658f576c0a3fe83c9c2a79ec2a1727d0787efa40a8ad38004924fdc4f", "range": [367, 543]}, {"doc_id": "87653c5262ed80289a18be80545d5f2b1f1deb9e38cbb4dd790100f496765032", "range": [0, 155]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.001750361523590982, -0.10321489721536636, -0.0395471453666687, 0.030752506107091904, 0.016742203384637833, 0.029746858403086662, 0.03470369055867195, -0.04186441749334335, 0.020822199061512947, 0.0037321217823773623, -0.0014073302736505866, -0.001082423492334783, -0.009156919084489346, 0.006421660538762808, 0.0001534491020720452, -0.06205984577536583, -0.015432136133313179, 0.044559892266988754, -0.07835658639669418, 0.026140326634049416, -0.006250778213143349, 0.030300376936793327, -0.031113551929593086, 0.03327934443950653, 0.025232486426830292, -0.02031094767153263, 0.04269469156861305, -0.02495417185127735, 0.041490428149700165, -0.04165692627429962, 0.04277195781469345, 0.0009851825889199972, 0.00015290752344299108, 0.00039810340967960656, 2.