 {"id": "c46c14832501eb72270ee667d9e33b5c5ca04071558658bdfeffb6dd426f168d", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study F, which describes the innovative curriculum adaptations at Phoenix School, including the use of themed learning environments like a jungle and a film studio to engage students. It also mentions the outreach team's efforts to support autistic girls, highlighting targeted initiatives for their needs.Another topic covered was the jungle. This type of work is continued throughout the school with a whole area upstairs being adapted to suit particular purposes. A recent focus saw this area transformed into a film studio.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n53 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nAutism and girls\nThe head of the school outreach team is leading some work on autism and girls. This involves 100 girls out of a 600 caseload across different settings. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 52, "split_id": 228, "split_idx_start": 116401, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "d8b35d8e21a7367a16b3b9e19505338444fb95aed9e8a1d133dd08006b262cbb", "range": [350, 388]}, {"doc_id": "f283463972e80bcc5575bc9e06dbf020949690475e99174abf807b6e4c377b75", "range": [0, 73]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06346915662288666, -0.05958297476172447, -0.02450677938759327, -0.01627556048333645, 0.02058488130569458, 0.034733593463897705, 0.014070126228034496, -0.057951752096414566, -0.09735793620347977, -0.021702731028199196, 0.02440682053565979, -0.03049820475280285, 0.022855795919895172, 0.04992426559329033, -0.018871523439884186, -0.05656855180859566, 0.010654107667505741, 0.0020314815919846296, -0.050159744918346405, 0.007436229847371578, -0.04164471849799156, 0.0389825701713562, 0.012866352684795856, 0.04127706587314606, 0.02925