etails how girls with autism can present. This was created by the Westminster Special Schools Training and Outreach team and is attached to this case study. \u2013 (see separate pdf document).\nThe school has invited some autistic women to talk and they plan to have a professionals\u2019 conference on this topic in the future. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 53, "split_id": 231, "split_idx_start": 117308, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "30123d7fc322ed4a0f94726ed48b18e5aa7fc18925f6644c247ee9d320509b52", "range": [291, 459]}, {"doc_id": "819cddfbdb94ba9efc1b30d5c3cadb5288911fb8ae5cad04b0ae7ed64c70efa7", "range": [0, 130]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.023008577525615692, -0.06764382123947144, -0.03077847696840763, 0.027955975383520126, 0.028797632083296776, 0.04729125648736954, -0.0039022539276629686, -0.0795782059431076, -0.039991941303014755, -4.883592737314757e-06, 0.023449599742889404, -0.06149191036820412, 0.029849441722035408, -0.001864610705524683, 0.011222961358726025, -0.06674205511808395, 0.03377233073115349, 0.031644586473703384, -0.01710977964103222, 0.017129290848970413, 0.0211544968187809, 0.04460596665740013, -0.0210080835968256, 0.03838250786066055, 0.03832901641726494, -0.05753232538700104, 0.0018864808371290565, 0.007754402235150337, 0.01683657243847847, -0.033296503126621246, 0.022162824869155884, -0.019888797774910927, 0.004232616163790226, -0.010772534646093845, 2.503865289327223e-06, 0.031761497259140015, 0.021808810532093048, -0.005216557532548904, -0.025131776928901672, 0.00041460624197497964, -0.08212579041719437, 0.020712662488222122, 0.00370498257689178, 0.07637520134449005, 0.009935515001416206, -0.049370456486940384, 0.008904898539185524, 0.06421732902526855, 0.024113411083817482, -0.02790413424372673, -0.00