3900228e-34, -0.005697272717952728, 0.009127623401582241, 0.013980909250676632, -0.04943041503429413, 0.02629913203418255, -0.011651185341179371, -0.029497694224119186, 0.0010170849272981286, 0.033093467354774475, 0.02245289459824562, -0.003022268647328019], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "e80dae41d43ece462dd5c02231b2ea0792226630bfb81cc7e56781d8de3510e7", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study F from Phoenix School, which focuses on autism outreach work, specifically a program designed to support autistic girls in developing social understanding and identity. The activities involve collaboration with a Speech and Language Therapist (SALT) and include engaging, motivating items to enhance participation and learning.There is a focus on social understanding. The girls work with the SALT on a different activity each week. The activities and outcomes are added into a shoe box each week. This box contains motivating items such as magazines, make-up, nail polish and cupcakes. Part of the aim of the programme is to support the girls in developing their identity and their social understanding. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 53, "split_id": 233, "split_idx_start": 118074, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "819cddfbdb94ba9efc1b30d5c3cadb5288911fb8ae5cad04b0ae7ed64c70efa7", "range": [357, 399]}, {"doc_id": "c0cb5b933d9b1bcdc3cac122bd2fce499fe79bd41ed13466c2a1a8ed37b7c818", "range": [0, 118]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.044131021946668625, -0.04470699280500412, -0.005392607767134905, 0.027083156630396843, 0.020078694447875023, 0.04313137009739876, 0.025725653395056725, -0.08066850155591965, -0.055615365505218506, -0.0008862336981110275, 0.01936468482017517, -0.04394693672657013, 0.007129801902920008, 0.04304557666182518, -0.02795523218810