7803871632, 0.007798316888511181, 0.022117752581834793, -0.012809596955776215, -0.024120420217514038], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "cca873c14a17d5f2571bcca3a8552564035fe7eae705cb1e077a03df89a32c5a", "content": "This chunk is situated within Case Study F: Springfields School, which discusses targeted support and measuring progress for autistic children. It specifically relates to the school's use of the Continuum of Skill Development (CSD) as a tool for assessing student progress in Key Stage 4 (KS4), focusing on personal growth and independence in learning tasks.The CSD is an independent tool and can be used to evaluate progress against learning intentions which are drawn from sources other than Section 1 of MAPP. The CSD resources look at the four domains of prompting, fluency, maintenance and generalisation and is used to measure personal progress. This is being used\nin a pilot project in one class in KS4 to try to ascertain the level of independence within tasks. The CSD resources can be downloaded from the website at http://www.thedalesschool.org/article/assessment-progression-mapp/275 .\nThe focus is on making progress more explicit and developing a shared understanding and a scale to define what different areas might mean. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 54, "split_id": 240, "split_idx_start": 120831, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f2cfacf597bdd7f35c1a4c2f398e45b2456245164697c93e2616bb0511f9d059", "range": [486, 641]}, {"doc_id": "9fdb2f80944ef0d3f780eb8a6e482e754f4e695cae15a37189b27c28b22331bd", "range": [0, 139]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [-0.0006993370479904115, -0.030663518235087395, -0.024122120812535286, -0.03481844440102577, -0.04682490974664688, 0.030580978840589523, 0.03168778121471405, -0.06847355514764786, -0