hich focuses on Springfields School, a specialist provision for pupils with autism and other learning difficulties. It highlights how students engage in GCSE sessions with the support of teaching assistants (TAs) and describes the systematic instruction method employed to facilitate effective learning.They attend their GCSE sessions with a TA.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n55 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nSome of the assessment involves systematic instruction. This involves breaking tasks down into tiny steps and was developed by Marc Gold in the 1960s ( http://www.marcgold.com/\nmarc-gold ; http://www.mn.gov/mnddc/extra/marc-gold2.html). There is a 5-day training programme on how to do this. Teaching is in context and the task is modelled, staff use reduced language and only single prompts.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 54, "split_id": 243, "split_idx_start": 122235, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "2b15fcacf15b964e76b964ae78ac7a05e86d871f217071066615328e9722b686", "range": [418, 461]}, {"doc_id": "40188b07c334372fb16a4ea688ff6cc896ac2c19b7dc81bb4743567e7b35bbf0", "range": [0, 101]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0352865494787693, -0.10517434030771255, -0.024234075099229813, 0.016687940806150436, -0.02969757840037346, 0.01610487885773182, 0.015527759678661823, -0.06998436897993088, -0.08801613003015518, -0.009862528182566166, 0.04514562338590622, -0.031982723623514175, 0.026211855933070183, -0.019911568611860275, -0.011382189579308033, -0.1408924162387848, 0.001363042276352644, 0.020261099562048912, -0.07392756640911102, 0.019660230726003647, 0.023067569360136986, 0.005304496735334396, -0.027538875117897987, 0.010741365142166615, -0.012119908817112446, -0.05048385262489319, -0.04812699556350708, -0.00277