gage with parents about progress and the increasing use of visual documentation, such as photos and videos, to track students' learning and independence, enhancing their educational experience.Staff describe to parents what these mean.\nThere has been an increase in the use of photo and video evidence to show pupils\u2019 learning. This often takes the format of a picture with a comment underneath using their marking code which focuses on the level of communication and level of independence achieved by the young person. The marking code is shown here.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n56 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nP8 \u2013 Adapting the curriculum, teaching and learning to promote wellbeing and success for autistic children and young people\nActivity sheets are adapted to suit the needs of the children using symbols and words. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 55, "split_id": 247, "split_idx_start": 123702, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f3d2df1a2486ebe1518e6dbfed45c262323301da22939c05eaf6f703a0081470", "range": [269, 312]}, {"doc_id": "f456e854979a61611b2e2bd9fcae88bfde86ebab9281c780f93c9210b50c2f84", "range": [0, 295]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.015042874030768871, -0.08289125561714172, -0.02645605243742466, -0.006090087350457907, -0.013265471905469894, 0.049360714852809906, 0.004456236958503723, -0.028155049309134483, -0.046409085392951965, -0.014480898156762123, 0.033043500036001205, -0.03183193504810333, 0.013489819131791592, -0.0006466462509706616, -0.014019175432622433, -0.07349483668804169, -0.006193819921463728, -0.007434474769979715, -0.033627454191446304, 0.02180507592856884, 0.007853114046156406, 0.021243611350655556, -0.010991819202899933, 0.03571103513240814, -0.01907375641167164, -0.0493204