1774986982346, 0.019941022619605064, -0.01574883982539177, 0.08711697161197662, -0.022852132096886635, 0.008170691318809986, -0.012788104824721813, -0.046851664781570435, 0.025510570034384727, -0.02485392987728119, 0.04561875760555267, 0.016397636383771896, -0.02571304887533188, -0.0009508043876849115, 0.017797347158193588, 0.026489226147532463, 0.009126937948167324, -0.04038102552294731, 0.015961769968271255, -0.035455480217933655, 0.010549486614763737, -0.004358782432973385, 0.06279433518648148, -0.05202958732843399, -0.031543683260679245, 0.04117782413959503, -0.0062295482493937016, 0.005501851439476013, -0.06073546037077904, -0.06680309027433395, -0.046446725726127625, 2.5813683752502137e-34, -0.004024438560009003, -0.02205362357199192, 0.0170479416847229, -0.10949627310037613, -0.0014490613248199224, 0.0024835215881466866, 0.019085248932242393, 0.0031369340140372515, 0.008361373096704483, -0.006168798543512821, -0.011712098494172096], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "379e7724dbf88ca2a28518f96ebf1e41e83a0ceb88045dbc1e71ba4a4063c08e", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Further resources\" and \"Transferable practice\" sections within the report focusing on effective strategies for supporting autistic students. It emphasizes practical actions that educators can implement, including sharing pupil profiles, using sensory strategies, and utilizing resources to enhance understanding of sensory differences and self-regulation for better engagement in learning.These are free to download from the AET website www.autismeducationtrust.org.uk.\n\u2022 Share pupil passports/profiles with staff and others who have direct contact with the children and students, including drivers and escorts\n\u2022 Use the girls checklist (kindly provided by the City of Westminster Outreach Team) to identify girls on the autistic spectrum and begin to support with appropriate strategies\n\u2022 Consider using sensory strategies at the beginning of the school day to see what impact these have on students\u2019 regulation and their ability to engage in learning. Use a sensory checklist and shared sensory strategies\n\u2022 Use Sensory and Motor Strategies by Corinna Laurie (2018) to help understand sensory differences and plan appropriate and individualised activities for students \u2013 alerting, organising and calming. The link is https://www.autism.org.uk/products/core-nas-\npublications/sensory-strategies.aspx .\nReferences\nBondy, A and Frost, L (2002) The Picture Exchange Communication System Training Manual , Second Edition, Pyramid Consulting\nKershaw, P (2011) The ASD workbook: understanding your autism spectrum disorder , London: Jessica Kingsley\nKuypers, L (2011) The zones of regulation: a curriculum designed to foster self regulation and emotional control, Think Social Publishing\nMoran, H (2006) Drawing the Ideal Self \u2013 A very personal assessment: using a Personal Construct Psychology assessment technique with young people with ASD to explore the child\u2019s view of self. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 57, "split_id": 252, "split_idx_start": 125932, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "c491b365f14f5b1b3e2bcc03b2db83ebf5f94196ea5ca02504fe1c66b8ad13af", "range": [692, 773]}, {"doc_id": "39eb549e0a165834cc2abceecb7a9f616c34054512283ded5599a0b96224ce97", "range": [0, 572]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.008875440806150436, -0.1224544420838356, -0.0259257722645998, 0.007904049940407276, 0.021429669111967087, 0.026749759912490845, 0.043691717088222504, -0.06377369165420532, 0.00404216255992651, -0.006855370476841927, -0.0036516976542770863, -0.05578886345028877, -0.020342310890555382, 0.014686300419270992, -0.015847548842430115, -0.07375866174697876, 0.010243128053843975, 0.00920200813561678, -0.0453626550734