06cafafdd9f81e95652fde08ce360d0bec2213", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Further resources\" section of the Good Autism Practice Report, which provides information about autism training resources available through the Autism Education Trust (AET). It specifically mentions the training hubs across England that offer tailored training for different age groups, supporting educational staff in their professional development.The AET also has a number of autism training hubs in different parts of England which offer training on autism at different levels and for the different age phases ( i.e. Early Years, 5 to 16 and 16 to 25 years) \u2013 see the AET website ( http://www.autismeducationtrust.org.uk /) for details of the training hub closest to you\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n59 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nCase Study G: Springfields School\nSchool information Sponsor led academy for 122 pupils aged 5 to19.\nSpecial school provision for SpLD (Specific Learning Difficulty), SLCN (Speech, language and Communication), Autism Spectrum, SEMH (Social, Emotional and Mental Health) and MLD (Moderate Learning Difficulty).\nSchool website www.springfields.wilts.sch.uk\nFocus Vocational Pathways at KS4 to Post 16 and beyond\nMain themes Pupil voice, vocational pathways at KS4\nPrinciples illustrated\n1. Understanding the strengths, interests and challenges of the autistic child and young person\n2. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 58, "split_id": 255, "split_idx_start": 129843, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "45909456380550693152b9c01c601d3c535e8006977fc97fb2311b302b631f5c", "range": [1748, 1919]}, {"doc_id": "473a3a4fb54f03620f1bab0e855c91314843b42535d3608366cc9034b9d2ca8f", "range": [0, 96]}]}, "score": null, "emb