hlights the school's approach to personalized learning pathways in Key Stage 4 (KS4) that help students develop academic and life skills in a supportive environment.Context\nThe school is an independent specialist provision for pupils aged 5\u201316. In KS4, staff provide personalised pathways designed to enable pupils to reach their full potential in a safe and nurturing setting. Students gain qualifications and life skills in a calm, supportive and therapeutic environment enabling them to excel both academically and socially.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n60 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nUnderstanding the individual with autism\nP1 \u2013 Understanding the strengths, interests and challenges of the autistic child and young person\nFortnightly learning walks are undertaken by staff to monitor provision. There is a focused work scrutiny termly to monitor evidence of personalised strategies to enable students to achieve their outcomes independently and to support students to be engaged with their learning. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 59, "split_id": 257, "split_idx_start": 131247, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "473a3a4fb54f03620f1bab0e855c91314843b42535d3608366cc9034b9d2ca8f", "range": [507, 587]}, {"doc_id": "5f42d0e6189a5230e2563723eeb530750a3057f7651cd986a03d1b9651927ed6", "range": [0, 205]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.060742173343896866, -0.10209543257951736, -0.020822720602154732, 0.006778419949114323, -0.02907799929380417, 0.018825720995664597, 0.036978404968976974, -0.057425159960985184, -0.047988906502723694, 0.0074375709518790245, 0.060878120362758636, -0.012842237949371338, -0.006468983832746744, 0.0007851358386687934, -0.009116779081523418, -0.08824247866868973, 0.02954774908721447, 0.0160