8, -0.0035412805154919624, 0.01720232143998146, 0.02327616512775421, -0.04593044891953468, -0.045246951282024384], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "01446fee851b929bedc429c8b26c71652e44e99ff61a79a1967129d5cfa9953c", "content": "This chunk is part of the case study on Springfields School, detailing their initiatives to support autistic students in developing independence and advocating for their voices. It describes the use of learning support resources and a three-pronged approach to capture student perspectives on their experiences and preferences.There are also learning support resources on desks including a checklist to develop independence and personal schedules also include who is supporting a child as well as a task list so that items can be moved from left to right when completed.\nP2 \u2013 Enabling the voice of the autistic child and young person to contribute to and influence decisions\nThe school is currently piloting a research based three-pronged approach to capturing the autistic voice. This includes:\n\u2022 Wall-wisher \u2013 a visual bulletin board where pupils post a message on one of three boards. Board topics could be around questions such as: What do you enjoy? What makes you take part in lessons/activities? ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 60, "split_id": 260, "split_idx_start": 132938, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "e10716d3e97317619fa10f0235d4dbc3e25b87b7a88e26707a4b98bbff086a74", "range": [392, 636]}, {"doc_id": "2133dbbf9c458509ab59efeab2bb4f0c0f62406a85f04b838dfbc3b7ab1a1138", "range": [0, 48]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03820747882127762, -0.0750860720872879, -0.018648935481905937, -0.009790218435227871, -0.03247548267245293, 0.03340404853224754, 0.042232587933540344, -0.06862036138772964, -0.0192605890