97165, 0.04909484460949898, 0.01983531005680561, -0.04724102094769478, 0.023232316598296165, -0.01318085566163063, 0.07516339421272278, -0.01200020406395197, -0.014970874413847923, -0.07075471431016922, 0.022446196526288986, 0.03791647031903267, 0.029822727665305138, -0.005828748922795057, 0.039291076362133026, -0.0004235196684021503, 0.021123602986335754, -0.03862038999795914, 0.057299431413412094, -0.02987511269748211, -0.043326761573553085, 0.03498099744319916, 0.00794779509305954, 0.0012480189325287938, -0.03578302264213562, -0.008738069795072079, -0.00927871186286211, 1.9432287672097763e-34, 0.001070266356691718, 0.011319195851683617, 0.005968754645437002, -0.11138542741537094, 0.0004985997802577913, 0.009948929771780968, -0.03534470126032829, -0.0311803687363863, 0.0263635516166687, -0.002434699097648263, -0.03931745886802673], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "0e73ac130f66ca9c8227d3b17de56cb8db003aecf63611fa6221fac49ec262ca", "content": "This chunk is part of the case study for Springfields School, which focuses on the implementation of personalized transition plans for Key Stage 4 (KS4) students. It outlines how the school prepares students for adulthood by providing tailored strategies and student passports that emphasize their development in various life skills and academic areas. The curriculum is designed to be engaging and collaborative, promoting overall wellbeing and success for autistic students.Students in KS4 have an active transition plan which includes personalised strategy suggestions for teaching and learning.\nStudent passports are based around the Department for Education (DfE), Preparation for Adulthood (DfE, 21 February 2017) and include the headings Employment, Independent Living, Community Inclusion, Health, and Academic. The school works towards the achievement of academic outcomes and also outcomes on the preparation for adulthood in line with their developmental ability. Students are placed in an appropriate Post-16 Provision that aims to engage and inspire them and support them to fulfil their aspirations.\nP8 \u2013 Adapting the curriculum, teaching and learning to promote wellbeing and success for autistic children and young people\nThe specialist Key Stage 4 curriculum is based on five key principles:\n\u2022 Personalisation and choice\n\u2022 Challenge and enjoyment\n\u2022 Breadth and depth\n\u2022 Progression and outcomes\n\u2022 Collaboration.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 61, "split_id": 264, "split_idx_start": 135052, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b83ae430dcff5c99d8b4dde881e32d79eddf6e25991de6a7ddb27cea21bd3d07", "range": [596, 719]}, {"doc_id": "c86fd30d72fd2b926c4eaaec00b5b041c4bc4fff3157921d647f0531356b5aec", "range": [0, 314]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.027978738769888878, -0.08154522627592087, -0.008621475659310818, -0.03363027796149254, -0.008256674744188786, 0.014359362423419952, 0.023803377524018288, -0.07034941762685776, -0.032125070691108704, 0.024521078914403915, 0.04933862015604973, -0.0260652843862772, -0.02699689194560051, 0.02133850008249283, -0.032291170209646225, -0.07411682605743408, 0.018352972343564034, -0.010769163258373737, -0.061634477227926254, 0.00289167370647192, -0.056001100689172745, 0.032047972083091736, -0.02649766393005848, 0.025462409481406212, 0.012886452488601208, -0.025437742471694946, 0.0150361442938447, 0.015823839232325554, 0.054190974682569504, -0.03630087897181511, 0.02470911480486393, 0.036387521773576736, -0.024640753865242004, -0.019195228815078735, 2.545146116972319e-06, 0.02596447989344597, 0.015386690385639668, -0.033602673560380936, -0.037729762494564056, -0.019410058856010437, -0.0538279265165329, 0.02524397149682045, 0.022059086710214615, 0.0510442815721035, -0.013532205484807491, 0.001909528858959