6, 0.02086934819817543, 0.005944627337157726, -0.0519951693713665, -0.007427089847624302, 1.9257726761000653e-34, 0.014754526317119598, 0.03879816085100174, -0.0022213186603039503, -0.07287570834159851, -0.001384042203426361, -0.017470182850956917, 0.0007779659936204553, -0.022872308269143105, -0.006063369568437338, 0.007291298359632492, -0.031141161918640137], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "87a77ebcef8130a93a342e933dc77e42259cf780b0e6bd420054fa6337846832", "content": "This chunk is part of the case study for Springfields School, which focuses on vocational pathways for students in Key Stage 4 and Post-16 education. It highlights specific pathways available to students, such as Outdoor Learning and Hair and Beauty, detailing the qualifications they pursue and the practical experiences they gain to prepare for future employment.The Outdoor Learning pathway sits alongside their core subjects of English, Maths and Science. Students study for a range of qualifications such as the Duke of Edinburgh Silver Award, a First Aid qualification, BTEC Outdoor Learning 1 and a Paddleboard Qualification.\nOn the Hair and Beauty pathway, students study for a City & Guilds in Hair & Beauty, various diplomas and certificates in Hairdressing and Make-up and Gateway qualifications, alongside their core subjects. The school has a fully functioning hair and beauty salon on site. The hair salon gives young people a real taste of what the work involves and supports them to build independence in that environment. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 62, "split_id": 268, "split_idx_start": 137559, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "e5c542c431395069591b39fc138f8e2b9d8cceaffa9a4eda3997adbf6ade1511", "range": [497, 592]}, {"doc_id": "128aa7517a1749249978abd946ee2ef74d481