5094792843, -0.016956422477960587, 0.030202195048332214, 0.0456545427441597, -0.05674238130450249], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "4c00ce3144c79ac74a6ac321e9fee2b358e82b3c18bff973ce27768f3a6f08c0", "content": "The chunk is situated within Case Study G, which discusses the vocational pathways implemented at Springfields School for students with autism. It highlights the school's approach to employing teachers who can enhance these pathways, ensuring students gain essential life skills for adulthood and increased motivation through personalized learning experiences.Some teachers come into school to fill in the gaps in skills. When employing new teachers, the school carefully considers how they might fit into their vocational pathways approach and where the gaps in skills exist.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n63 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nStudents learn life skills when they are following the pathways. They are prepared for adulthood and learn how to be employable, healthy and independent. School staff say students are happiest to learn when they are following a pathway \u2013 they are very motivated. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 62, "split_id": 271, "split_idx_start": 138943, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "bb1869543b5596fcaf0bd30d5235fd5dbb4c7cda688b5cacbfe6fd1154a4ed91", "range": [398, 460]}, {"doc_id": "c62a724ee0ebcbdf66a9514fc3a46b67c6629fd8e91238638e0ba87ce3e1db0f", "range": [0, 109]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.053391728550195694, -0.06093590706586838, -0.01684730499982834, -0.0035961626563221216, -0.0069256741553545, 0.0336071141064167, 0.015912260860204697, -0.059332650154829025, -0.07111179083585739, 0.0042844731360673904, 0.06483208388090134, 0.015958867967128754, 0.023426750674843788, 