2016f76765ca362f0d65836cfc5b8c25c72e2cc54d58ee64", "content": "This chunk is situated within Case Study G about Springfields School, which focuses on vocational pathways for autistic students in Key Stage 4 to Post-16. It highlights the Engineering and Transport Pathway, detailing methods used to engage autistic learners, like visual aids and technology, through the example of Ben, a student passionate about vehicles.Parents are very pleased with the pathways approach as they are keen for their child to be engaged in learning and then to go on to meaningful employment.\nEngineering and Transport Pathway Example\nAs autistic young people are likely to be visual learners, the following methods are employed to support their engagement in the motor vehicles\u2019 course:\n\u2022 Use of graphics to help students to express their views\n\u2022 Use of smart phones to take photographs and make videos\n\u2022 Viewing platforms such as YouTube to demonstrate skills and processes, capture and share information with each other\n\u2022 Making a visual tour of the motor vehicles workshop using a graphic design program.\nCase Study of a student on the Engineering and Transport Pathway\nBen is a 17-year-old student with autism. He has had an interest in vehicles of all types since he was 5 years old. Ben wanted a career as a racing driver and liked to spend time at car rallies and shows with his father. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 63, "split_id": 274, "split_idx_start": 140279, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "ac18d604602c1d0f470a57777cfc2fb4b7a6d1f3f2b44155ad30754acc77bbb2", "range": [405, 560]}, {"doc_id": "2a3375b4c94a8d639be918a467ae39afbcb6f082bd67b2bbaa09e76f3ae95395", "range": [0, 105]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.005035060923546553, -0.0