 visual work schedules and timetables so that he could see the order of the work to be done and when each stage would be completed with specific days and dates. This reduced Ben\u2019s anxiety considerably and he was able to use these strategies to work on other work.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n64 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nBen was able to spend time working in a garage environment on an area of interest for him.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 63, "split_id": 276, "split_idx_start": 141467, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "2a3375b4c94a8d639be918a467ae39afbcb6f082bd67b2bbaa09e76f3ae95395", "range": [336, 434]}, {"doc_id": "35e28a15c4122dde183b8829ad04d706ecc63f50caf969c8b7d7a7b478805637", "range": [0, 175]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [-0.017745114862918854, -0.044469695538282394, -0.03952326625585556, 0.013850183226168156, -0.012619979679584503, 0.014050428755581379, 0.056248221546411514, -0.021219544112682343, -0.03926568105816841, 0.02488846145570278, 0.06374702602624893, -0.0069685340858995914, -0.004906929098069668, 0.0066556804813444614, -0.014183319173753262, -0.0621173195540905, -0.019664166495203972, 0.024320779368281364, -0.05162736028432846, 0.02080709859728813, -0.007352776359766722, 0.002261081011965871, -0.027073167264461517, 0.04491942375898361, -0.015822554007172585, -0.07000277936458588, 0.011496750637888908, 0.02308044023811817, 0.04001437872648239, -0.02889256365597248, -0.007318452931940556, 0.009248201735317707, 0.01669776253402233, 0.013136681169271469, 2.340607807127526e-06, 0.0725891962647438, 0.005024613346904516, -0.0179792121052742, 0.0026647120248526335, -0.035818345844745636, -0.03223520144820213, -0.02807626686990261, 0.02430887334048748, 0.04741332307457924, -0.023805122