rust (AET) and its training initiatives aimed at educators across England. It emphasizes the availability of structured training hubs that cater to various educational phases, thereby supporting teachers in implementing effective autism practices, as illustrated in the case study of St. John the Baptist Church of England Primary School.The AET also has a number of autism training hubs in different parts of England which offer training on autism at different levels and for the different age phases ( i.e. Early Years, 5 to 16 and 16 to 25 years) \u2013 see the AET website ( http://www.autismeducationtrust.org.uk/ ) for details of the training hub closest to you\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n66 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nCase Study H: St. John the Baptist Church of England Primary School\nSchool information Primary school in the North East of England\nSchool\u2019s website st-johnthebaptist.org.uk\nNumber on roll 249\nAge range 3 to 11 years\nFocus of the case study\nEarly Years: Inclusion of a nursery child with autism. Impact of the AET training on practice\nPrinciples illustrated\n1. Understanding the strengths, interests and challenges of the autistic child and young person\n3. Collaboration with parents and carers of autistic children and young people\n4. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 65, "split_id": 279, "split_idx_start": 145009, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "15e4bb4ad9547c6151dde8eb75ef87a9b4a1e577407a2289ae7f4a2c405edacd", "range": [1537, 1708]}, {"doc_id": "959ee95f1b9f109b005de179e9d18a78a1266dfd0a83d54b903723b02a08ea42", "range": [0, 79]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.02824503928422928, -0.09437474608421326, -0.022399526089429855, 0.02424320951104164, 0.004339415580034256, 0.028057100251317