n the inclusion of a nursery child named John, who is on the autism spectrum. It highlights the nursery teacher\u2019s proactive approach to prepare for John's integration into the school by attending AET training on autism and implementing supportive strategies, ultimately facilitating his gradual transition into the nursery environment.The nursery teacher attended the AET training on autism to prepare for working with John. She implemented a number of actions as a consequence of the training and John started to attend the nursery on a graduated basis. The AET training team supported the teacher through this process.\fGood Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n67 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nUnderstanding the individual with autism\nP1 \u2013 Understanding the strengths, interests and challenges of the autistic child and young person\nThe teacher noted that there were parts of the nursery environment John did not use ( e.g. the non-carpeted area of the classroom). ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 66, "split_id": 282, "split_idx_start": 146683, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "a23fad107ebc0c683c02afd2ccb091e8f6ce954f70968d1815de775de5b934b9", "range": [314, 404]}, {"doc_id": "466d95adad4cd4cdd8d860fb7dc64ab5416889b01c58c0fbad9383aebd8690de", "range": [0, 41]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03469309210777283, -0.07008537650108337, -0.031390756368637085, 0.01448787096887827, -0.021487941965460777, 0.029584234580397606, 0.0069998763501644135, -0.05939139425754547, -0.08651980757713318, 0.004208141937851906, 0.07180614024400711, -0.03710567206144333, 0.03255421295762062, -0.00741295563057065, -0.014684369787573814, -0.06050378456711769, 0.01223406195640564, 0.05169020965695381, -0.052744463086128235, 0.03428870067000389, -0.0