, "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study H, which focuses on the inclusion of a nursery child named John, who is on the autism spectrum. It describes the nursery teacher's efforts to prepare John for school through gradual transition techniques, including home visits and engaging activities to build rapport and comfort.Before John started school, the nursery teacher made a home visit at 10 am every Monday morning with resources. At first, John did not want to engage with her. However, eventually he did allow her to play with him and she read him a story. This built up to sessions lasting about 30 minutes.\nJohn was transitioned into the nursery very gradually in stages.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 67, "split_id": 285, "split_idx_start": 148296, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "d846081a6caa2340849b6b28800cac506e4f40ed854cc849747da171bb2d65f3", "range": [619, 731]}, {"doc_id": "291bf0f52d2a0500a1c4746e727f5ae522480c0c0dee27bc46749f11e48e8240", "range": [0, 65]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.020221734419465065, -0.03160782530903816, -0.02823752351105213, 0.00403651874512434, -0.029160186648368835, 0.014095565304160118, 0.005186860915273428, -0.0848599225282669, -0.09399104863405228, 0.010040286928415298, 0.05137286335229874, -0.030069826170802116, 0.057248033583164215, -0.01488671638071537, -0.04361109808087349, -0.08745253086090088, 0.008120201528072357, 0.04002077132463455, -0.061609264463186264, 0.03742920979857445, -0.03327357396483421, 0.03236323967576027, 0.009849795140326023, 0.0044621569104492664, 0.020923759788274765, -0.029978886246681213, -0.022600609809160233, 0.020787423476576805, 0.036597516387701035, -0.018416063860058784, 0.03111075423657894, 0.02172844484448433, 0.041734155267477036, -0.004277918487787247, 2.48