1626, 0.023404277861118317, -0.03464610129594803, 0.032620832324028015, -0.0011778679909184575, -0.002554382663220167, -0.007611778564751148, 0.018696114420890808, 0.02726130560040474, -0.02993580885231495], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "b1e69bfa45074274c64d14c31ed32c63a0dc9d638a876bd559d1421a3a91d37a", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study H, which focuses on the inclusion of a nursery child with autism at St. John the Baptist Church of England Primary School. It discusses the impact of AET training on the nursery teacher's practices, collaboration with parents, and how the teacher's increased confidence and knowledge benefited the entire school.She said it inspired her to find out that small changes she could make straight away could make a big difference to a child.\nThe SENCo created time for the nursery teacher to attend training and encouraged her as a leader. The nursery teacher led on meetings with John\u2019s parents which made her feel really valued. The school SENCo and other teachers now come to her for advice about autistic children elsewhere in the school.\nThe nursery teacher has also presented to a whole school staff meeting to spread the practice through the school. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 68, "split_id": 292, "split_idx_start": 151524, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "9f0316e4ca6beaac6ac5a769cc3e6a5073fb49e89f37fbf55eb6eadcf66edaf2", "range": [492, 617]}, {"doc_id": "70240e8fbb1a583ab77d855ea79732e34a785bf4b3bfd986d4b2950ffc84ce53", "range": [0, 114]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.01499409880489111, -0.055656056851148605, -0.034626297652721405, 0.040483519434928894, 0.005848229862749577, 0.03393752500414848, -0.020786788314580917, -0.0686190277338028, -0.07813470810651779, 0.026538662612438202, 0.0