a21e41e6900", "content": "This chunk is part of Case Study H, which focuses on the inclusion of a nursery child with autism named John at St. John the Baptist Church of England Primary School. It discusses the teacher's adjustments to the classroom environment and social groupings, highlighting the impact of AET training on fostering social skills and interactions among students.The teacher then added paper and pens to the area.\nAnother example of the impact of the AET training was around social inclusion and working with other children. Initially, the teacher arranged for John to play a game with a group of his own friends. She then followed this up by including another child who was not part of his friendship group. Over time, she gradually rotated the groupings so that different children replaced friends within the group to build John\u2019s social skills and to familiarise other children with John. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 68, "split_id": 295, "split_idx_start": 152850, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "7abdcebd0638144a5e45f08f120daa4d7f0663cdfe2951399813ece96f6563c9", "range": [325, 376]}, {"doc_id": "b99b0b5cf6fd505c909b569bf9c3344754d15146df19ef27a5d75dd5d0042cbb", "range": [0, 183]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.02231934852898121, -0.09104986488819122, -0.030255895107984543, 0.05034396052360535, 0.015059387311339378, 0.02648857608437538, 0.0039153797551989555, -0.05123556777834892, -0.054240643978118896, 0.010225415229797363, 0.046109024435281754, -0.04243854805827141, 0.04210343584418297, -0.030395105481147766, 0.012797679752111435, -0.07383392006158829, 0.02534523792564869, 0.04956084489822388, -0.054142065346241, 0.016397615894675255, -0.012456986121833324, 0.023435251787304878, 0.02568260207772255, 0.0096071921288967