ning and development\nP8 \u2013 Adapting the curriculum, teaching and learning to promote wellbeing and success for autistic children and young people\nThe teacher believes her priorities are on skills such as turn-taking and developing interactions with peers. One of the key skills she has focused on is for John to wait and take turns. She uses his name to cue him in. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 69, "split_id": 297, "split_idx_start": 153697, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b99b0b5cf6fd505c909b569bf9c3344754d15146df19ef27a5d75dd5d0042cbb", "range": [501, 687]}, {"doc_id": "40e50a3ba0c6c21151ab14a84900aa03ebd9fb4f29af8b2a893622585a5fe3e2", "range": [0, 33]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.06615153700113297, -0.0733419880270958, -0.02794683538377285, 0.05155804380774498, -0.01694529876112938, 0.03235885500907898, 0.026942744851112366, -0.052131980657577515, -0.054270073771476746, 0.02471054345369339, 0.03487355634570122, -0.042444631457328796, 0.031775590032339096, -0.033054474741220474, -0.023866871371865273, -0.10484035313129425, 0.02757914364337921, 0.013286232948303223, 0.0006540671456605196, -0.0028175683692097664, -0.007816393859684467, 0.014154629781842232, -0.010584509000182152, 0.03882472962141037, 0.013816889375448227, -0.004650746006518602, -0.01711437664926052, 0.004548337776213884, -0.0048270621336996555, -0.011504562571644783, 0.02849658578634262, 0.02790159545838833, 0.01767652854323387, 0.026658279821276665, 2.351214789086953e-06, 0.026016829535365105, 0.025390340015292168, -0.041545312851667404, -0.012399738654494286, -0.01385700423270464, -0.038342248648405075, 0.028235146775841713, 0.025154350325465202, 0.027462581172585487, -0.026171045377850533, 0.0004978177603334188, 0.007735774386674166, 0.04486438259482384, 0.