bd9fb4f29af8b2a893622585a5fe3e2", "content": "This chunk discusses the progress of John, a 4-year-old child with autism, in a nursery setting. It highlights how the nursery teacher uses specific strategies, such as verbal cues and repetition of phrases, to enhance John's communication skills and social interactions, including his participation in class activities like distributing milk.She uses his name to cue him in. He will now wait and point and attempt to say the place he wants to go.\nShe repeats useful phrases to help develop his verbal and communication skills and, as a result, these are beginning to develop. Recently, he gave the milk out to everyone in the circle. Every child said, \u2018 Thank you John\u2019 and he smiled in acknowledgement. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 69, "split_id": 298, "split_idx_start": 154311, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "44aae7aae32b596c0256aa750522675ada4367ecbb9480a711dd779314fd8e8f", "range": [614, 647]}, {"doc_id": "6dcc6c6593235b248230fda0c19542c67ea8a4f8f8a5980e41dca8be4e528d6d", "range": [0, 70]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.054472506046295166, -0.02545764669775963, -0.04134362190961838, 0.029507780447602272, 0.008043023757636547, 0.026531318202614784, 0.011711107566952705, -0.025932200253009796, -0.06390101462602615, 0.01278007309883833, 0.044380903244018555, -0.05557167902588844, 0.070098876953125, -0.005012644454836845, -0.014366568997502327, -0.08513262122869492, 0.018832825124263763, 0.002601826097816229, -0.00208200141787529, 0.01302528940141201, 0.00010134106560144573, 0.019914256408810616, 0.006373353768140078, 0.01963159255683422, -0.01979842595756054, -0.0032796000596135855, 0.00010644977010088041, -0.01756814494729042, 0.011882618069648743, -0.05745267868041992, -0.0009366145