029349923134, -0.07813428342342377, -0.014980627223849297, -0.06113170087337494, 0.06564067304134369, -0.01808815635740757, 0.03200370445847511, -0.024284644052386284, -0.014848790131509304, 0.04019070044159889, -0.054098762571811676, 0.07014806568622589, 0.03759864345192909, -0.012394492514431477, -0.004902933724224567, 0.016284769400954247, 0.052924737334251404, 0.02532476745545864, 0.012441382743418217, -0.004282035399228334, -0.04167946055531502, -0.011862160637974739, -0.008741124533116817, 0.055284611880779266, -0.010349837131798267, -0.03256922587752342, -0.008820380084216595, 0.023347556591033936, -0.03167368099093437, -0.06804408878087997, -0.018803417682647705, -0.010086661204695702, 1.9393280545104656e-34, 0.00694841705262661, -0.0038443882949650288, 0.01201377622783184, -0.022538546472787857, 0.053523898124694824, -0.02362574078142643, -0.004224497824907303, -0.011579405516386032, 0.03190342336893082, 0.003138381289318204, -0.008203539066016674], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "edf8bb3ccc9e4abefae979386dc34ef63993911fe7e2973085c5c8417a7f8101", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Good Autism Practice Guide,\" specifically under the sections detailing transferable practices for educators working with autistic children. It outlines actionable strategies that can be implemented in various educational settings to enhance learning, social interaction, and overall engagement for autistic students.Good Autism Practice Guide \u2013 Case Studies\n70 Doc ref: GAP report - case studies_I-S\nTransferable practice \u2013 actions you could try in your setting\n\u2022 Use familiar and favourite items to encourage children to use classroom areas and equipment they are not making use of.\n\u2022 Change the physical level of activities so that they are lower to the ground and easier to access.\n\u2022 Gradually change the social groupings of the children so they can play with familiar children but also with others to develop their social interaction.\n\u2022 Send items home so that autistic children can use these in a familiar environment\n\u2022 Plan carefully for any transition and allow as much time as is needed for the child to feel comfortable\n\u2022 Invite parents in to support their child in the classroom.\n\u2022 Explain your approach in detail to parents so that they understand and can work in partnership.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "gap-report-case-studies_i-s.pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1xo_7Q7LxUFHSLjQLhEE8MuxPnqGFEGEo", "source_id": "8bfe7c3cc9a918e195ac64f0cc2adc98cd589bcc8b9655b9f78b69ba9bfddeb0", "page_number": 70, "split_id": 300, "split_idx_start": 154937, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "6dcc6c6593235b248230fda0c19542c67ea8a4f8f8a5980e41dca8be4e528d6d", "range": [334, 602]}, {"doc_id": "979129444fb46934cd5a2f888ada2c67c6852805e08613654ddc533246c6d379", "range": [0, 98]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03275051712989807, -0.08233782649040222, -0.012956144288182259, 0.03881561756134033, 0.019261639565229416, 0.009299704805016518, 0.030794069170951843, -0.03789105638861656, -0.03526165708899498, 0.0009502698667347431, -0.007309000473469496, -0.055507101118564606, 0.015418061055243015, 0.010255511850118637, -0.027477029711008072, -0.075228750705719, 0.0397707037627697, 0.04256824776530266, -0.03409910202026367, -0.00834629125893116, -0.0029384316876530647, 0.0013004483189433813, -0.013637100346386433, 0.007625062484294176, 0.04261878877878189, -0.028718503192067146, -0.0019480251939967275, -0.0059509859420359135, 0.018211742863059044, -0.047695714980363846, 0.05459621548652649, 0.0184573233127594, 0.010449123568832874, 0.03438396751880646, 2.088793735310901e-06, 0.0005185434129089117, 0.03718281164765358, -0.03935106471180916, 0.006538514979183674, -0.06041691452264786, -0.0435207337141037, 0.0061273896135389805, 0.05419997125864029, 0.05427732318639755, -0.019762735813856125, -0.02686302177608013, 0.02520396187901497, 0.043606359511613846, -0.003188434289768338