9767991602421, 0.018423691391944885, -0.04343237727880478, 0.011338199488818645, -0.0032121564727276564, -0.03660377115011215, 0.017831411212682724, 0.009691845625638962, 0.0017439296934753656, -0.023338695988059044], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "9e59b27af54c44282f27514d4adedb989fb121bde91b7921aac00fe0a570960c", "content": "This chunk is part of the section that outlines the AET Post-16 Professional Development Programme, emphasizing its role in providing resources, modules, and frameworks for staff supporting autistic learners in Post-16 educational settings. It highlights the Competency and Progression Frameworks designed to enhance practice and track progress for autistic students.This Programme contains a set of modules and materials for staff working with autistic learners in Post-16 provisions. In addition to the Standards, the AET Post-16 Professional Development Programme consists of:\n\u2022 A Post-16 Competency Framework that enables practitioners to evaluate and reflect upon their own practice when working with autistic learners.\n\u2022 A Progression Framework that serves as a comprehensive interactive assessment tool that supports practitioners to identify learning priorities, set key learning intentions, and track progress for autistic learners in both mainstream and specialist educational provisions.\nThe Post-16 Professional Development Programme also has a range of training modules for those working in Post-16 settings.\nFor further information, please visit the AET website: www.autismeducationtrust.org.uk/training\nThe AET Post-16 Professional Development Programme\nThe AET Schools Standards Framework is part of the Schools Professional Development Programme. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 6, "spl