 This Programme contains a set of modules and materials for staff working in Schools across mainstream and specialist.\nIn addition to the Standards the AET Schools Professional Development Programme consists of:\n\u2022 The Schools Competency Framework that enables practitioners to evaluate and reflect upon their own practice when working with autistic children.\n\u2022 A Progression Framework that is a comprehensive interactive assessment tool that supports practitioners to identify learning priorities, set key learning intentions, and track progress for autistic children and young people in both mainstream and specialist educational provisions.\nAET Schools Professional Development Programme.\f", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 6, "split_id": 11, "split_idx_start": 7373, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "9e59b27af54c44282f27514d4adedb989fb121bde91b7921aac00fe0a570960c", "range": [755, 997]}, {"doc_id": "f356289bfb3c16207406feae54c05d03df558ac0177374b3e48e87b5aafce5b9", "range": [0, 48]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.004339719191193581, -0.10446763783693314, -0.021704593673348427, -0.018974989652633667, 0.0012003243900835514, 0.028234323486685753, 0.01349569484591484, -0.032993290573358536, -0.04036388546228409, 0.04628469794988632, 0.039631519466638565, -0.044497404247522354, 0.01374101173132658, 0.01381216011941433, -0.002121241530403495, -0.0709511861205101, 0.02455570548772812, 0.026028240099549294, -0.04376967251300812, 0.024938059970736504, 0.026086844503879547, 0.008244817145168781, -0.048572830855846405, 0.0497499518096447, 0.026007765904068947, -0.00623730942606926, -0.0028712470084428787, 0.0016160189406946301, 0.05555729195475578, -0.027735276147723198, 0.033921658992767334, 0.018741559237241745, 0.008690044283