7723591327667], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "77fc65d5bdf92e35ca8cc608c5a903afd32df8d6f33622d08cf7504c3ec2d9c1", "content": "This chunk emphasizes the importance of involving autistic learners in their educational journey by seeing them as partners in the \u2018Assess, Plan, Do, Review\u2019 cycle. It aligns with Principle Three of the AET Post-16 Standards, which focuses on fostering ongoing collaboration among autistic learners, staff, families, and external services.I see the autistic learner as a partner in their learning and actively involve them as part of the \u2018Assess, Plan, Do, Review\u2019 cycle so that the autistic learner is at the centre of educational planning.\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n9 Positive and effective relationships\nSTANDARDS COMPETENCIES\nSTANDARDS COMPETENCIES\nPrinciple Three: Ongoing and positive collaboration between the autistic learner, staff, a range of services, and parents/carers.\nPrinciple Four: Workforce development related to Good Autism Practice.\nS5. We support the autistic learner to share information with a range of professionals and their family about what is important to them at key transition points in their life.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 9, "split_id": 22, "split_idx_start": 12229, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "571b1061a3bb8cd994130f9a0927af8d36513447acf2e88a768d2bb9a7cd1889", "range": [332, 535]}, {"doc_id": "2eff01a5572e04b906f75f4f1786178956cb410d9a0f1e7a35d65c63ff7f57af", "range": [0, 172]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.010717806406319141, -0.06926140189170837, -0.02757878601551056, -0.003247385611757636, 0.01342807151377201, 0.023503590375185013, 0.017823833972215652, -0.051104795187711716, -0.023159731179475784, 0.02965841442346573, 0.01113939285