on discussing the importance of collaboration between autistic learners, staff, parents/carers, and various professionals. It emphasizes the need for understanding the perspectives of autistic individuals and the use of the AET Competencies framework to enhance staff development and improve practice in supporting autistic learners.I take onboard the perspectives of autistic young people and adults.\nS6. We work collaboratively with the autistic learner, and with health, social care, mental health services, parents/carers (if appropriate), and other professionals to help the autistic learner to consider future pathways, and to ensure that the autistic learner is supported by a range of professionals to have as much control as possible of their lives. S8. We use the AET Competencies framework to audit staff confidence levels, understanding and knowledge of autism, and the changes staff make to their practice as a result of undertaking professional development. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 10, "split_id": 25, "split_idx_start": 13558, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "aa95bb5cfc3d04fa1a23f1d643a0629625303c8d59dd4cc33db12d412e26cd10", "range": [399, 468]}, {"doc_id": "61bafaf7e5f03eb9257e5a6f95d2352b11b4cfd77a5eeec7851d225aea6266d3", "range": [0, 209]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.032239191234111786, -0.10035373270511627, -0.023484377190470695, 0.010956278070807457, -0.000995500129647553, 0.03878325596451759, 0.0454348586499691, -0.04313556104898453, -0.041234321892261505, 0.01109267957508564, 0.014193865470588207, -0.07329726964235306, 0.021917158737778664, -0.002930206013843417, 0.010786675848066807, -0.03868864104151726, 0.026475531980395317, 0.02819133549928665, -0.021692609414458275, 0.016447316855192184, 0.00605465