.02424025349318981, 0.012140624225139618, -0.008034094236791134, -0.00033191763213835657, -0.02723938599228859], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "edf6774d0584e053aebfeed333ccd7d3b2cf4dd4de0858d3c23d136e3173cd37", "content": "This chunk is situated within the section discussing \"Enabling environments\" in the AET Post-16 Standards Framework. It emphasizes the importance of creating a supportive atmosphere where staff are well-informed about autism, fostering a calm learning environment, and ensuring proactive collaboration among staff to implement Good Autism Practice effectively for autistic learners.We promote a supportive, enabling environment in which all staff are knowledgeable about autism and we empower staff to approach senior staff when their input is required.\nS11. Our enabling approaches foster a calm, low-arousal learning environment and we promote a sense of wellbeing, security, and belonging for all our autistic learners.\nC9. I proactively work with my line manager and/or Learning Support Manager to identify, share, and embed Good Autism Practice.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 11, "split_id": 28, "split_idx_start": 14899, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "54c62855c1e0ef0a3b317feedc02a7c61304a17f81f518e644a78a11d5959af6", "range": [509, 681]}, {"doc_id": "fcb25db5d0388d68f43035a324bb8ce771c2b0d4fc7e6ccb4892198cd3939f44", "range": [0, 124]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03198690712451935, -0.13589607179164886, -0.028342435136437416, 0.02196480892598629, 0.015840157866477966, 0.03785613179206848, 0.03622424975037575, -0.03143603727221489, -0.05198315158486366, 0.010658505372703075, 0.024800650775432587, -0.024828186258673668, 0.025841766968369484, 0.017753293737769127, 0.018435772508382797, -0.046480379