 0.0132726626470685, 0.018905315548181534, -0.032773956656455994, 0.01028947439044714, 0.01276399940252304, -0.05254087224602699, -0.05458113178610802, 0.014166445471346378, 0.056844957172870636, -0.017732691019773483, 0.06986864656209946, -0.04368273541331291, 0.01244459766894579, 0.009677337482571602, -0.022088617086410522, 0.002847612602636218, -0.021526528522372246, 0.02462812140583992, -0.04160257801413536, 0.06345557421445847, -0.0074583436362445354, 0.03382498025894165, -0.019102435559034348, -0.06689991056919098, 0.03389006853103638, -0.007623129989951849, 0.04944881424307823, 0.011980322189629078, -0.018691182136535645, 0.01867326721549034, 0.03698468208312988, 0.022801833227276802, 0.03072071075439453, -0.012678544037044048, 0.0014554958324879408, -0.06422894448041916, 0.0015871705254539847, -0.04160602390766144, 0.0695592388510704, -0.0068483310751616955, -0.03394344449043274, 0.018877044320106506, 0.00839377660304308, 0.00294022005982697, -0.032315485179424286, -0.05946847423911095, -0.014703482389450073, 1.794258505883312e-34, -0.00014991022180765867, 0.010319758206605911, 0.019557658582925797, -0.10294083505868912, 0.006552782375365496, -0.001277355826459825, -0.04412315785884857, 0.012655538506805897, 0.0021927307825535536, -0.026530403643846512, -0.02603268250823021], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "d8b159c5746b35bc7a3b131a07a974e16e9f9b401d248a0e8f68d5f6c030eb8a", "content": "This chunk is part of the AET Post-16 Standards Framework, specifically addressing Principle One, which focuses on understanding the strengths, interests, and needs of each autistic learner. It emphasizes the importance of recognizing co-occurring differences, such as anxiety and stress, that may impact behavior and learning, and outlines the need for close collaboration with autistic learners to identify effective strategies for support and regulation.We engage with the autistic learner to find ways of making reasonable adjustments and regulating behaviour. ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING DEVELOPING DEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nPrinciple One: Understanding the strengths, interests, and needs of each autistic learner.\nStandard Two: We take account of how each autistic learner\u2019s co-occurring differences, including anxiety and stress, can affect behaviour and can cause barriers to learning. We work closely with the autistic learner to understand their needs, and to find strategies for regulating feelings and emotions.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we do this: Link to statutory framework\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n16 Understanding the learner\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 16, "split_id": 42, "split_idx_start": 21683, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f9d17ed13a26fd2e7831f95de95ebd11d0e28c234ffdcf8c023d38068a2d542e", "range": [700, 808]}, {"doc_id": "ad11c841feb72a821769e4e572f6457c1ed6171d7adb1247ebe6617d71d80367", "range": [0, 224]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.015874411910772324, -0.08124774694442749, -0.02539096027612686, -0.006043748464435339, 0.004254951607435942, 0.02041744813323021, 0.03396342322230339, -0.021422483026981354, -0.05341465771198273, -0.015553733333945274, 0.013814629055559635, -0.06939393281936646, -0.01720999926328659, 0.0023016869090497494, -0.007750266697257757, -0.06313235312700272, 0.025777073577046394, 0.0362095907330513, -0.005022135097533464, 0.025187768042087555, 0.025449560955166817, 0.0049124169163405895, -0.020032024011015892, 0.033173609524965286, 0.03645367920398712, -0.02779579348862171, 0.014454752206802368, 0.01147453486919403, 0.0243779029697179