843848467, -0.01898837462067604, -0.07948983460664749, -0.06680204719305038, 0.00939223263412714, 2.016544258035066e-34, -0.01568201743066311, 0.02547694556415081, 0.033491749316453934, -0.043067336082458496, 0.01987585797905922, -0.0018379647517576814, -0.03818950429558754, 0.01363085862249136, -0.01342710480093956, -0.030316930264234543, -0.026017602533102036], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "ad11c841feb72a821769e4e572f6457c1ed6171d7adb1247ebe6617d71d80367", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Understanding the learner\" section within the AET Post-16 Standards Framework. It discusses the assessment of practices related to supporting autistic learners by evaluating their strengths and aspirations, documenting evidence of compliance, and identifying areas of improvement, development, and effectiveness in implementation.ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we do this: Link to statutory framework\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n16 Understanding the learner\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn autistic learners:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn staff:\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? We document evidence of working on this standard through assessment results, the production of resources, case studies, learner profiles, and the goals we co-\ncreate with autistic learners and parents/carers (where appropriate/possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\nEvidence to show how we meet this standard:\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n17 Understanding the learner\nWe enable autistic learners to identify and celebrate their strengths, hopes, dreams, and aspirations. We work with them to record this information in their learner profile.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff246