en staff and autistic learners, promoting active communication and involvement in decision-making, particularly during review meetings and transition planning, highlighting areas for improvement and current practices.ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we do this: Guidance\nWe establish strong relationships between staff and autistic learners, promoting active listening and the exchange of information and ideas, using person-centred approaches to ensure young people are involved in decision-making. The autistic learner\u2019s perspective is central in review meetings and transition planning.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n20 Understanding the learner\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn autistic learners:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn staff:\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? We document evidence of working on this standard through assessment results, the production of resources, case studies, learner profiles, and the goals we co-\ncreate with autistic learners and parents/carers (where appropriate/possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 20, "split_id": 50, "split_idx_start": 27452, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f26dc9ae6525203b2064d3ed2cff9f1a232050395c88b9222361282a31fce464", "range": [716, 1037]}, {"doc_id": "8224d2bd9f0439e032300a85e20dd7e922151933404a3bd88b858479bab315d7", "range": [0, 309]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0319160632789135, -0.09984447062015533, -0.024350330233573914, 0.011333378963172436, 0.012658124789595604, 0.031732309609651566, 0.0281960591673851, -0.03540697693824768, -0.03860543295741