046631, -0.021663660183548927, -0.003958819434046745, 0.014175456017255783, -0.04331127926707268, 0.007320493459701538, -0.021294161677360535, 0.05562261864542961, 0.037972837686538696, -0.021588129922747612, -0.01482674852013588, 0.016580257564783096, 0.016127509996294975, 0.04900693893432617, -0.004704528022557497, 0.002594843041151762, -0.048416897654533386, 0.017624367028474808, -0.04134153202176094, 0.07373739033937454, -0.00206015189178288, -0.016956517472863197, 0.001975411083549261, 0.020220573991537094, 0.014588134363293648, -0.024089684709906578, -0.048420149832963943, 0.0148454075679183, 2.179775653559905e-34, -0.011465480551123619, -0.023046189919114113, 0.041300415992736816, -0.04504786804318428, 0.00047728329082019627, -0.013656200841069221, -0.020381206646561623, 0.018631888553500175, -0.006725889630615711, -0.0047972844913601875, -0.0355248786509037], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "f5085a4b27de5fa2958c9d13ac69b0ccdb5466e4331a243e821d44377b635250", "content": "This chunk is part of the AET Post-16 Standards Framework, specifically addressing Standard Six under Principle Three, which focuses on fostering ongoing collaboration between autistic learners, staff, and various professionals. It emphasizes the importance of providing guidance for future pathways, promoting autonomy for autistic learners in decision-making, and improving their overall support and outcomes.ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING DEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nPrinciple Three: Ongoing and positive collaboration between the autistic learner, staff, a range of services, and parents/\ncarers.\nStandard Six: We work collaboratively with the autistic learner, and with health, social care, mental health services, parents/\ncarers (if appropriate), and other professionals to help the autistic learner to consider future pathways, and to ensure that the autistic learner is supported by a range of professionals to have as much control as possible of their lives.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we do this: Link to statutory framework\nWe involve other professionals in providing guidance and support for the preparation of Education, Health, and Care (EHC) plans, social care packages or DSA support, as well as employment advice and how to access support and benefits, according to the needs of the autistic learner. ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n25 Positive and effective relationships\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn autistic learners:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn staff:\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 25, "split_id": 56, "split_idx_start": 32327, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "358a79ce525bc3604c7210a05c1c3ece36a182c62703af4262edcf8186438bd6", "range": [643, 884]}, {"doc_id": "0bb5d2e912cff97a0fe165b5b3fa17e80af619ccf3e3024329be35d3daad1672", "range": [0, 108]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03736915439367294, -0.08981988579034805, -0.017658565193414688, -0.015250132419168949, -0.0011536028468981385, 0.02466326765716076, 0.05220091715455055, -0.02756643109023571, -0.0399942472577095, -0.006181286182254553, 0.02529776096343994, -0.07064472883939743, 0.014170253649353981, 0.0011421421077102423, 0.003884037723764777, -0.04704437404870987, 0.028038805350661278, 0.03154497221112251, -0.015575647354125977, -0.003043966833502054, 0.013163388706743717, 0.022853916510939598, -0.030240660533308983, 0.03172210231423378, 0.024005502462387085, -0.004822654649615288, 0.017158960923552513, 0.018175121396780014, 0.014936630614101887, -0.04143723100423813, 0.027534112334251404, -0.007205166853964329, 0