9685211182, 0.034700147807598114, 2.012722983039932e-34, -0.010031169280409813, 0.00037962140049785376, 0.021379532292485237, -0.03703349456191063, 0.007320518605411053, 0.002888251794502139, -0.006310012191534042, 0.022765859961509705, -0.00976648274809122, -0.015162772499024868, -0.009242454543709755], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "0bb5d2e912cff97a0fe165b5b3fa17e80af619ccf3e3024329be35d3daad1672", "content": "This chunk is part of the section discussing the evaluation and documentation of standards related to positive and effective relationships in the AET Post-16 Standards Framework. It emphasizes the importance of documenting evidence of practice improvements for autistic learners, parents/carers, and staff, and highlights the role of professional development in enhancing educational outcomes for autistic students.On autistic learners:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn staff:\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? We document evidence of working on this standard through assessment results, the production of resources, case studies, learner profiles, and the goals we co-\ncreate with autistic learners and parents/carers (where appropriate/possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\nEvidence to show how we meet this standard:\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n26 Positive and effective relationships\nWe recognise the importance of high-quality professional development in the education of autistic learners. As knowledge is continuously developing, there is a need to regularly update the knowledge, skills, and practice of the workforce. The governing bodies of colleges should ensure that all staff interact appropriately and inclusively with learners who have SEN or a disability and should ensure that they have appropriate expertise within their workforce. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_w