ately and inclusively with learners who have SEN or a disability and should ensure that they have appropriate expertise within their workforce. They should also ensure that curriculum staff are able to develop their skills, are aware of effective practice and keep their knowledge up to date. Colleges should make sure they have access to specialist skills and expertise to support the learning of learners with SEN [...] They should ensure that there is a named person in the college with oversight of SEND provision to ensure coordination of support (SEND Code of Practice, 2015:116).\nOur setting empowers and supports staff to share, learn, and enhance knowledge and skills to develop greater understanding of autism and common co-occurring differences. Ongoing continuous professional development and learning (CPD) includes self-directed learning, mentoring, coaching, and discussion and collaboration with colleagues.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 27, "split_id": 58, "split_idx_start": 34277, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "0bb5d2e912cff97a0fe165b5b3fa17e80af619ccf3e3024329be35d3daad1672", "range": [768, 991]}, {"doc_id": "c6643b94ee0ee645f1a799a936b3ce535a2a5d0f50ec353d475d1776e3f72ae5", "range": [0, 167]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03904030844569206, -0.07335491478443146, -0.0370146706700325, 0.010614159516990185, 0.02511717937886715, 0.05033431947231293, 0.03922518715262413, -0.07194387167692184, -0.012745152227580547, 0.006497727707028389, 0.04464295879006386, -0.027633868157863617, 0.010746327228844166, 0.018611516803503036, 0.02403506636619568, -0.056494466960430145, 0.018357396125793457, 0.04363352060317993, -0.019043879583477974, 0.026315409690141678, 0.0029240401927381754, 0.02856912836432457, -0.03895893320441