the AET Post-16 Competencies to identify the professional development needs of staff who work with autistic learners.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n27 Positive and effective relationships\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn autistic learners:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn staff:\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? We document evidence of working on this standard through assessment results, the production of resources, case studies, learner profiles, and the goals we co-\ncreate with autistic learners and parents/carers (where appropriate/possible), and by documenting our reasonable adjustments and the impact of those.\nEvidence to show how we meet this standard:\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n28 Positive and effective relationships\nAll staff attend ongoing training appropriate to their role, and understand how autism can impact on individual learners. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 27, "split_id": 60, "split_idx_start": 35710, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "c6643b94ee0ee645f1a799a936b3ce535a2a5d0f50ec353d475d1776e3f72ae5", "range": [597, 833]}, {"doc_id": "81c391a4ddb6d75de8ee43420c45c8a6b43d5cce06b233baf27a331250aa08f2", "range": [0, 234]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03195340186357498, -0.07281684875488281, -0.01814972423017025, 0.005957012064754963, -0.0035227767657488585, 0.051597900688648224, 0.04017586261034012, -0.0217339638620615, -0.04123809561133385, 0.0014520753175020218, 0.0561102069914341, -0.045779623091220856, 0.029380997642874718, -0.026386909186840057, 0.014630314894020557, -0.06424500048160553, 0.027476171031594276, 0.0452413372695446, -0.05259674787521362, 0.020747536793351173, 0.009533757343888283, 0