33972931, -0.05309496447443962, 0.02069493941962719, -0.03358546644449234, 0.08192338794469833, 0.01226404495537281, -0.02337353676557541, 0.002405736828222871, 0.02076752670109272, -0.0024399368558079004, -0.01510297879576683, -0.046591658145189285, 0.009772535413503647, 1.960807458706858e-34, -0.006811991799622774, -0.00942692905664444, 0.01764584705233574, -0.07170941680669785, 0.014057195745408535, -0.00040061090840026736, -0.0118870185688138, 0.011141203343868256, -0.024808021262288094, -0.009605379775166512, -0.02732560597360134], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "81c391a4ddb6d75de8ee43420c45c8a6b43d5cce06b233baf27a331250aa08f2", "content": "This chunk is part of the \"Positive and Effective Relationships\" section in the AET Post-16 Standards Framework. It emphasizes the importance of ongoing training for staff to understand autism, highlighting their reflective practices and commitment to ethical behavior, ultimately ensuring that they support autistic learners effectively and promote their independence in educational settings.Evidence to show how we meet this standard:\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n28 Positive and effective relationships\nAll staff attend ongoing training appropriate to their role, and understand how autism can impact on individual learners. This includes safeguarding autistic learners.\nTeachers and trainers are reflective and enquiring practitioners who think critically about their own educational assumptions, values, and practice in the context of a changing contemporary and educational world [...] They draw on relevant research as part of evidence-based practice. They act with honesty and integrity to maintain high standards of ethics and professional behaviour in support of learners and their expectations (Education and Training Foundation, Professional Standards for Teachers and Trainers in Further Education, 2014:1).\nWe ensure our staff have the confidence to support autistic learners, and we support them to be as independent as possible and to work towards outcomes that are important to the autistic learner. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 28, "split_id": 61, "split_idx_start": 36542, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "b1caf04d0df06134e0866ef8abce3d01a0c9dac012ae6bf987d9ad713bd1fb5d", "range": [832, 1066]}, {"doc_id": "5e6ade2d4ded87159210ba0251445c78b76d45340ca9dc360f0485e95066ebaf", "range": [0, 196]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.03750970959663391, -0.08435699343681335, -0.017444731667637825, 0.01797477900981903, -0.008490195497870445, 0.03695397824048996, 0.031352054327726364, -0.03606945276260376, -0.06286779046058655, -0.009793559089303017, 0.010985790751874447, -0.04713352397084236, 0.00021708749409299344, -0.015202712267637253, -0.0016769671346992254, -0.05008183419704437, 0.026700034737586975, 0.043093111366033554, -0.00830853171646595, 0.013892129994928837, 0.005169490817934275, 0.029384616762399673, -0.026864059269428253, 0.030988546088337898, 0.010481078177690506, -0.02122855745255947, 0.035802800208330154, -0.009919984266161919, 0.020655637606978416, -0.042719628661870956, 0.03333868086338043, -0.02921951375901699, -0.0005093306535854936, -0.015862824395298958, 2.1359762740758015e-06, 0.023852761834859848, -0.004709533415734768, -0.009721716865897179, 0.009595557115972042, -0.032376084476709366, -0.07249198853969574, 0.02500978857278824, 0.040374722331762314, 0.06805668026208878, -0.028782173991203308, -0.00892006978392601, 0.014135188423097134, 0.041789766401052475, 0.01223804522305727, 0.006205891724675894, -0.005649255122989416, 0.03252745419740677, 0.027249785140156746, -0.03869140148162842, -0.03769340366125107, -0.01796107552945614, 0.02467205561697483, -0.07115207612514496, -0.01649656891822815, 0.05193870887160301, -0.01363250