 staff competence in supporting autistic learners through continuous professional development and self-evaluation, highlighting the use of the AET Competencies framework to measure staff effectiveness.We ensure our staff have the confidence to support autistic learners, and we support them to be as independent as possible and to work towards outcomes that are important to the autistic learner. Staff complete self-evaluation forms about their knowledge, confidence, and practice related to autism before and after undertaking continuous professional development (CPD).\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING DEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nPrinciple Four: Workforce development related to Good Autism Practice .\nStandard Eight: We use the AET Competencies framework to audit staff confidence levels, understanding and knowledge of autism, and the changes staff make to their practice as a result of undertaking professional development.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we do this: Link to statutory framework\nWe gather information from staff about the changes they make to their practice as a result of professional development and for performance management purposes through the AET Competencies working document. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 29, "split_id": 62, "split_idx_start": 37369, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "81c391a4ddb6d75de8ee43420c45c8a6b43d5cce06b233baf27a331250aa08f2", "range": [827, 1023]}, {"doc_id": "842eec744afcc04fc18823ce901f323fcee4178ae8e30d5704068bab35a12c76", "range": [0, 317]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.003397447755560279, -0.10663628578186035, -0.02636818401515484, 0.009453793056309223, -0.014141896739602089, 0.039