17977690697, -0.02402196079492569, 7.53394779167138e-05, 0.023034092038869858, -0.02468900755047798, 0.04898184537887573, -0.02230716496706009, 0.08727661520242691, -0.00025344479945488274, -0.009550600312650204, -0.008518893271684647, -0.042407482862472534, 0.02344491146504879, -0.006115845870226622, 0.041255902498960495, 0.015432938002049923, -0.07207418978214264, -0.010387998074293137, -0.008822271600365639, 0.024828637018799782, 0.03393781930208206, -0.025452181696891785, -0.015036211349070072, -0.05788591876626015, 0.0022587657440453768, -0.03461678326129913, 0.07678868621587753, -0.022727224975824356, -0.01856139861047268, 0.008309418335556984, -0.006654271390289068, -0.008700764738023281, -0.02648625150322914, -0.04539993405342102, -0.0031815452966839075, 2.4031859313621137e-34, -0.005675039254128933, -0.003881500568240881, 0.0220920592546463, -0.05089399963617325, 0.007529699709266424, -0.00014074901991989464, 0.01776162162423134, 0.0009670044528320432, -0.02438906393945217, 0.0059893387369811535, -0.037061743438243866], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "007187f5ba07c7a2de68267c05f078941b5092f76e45c14d3212e5e33a269c56", "content": "This chunk appears in the section discussing the importance of leadership and management in promoting Good Autism Practice within educational settings. It emphasizes the need for high expectations and inclusion for children and young people with Special Educational Needs and Disabilities (SEND), highlighting the intersection of SEN and disability legislation in the context of creating supportive environments for autistic learners.The leaders of Early Years settings, Schools and Colleges should establish and maintain a culture of high expectations that expects those working with children and young people with SEND to include them in all the opportunities available to other children. There is a significant overlap between children and young people with SEN and those with disabilities and [many] are covered by both SEN and equality legislation\n(SEND Code of Practice, 2015:27).\nInformation about how we support autistic learners is referenced in our quality improvement plan, in policies (particularly the SEND policy and the behaviour policy) and in our Equality Duty objectives.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING DEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nPrinciple Five: Leadership and management that promotes and embeds Good Autism Practice.\nStandard Nine: We promote a supportive, enabling environment in which all staff are knowledgeable about autism and we empower staff to approach senior staff when their input is required.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 32, "split_id": 65, "split_idx_start": 39617, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "f9039e066ca84fcb6194bcb5e29bad08fe5b79ed65fa3026937895a792be67a8", "range": [557, 814]}, {"doc_id": "6d544d177a62cae5c475647ee42da5c2410a018fec9adb977dfc8f31b7dd81ab", "range": [0, 187]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.050013359636068344, -0.0666714608669281, -0.026080533862113953, 0.03712441399693489, 0.023687219247221947, 0.05212445557117462, 0.03420046344399452, -0.04949065297842026, -0.03055126592516899, 0.005901399068534374, 0.06251989305019379, -0.06509707123041153, 0.0448240227997303, 0.027998564764857292, 0.0146391112357378, -0.041648294776678085, 0.03394613415002823, 0.06365615129470825, -0.011673413217067719, 0.026665018871426582, 0.001748797600157559, 0.01296069286763668, -0.014174327254295349, 0.029494356364011765, 0.025720693171024323, -0.007553585339337587, 0.012955937534570694, 0.013746085576713085, 0.009849119000136852, -0.029776064679026604, 0.038534753024578094, -0.027212778106331825, -0.003743294859305024, -0.04229762777686119, 1.973118060050183e-06, 0.0162731446