549357891, 0.04625268280506134, 0.028201064094901085, 0.004857908934354782, 0.00809228140860796, 0.005462546832859516, -0.028501547873020172, -0.04474267736077309, 0.03858252242207527, 0.04638480395078659, -0.024939147755503654, 0.017543841153383255, -0.003656328422948718, 0.015022093430161476, -0.01055548619478941, -0.01152640487998724, 0.014529973268508911, -0.02588682994246483, 0.037033189088106155, -0.03734837472438812, 0.10258571803569794, -0.017783161252737045, 0.011785601265728474, 0.009031422436237335, -0.022326689213514328, 0.0258233230561018, -0.036135945469141006, 0.028297046199440956, 0.014287474565207958, -0.021819833666086197, 0.008729258552193642, 0.024384355172514915, 0.03440520912408829, 0.027966434136033058, -0.01710512489080429, 0.0004241527058184147, -0.06649685651063919, 0.005523291882127523, -0.04719652980566025, 0.06330305337905884, -0.016278166323900223, -0.03274470195174217, 0.038435839116573334, -0.0007507649715989828, 0.03723185881972313, -0.012942523695528507, -0.03328331559896469, 0.007516955491155386, 2.1584509921745385e-34, -0.002276788931339979, 0.01224254909902811, 0.010432538576424122, -0.09086617827415466, 0.013733160682022572, -0.02560739405453205, -0.009780270978808403, 0.004986392334103584, -0.022285256534814835, 0.019046105444431305, -0.02386130951344967], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "c28173bbf151543337141dd311af568cce0f6b542b61bca54c27eaba03388691", "content": "This chunk discusses Standard Ten under Principle Five of the AET Post-16 Standards Framework, focusing on leadership and management practices that promote Good Autism Practice. It addresses the importance of creating inclusive environments, reducing social exclusion, and facilitating pathways to employment for autistic learners through mutual support and understanding among peers and staff.ROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING DEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nPrinciple Five: Leadership and management that promotes and embeds Good Autism Practice.\nStandard Ten: We embed Good Autism Practice in the organisation and work with all staff to ensure this is consistent across the setting. We address the risk of social exclusion for autistic learners, enable autistic learners to access college and community activities, and develop pathways to employment.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we do this: Link to statutory framework\nOur provision implements approaches to develop the mutual understanding, communication, and support between autistic learners, their autistic and non-autistic peers, staff and employers. For example, we set up buddy systems and peer mentoring schemes, with both autistic and non-autistic peers. ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 34, "split_id": 69, "split_idx_start": 42680, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "225771e35521fa2e322ef1ffac95aa383c5c9813ac5815b0ea29ce65eeeae4d4", "range": [585, 784]}, {"doc_id": "c6ffba4ba01b6d6951f488c6ce9866d97c987c7023b639b69caae6cc517c6214", "range": [0, 108]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.029599381610751152, -0.06323954463005066, -0.02654253877699375, 0.009100734256207943, 0.03780500590801239, 0.01073993369936943, 0.03984185308218002, -0.03641531616449356, -0.02926381677389145, 0.006399218924343586, 0.020040296018123627, -0.04533564671874046, 0.011865755543112755, 0.002282487228512764, 0.003560528391972184, -0.05136389285326004, 0.033482011407613754, 0.041788630187511444, -0.03073917143046856, -0.005978683475404978, 0.026129812002182007, 0.03794291615486145, 0.003022217657417059, 0.035577837377786636, 0.03181331232190132, -0.012263279408216476, 0.038059644401073456, 0.018442953005433083, 0.049520719796419144, -0.011552129872143269, 0.05274274945259094, -