471299447119236, -0.012146677821874619, 0.017351413145661354, 0.008633595891296864, -0.0068635037168860435, 0.007953213527798653, -0.032350022345781326], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "138851026035d9e507cb1829855f4bb8283a3c5949844b75027909be14e11bb0", "content": "This chunk is part of the AET Post-16 Standards Framework, specifically under Principle Six, which emphasizes creating an inclusive and supportive environment for autistic learners. It describes the importance of facilitating low-arousal spaces and activities to support autistic learners' engagement and well-being during unstructured times on campus.We talk to young people about what they want to do in their free time (i.e. all unstructured times). We facilitate support for this, for example by the provision of quiet space, a range of activities, and opportunities for interactions with others as appropriate. Low-arousal spaces are identified on the college campus so that autistic learners can access these if and when they feel they need to do so.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING DEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nWE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nPrinciple Six: An ethos and environment that fosters social inclusion for autistic learners.\n", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 36, "split_id": 72, "split_idx_start": 44866, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "cac0fc3d25aee9dc3a69c2bd312faefefc4dc383f3b2c2e780b535a0c49e0574", "range": [695, 771]}, {"doc_id": "9f9d89810c079bd89203f6867541306fae8317c53d21ed50c7c6b37b68627562", "range": [0, 203]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.0464516207575798, -0.10860813409090042, -0.022146495059132576, 0.006640351377427578, 0.014626829884946346, 0.04266497120261192, 0.049534764140844345, -0.044977329671382904, -0.04495687410