5949, -0.003621799172833562, -0.005825620610266924, -0.03806404396891594], "sparse_embedding": null}, {"id": "8e494cc4ac5732f0373294caeca4df06224ec8c963fac7f90144150ddc492e03", "content": "This chunk is part of the section on \"Enabling Environments\" within the AET Post-16 Standards Framework. It specifically addresses the need for colleges to adapt their practices and policies to accommodate the individual needs of autistic learners, particularly concerning access arrangements for exams and reasonable adjustments as outlined in SEND and equality legislation.We are constantly mindful of adapting to the needs of individual autistic learners.\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\nExamples of how we do this: Link to statutory framework\nWe have a good understanding of access arrangements for exams and reasonable adjustments that could be made to deliver best results for autistic young people under the SEND Code of Practice (2015) and the Equality Act 2010. We share this information with autistic learners and their parents/carers (when appropriate).\nROOM FOR IMPROVEMENT\nDEVELOPING WE DO THIS REALLY WELL\fPost-16 Standards Framework\n38 Enabling environments\nWhat has been the impact of implementing this standard?\nOn autistic learners:\nOn parents/carers:\nOn staff:\nHow do we document evidence of working on this standard? ", "dataframe": null, "blob": null, "meta": {"file_path": "Post-16-Standards-Framework_T-HUB-Sc-Mt (1).pdf", "url": "https://drive.google.com/file/d/1J2sZ87itIDhKcF_wmZN2TcBeZRLjlMJP", "source_id": "8c4c774884107306cf77966fe0ff24690d0139f6223da0babe2c1bcd4b2a95b5", "page_number": 38, "split_id": 77, "split_idx_start": 47790, "_split_overlap": [{"doc_id": "df213e444e2ca78072eb3d1ddb8e51801450be656e277b3d656e27f3e56bb5ba", "range": [536, 620]}, {"doc_id": "c1be6928151645f01d12b6aa46943924f94897e0244dd4c8271d7f99afc769aa", "range": [0, 108]}]}, "score": null, "embedding": [0.020246833562850952, -0.10305709391832352, -0.028694497421